<node id="Carbonation">
  <data key="d0">Carbonation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonation is a chemical treatment process applied to solid phases, primarily designed to induce weathering or bubbling reactions that yield modified solid products. In its general form, it serves as a method for altering the physical and chemical properties of solid materials through controlled reaction pathways.

Within industrial and environmental contexts, carbonation is extensively utilized in phosphogypsum management strategies. The process typically involves the reaction of phosphogypsum with reagents such as sodium hydroxide, and is often enhanced by the introduction of ammonia and elevated carbon dioxide pressure. These conditions facilitate the dissolution of the phosphogypsum matrix and drive subsequent chemical transformations.

The primary objective of this phosphogypsum-focused carbonation process is to convert the waste material into valuable compounds, specifically calcium carbonate and ammonium sulfate. A key application lies in indirect rare earth element leaching, where the process is engineered to dissolve phosphogypsum and selectively precipitate calcium carbonate enriched with rare earth elements, thereby enabling their recovery.

Beyond resource recovery, carbonation is also studied for its impact on the microstructure and engineering properties of phosphogypsum-based cementitious materials. By modifying the solid phase through carbonation, researchers aim to improve the durability, strength, and overall performance of construction materials derived from phosphogypsum, aligning waste treatment with sustainable building practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonation is a physicochemical pre-treatment technique applied to increase rare earth element concentration in phosphogypsum prior to extraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcination">
  <data key="d0">Calcination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcination is a high-temperature thermal treatment and synthesis process widely utilized in industrial and material science applications to decompose, transform, or modify chemical compounds and raw materials. Typically conducted under controlled conditions, such as in a nitrogen atmosphere, the procedure generally operates between 500°C and 900°C, with specific protocols tailored to target feedstocks. The process functions by disrupting molecular bonds, inducing dehydration, altering impurity profiles through eutectic mechanisms, and facilitating phase changes that transform soluble compounds into stable forms. By applying precise heat, calcination effectively alters crystallinity, phase composition, microstructure, and crystal growth orientation, thereby enhancing material reactivity, reducing porosity, and mitigating strength degradation.

A primary application of calcination is the treatment of phosphogypsum, where it serves as a prevalent purification and valorization technology. The efficiency of this process is influenced by the material's texture and morphology. Heating phosphogypsum at temperatures such as 600°C for four hours eliminates moisture, organic waste, fluoride, soluble contaminants, and initiates heavy metal reduction, while also decreasing radioactivity and reducing the material's retardation effect on setting time. This thermal pretreatment converts the waste into recyclable forms like anhydrite, calcium sulphate hemihydrate, and β-building gypsum powder, which are subsequently utilized in construction-grade bricks, gypsum plaster, enhanced fly ash-lime systems, ceramic molds, and fireproof coatings. Calcination is also critical in material synthesis, particularly for hydroxyapatite and bone ash, where heating at 600°C and 900°C facilitates surfactant evaporation, particle shrinkage, and significant improvements in crystallinity. Additionally, the technique is applied to brushite and ardealite to study dehydration and phase transformation behavior, with transformations monitored via X-ray diffraction. Beyond these, calcination is employed on diverse substrates including raw material pellets, feldspar, beneficiated solid phases, enriched concentrates, WBS, and crushed rock to alter physical and chemical properties and remove water-soluble impurities.

Despite its effectiveness in waste valorization, impurity removal, and structural modification, calcination faces notable limitations. It is currently recognized as a successful laboratory-scale purification technology for phosphogypsum but lacks large-scale industrial scalability. Furthermore, the process carries inherent environmental risks, primarily due to its high energy demands, which increase the overall carbon footprint, and the potential release of sulfur dioxide when processing certain materials like feldspar. Nevertheless, calcination remains a vital thermal process for studying dehydration behavior, managing impurity dynamics, and enabling the sustainable recycling of industrial substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal treatment process applied to phosphogypsum to produce hemihydrate or anhydrite forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal treatment process used to reduce impurities like phosphorus pentoxide and fluorides in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a heat treatment process applied to PG at various temperatures to alter its chemical and compound composition.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal treatment process applied to phosphogypsum samples at temperatures ranging from 170°C to 950°C.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal process that effectively removes water and volatiles from the gypsum structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal treatment process applied to phosphogypsum that significantly improves flexural strength retention at high replacement levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-016&lt;