</node>
<node id="Rice Paddy Ecosystem">
  <data key="d0">Rice Paddy Ecosystem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rice Paddy Ecosystem is a flooded agricultural environment characterized by distinct soil layers and active methane cycling.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rice Paddy Ecosystem is a flooded soil environment characterized by distinct redox layers that facilitate methane production and consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanotrophs">
  <data key="d0">Methanotrophs</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanotrophs are microorganisms residing in the rhizosphere that biologically consume methane before atmospheric release.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanotrophs are microorganisms located in the rhizosphere that consume methane.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790847976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aerenchymal Transport">
  <data key="d0">Aerenchymal Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerenchymal transport is a biological mechanism that facilitates the movement of methane from submerged soil to the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Aerenchymal Transport is a plant-mediated mechanism for moving gases like methane through waterlogged soils.&lt;SEP&gt;Aerenchymal transport is a mechanism for methane release from rice paddies to the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="El Zrelli, R.">
  <data key="d0">El Zrelli, R.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">El Zrelli, R. is a researcher whose scientific contributions center on environmental radioactivity, industrial waste evaluation, and contamination monitoring in Tunisia and the broader Mediterranean region. Operating as both a primary and co-author, El Zrelli, R. has led and collaborated on multiple peer-reviewed investigations. A key contribution includes a 2019 study that systematically assessed natural radioactivity and radiation hazards linked to industrial wastes in Gabes, Tunisia. This work underscores a methodological focus on quantifying radiological risks in industrial byproducts.

Beyond radiological assessments, El Zrelli, R. has extensively documented heavy metal contamination across various Tunisian sites. The researcher’s scope also encompasses the environmental transport and dispersion of phosphogypsum foam, with specific attention to its movement and ecological implications within the Mediterranean Sea. Together, these studies reflect a consistent research trajectory dedicated to hazard characterization, industrial waste management, and geochemical pollution tracking in North African and Mediterranean environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792400414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marine Pollution Bulletin">
  <data key="d0">Marine Pollution Bulletin</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Marine Pollution Bulletin is a scientific journal that published research on the environmental impact of coastal phosphate treatment plants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
