<node id="Southern Mediterranean Sea">
  <data key="d0">Southern Mediterranean Sea</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Southern Mediterranean Sea is a geographical and marine region that encompasses and borders Gabes, Tunisia. It serves as the body of water directly adjacent to the coastal phosphate treatment plants located in this area.

This region has been the focus of environmental and scientific research, particularly concerning the ecological impacts of industrial activities. Studies, including those conducted by Zrelli, have analyzed the transport effects of phosphogypsum foam within these waters. Specifically, the Southern Mediterranean Sea has been examined as a marine environment where the movement and dispersion of metals and radionuclides, facilitated by phosphogypsum foam, are actively monitored and evaluated.&lt;SEP&gt;The Southern Mediterranean Sea is the marine region studied for metal and radionuclide transport via phosphogypsum foam.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791428038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coastal Phosphate Treatment Plants">
  <data key="d0">Coastal Phosphate Treatment Plants</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Coastal phosphate treatment plants are industrial facilities in Tunisia that generate industrial wastes assessed for radiation hazards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790847976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Building Materials">
  <data key="d0">Building Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Building Materials constitute a fundamental category of construction products designed for structural and functional use within the built environment, serving as the primary global and Chinese application field for phosphogypsum (PG) utilization. In this domain, PG is incorporated as a primary constituent, additive, raw material, or binding component to manufacture a diverse range of substances, including cement, bricks, gypsum blocks and boards, cement mortar, cement-stabilized PG, plaster, and cement retarders. This high-volume application supports closed-loop resource utilization, effectively alleviating material shortages, reducing industrial waste, enhancing material properties, and promoting sustainable practices. However, only a small percentage of PG is currently recycled into this product category. The structural integrity of these materials is significantly influenced by PG impurity levels, and in specific applications, modified phosphogypsum (MPG) leverages its gelling activity under strict heavy metal limits. While traditionally viewed as a key utilization pathway, particularly in regions like Hubei, Yichang, and Yunnan provinces, this application is increasingly regarded as a traditional approach rather than a long-term solution due to its relatively low added value.

Commercial deployment of Building Materials encounters notable market constraints, including regional demand limitations and public perception concerns regarding safety and environmental impact. Because these construction products frequently incorporate industrial byproducts, they function as the primary context for rigorous radioactivity and safety evaluations. Manufacturing processes require continuous monitoring to prevent the release of radioactivity into the environment, with comprehensive assessments encompassing Radium Equivalent (Ra-Eq) calculations, radon-222 emanation power analyses, and structural property evaluations. These measures are essential to ensure that final products comply with established safety protocols and regulatory standards before market distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Application field where phosphogypsum is reviewed as a potential construction material.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction products that incorporate phosphogypsum to enhance properties like strength and durability.&lt;SEP&gt;Building materials represent the broad category of construction products where phosphogypsum and other industrial wastes are applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Building materials are a potential application for phosphogypsum, though its use is restricted by impurities and regional regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Building materials are products manufactured using phosphogypsum as a raw or calcined component to reduce clinkerization temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction products, such as cement and hollow blocks, that incorporate phosphogypsum as a component.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
