<node id="Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate (CaSO4·2H2O), commonly known as gypsum, is the primary chemical compound and main phase constituting phosphogypsum (PG) and related materials such as phosphogypsum effluent, high-silica phosphogypsum, early-stage magnesium phosphate gypsum, and mortar samples. It typically comprises 75% to 95% of the mass in these mixtures and serves as the principal source of calcium in relevant chemical reactions. Produced industrially as a solid byproduct during the wet-process phosphoric acid extraction and acidulation, it can also be obtained at temperatures between 70 and 80 degrees Celsius via the dihydrate process, and was notably precipitated in the 2011 study by Bard and Bilal.

In its natural state, the compound crystallizes in plate-like or prismatic formations, though treated, hydrated, or colloidal variants may exhibit globular morphologies, preferred orientation growth, or exist as amorphous substances. Analytically, it is frequently identified alongside quartz in XRD and SEM analyses, displaying a strong diffraction peak at 11.588° that serves as a standard reference; peak intensity correlates with concentration and vanishes when the compound is fully consumed during hydration below 15%. Chemically, it exhibits notable stability, lacks initial gelling activity, and generally increases setting times in phosphogypsum mixtures. It functions as an electrical insulator in pure phosphogypsum forms and cross-links calcium and sulfate ions to enhance structural strength. The compound readily dissolves to release ions, participates in redox reactions, reacts with phosphoric acid, and acts as the predominant solubilized species in nitric acid and alkaline treatments. Additionally, it can form a hydration gel that effectively adsorbs heavy metals such as chromium and mercury.

Thermal and process treatments significantly alter its properties. As an initial phase, its content decreases with rising calcination temperatures and extended holding times. Temperature exposure transforms its crystal structure, facilitates heavy metal replacement, and drives phase transitions to anhydrous forms or decomposition into calcium oxide at high temperatures, which aids impurity removal during potassium persulfate decomposition. Industrially, it serves as a solid starting material for plaster manufacturing, undergoing dehydration to form hemihydrate and anhydrite, or being modified into hemihydrate phosphogypsum. Advanced recovery workflows utilize mass spectrometry combined with EDTA to extract high-purity gypsum (often exceeding 95%) from calcium-EDTA complexes. Environmentally, its distinct solubility and crystal structure limit radium incorporation, while it plays a crucial role in resource sequestration by capturing between 70% and 80% of a system's total rare earth elements. Through these combined structural, chemical, and environmental attributes, Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate remains a central focus in the purification, industrial management, and analytical study of phosphogypsum and related materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Primary chemical component of phosphogypsum, constituting over 90% of its composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound constituting over 95% of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate is a compound derived from PG and pure gypsum used in stoichiometric mixtures for mineral synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-00