<node id="Calcium Carbonate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Carbonate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium carbonate (CaCO3) is a stable chemical compound and mineral powder with a molar mass of 100.09 g/mol. It serves as a biogenic calcium precursor, constituting 95–97% of chicken eggshells, and is widely utilized across industrial, environmental, and biomedical sectors. Production emphasizes resource recovery, utilizing feedstocks such as phosphogypsum, waste gypsum, steel converter slag, feldspar pellets, and portlandite. Synthesis pathways include reductive decomposition of phosphogypsum, aqueous conversion, carbonation, reactions with hydroxides or soda, CO2 capture into alkaline solutions, and processing of hydrolysates or calcium sulphide. Depending on the process stage and objective, it functions as a primary high-purity product, an intermediate, or a byproduct. The typical manufacturing process involves precipitating carbonate and calcium ions, followed by filtration, drying, and crystallization, often concluding within 74 minutes. It is also recovered from waste gypsum alongside sulfur, mixed with phosphate ore in wet method production, found in sodium bicarbonate-leached materials, and can form indirectly to leach rare earth elements from phosphogypsum. Additionally, a 0.01 mol/L STMP concentration yields it as a byproduct with inhomogeneous morphologies, and it is actively employed in phosphogypsum treatment methods.

In aqueous and soil environments, calcium carbonate participates in dynamic equilibriums via dissolution and hydrolysis, heavily influencing the Calcium Carbonate Equivalent (CCE) system. Its solubility responds to ionic conditions, depositing when calcium, bicarbonate, and carbonate ions are removed and dissolving with carbonate fluctuations. It deposits or dissolves due to ion adsorption in the soil solution and is notably present in Haplic Chernozem, with concentrations varying by soil depth. Functionally, it acts as a chemical additive that provides calcium ions to immobilize phosphates and fluorides, reacts with soluble impurities to form insolubles, accelerates condensation, and maintains high pH levels.

Applications span environmental remediation, including acidic water neutralization, contaminated water treatment, and acid mine drainage cleanup. In construction, it is incorporated into mortar and cementous materials, serves as a phosphogypsum substitute in quick lime-GGBFS-cement systems, and is used in modified polymers. It is also utilized as a building material or for lime production, and in analytical chemistry to standardize potassium hydroxide solutions. Biomedically, it serves as a substrate and spherical substance for depositing hydroxyapatite layers, acts as a starting material for synthesizing carbonate-containing apatite, and is studied for degradation in porous microspheres for bone tissue engineering due to its biocompatibility. In composite materials, it forms a protective layer that enhances durability in marine environments, though these protective benefits can be neutralized by high active lime content. Research contexts frequently analyze samples for trace elements, decomposition kinetics, and construction suitability. X-ray diffraction frequently identifies it alongside Portlandite, Calcite, and Quartz, while studies often evaluate high calcium oxide content samples alongside commercial forms using SEM-EDS to compare purity, morphology, and quantity, confirming its role as a benchmark material in chemical and materials science.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-04