<node id="Calcium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH)2), also recognized as portlandite and slaked lime, is a versatile alkaline base compound extensively utilized across industrial, environmental, and materials science applications. Identified by its characteristic O-H stretching vibration band and detectable in XRD patterns, it functions as both an active reactant and a byproduct. The compound is primarily produced through the hydration of calcium oxide, though it can also be generated via calcium sulfide hydrolysis, calcium aluminate hydrate decomposition, the precipitation of dissolved calcium and hydroxide ions, or as a product of calcium silicate hydration in PBSLM6. Commercially procured as an extra pure reagent from suppliers such as Aldrich and CHEMPUR, alternative synthesis routes include soda conversion of phosphogypsum, potassium hydroxide treatment, and processing eggshell powder with hydrochloric acid.

In environmental and waste management contexts, calcium hydroxide is critical for water treatment and phosphogypsum remediation. It effectively neutralizes and modifies the internal structure of phosphogypsum, immobilizes soluble phosphorus and fluorine impurities, and reacts with calcium phosphate salts and phosphoric acid during thermal treatment to generate inactive compounds. During fluorine immobilization, calcium fluoride precipitates form on its surface, which can subsequently limit further reactivity. The compound is also integral to mineral carbonation and carbon sequestration processes, where it reacts with carbon dioxide to form calcium carbonate. Within construction and materials engineering, calcium hydroxide serves as a primary mineral in phosphogypsum slag cement and composite filling bodies, directly influencing the bleeding rate, porosity, and unconfined compressive strength of resulting materials. Its diffraction peak intensity remains stable in modified and unaltered phosphogypsum samples but progressively diminishes and vanishes at 30% phosphogypsum content, signaling promoted hydration. Although it can adsorb onto gypsum crystals and potentially inhibit further hydration in certain cement mortars, it simultaneously reacts with phosphogypsum, fly ash, and slag on recycled aggregate surfaces to significantly enhance the interfacial transition zone. It is frequently employed as a starting point for improving lime for construction use and acts as a chemical additive in cement mixtures, including those prepared by Singh and Garg, as well as mixtures containing calcined phosphogypsum and slag. When added to calcined phosphogypsum, it functions as an accelerator that improves setting time and compressive strength.

In chemical synthesis, calcium hydroxide acts as a fundamental base reactant and precursor. It is calcined to form calcium oxide, thereby improving lime reactivity, and is utilized in neutralization reactions to synthesize hydroxyapatite (HAp Type 1) via both hydrothermal and precipitation methods. During hydrothermal synthesis, it appears as a transient side phase at 150 °C before being eliminated at higher temperatures, and when homogenized using a planetary mill in modified wet chemical precipitation processes, it acts as a precursor for synthesizing thermally stable hydroxyapatite. Its dehydroxylation kinetics and thermodynamics are actively studied, underscoring its broad utility as both a functional material and a chemical additive.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium hydroxide is an accelerator added to calcined Phosphogypsum to improve setting time and compressive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001</data>
