<node id="Fertilizers">
  <data key="d0">Fertilizers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fertilizers are agricultural and industrial products engineered to enhance crop growth by supplying essential nutrients, specifically calcium, potassium, phosphorus, and silicon. Chemically, these formulations frequently utilize hydroxyapatite and commonly contain dicalcium phosphate dihydrate as core components. Their manufacturing is deeply integrated into industrial chemical processes, notably serving as a commercial output and primary application sector for phosphoric acid produced via the wet process pathway. Production methods often incorporate recycled or allocated phosphogypsum to extract and deliver vital nutrients, while also functioning as a major application sector for calcite and other processed materials. Within technical contexts, fertilizers are frequently cited as example substances in the description of these chemical processes.

The utilization of fertilizers represents a minor category for phosphogypsum recycling, currently accounting for only a small percentage of the byproduct (specifically 3.2% value, assigned a grey color code in industrial legends). Geographically, the application of these phosphogypsum-derived fertilizers is concentrated in regions such as Guizhou Province, where they are deployed to improve soil fertility and support agricultural output. Despite their functional benefits in bridging industrial byproduct management and agricultural productivity, their composition requires careful oversight. Certain fertilizer formulations contain cadmium, a heavy metal that accumulates in soil over time and introduces notable environmental risks. Consequently, balancing crop enhancement with ecological safety remains a critical consideration in their production and application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484618</data>
