</node>
<node id="Agriculture">
  <data key="d0">Agriculture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agriculture serves as a fundamental component of the global food supply chain and a critical downstream sector for crop cultivation, encompassing crop-based systems that include soil, crops, and crop residues. It functions as a key sector for tracking fertiliser application rates and soil erosion, while also experiencing substantial phosphorus losses primarily driven by soil erosion, with the subsequent recycling of these losses typically managed within the food production sector. In Australia, agriculture stands as the largest contributor to the national GDP and occupies over half of the country's land area. Functioning as a primary destination for processed materials and industrial byproducts, the sector receives recycled biosolids, recycled effluent (specifically 0.9 units from the Recycled Effluent Box), and facilitates phosphorus reuse.

A notable application area within agriculture is the utilization of phosphogypsum, a material extensively tracked in scientific literature. Treated phosphogypsum is applied as a soil amendment, low-grade fertilizer, nutrient replacer, and as a feedstock for producing compounds like potassium sulfate and calcite, offering tangible benefits for soil improvement and industrial recycling. Perspectives on the scale of phosphogypsum valorization in agriculture vary; while some frameworks classify it as a primary field for phosphogypsum reuse, other data indicate it constitutes a minor usage sector accounting for approximately 1% of total applications. Despite this discrepancy, it is recognized as a rapidly developing application field, with commercialized implementations established in Russia and more limited adoption in the United States. Large-scale, high-value deployment remains constrained by practical challenges such as high costs and product instability. Furthermore, the agricultural use of phosphogypsum necessitates rigorous evaluation of potential radiological impacts, contamination risks, and occupational dosimetry concerns. Consequently, its deployment remains contingent upon comprehensive safety assessments, underscoring the sector's ongoing effort to balance industrial resource recovery with environmental protection and agricultural safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Agriculture is a primary application area for the resourceful utilization of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Agriculture represents an application scenario where MPG improves soil properties under strict heavy metal concentration controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Agriculture is a potential application sector for phosphogypsum groups 3 and 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Construction Materials">
  <data key="d0">Construction Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Construction Materials represent a broad category of building supplies and fundamental matrices, encompassing products such as cement pastes, geopolymers, mortars, blocks, plasterboards, and roadbed or paving materials. This sector frequently incorporates calcite and related compounds, serving as a primary application pathway for the final Calcite product. Within the broader context of industrial byproduct utilization, Construction Materials constitute the largest and most major application sector for recycled and processed phosphogypsum (PG). PG is valorized and reused extensively within this field, particularly across multiple Chinese provinces, where it is integrated into building matrices to enhance mechanical properties. The application of recycled PG in construction is often discussed alongside other utilization fields such as agriculture and engineering.

From an industrial and economic perspective, Construction Materials are conventional products manufactured by integrated phosphogypsum companies. Despite their significance, the widespread promotion and adoption of PG-based construction materials face notable constraints, primarily driven by high transportation costs and existing technical and economic limitations. Environmental and safety assessments are also integral to this sector, as these materials are rigorously evaluated for their potential to emit Radon-222 into the surrounding environment.

In academic and data visualization contexts, Construction Materials serve as a primary research focus area for scholars such as Dr. Marc Azab. Additionally, in specific classification systems or legends, these building supplies are distinctly identified by a light blue color code. Overall, the sector functions as a critical intersection of material science, sustainable resource management, and environmental monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad category of building products and structural elements incorporating phosphogypsum and other industrial byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction Materials is a sector where phosphogypsum is recycled and applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction Materials represent the application category for recycled phosphogypsum, including plaster and concrete.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction materials represent a primary resource utilization pathway for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Building products and composites that incorporate phosphogypsum and other industrial wastes.</data>
