<node id="CaS">
  <data key="d0">CaS</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CaS (calcium sulfide) is a multifunctional chemical compound utilized across material science, industrial chemistry, and biomedical engineering. In composite materials, it exhibits distinct morphological traits, forming needle-like, interlocked crystals, and contributes to a binding energy peak at 161.49 eV. Within biomedical applications, CaS serves as a primary component in composite bone cements, where it is synthesized alongside hydroxyapatite (HAP) to establish the base matrix, specifically identified as the calcium sulfide phase in x = 0 sample compositions.

Chemically, CaS actively participates in oxidation and solid-solid reactions. Its formation is notably constrained by the presence of iron (Fe) and nickel (Ni), and it is generated as a reduction product during specific procedural stages, namely Steps 3 and 5. The compound is extensively studied in the context of phosphogypsum (PG) decomposition and processing. During the intense competition phase of PG decomposition, CaS forms alongside calcium oxide (CaO). In a two-step decomposition approach, CaS is oxidized with carbon dioxide (CO2) to facilitate PG breakdown.

Experimental investigations frequently utilize CaS to analyze the melting characteristics of phosphogypsum, with findings indicating that these characteristics are significantly influenced by the addition of kaolinite. Furthermore, CaS plays a central role in environmental sustainability initiatives, particularly in the renewable processing and treatment of phosphogypsum. Its applications in this domain were highlighted in a 2020 study focusing on sustainable and renewable methods for managing phosphogypsum waste, underscoring its importance in both advanced material formulations and specialized chemical reaction analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;CaS is an intermediate chemical compound whose production decreases with larger coal sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006</data>
