<node id="Thermal Decomposition">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Decomposition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal Decomposition is a chemical reaction and industrial process in which a compound breaks down into simpler substances when subjected to controlled heating. This phenomenon is typically identified and analyzed through thermogravimetric and differential scanning calorimetry measurements, where it is characterized by a distinct correlation between mass loss and a downward trend in heat absorption data.

In industrial and materials processing contexts, Thermal Decomposition is extensively applied to phosphogypsum. Controlled heating facilitates the breakdown of aluminum-containing phases and converts the material into compounds such as anhydrite. This high-temperature treatment releases sulfur trioxide, promotes mineral release, and enables the recovery of valuable elements. The process is also frequently employed in conjunction with K-feldspar to study reaction mechanisms and optimize resource extraction.

Beyond inorganic waste treatment, Thermal Decomposition functions as a synthesis method in material science, notably for producing hydroxyapatite. In this application, bovine bones undergo boiling, drying, and calcination at 800 °C to effectively remove organic matter. Additionally, the reaction type generally encompasses the thermal breakdown of various compounds into simpler chemical species, such as calcium hydroxide and aluminum hydroxide, underscoring its broad utility across chemical and industrial research.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal Decomposition is a recycling method for phosphogypsum that recycles sulfur and produces cement.&lt;SEP&gt;The chemical breakdown of phosphogypsum induced by heat, illustrated by the shifting peaks in the DTG plot.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792362494</data>
