</node>
<node id="Orthosilicic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Orthosilicic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Orthosilicic acid is the chemically correct form for the silicon-oxygen-hydrogen species released during the hydrolysis reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Orthosilicic Acid is a specific chemical form of silicic acid, potentially represented by the notation H2SiO4 in the equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cementitious Materials">
  <data key="d0">Cementitious Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cementitious materials are binding construction composites and geotechnical building materials primarily synthesized using phosphogypsum (PG) as a core component or admixture, frequently coupled with industrial solid waste. These materials function as essential elements in construction applications, where the incorporation of phosphogypsum enables the transformation of industrial byproducts into viable building composites. Their development and utilization are deeply embedded within industrial and research frameworks, providing a broader context for studying phosphogypsum and its associated chemical reactions.

In practical and experimental settings, cementitious materials are extensively utilized to evaluate critical performance metrics, particularly durability and mechanical properties. Despite their functional role in construction and waste valorization, they are also characterized economically as low-value-added products generated through PCR technology. Collectively, these materials represent a specialized intersection of construction engineering, industrial waste management, and materials science, highlighting ongoing efforts to optimize phosphogypsum-based composites while acknowledging their current market classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious Materials are construction products enhanced by PG additives to achieve important mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious materials are binding substances used in construction, frequently modified with additives to achieve specific engineering properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious materials are incorporated to compensate for impurities in PG and control environmental pollution, increasing CPGFM costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious materials are composite construction materials that incorporate phosphogypsum, often modified with industrial additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious materials are binding agents that can be optimized with activators when filled with industrial slags.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementitious Materials are amorphous colloidal substances formed during hydration that enhance mechanical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301341</data>
