<node id="Bauxite Residue">
  <data key="d0">Bauxite Residue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bauxite Residue is an industrial waste material characterized by its pronounced alkaline and saline-alkaline properties, which directly influence its aggregate stability. These inherent chemical traits define its environmental behavior and necessitate specific management strategies to mitigate its impact.

The material's alkaline characteristics can be effectively stabilized and neutralized through the application of phosphogypsum. Additionally, the combined use of phosphogypsum and poultry manure further modifies and influences the residue's alkaline profile. Together, these amendments address the material's chemical composition, offering a viable approach for its stabilization and potential utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019</data>
