<node id="Copper">
  <data key="d0">Copper</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Copper is a chemical element that functions as both an essential trace nutrient and a regulated heavy metal pollutant, with significant relevance across geological, environmental, and materials science domains. Geologically, it is depleted in phosphorites relative to crustal abundance and associates with organic matter. In industrial contexts, copper is transferred from phosphate rock to the byproduct phosphogypsum, where it is recognized as a highly mobile trace metal and often the most abundant heavy metal, typically measured at concentrations around 117 ppm, though specific analyses report ranges from 21 to 28 μg/g. During processing, it exhibits a transfer rate of 64 to 100 percent. Its presence in phosphogypsum is routinely quantified using techniques such as LA-ICP-MS and ICP-MS, with concentrations measured across various sampled locations and data tables in parts per million.

Environmentally, copper exhibits high dissolution rates in distilled water and sequential leaching, characterized by weak bonding or adsorption to gypsum surfaces that cause its leaching rate to increase over time. In phosphogypsum solutions, its concentration tends to decrease alongside cadmium as pH rises, with experimental tracking measuring levels in micrograms per liter over time and TCLP tests quantifying it in milligrams per liter. As a regulated heavy metal contaminant, copper is strictly monitored in surface and irrigation waters, with a maximum allowable concentration of 1 mg L⁻¹. It is also tracked against leaching toxicity thresholds in phosphogypsum-amended soils, where it can cause slight contamination, and atmospheric emissions contribute to terrestrial ecotoxicity potential. Life cycle inventories record copper as a liquid and groundwater emission during phosphogypsum disposal, quantified at 7.94 × 10⁻⁴ kilograms, with an estimated 1158 tons released into estuaries. Mitigation strategies include adsorption and ion-exchange technologies, such as nano-NaX zeolite and phosphogypsum-based adsorbents, while strategic phosphogypsum reuse aids in remediation.

In materials science, copper serves as a versatile functional dopant and catalyst. When combined with phosphogypsum, it synthesizes compound oxygen carriers that lower reaction temperatures. Doping hydroxyapatite matrices with copper enhances photocatalytic properties for formaldehyde oxidation and selective nitric oxide reduction with ammonia, while also altering degradation kinetics, such as slowing the breakdown of 17α-methyltestosterone. It is additionally impregnated into synthetic nanohydroxyapatite for agricultural applications. Beyond its industrial and environmental roles, copper is also identified as a trace element in AZ31B magnesium alloys. Analytically, it may occasionally appear as an elemental component during Scanning Electron Microscopy sample preparation, underscoring its broad relevance across scientific monitoring and industrial applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
