  <data key="d0">Algae</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Algae are photosynthetic organisms used to test the toxicity of elutriates from phosphogypsum-amended soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Algae are photosynthetic organisms used to test the toxicity of elutriates from phosphogypsum-amended soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Algae are microorganisms that may grow in the phosphogypsum settling ponds due to nutrient runoff.&lt;SEP&gt;Algae are aquatic plants whose growth is stimulated by appropriate phosphorus hydride levels but inhibited by excess.&lt;SEP&gt;Algae are photosynthetic organisms used to test the toxicity of elutriates from phosphogypsum-amended soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Algae are aquatic plants that grow rapidly due to eutrophication, contributing to oxygen depletion in water.</data>
