<node id="Thermal Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal Treatment is a high-temperature processing technique primarily utilized for material synthesis and the modification of various mineral and industrial materials. It is extensively applied to phosphogypsum to fundamentally alter its physical, chemical, and structural properties, rendering it suitable for industrial reuse, particularly in the production of Portland slag cement, cement, and concrete. The process operates by heating the material under specific temperature and holding time conditions, which induces dehydration, eliminates free water and water of crystallization, and removes impurities, volatile components, and phosphorus pentoxide (P2O5). These thermal actions trigger phase transitions and decomposition, effectively inertizing harmful impurities and converting the material into anhydrite. Consequently, the treatment enhances the material's crystallinity, homogeneity, and morphological stability, often evidenced by distinct shifts in analytical peaks.

Beyond phosphogypsum, Thermal Treatment demonstrates significant versatility across specialized mineral processing and material synthesis workflows. It is widely adopted for phosphate ores and calcined washed beneficiated solids, where it actively promotes the crystallization of calcium fluoride and optimizes material composition. In rare earth extraction flowsheets, the technique is strategically implemented following washing stages to substantially increase the concentration of rare earth elements within the final concentrate. For HAP samples, a standardized protocol of heating at 400 °C for 30 minutes is commonly applied to modify properties, evaluate morphological stability, and improve structural homogeneity. Despite its broad industrial utility and effectiveness in concentrating valuable elements and optimizing compositions, the implementation of Thermal Treatment is frequently constrained by significant operational bottlenecks, most notably high energy consumption and the release of volatile components during processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001</data>
