  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclave method is a pressurized steam processing technique used to prepare calcium sulfate hemihydrate whiskers from phosphogypsum.</data>
