<node id="Gypsum Blocks">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Blocks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Blocks are construction and building materials primarily derived from phosphogypsum and its derivatives. These materials can also be produced directly from standard gypsum. The manufacturing process involves utilizing processed phosphogypsum (PG) and, in specific cases, recovering β-building gypsum powder through PBG technology. This production methodology highlights the material's reliance on industrial by-products and specialized processing techniques to achieve its final form.

In terms of commercial production, Gypsum Blocks are manufactured by specific entities, notably Company Q and Company R, both of which utilize processed PG in their operations. Functionally, these blocks share the exact same application domain as burn-free bricks, making them a direct alternative in various construction projects. By repurposing phosphogypsum and employing targeted manufacturing methods, Gypsum Blocks serve as a specialized, application-verified building material.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum blocks are physical products manufactured in Scenario 2 using PG, contributing to local renewable input shares.&lt;SEP&gt;A final construction product formed by molding, drying, and processing gypsum powder with additives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018</data>
