<node id="Acid Leaching">
  <data key="d0">Acid Leaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acid Leaching is a hydrometallurgical and chemical separation technique utilized to extract valuable elements, particularly rare earth elements, rare earth metals, and lanthanides, from solid materials. The process functions as a chemical decomposition and extraction method that employs acidic solutions, specifically mineral acids such as hydrochloric acid (HCl), nitric acid (HNO3), and sulfuric acid (H2SO4). By introducing these acids to the target material, the technique dissolves the underlying matrix, a mechanism that is frequently represented and analyzed through chemical reaction equations. This chemical breakdown releases soluble valuable components into an aqueous solution for subsequent recovery.

The primary application of Acid Leaching involves recovering critical metals from industrial waste and solid byproducts, with extensive research and operational focus directed toward phosphogypsum and phosphohemihydrate. In these specific contexts, the process targets the gypsum matrix to break it down and release soluble rare earth elements while simultaneously removing impurities. Beyond industrial residues, the technique is also widely applicable to raw mineral ores, serving as a versatile hydrometallurgical approach for converting solid-bound valuable elements into a liquid form for further processing.

Operationally, Acid Leaching typically involves sequential steps of mixing, stirring, and filtering the solid material with the chosen acid. Recent methodological developments have also explored integrating this chemical extraction technique with biological processes to enhance recovery efficiency. Overall, it stands as a conventional and highly adaptable extraction method for recovering valuable metals and lanthanides from diverse solid feedstocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid leaching is a chemical process used to purify rare earth solutions from phosphogypsum with high purity rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A process investigated for extracting rare earth elements from phosphogypsum using acids like HCl, HNO3, and H2SO4.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid leaching is a chemical extraction technique used to recover rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-034</data>
