<node id="Natural gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Natural gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural gypsum is a naturally occurring mineral and conventional resource extensively utilized in construction and industrial applications. Chemically, it shares a composition similar to the primary constituent of phosphogypsum, which frequently leads to direct chemical and performance comparisons between the two materials. As the established industry standard, natural gypsum serves as the benchmark that various processed forms of phosphogypsum aim to replace.

Research and industrial development focus on modifying, recycling, and purifying phosphogypsum to replicate the functional properties of natural gypsum. While purified phosphogypsum has been shown to yield performance metrics similar to those of natural gypsum in construction settings, unmodified phosphogypsum generally exhibits a lower curing effect. Consequently, natural gypsum remains the critical reference material against which the chemical characteristics and practical efficacy of phosphogypsum derivatives are evaluated.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural gypsum is a traditional cementitious material used in self-leveling mortar, now limited by environmental targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001</data>
