<node id="Liu, S.">
  <data key="d0">Liu, S.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Liu, S. is a researcher whose academic work centers on the modification and sustainable utilization of industrial gypsum byproducts, with a particular emphasis on cementitious applications and resource recovery. In 2020, Liu, S. served as a lead author and co-author on a study that investigated the calcination modification of phosphogypsum and evaluated its impact on the hydration properties of supersulfated cement. This research provided critical insights into how thermally treated phosphogypsum can be effectively integrated into advanced cement systems to enhance material performance.

In addition to work on phosphogypsum, Liu, S. has also contributed to research focused on the effective recovery of calcium and sulfur resources from flue gas desulfurization (FGD) gypsum. These combined efforts demonstrate a consistent research trajectory aimed at optimizing industrial mineral processing, improving cement hydration mechanisms, and developing environmentally responsible methods for repurposing gypsum waste streams in construction and resource recovery applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Liu, S. is a researcher who investigated the application of lime neutralised phosphogypsum in supersulfated cement production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-029</data>
