<node id="Steel Slag">
  <data key="d0">Steel Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Steel slag is an industrial byproduct and waste material generated during steel production, recognized for its versatile applications across construction engineering, environmental management, and resource recovery. Primarily utilized as a supplementary material, it serves as a key component in cement formulations, concrete mixtures, and cementitious composite materials, where it effectively enhances the mechanical properties of the resulting structures. In practice, steel slag is frequently blended with other industrial materials to optimize performance and functionality. These combinations include phosphogypsum, fly ash, granulated blast-furnace slag, limestone, and sodium hydroxide. For instance, research by Huang et al. and Huang and Lin has incorporated steel slag with pretreated phosphogypsum and limestone in concrete specimens, while other studies utilize it as a main component in composite cement or as a specific proportion, such as a 5% additive in sodium hydroxide-modified phosphogypsum blends. Additionally, it is combined with fly ash and phosphogypsum to produce solidified road base materials.

Beyond its structural utility, steel slag is actively deployed for environmental mitigation and remediation purposes, often working in tandem with other industrial byproducts to address ecological challenges. The material is also processed to recover rare earth elements and extract value-added products, underscoring its potential as a secondary resource within sustainable and circular industrial frameworks. Collectively, these multifaceted applications position steel slag as a highly adaptable industrial material that effectively bridges construction engineering, ecological sustainability, and advanced resource recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
