<node id="Supersulfated Cement">
  <data key="d0">Supersulfated Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Supersulfated cement is a specialized construction material and a distinct type of cement widely utilized in the building sector. Within the cement industry, it is specifically recognized as a primary application for phosphogypsum, highlighting its role in industrial byproduct utilization.

The performance and chemical behavior of supersulfated cement are fundamentally influenced by the incorporation of phosphogypsum. When calcination-modified phosphogypsum is used, it significantly alters and modifies the hydration properties of the cement. Additionally, the addition of phosphogypsum directly impacts the material's curing process by shortening its setting time. These combined effects define the functional characteristics of supersulfated cement in practical construction applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lime">
  <data key="d0">Lime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime (calcium oxide, CaO) is a versatile alkaline chemical reagent and mineralogical compound derived from nonrenewable sources, primarily produced via carbothermal reduction or generated as a byproduct alongside sulfuric acid during traditional phosphogypsum processing. Functioning as a critical alkaline activator, neutralizing agent, and chemical stabilizer, lime rapidly adjusts pH levels and neutralizes the initial acidity of phosphogypsum mixes. It reacts with soluble phosphorus and fluorine compounds to precipitate them into insoluble forms, effectively reducing hazardous content and mitigating environmental risks. Additionally, it serves as a targeted chemical additive to activate composite systems alongside fly ash and phosphogypsum.

In agricultural and soil management contexts, lime acts as a safe soil amendment that interacts with clay minerals to modify soil plasticity. It is specifically applied in tropical no-till systems to enhance upland rice fertility and grain yield. In civil engineering and industrial applications, lime is extensively blended with phosphogypsum, fly ash, yellow phosphorus slag, sand, and other materials to manufacture durable construction binders, concrete mixtures, road surfaces, low-cost housing, and bricks. It significantly enhances the unconfined compressive strength, durability, stability, plasticity, and finesse of these cementitious matrices. Within brick manufacturing, lime serves as a primary binding agent that is sometimes partially replaced by calcined phosphogypsum, as documented in Kumar’s study, to increase brick density and further improve compressive strength. When heated to approximately 830°C, lime decomposes into micropores that improve the thermal conductivity and porosity of construction composites. It also functions as a binding agent in adobe construction and as a raw material for gypsum blocks, cement retarders, and specific industrial formulations, such as comprising 4% of the CPGFM formulation at the Qingping Phosphate Mine.

From an economic and emergy analysis perspective, lime represents a material input that contributes to the nonrenewable portion of investment costs. In Scenario 1, it accounts for 6.04% of the system’s total emergy input and is utilized during the cement retarder manufacturing stage. Conversely, in Scenario 4, while lime enhances specific emergy proportions, it simultaneously worsens the overall resource structure and decreases production sustainability. Consequently, structural adjustments to lime utilization are recommended to optimize resource allocation and improve environmental sustainability within this scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is a material used alongside class C fly ash to stabilize phosphogypsum for marine applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A material used as an activator alongside phosphogypsum and waste lime in cement production.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical additive used alongside fly ash and phosphogypsum for developing low-cost housing materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011</data>
