<node id="Phosphorus Impurities">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus Impurities</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorus impurities are contaminants in phosphogypsum that affect the preparation of alpha-calcium sulfate hemihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus impurities are contaminants in phosphogypsum that affect the preparation of alpha-calcium sulfate hemihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus impurities are contaminants in phosphogypsum that affect the preparation of alpha-calcium sulfate hemihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants in PG that can cause severe eutrophication when entering surface waters.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus impurities are harmful contaminants in phosphogypsum that are difficult to remove at lower calcination temperatures.</data>
