<node id="Kunming University of Science and Technology">
  <data key="d0">Kunming University of Science and Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Kunming University of Science and Technology is a Chinese academic institution that serves as the primary affiliation for numerous researchers and lead authors across various scholarly publications. The university is closely associated with a broad spectrum of academic endeavors, including multiple cited doctoral dissertations and extensive research initiatives. Its consistent role as a central academic hub is clearly reflected in its widespread institutional backing of published scientific work.

In terms of specific research contributions, the institution is notably linked to a 2015 study examining phosphogypsum fluidization, as well as additional investigations focused on the hydrothermal treatment of phosphogypsum. These specialized studies highlight the university's active engagement in applied scientific research and its ongoing commitment to advancing technical knowledge in material processing and environmental engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Kunming University of Science and Technology is the academic institution affiliated with the authors.</data>
