<node id="Iron Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Iron Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron oxide is a chemical compound and mineral component that plays a multifaceted role in phosphate-related materials, industrial processing streams, and environmental applications. Naturally occurring as a minor constituent, it accounts for approximately one percent of phosphorite composition. During the beneficiation of phosphate ores, iron oxide co-occurs with other minerals, and its concentration notably increases in the resulting concentrates, particularly alongside rare earth elements. It is also a persistent oxide component found throughout the phosphate manufacturing lifecycle, serving as a minor impurity in phosphogypsum—a byproduct of phosphate production. This impurity is present in the initial phosphogypsum mixture and remains stable before and after treatment, significantly contributing to the material's complex chemical makeup.

Beyond its presence in raw ores and industrial byproducts, iron oxide exhibits notable chemical and functional properties. It acts as a conventional absorbent material utilized for pollutant removal and co-precipitates with thorium in sedimentary phosphate environments. In modified phosphogypsum applications, it functions to reduce and dissolve cadmium. Additionally, iron oxide can be recovered from iron-rich chloride waste through the use of calcium carbonate. Analytical techniques, such as X-ray fluorescence (XRF), have successfully identified it as a distinct chemical component in various contexts, including the PBSLM6 sample. Collectively, these characteristics underscore iron oxide's consistent presence and versatile chemical behavior across raw phosphate minerals, processed concentrates, industrial byproducts, and remediation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron oxide is an acid-soluble impurity in PG that dissolves in hydrochloric acid and is later precipitated as hydroxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003</data>
