</node>
<node id="Lignite">
  <data key="d0">Lignite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lignite is a low-rank, low-grade fossil fuel classified as a type of coal that serves as a carbon-containing feedstock and primary reactant in advanced energy conversion technologies. It is extensively utilized in the chemical looping gasification process, where it functions as a fuel source to produce syngas and facilitate the development of clean energy. The gasification process involving lignite is notably enhanced by the integration of phosphogypsum, specifically through the use of phosphogypsum-based and multimetal phosphogypsum-based oxygen carriers. In this coupled system, lignite acts as the starting material that reacts with phosphogypsum, where adjusting the lignite ratio directly influences the resulting product phases.

Beyond its industrial applications, lignite is actively studied for its specific fluidization characteristics and reaction behavior within chemical looping environments. Researchers examine how these properties affect overall process efficiency, making lignite a critical component in optimizing gasification techniques and sustainable fuel processing. Its role as a versatile reactant in phosphogypsum-coupled systems highlights its importance in modern chemical looping research aimed at improving energy yield and environmental sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Lignite is a coal type used as a feedstock in the chemical looping gasification process to produce syngas.&lt;SEP&gt;Lignite is utilized in chemical looping gasification with PG to produce syngas by leveraging carbon monoxide from PG decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Lignite is used as a reducing agent in fluidized bed processes to prepare calcium sulfide from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Lignite is a type of coal burned to produce Class C fly ash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000</data>
