<node id="Hydrogen">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen is a fundamental chemical element that appears across various industrial and chemical contexts, frequently depicted in molecular diagrams such as those of PTEs. In chemical reactions, the atom count of hydrogen is strictly balanced on both sides of the reaction equation. Beyond its basic chemical identity, hydrogen functions as a gaseous product and is widely recognized as a green and sustainable energy carrier, with ongoing research focused on developing safe and efficient storage technologies for its practical application.

In industrial settings, hydrogen is primarily generated as a key gaseous component of syngas through the gasification of lignite and its volatile components. This production process heavily relies on the reaction between carbon and water vapor, making the output of hydrogen strongly dependent on the concentration of water vapor present during the reaction.

Hydrogen can also be synthesized through specialized catalytic and chemical processes. It serves as the target product in the hydrolysis of hydrazine-borane, a reaction facilitated by rhodium nanoparticles. Additionally, hydrogen generation is achieved using cobalt catalysts supported on hydroxyapatite, highlighting its versatility in advanced chemical synthesis and catalytic systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a reducing gas used in experimental settings for phosphogypsum decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element represented by a white circle, present as an ion in CPB mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is an elemental component with 38 atoms balanced on both sides of the reaction equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791749368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen Sulfide">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Sulfide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen sulfide is a byproduct generated during the crystallization process, which can be used to reduce phosphogypsum or prepare thiourea.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a decomposition product of PG produced alongside calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;A hazardous gas released during CPGFM preparation that exceeds safety limits and can be inhibited by oxidizing agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen sulfide is a compound whose production is inhibited by silicon dioxide during chemical looping gasification, making the process desirable for clean production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbon">
  <data key="d0">Carbon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon (symbol C) is a fundamental chemical element with critical roles across biological, industrial, and materials science domains. Ecologically, it serves as an essential component actively cycled by soil microorganisms such as Actinobacteria. Industrially, carbon functions as a major constituent in processed materials like phosphogypsum, typically comprising mass fractions between 0.030% and 0.230%, and is recognized as a chemically reactive solid derived from the thermal decomposition of lignite. In metallurgical and chemical applications, it frequently acts as a reducing agent in high-temperature reactions, participating in carbothermal reduction, reducing iron oxides, and reacting slowly with calcium sulfate under reducing atmospheres during phosphogypsum decomposition. It also serves as a primary elemental component of synthesized calcium carbonate, constituting 14.54 wt% of its composition.

Analytically, carbon is routinely identified and quantified in various samples using techniques such as X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy and energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy. In EDS spectra, it appears in the low-energy region near 0.28 keV, often detected alongside oxygen. Its concentration varies significantly across different matrices, with recorded weight percentages including 11.41%, 11%, 7.03%, and 14.54%. In specific analyses, it may manifest as a smaller peak with low intensity around 200-300 counts at designated measurement points, or appear as granular clusters indicative of organic impurities. Detection is documented in hydroxyapatite, 20HPA-HAP, and MPG samples under specific temperature and time conditions, with its presence in these contexts generally attributed to multiple origins such as biochar substrates, atmospheric capture, surfactant residues, surface contamination, or inherent organic molecules.

Across scientific literature and data resources, carbon is noted to have more abundant analytical data compared to phosphorus. Collectively, these characteristics underscore carbon’s versatility as a naturally occurring element vital to ecological cycles and a detectable, functionally significant component in engineered or processed materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon acts as a reactant in the reduction environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon in the mixture oxidizes between 750 and 800 °C, causing small mass loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon is the elemental reducing agent that reacts with calcium sulfate during phosphogypsum decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
