<node id="Electrodialysis">
  <data key="d0">Electrodialysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrodialysis is a recycling process combined with bipolar membranes to improve the sustainability of phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrodialysis is a separation technique integrated with bipolar membranes to enhance the sustainability of phosphogypsum recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrodialysis is a recycling process combined with bipolar membranes to improve the sustainability of phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrodialysis is a separation technique integrated with bipolar membranes to enhance the sustainability of phosphogypsum recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrodialysis is a recycling process combined with bipolar membranes to improve the sustainability of phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrodialysis is a separation technique integrated with bipolar membranes to enhance the sustainability of phosphogypsum recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;A separation process integrated with bipolar membranes to enhance phosphogypsum recycling sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792096852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raman Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">Raman Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Raman Spectroscopy is an analytical and spectroscopic characterization technique primarily utilized to investigate molecular vibrations, vibrational properties, and functional groups within various materials. It is particularly effective at resolving the vibrational modes of specific chemical groups, such as the phosphate group, and is frequently employed to differentiate calcium phosphate compounds and analyze the molecular vibrations and phases present in synthesized powders.

In practical applications, Raman Spectroscopy is used to study the thermal reduction of phosphogypsum when combined with carbonaceous materials, as well as to identify hydroxyapatite phases, evaluate their functional groups, and assess crystallinity through the analysis of hydroxyl group peaks. A key advantage of the technique is its high sensitivity, enabling it to detect phase abundances below the thresholds of other methods and complement analytical techniques with higher detection limits. Furthermore, it serves as a valuable complementary tool to Fourier-transform infrared (FTIR) spectroscopy, providing a comprehensive understanding of material composition and structural properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Raman Spectroscopy is an alternative analytical technique mentioned as applicable to the spectral analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Raman spectroscopy is a spectroscopic analysis technique used to identify wavenumbers corresponding to molecular vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Raman Spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to study the spectra of carbonates.</data>
