<node id="Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature is a fundamental physicochemical quantity and environmental factor, quantitatively measured in Kelvin and degrees Celsius, and frequently represented by variables such as T1 and T2 in logarithmic ratio equations relating to energy parameters. As a critical experimental variable and controlled parameter, it dictates reaction conditions, influences reaction rates, and affects gas production concentrations. Its application spans scientific, industrial, and biological domains, serving as an indispensable metric for tracking thermal events, optimizing synthesis, and understanding complex physicochemical and biological dynamics.

In thermal analysis, Temperature functions as the horizontal axis variable on graphs, including DTG plots where it is measured in degrees Celsius across ranges such as 1050 to 1200°C, with broader scales typically spanning 0 to 1500°C and specific thermogravimetric or calorimetric plots covering 0 to 1000°C or 100 to 900°C. It marks critical thermal points associated with mass loss and decomposition events. As an independent variable, it represents reaction conditions tested across distinct thermal levels, with specific controlled values including 170, 600, 750, and 850°C, while heating rates and specific reaction temperatures generally range from 300 to 1500°C.

In materials science, chemical engineering, and mineralogy, Temperature acts as a primary driver of phase transformations, reaction kinetics, particle formation, and crystal morphology, directly dictating material properties, crystallinity, crystal growth, product structure, and phase purity. Typical experimental ranges span 373 to 1573 Kelvin, 40 to 400°C, and 100 to 200°C, with specific thermal markers like 66°C, 133°C, and 428°C denoting significant physicochemical changes. It strongly influences the morphology, size, crystalline phases, and composition of hydroxyapatite, with optimized formation often studied at 40°C. Temperature also drives phosphogypsum dehydration, governs gypsum crystal growth kinetics and morphology, impacts purification and calcination processes by modulating reaction rates, and correlates with phase composition changes during thermal treatment, though its effect on phosphogypsum solubility in chloride solutions remains minor compared to ionic strength. Additionally, it accelerates hydration reactions, increases flow resistance loss in slurries, is routinely maintained at 180°C for 24 hours in hydrothermal autoclave treatments to affect chemical leaching efficiency and morphological transitions, and governs the dehydration process and phase stability of brushite during thermal treatment. As a primary environmental factor, it also dictates whether crystals form as fibrous or blocky structures.

In hydrometallurgical and chemical processing operations, Temperature is a crucial controlling parameter that is carefully optimized. During leaching procedures, it is a key optimization factor, with investigations into the TBP-TOPO leaching process conducted at room temperature to evaluate process synergism. For solvent extraction, it is consistently maintained at 50°C to optimize controlling factors, whereas room temperature is identified as optimal for the stripping process to prevent efficiency loss. Temperature also serves as a controlled operating parameter in the MSS2 reactor, reaching up to 260°C, where it functions as a synthesis parameter that, when increased, leads to a reduced specific surface area. Furthermore, it is investigated as a physical parameter influencing the mobility and release rate of trace elements during phosphogypsum leaching. As an experimental variable, Temperature influences the adsorption process, affecting adsorption rate, equilibrium amount, and intraparticle diffusion. It is measured in Kelvin and positively influences the adsorption capacity of fluorine onto adsorbents, with higher values favoring the endothermic process.

Beyond industrial and chemical systems, Temperature functions as a vital biological and environmental regulator. In waste management and composting, it controls microbial reproduction and bacterial distribution, with characteristic temperature trajectories serving as reliable indicators of biological activity. As a physical factor, it also inversely affects the solubility of Radon-222 in water and influences crystal decomposition and setting time. Collectively, these roles highlight Temperature as an indispensable parameter for tracking thermal events, optimizing synthesis, and understanding complex physicochemical and biological dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-00