<node id="Calcium Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate is a broad class of insoluble chemical compounds and bioceramics characterized by high stability, low solubility, and refractory phosphorus properties. Its general stoichiometry is frequently approximated as Ca10(PO4)6Y2, encompassing various salts such as dicalcium phosphate dihydrate and tricalcium phosphate (Ca3(PO4)2). It represents an insoluble form of total phosphorus and consistently aligns with the detected elemental composition of analyzed samples. The compound typically precipitates under alkaline conditions when calcium ions react with soluble phosphorus or phosphate ions. It serves as a foundational chemical class to which hydroxyapatite belongs, and researchers frequently study its properties across varying calcium-to-phosphate ratios, including experiments specifically targeting a 1:1 Ca/P ratio.

Calcium phosphate can be synthesized through multiple pathways, including the reaction of calcium carbonate with orthophosphate, the interaction of quicklime with phosphoric acid (which simultaneously removes harmful impurities), or the combination of calcium ions with phosphorus in treated leachate. In specialized laboratory environments, it forms as a compound on the surface of surfactant assemblies upon the addition of calcium precursors. Acting as a monobasic reagent and primary precursor, it subsequently converts to hydroxyapatite during further processing. Structurally, it is identified as a distinct chemical phase, often labeled CP, corresponding to diffraction peaks around 25 and 34 degrees, and is detectable via calcium-oxygen bonds in X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy spectra.

In industrial and materials science contexts, calcium phosphate is frequently encountered as a precipitate originating from phosphogypsum impurities. It acts as an abundant raw material component that provides calcium for phosphogypsum building blocks and is hypothesized to precipitate directly onto phosphogypsum crystal surfaces. Within cementitious systems, it functions as an inactive component that coats cement particles, significantly retarding setting times due to its phosphorus impurity content. Beyond construction materials, it is utilized to form protective coatings and serves as an adhesive agent binding particles together in specialized oxygen carrier systems, with industrial processes actively targeting its stabilization and recovery.

From a biomedical perspective, calcium phosphate is recognized as a vital class of bioceramics due to its excellent biological compatibility and medical significance. It is extensively utilized in advanced drug and gene delivery applications. Ongoing research continues to investigate its spectroscopic and X-ray diffraction properties, underscoring its distinct chemical, structural, and functional versatility across both industrial material systems and biomedical technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate is an inactive material derived from phosphogypsum that coats cement particles during mixing, influencing setting time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-00