<node id="Adsorption">
  <data key="d0">Adsorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorption is a fundamental physicochemical surface phenomenon and separation process characterized by the adherence or binding of atoms, ions, molecules, or contaminants to the surfaces of solid materials. As a versatile mechanism, it facilitates the transfer, capture, immobilization, and stabilization of substances across solid, liquid, and gaseous phases, making it a cornerstone of environmental remediation and contaminant management. The process is widely recognized for its effectiveness, cost-efficiency, and eco-friendly nature, particularly in treating industrial wastewater and aqueous solutions contaminated with heavy metals and toxic ions.

In environmental engineering and waste management, Adsorption is extensively applied to remediate contaminated water, soil, and industrial byproducts. Specific materials leverage this mechanism for targeted pollutant removal. For instance, phosphogypsum and its modified variants are utilized to solidify, stabilize, and immobilize potentially toxic elements, heavy metals, lead, and cadmium from liquid solutions. Similarly, hydroxyapatite-based materials, including HPA-functionalized frameworks and hybrid nano-hydroxyapatite, serve as highly effective adsorbents for capturing a broad spectrum of contaminants such as heavy metals, various ions, chromium(III), fluoride, selenium, dyes, fulvic acid, and antibiotics. During processes like gypsum phase formation, elements may also attach to organic or inorganic compounds through surface adhesion. The phenomenon also encompasses gas molecules adhering to solid surfaces.

Beyond terrestrial and aquatic applications, Adsorption operates in atmospheric contexts, such as facilitating the movement of fluorine from smoke clouds into the atmosphere. The process is frequently investigated as the primary mechanism for trapping heavy metals from water, with scientific literature documenting its application for specific metals like nickel and cobalt. Overall, Adsorption functions as a critical physicochemical tool that enables the targeted removal and stabilization of diverse harmful impurities, underpinning numerous remediation strategies and material science investigations.&lt;SEP&gt;A retention mechanism where molecules attach to the surface of solids, occurring as physisorption or chemisorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption is the surface attachment process by which fluoride ions bind to nHAp, heavily influenced by dosage, pH, and temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption is the process studied to understand the effect of temperature on thermodynamic parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption is a key scientific process and research topic covered extensively across the referenced literature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-012</data>
