<node id="Sodium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium Hydroxide is a strong alkaline base and highly versatile chemical compound widely utilized across industrial, materials science, analytical, and resource recovery applications. In resource recovery and phosphogypsum processing, it serves as a critical reactant and alkaline medium for conversion, carbonation, and the preparation of derived compounds. It dissolves processing materials to facilitate the production of portlandite and sodium sulfate while enriching residues with rare earth elements, frequently acting as a preparatory step prior to citric acid leaching. It is specifically purchased for pH adjustment during phosphogypsum powder preparation and functions as an alkaline additive to control phosphorus migration. Additionally, it is employed to wash phosphogypsum to eliminate impurities. Research indicates that Sodium Hydroxide significantly impacts phosphogypsum-based cement properties, though its use increases energy demand during conversion.

In advanced materials and construction chemistry, Sodium Hydroxide functions as an essential alkaline activator in geopolymer production and cementitious composites, exerting the greatest impact on composite strength. It promotes early hydration reactions to accelerate material formation and enhance structural development, though prolonged exposure can initially accelerate hydration product formation before eventually leading to tension and shear failure. The compound weakens the inhibitory effects of phosphate and fluoride on binder hydration and is consumed as a primary input in PBG technology. As a chemical additive, it reduces setting time and enhances early compressive and flexural strength in phosphogypsum mixtures, although higher concentrations may decrease 28-day strength. It is commonly used at a 1% concentration to alter matrix characteristics.

In analytical chemistry and laboratory settings, Sodium Hydroxide establishes controlled reaction environments through its strong alkaline properties. It ensures the complete decomposition of hydrogen ions during nitrogen analysis, is incorporated into sodium tetraphenylboron solutions for accurate potassium quantification, and dissolves samples for total sulfur content analysis. It is also dissolved in water to prepare standard solutions at target concentrations, such as 0.1 mol/L and 0.15 mol/L. During synthesis and hydrothermal processing, it precisely adjusts the pH of solutions, typically within a range of 5 to 11, and is added to calcium mixtures to facilitate precipitation during precursor preparation and hydroxyapatite synthesis. Its high solubility under elevated conditions effectively dissolves impurities like quartz. Furthermore, it serves as an alkaline medium in desorption studies to test fluoride release from nano-hydroxyapatite, demonstrating high fluoride release due to hydroxyl anion replacement. Through these diverse roles, Sodium Hydroxide remains fundamental to quantitative analysis, construction materials, resource recovery, and industrial chemical processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-00