<node id="Silica">
  <data key="d0">Silica</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silica, commonly known as silicon dioxide, is a versatile chemical compound with significant applications across industrial, geological, and materials science domains. Its role and concentration vary considerably depending on the specific context and source material. In phosphogypsum-based systems, silica can act as a primary constituent, comprising over ninety percent of the material alongside calcium sulfate dihydrate, or as a minor impurity at approximately 1.37 weight percent, potentially introduced during manufacturing or through process water. Within these industrial applications, it serves as an additive to meet slag wool production requirements and is combined with phosphogypsum to form a eutectic system that promotes efficient decomposition. Silica also reacts with calcium sulfate or calcium oxide, contributing to side reactions and eutectic mixture formation, and specifically reacts with calcium oxide during thermal reduction processes to yield calcium silicate. Depending on the intended use, silica can be processed using sulfuric acid at varying pH levels to reduce impurities, largely removed through water-washing purification, or allowed to form aluminosilicate phases that reduce the thermal energy required for brick manufacturing at lower concentrations.

Beyond phosphogypsum applications, silica plays a crucial role in construction and geological materials. It is a key chemical component in fly ash, where it contributes to pozzolanic properties, and it abundantly occurs in volcanic ash, where hydration reactions substantially enhance the structural strength of resulting materials. Additionally, silica reacts with lime and fly ash to form strong cementitious bonds. In experimental and analytical settings, silica is frequently added to samples, often denoted as "+ SiO₂" in X-ray diffraction analyses, and is utilized as a spherical substrate for the deposition of hydroxyapatite. Whether identified as a major component, a removable impurity, a reactive additive, or a structural substrate, silica remains a fundamental material whose behavior and utility are highly dependent on its specific chemical environment and intended application.&lt;SEP&gt;Silica exists in phosphogypsum as amorphous SiO2, quartz, or SiO2-containing minerals.&lt;SEP&gt;Silica tends to form complexes with fluorides, modifying the distribution of ionic species in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;A material mixed with sulphuric acid to treat phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical constituent showing significant variation, ranging from 0.44% to 8.82%.&lt;SEP&gt;Silica is a component mixed with sulphuric acid in proposed phosphogypsum treatment methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
