<node id="Moisture Content">
  <data key="d0">Moisture Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is a data attribute of PG ranging from 8wt% to 30wt%, influenced by draining duration and local weather conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is a factor influencing the mechanical properties and formation of the ettringite phase in the mix.&lt;SEP&gt;The water content within MPG that decreases as treatment temperature and holding time are reduced.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is a physical property of phosphogypsum that fluctuates and influences its density.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000</data>
