<node id="Arsenic">
  <data key="d0">Arsenic</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Arsenic is a naturally occurring toxic chemical element that is frequently classified as a heavy metal in environmental and agricultural literature. It is notably enriched in phosphorites relative to crustal abundances and is commonly associated with organic matter. In industrial and environmental contexts, arsenic is a characteristic heavy metal impurity found in phosphogypsum (PG), modified phosphogypsum (MPG), and PBSLM6, where its concentration varies significantly across samples and applications. Analytical detection via methods such as Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass-Spectrometry (ICP-MS), the Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure (TCLP), and spectroscopic analysis (revealing multiple peaks between 10 and 15 keV) indicates that arsenic is typically localized in specific bright hotspots rather than being uniformly distributed. Reported concentrations range widely, from trace levels of 2.00 to 4.50 μg/g in PG (often below detection or rare effect concentration thresholds) and a concentration value of 0.3 in specific samples, to a weight percentage of 15.76% in others. Processing and environmental conditions heavily influence its behavior; for instance, concentrations decrease from 2.77 mg/kg in PG to 0.05–0.86 mg/kg in MPG, and thermal treatments at 185°C and 190°C pose safety concerns, with concentration levels slightly lower at 180°C/10 h compared to 195°C/10 h due to crystal property influences.

Chemically, arsenic exists as H2AsO4- in weakly acidic or alkaline conditions and reacts with calcium ions during hydration to form calcium dihydrogen arsenate, a compound soluble in acid that can increase arsenic content. Its environmental mobility is characterized by leaching rates that tend to increase over time, with recorded values as low as 0.2 µg/L. Due to its persistence and tendency to accumulate in soil without significantly decreasing at higher pH levels, arsenic poses substantial ecological and public health threats. Its bioavailability facilitates uptake by various crops, leading to bioaccumulation and entry into the human food chain through contaminated agricultural produce, and it has been reviewed for its role in disease initiation. Consequently, arsenic is rigorously assessed for ecological and human health risks across various environmental matrices, with its concentration closely monitored during hydration and leaching processes.

To mitigate these risks, integrated management strategies combine agricultural adaptation, material engineering, and strict regulatory oversight. Sprinkler irrigation has proven effective in reducing arsenic concentrations in rice grains, while mixing PG with other minerals or red mud enhances its adsorption capacity as a contaminant. Regulatory frameworks establish precise concentration limits to protect water resources and crop cultivation, including standards of 0.05 mg/L for general water quality and 5 mg/L under US-EPA guidelines for mixtures, alongside specific thresholds for dry crop irrigation. Through continuous monitoring, agricultural adaptation, and regulatory oversight, the management of arsenic seeks to balance the industrial utilization of byproducts like phosphogypsum with the safeguarding of ecological integrity and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a trace metal element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a toxic element classified by the United States EPA, found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a trace metal found in Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured across the sampled locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
