<node id="Portland Cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Portland cement is a widely utilized traditional binding material and primary construction agent that conforms to ASTM C150 standards and is commonly applied in soil-cement applications. Composed of approximately 62% calcium oxide, it functions as a standard baseline and reference material for comparative research involving treated phosphogypsum and other supplementary additives. A critical component of its formulation is gypsum, which is incorporated to prevent the flash setting of concrete. The material’s setting behavior, mechanical properties, and hydration process are extensively studied, particularly regarding its interactions with industrial byproducts such as phosphogypsum, fly ash, and ground granulated blast furnace slag.

When integrated with phosphogypsum, Portland cement exhibits variable performance depending on the additive's purity and dosage. Weathered or impure phosphogypsum typically acts as a set retarder that extends setting times and reduces compressive strength, while purified phosphogypsum at low replacement levels can enhance cement properties and is frequently used as a direct additive or raw material during manufacture. The initial hydration process is notably influenced by phosphorus from phosphogypsum, particularly in the presence of superplasticizers. Research also examines solid-state reactions involving calcium hydroxide and calcium carbonate transformations within cement-phosphogypsum mixtures, alongside comparative studies on chloride diffusion properties and setting times. Early experimental applications indicated that combining phosphogypsum with Portland cement can significantly increase overall material costs, though it is often modified or retarded by the additive in practical settings.

Production pathways for Portland cement have evolved to incorporate phosphogypsum through methods such as co-production with sulfuric acid and processes utilizing calcium carbonate or calcium oxide derived from phosphogypsum via PSC technology. Despite these sustainable innovations aimed at optimizing construction materials and promoting eco-efficient building applications through waste valorization, conventional production still relies on burning natural gas to dry gypsum, contributing to notable environmental impacts. Nevertheless, Portland cement remains central to both conventional construction and innovative sustainable engineering, with ongoing research focused on balancing performance, cost, and environmental efficiency through strategic additive integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland Cement is an industrial product that utilizes Phosphogypsum as a set controller during its manufacture.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a construction material manufactured using phosphogypsum as a set controller.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a binding material combined with stabilized phosphogypsum and fly ash for construction composites.&lt;SEP&gt;A construction material whose setting and mechanical properties are analyzed in relation to phosphogypsum additives.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of cement whose mechanical properties are influenced by the addition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a cement type requiring purified Phosphogypsum for use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001</data>
