<node id="Anhydrite">
  <data key="d0">Anhydrite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Anhydrite is a crystalline, orthorhombic mineral compound representing the anhydrous form of calcium sulfate. It primarily occurs as a major or trace component in phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct of phosphoric acid production derived from waste gypsum. The formation of anhydrite is heavily dependent on thermal processing conditions, typically emerging as a dominant phase at temperatures of 600°C and above, and frequently coexisting with bassanite, dihydrate gypsum, and calcium sulfide during calcination below 1000°C. Its development is further influenced by solution composition, phosphorus and fluorine impurities, and its analytical identification relies on distinct hydration state markers. Chemically defined as dehydrated calcium sulfate, it is sometimes broadly categorized under calcium sulfate or described as a hydrated phase in certain industrial contexts. During thermal processing, it often represents the final crystalline stage derived from anhydrite II.

In construction and materials engineering, anhydrite serves multiple functional roles. It is widely utilized in cement and plaster manufacturing, where it can act as an activator for granulated blast furnace slag. When incorporated into building materials such as bricks and autoclaved aerated concrete, increasing anhydrite proportions generally enhance structural effectiveness and compressive strength, particularly at concentrations up to 12%. Additionally, its hydration properties contribute to cementing value and gel formation when mixed with water. However, conflicting observations exist regarding its impact on cement hydration kinetics; while some applications demonstrate a reduction in setting time, other studies indicate that anhydrite present in phosphogypsum or mortar systems may retard cement reactions and prolong setting times. Overall, anhydrite remains a critical subject of study in industrial mineral processing, waste management, sustainable construction, and calcium sulfate phase transformations, underscoring its versatility as an alternative chemical form of phosphogypsum beyond standard wet-process methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
