<node id="Egypt">
  <data key="d0">Egypt</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Egypt is a North African country and geographic region that serves as a foundational location for extensive industrial and scientific investigations, particularly those centered on phosphate processing, waste management, and related byproducts. It functions as the geographic origin of key phosphate rock sources and hosts critical operational facilities, most notably the Abu-Zaabal phosphate plant, which is dedicated to phosphoric acid production. The region is also home to phosphate fertilizer plants that have been the subject of targeted environmental and industrial studies. Egypt produces phosphogypsum, contributing to worldwide production statistics with an annual output of 5.4 million metric tons, and serves as the primary origin for phosphogypsum feedstock.

A significant portion of research conducted in Egypt focuses on the comprehensive sampling, chemical characterization, and beneficiation of phosphogypsum. Samples are systematically evaluated for their chemical composition, impurities, and major element profiles, with data derived from these analyses prominently featured in scientific literature where Egypt is frequently represented with a specific weight percentage measurement of approximately 38%. Notably, analyses of Egyptian phosphogypsum samples have documented the lowest Sulfur Trioxide levels among studied datasets. Beyond chemical profiling, Egypt is a central location for radiological and environmental assessments. Scientific investigations have evaluated the natural radioactivity, radionuclide content, and fluoride contamination of phosphate rocks, phosphogypsum, and fertilizers, while also examining lanthanide recovery processes and radon emanation phenomena linked to the petroleum industry. The Red Sea Coast within Egypt serves as a key sample collection site for these multidisciplinary studies.

The country hosts key research institutions, such as the Housing &amp; Building National Research Center, which support these ongoing evaluations. Overall, Egypt functions as both the geographic source of essential phosphate resources and the operational base for examining the chemical, radiological, and material characteristics of phosphate and petroleum byproducts, thereby supporting advancements in waste management and resource processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019</data>
