<node id="Phosphogypsum Waste">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum Waste is an industrial solid byproduct generated during the wet processing of phosphate rock for the production of phosphoric acid and fertilizers. It is characterized by a distinct mineralogical and elemental composition, notably high concentrations of radionuclides, and the presence of rare earth elements as impurities. Due to its substantial volume and chemical makeup, the material frequently accumulates in large mounds, posing significant environmental risks while simultaneously presenting substantial recycling potential. Consequently, it is extensively analyzed as a raw industrial sample for its radiological profile, radioactive decay properties, and mineral composition across numerous scientific studies.

Researchers are actively investigating Phosphogypsum Waste as a secondary source for recovering valuable rare earth elements. Furthermore, the material is being utilized as a precursor and raw material for advanced industrial conversions, including the synthesis of nano-calcium fluoride and hydroxyapatite nano-materials. These applications highlight its growing relevance in sustainable resource recovery and advanced material science, cementing its status as a focal point for environmental management and industrial utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum waste is an industrial byproduct utilized as a raw material source for synthesizing hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum waste is an industrial byproduct that can be repurposed as a resource for rare earth element recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;A waste material containing mineral inclusions, serving as the subject of the chemical release analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum waste is an industrial by-product frequently analyzed in studies regarding waste-to-energy strategies and environmental assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-015</data>
