<node id="Garg">
  <data key="d0">Garg</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Garg is a researcher who has extensively investigated the processing and application of phosphogypsum (PG), with a primary focus on calcination techniques and composite mixture formulations. A significant portion of Garg’s work involves the calcination of PG for purification and the preparation of anhydrous calcium sulfate. By calcining PG at controlled temperatures for set durations, specifically within a range of 500 to 1000 °C, Garg determined that optimal mechanical properties are attained at 1000 °C. This research was conducted in collaboration with Singh, with whom Garg co-authored studies on PG calcination and its subsequent application in cement manufacturing, yielding consistent results.

In addition to calcination research, Garg has co-authored multiple studies examining mixtures that combine calcined phosphogypsum with slag. These investigations specifically address the prolongation of setting times and soundness expansion, including a dedicated 1995 study on mixture preparation. Furthermore, Garg’s research portfolio encompasses the evaluation of curing temperature effects on phosphogypsum-based mixtures and the impact of superplasticizers on the physical properties of calcined phosphogypsum plaster. Collectively, Garg’s contributions provide a comprehensive analysis of phosphogypsum treatment, mixture optimization, and industrial application in construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
