<node id="Gypsum Plaster">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Plaster</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum plaster is a construction and building material primarily manufactured through the recycling and calcination of phosphogypsum. The production process frequently utilizes purified phosphogypsum or phosphogypsum hemihydrate as its core raw material, a preparation method notably detailed in a 2017 study. The efficiency of this manufacturing process is highly dependent on the specific calcination temperature applied during processing.

When produced from purified phosphogypsum, the resulting material exhibits distinct physical characteristics, including reduced normal consistency and increased strength. Furthermore, the physical properties of gypsum plaster are not fixed; they vary and are systematically detailed across different design formulations, allowing for tailored performance and adaptability in various construction applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a building material that utilizes phosphogypsum as a component.&lt;SEP&gt;A construction material produced by recycling phosphogypsum through calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a product manufactured using phosphogypsum in the gypsum industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792487165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mineral CO2 Sequestration">
  <data key="d0">Mineral CO2 Sequestration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mineral CO2 Sequestration is an environmental process and carbon capture technique designed to mitigate atmospheric greenhouse gases by utilizing recycled phosphogypsum industrial waste. This method operates by applying phosphogypsum, a byproduct generated during phosphate fertilizer production, to chemically react with carbon dioxide. Through a process of mineral carbonation, the calcium and magnesium compounds within the waste material bind with the CO2 to form stable carbonate minerals, effectively capturing and permanently storing the gas in a solid state.

As a dual-purpose environmental application, Mineral CO2 Sequestration addresses two critical industrial challenges simultaneously. It provides a sustainable pathway for the safe disposal and repurposing of phosphogypsum, which is otherwise considered a hazardous waste, while offering a scalable mechanism for long-term carbon storage. By transforming an industrial byproduct into a functional carbon sink, this technique contributes to climate change mitigation strategies and promotes circular economy principles in waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral CO2 sequestration is a process utilizing phosphogypsum industrial waste to capture carbon dioxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
