<node id="Journal of Environmental Management">
  <data key="d0">Journal of Environmental Management</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Journal of Environmental Management is a scientific and academic publication venue dedicated to research on environmental impact, resource management, and sustainable practices. A primary focus of the journal is phosphogypsum, with numerous articles addressing its recycling, environmental effects, management strategies, and impacts on soil fertility. The publication also features studies on the combined utilization of phosphogypsum and phosphate tailings, positioning it as a key resource for waste management and environmental science research.

In addition to its focus on industrial byproducts, the journal has published research on wastewater treatment, including a notable 2011 review on heavy metal ion removal from wastewaters. It has also served as the academic publisher for specific studies, such as a 2017 investigation into the application of phosphogypsum and phosphate tailings, as well as research authored by H. Tayibi and colleagues. Through these diverse contributions, the Journal of Environmental Management continues to disseminate critical findings across environmental management, resource recovery, and pollution control.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Journal of Hazardous Materials">
  <data key="d0">Journal of Hazardous Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Journal of Hazardous Materials is a scientific and academic publication dedicated to advancing research on environmental hazards, waste management, radiological safety, and the ecological impacts of hazardous substances. It functions as a key interdisciplinary resource for studies addressing the transformation, transport, and remediation of hazardous materials in various ecosystems.

The journal’s scope encompasses a wide array of specific investigations, with a notable emphasis on phosphogypsum waste. Published research includes studies on converting phosphogypsum into nanoparticles for environmental applications, utilizing the waste to prepare hydroxyapatite for fluoride removal, and examining phosphogypsum foam alongside radionuclide transport. Radiological safety and risk assessment are also central themes, featuring work on radioactivity contents in dicalcium phosphate, associated health risks, and uranium sorption on octadecyltrimethyl ammonium bromide-modified bentonite.

Beyond waste and radiological studies, the publication covers broader environmental and industrial topics, including groundwater quality, industrial by-products, lanthanide leaching, and phytostabilisation efficiency in contaminated soils. It has also documented specialized agricultural and material science research, such as tomato trace element uptake (with specific coverage in 2014) and graphene oxide nanocomposites, including contributions from researchers like F. Fang. Through this diverse portfolio, the Journal of Hazardous Materials remains a vital platform for disseminating critical findings on hazardous material management and environmental protection.&lt;SEP&gt;An academic journal that published research by M. Rentería-Villalobos and colleagues.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal publishing studies on phosphogypsum as a soil fertilizer and its ecotoxicity.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal of Hazardous Materials is a scientific publication that published research on phosphogypsum purification and stabilization techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific journal that published research on toxic element mobility and environmental impacts of phosphogypsum wastes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792482628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Construction and Building Materials">
  <data key="d0">Construction and Building Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Construction and Building Materials is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on construction materials and engineering. A prominent focus of its publication scope is the utilization of phosphogypsum within the construction sector, particularly as a sustainable alternative to natural gypsum. The journal regularly features studies that examine the purification, durability, and mechanical properties of phosphogypsum-based composites, alongside broader investigations into load-bearing materials prepared from autoclaved phosphogypsum.

Beyond composite development, the journal has published extensive research on the practical integration of phosphogypsum into various building products and engineering applications. These include its use in bricks, road materials, binders, cement mortar, and non-sintering cement. The publication also addresses recycling methodologies, notably featuring a 2020 study that outlines optimal calcination parameters for phosphogypsum recycling. Through this concentrated body of work, Construction and Building Materials serves as a vital resource for advancing the engineering, sustainability, and structural implementation of phosphogypsum in modern construction practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019</data>
