<node id="Kaolin">
  <data key="d0">Kaolin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Kaolin is a natural clay mineral primarily composed of kaolinite that serves a variety of industrial and chemical applications. In environmental and materials engineering, it is utilized as a raw material combined with phosphogypsum to synthesize low-cost inorganic sorption materials for ion uptake. These composites, which function within the CaO-Al2O3-SiO2 system, have been evaluated alongside phosphogypsum and red mud to enhance arsenic adsorption efficiency. Additionally, kaolin acts as a fundamental precursor in the production of metakaolin.

In high-temperature manufacturing processes, kaolin functions as a critical additive designed to modify thermal properties. When introduced to specific material mixtures, it increases the melting temperature to effectively prevent unwanted sintering. This thermal stabilization is particularly valuable during cement clinker firing and throughout the reduction of phosphogypsum, ensuring process stability and material integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;A raw material processed alongside phosphogypsum to prepare low-cost inorganic sorption materials for ion uptake applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018</data>
