<node id="Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulphate dihydrate is a mineral compound that serves as the primary chemical constituent forming the structural basis of phosphogypsum. It is consistently identified as the main component within phosphogypsum precursor materials, establishing its central role in the composition and formation of this industrial byproduct.

Recognized as a natural mineral form of gypsum, calcium sulphate dihydrate is the subject of extensive scientific research regarding its chemical behavior. Studies have specifically focused on its spontaneous precipitation characteristics when exposed to various metal ions, as well as its mechanisms for impurity incorporation during crystallization. These investigations highlight its complex interactions in both natural and industrial aqueous environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate is the main chemical compound constituting phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate is the primary chemical component of Phosphogypsum, constituting over 90% of its composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792482756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
