<node id="Organic Matter">
  <data key="d0">Organic Matter</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Organic Matter is a complex chemical component and impurity commonly found across phosphate-related materials, including phosphorites, natural apatitic materials, and phosphogypsum. In raw phosphogypsum and phosphorites, it typically constitutes approximately two percent of the total composition. It exists as suspended or soluble material, comprising inherent substances and added additives such as flocculants, aliphatic compounds, carbonic acids, amines, and ketones. These organic components frequently adhere to gypsum crystals or attach to the phosphogypsum surface. Within industrial processing, Organic Matter is classified as an undesirable contaminant that co-occurs with phosphorus, fluorine, heavy metals, and radioactive elements. Its presence necessitates removal during pretreatment to enable industrial applications, prevent adverse effects on material reuse, and facilitate direct agricultural use. Standard purification strategies specifically target its buoyant nature, employing methods such as slurry flotation, washing, chemical treatment with citric acid, and thermal processes like calcination and fluidized calcination. Notably, lime neutralization proves largely ineffective for its removal.

Beyond industrial considerations, Organic Matter exhibits significant geochemical and environmental behaviors. It frequently associates with enriched trace elements through complexation or adsorption. In coarse phosphogypsum fractions, it acts as a contaminant that adsorbs thorium, interferes with radium accumulation, and retains polonium activity, which subsequently decays into lead-210. Environmentally, it can accumulate in soils surrounding phosphogypsum storage or disposal sites, where it negatively impacts local ecosystems by diminishing the soil’s capacity to retain and supply essential nutrients. Conversely, in a broader biological context, Organic Matter functions as a decomposable substance during microbial fermentation, serving as a vital nutrient source that supports microbial growth. Ultimately, the careful management and targeted elimination of Organic Matter from phosphogypsum are critical to mitigating its environmental and industrial drawbacks while unlocking the material's practical utility.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is a resource contributing 2.12% to the total emergy input in Scenario 3 and serving as a source for FN.&lt;SEP&gt;An additive used in the phosphogypsum processing section.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is a contaminant in PG that is eliminated through treatment processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is an impurity in PG that is reduced through wet sieving and hydrocyclone treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009</data>
