<node id="SEM-EDS">
  <data key="d0">SEM-EDS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM-EDS is an analytical characterization technique that integrates microscopic imaging with spectroscopic analysis to perform detailed mineralogical and chemical examinations of solid materials. By combining high-resolution structural visualization with elemental composition data, this method provides comprehensive insights into the physical and chemical properties of various substances.

The technique is extensively applied across diverse industrial and geological contexts. It is frequently utilized to study phosphogypsum, where it facilitates thorough mineralogical and chemical analysis. SEM-EDS is also employed for the mineralogical characterization of coal waste, specifically to detect and analyze rare earth elements within the material. Additionally, the method serves as a general analytical tool for characterizing solid products and is adapted to examine the microstructure of slag at elevated temperatures, such as 1250 °C. Through these varied applications, SEM-EDS remains a versatile instrument for advanced material characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS is an analytical technique used to determine the elemental weight percentages of phosphogypsum and washed phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS is an analytical technique used to image particle morphology and determine elemental composition.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS is an analytical technique used for characterizing the morphology and elemental composition of synthesized materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopic and elemental analysis technique used to examine the morphology and composition of MPG.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS is a combined imaging and elemental analysis technique used to examine the powder sample.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS is an analytical technique used to examine the composition and structure of MPG after hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792293275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XRD">
  <data key="d0">XRD</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray Diffraction (XRD) is a fundamental analytical and crystallographic characterization technique primarily utilized for phase identification, structural analysis, and crystalline assessment of solid materials and powders. By analyzing diffraction patterns, the method provides critical insights into the chemical and crystalline properties of various compounds, enabling the determination of phase composition, phase purity, crystallinity, material homogeneity, crystallographic parameters, and nano-sized structures. The technique examines peak widening and lattice microstructure, typically utilizing diffractometers to systematically evaluate solid products and synthesized specimens.

In materials science and specialized industrial contexts, XRD is extensively applied across a diverse range of compounds and systems. It is frequently employed to characterize synthesized hydroxyapatite materials and their composites, such as 20HPA-HAP, by identifying specific crystal planes, analyzing elementary cell parameters, confirming phase purity, validating standard crystal structures, and detecting structural transformations like amorphous transitions or related phases such as β-tricalcium phosphate. The technique also confirms the crystalline nature of hydroxyapatite samples and verifies the pure phase of compounds like ammonium sulfate. In mineralogical and waste management analysis, XRD identifies main crystalline phases, confirms sulphate content, and detects elements and compounds in both raw and treated phosphogypsum samples, often correlating specific diffraction peaks, such as those corresponding to sodium chloride, with precise weight percentage measurements. It is similarly used to verify mixed powder identification for composite cement preparation and to identify the ettringite phase in mixes, tracking its development during hydration.

Beyond these specific applications, XRD serves as a versatile tool for analyzing reduction slags, bone china, and complex solid-state systems such as nickel/phosphogypsum compound oxygen carriers and PGEF materials. It is instrumental in characterizing carbonation products by identifying crystalline phases such as calcite and vaterite, while also confirming their crystal structure and purity. Additionally, the technique examines adsorbents by tracking structural and crystalline changes before and after metal adsorption processes to verify how metal loading impacts the material's framework. Across all these contexts, XRD remains a critical method for assessing crystallinity, confirming phase composition, and characterizing the crystalline structure of synthesized and natural materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A phase composition determination method using X-ray diffraction with continuous scanning.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is a diffraction technique used to analyze the crystal structure and phase purity of nHAp.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is an analytical technique used to examine decomposition products.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction is an analytical technique used to detect crystal phases and monitor mineral transformations during heat treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray powder diffraction is used to determine the crystallinity and primary crystallite size of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is a characterization technique used alongside FTIR to detect Carbonated Apatite and analyze material properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
