<node id="Calcium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium oxide (CaO), commonly known as quicklime, is a solid alkaline chemical compound with a molar mass of 56.08 g/mol. It functions as a highly reactive alkaline substance that readily combines with silicon dioxide and phosphorus pentoxide to form calcium phosphate reactants, while also driving calcium carbonate synthesis. In construction and materials science, it is routinely characterized alongside calcium carbonate and calcium hydroxide for lime improvement purposes.

Calcium oxide is a major constituent across various industrial materials and byproducts. It is particularly abundant in phosphogypsum, serving as a primary or secondary component typically comprising 25% to 43 wt% depending on geographic origin, analytical methodology, and specific analyzed regions. It is also a key component in slag wool (28–47 wt%), Portland and slag cement, fly ash, portlandite, cement clinker, and PBSLM6. During raw material processing, it can transfer to potassium sulphate as an impurity, and its concentration in industrial byproducts generally decreases following calcination pre-treatment. The compound is routinely identified as a crystalline phase in XRD patterns, labeled CaO, and detected at specific Bragg angles, particularly resulting from the release of carbonated hydroxyapatite during sintering. Quantification is commonly performed via XRF analysis, EDTA titration, and specific volume measurements.

Primary production involves the high-temperature decomposition of phosphogypsum and calcium sulfate at approximately 1250°C, often acting as an intermediate or final product. It is also formed through calcium sulfate reduction reactions, alongside alternative methods including calcium hydroxide calcination, calcium sulfate reaction with coke, low-temperature decomposition and reduction techniques, calcium sulfide oxidation at roughly 1000°C, and simultaneous calcium sulfide and calcium sulfate reactions. During synthesis, it frequently combines with silica, silicon dioxide, and undecomposed calcium sulfate. The resulting high-purity material can be refined using two-stage low-temperature purification technology and is well-documented in phosphogypsum system phase diagrams.

Industrially, calcium oxide serves diverse functional applications. It acts as a primary calcium source in synthetic hydroxyapatite production, contributing to the calcium-to-phosphorus molar ratio, and provides catalytically active basic sites that facilitate biodiesel synthesis. In phosphate processing, it reduces phosphorus and fluorine content in phosphogypsum, neutralizes precipitation mother liquid, and is incorporated into CPGFM slurry to inhibit hazardous gas generation by elevating alkalinity. Through these varied production routes and chemical functionalities, calcium oxide effectively transforms waste materials into valuable chemical and construction resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Oxide is a major oxide in phosphogypsum that remains stable during the calcination process.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical component that increases significantly after calcination, stabilizing around 40-41%.&lt;SEP&gt;A major component whose relative percentage increases as water and volatiles are lost during calcination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010</data>
