<node id="Phosphorus Pentoxide">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus Pentoxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorus Pentoxide (P2O5) is a chemical oxide compound that functions as a significant impurity or trace constituent within phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct of phosphate processing. Its presence is intrinsically linked to production processes, where it is typically entrained and often found at concentrations exceeding those of fluorine. Analytical frameworks classify it variously as a trace marker indicating industrial origin or as a major impurity contributing to environmental pollution. Within phosphogypsum, particularly in hemihydrate forms, it acts as a soluble impurity that combines with calcium ions, thereby hindering hydration, diminishing the retarder effect, and significantly influencing setting time and practical applications. The compound's concentration varies across samples and regions, generally remaining in low to minor amounts with documented values including 1.56 wt%, 1.45 wt%, 0.80%, and 0.69 ± 0.01, though higher concentrations are observed in Hubei phosphogypsum, which elevates total phosphorus levels in leachate. While it represents the phosphorus content in phosphogypsum, this content is relatively low and is often supplemented by additional phosphoric acid during synthesis.

Beyond phosphogypsum, Phosphorus Pentoxide is identified as a chemical component in other materials, such as PBSLM6, where it is detected via XRF analysis, and in nHAp, where it serves as a major component contributing to the calcium-to-phosphorus molar ratio. In material processing, it undergoes syn- or co-crystallization influenced by sulfuric acid levels, and its increased percentage is known to raise band intensity and shift absorption to higher wavelengths. In recrystallization processes, the recovery efficiency of P2O5 is a key target for enhancement.

To mitigate its environmental and industrial impacts, various treatment protocols are employed, including thermal processing such as calcination, chemical immobilization, and citric acid treatments. During purification, removal rates are actively monitored, and depending on the chemical processes, the compound can sometimes be recovered alongside rare earth elements during sulfuric acid processing. In analytical and laboratory contexts, Phosphorus Pentoxide is formally tracked as a key chemical parameter. It is routinely quantified using spectrophotometric parameters and formulas, targeted for quantitative analysis, and monitored through standardized datasets, statistical plots, and specific superscript notation to denote precise analytical values. Furthermore, spectroscopic analysis identifies it as a compound associated with P-O bonding in P 2p spectra. In broader environmental and industrial assessments, it is quantified as an air emission in Life Cycle Inventory data for brick production and is linked to a documented savings of 6.2 kilograms in inventory records. Overall, Phosphorus Pentoxide represents a critical chemical factor across multiple domains, necessitating careful monitoring, targeted removal, and precise analytical documentation to manage its effects on material properties and environmental compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide is a water-soluble impurity found in Phosphogypsum that contributes to setting time retardation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide is a primary chemical component of Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus pentoxide is a chemical impurity substituted in the phosphogypsum crystal lattice that requires thermal treatment for removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide is an impurity compound in phosphogypsum whose concentration decreases with higher calcination temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound starting at 0.90% that decreases in washed samples but remains higher in not-washed samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide is a chemical component that decreases in washed samples but remains higher in unwashed samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010</data>
