<node id="Iron(III) Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Iron(III) Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron(III) oxide is a chemical and mineral oxide compound with the formula Fe2O3 and a molar mass of 79.84 g/mol. It serves as a standard material for calibrating iron measurements and is routinely targeted as a primary analyte in laboratory quantitative procedures. Depending on the analytical protocol, its concentration is determined through spectrophotometric methods, EDTA titration calculations, and compositional table evaluations. The compound is a recognized chemical component in cement, fly ash, and phosphogypsum. In industrial and geological matrices, particularly phosphogypsum, it typically appears as a minor impurity or trace constituent, though it is classified as a main metal element compound in WBS and TWBS samples. Reported concentrations vary significantly across samples and measurement methods, ranging from 89.10 to 102.60 ppm, 0.07 wt%, 0.08% (the lowest recorded in Yunnan samples), 0.10%, and up to 1.74 wt%. During phosphogypsum purification processes, the compound demonstrates an 80.32% removal efficiency.

Beyond its analytical and geological roles, Iron(III) oxide holds significant functional utility in materials science and industrial manufacturing. It functions as a critical component within composite oxygen carriers, where it actively participates in oxygen release pathways with a defined release priority. In formulation systems, it is added in modest amounts to satisfy raw material specifications for products such as slag wool. In these applications, it influences pH and viscosity while having a negligible effect on the lowest eutectic point of the system. Chemically, Iron(III) oxide acts as a reactive species that undergoes reduction to form iron(II) oxide. When specifically reacted with carbon, it decomposes into iron(II) oxide and carbon dioxide. Collectively, these attributes highlight the compound's variable presence, analytical importance, and diverse technological applications across chemical, industrial, and materials science environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) Oxide is an impurity in phosphogypsum that leaves the length-to-width crystal ratio unchanged.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) Oxide is a primary chemical component of Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) Oxide is a chemical component that fluctuates between 0.40% and 0.83% across different calcination conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009</data>
