<node id="Magnesium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Magnesium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnesium oxide (MgO) is a chemical and mineral compound with a molar mass of 40.31 g/mol. It occurs naturally in gypsum, though typically in negligible amounts, and is frequently identified as a trace or minor impurity in phosphogypsum, where documented concentrations range from 180.49 to 235.40 parts per million or 0.02 to 0.20 weight percent. As an oxide component in the initial phosphogypsum mixture, it is integral to the system's phase diagram. During industrial processing and beneficiation, magnesium oxide concentrations typically increase and are often found alongside rare earth elements, yet the compound remains relatively stable before and after treatment, with its distribution routinely tracked in compositional and comparative analysis tables. Analytically, its weight percentage is commonly determined through standardized back titration using ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) and volume difference calculations, while its mass ratio is also factored into broader oxide and pH value calculations.

In materials engineering and industrial applications, magnesium oxide serves multiple functional roles. The precise ratio of magnesium oxide to monopotassium phosphate is a critical factor that directly enhances cement strength. It is also utilized as an additive in slag systems to adjust quaternary acidity coefficients and lower melting points through eutectic mixture formation. Specifically, magnesium oxide combines with calcium oxide to form eutectic phases such as spinel. Furthermore, it is incorporated into industrial solid wastes, including blast furnace slag and fly ash, to meet specific slag wool composition requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound (MgO) present in the chemical composition of Cement and FA.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium Oxide is a chemical component identified in PBSLM6 via XRF analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium oxide is an acid-soluble impurity in PG that dissolves in hydrochloric acid and is later precipitated as hydroxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium Oxide is a chemical component found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium oxide is a chemical specification metric for phosphogypsum, required to be less than 0.6 percent.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium Oxide is a chemical component that remains low but spikes to 0.51% in unwashed samples at 950°C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009</data>
