</node>
<node id="Potassium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium oxide (K2O) is a chemical compound systematically tracked as a standard analytical parameter to evaluate the compositional profiles and industrial viability of various materials. In geological and industrial byproducts, it is consistently identified as a minor constituent or trace impurity within both natural gypsum and phosphogypsum. Quantitative assessments place its concentration in phosphogypsum between approximately 0.01 and 0.08 weight percent, with specific measurements recording 0.01 ± 0.001 wt% in the upper sections of compositional tables. This trace presence remains chemically stable, exhibiting no significant variation before or after material treatment processes.

Beyond gypsum-related matrices, potassium oxide is a recognized component in cement and fly ash (FA). Its presence has been explicitly verified in the material designated as PBSLM6 through X-ray fluorescence (XRF) analysis. In specialized chemical manufacturing, the compound serves as a dominant constituent in both synthetic and commercial potassium sulfate. Furthermore, potassium oxide holds a defined role in chemical modeling, where its molar ratio is utilized as a key variable forming part of the denominator in the M_eta equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium oxide is a highly soluble impurity in PG that is removed by careful washing of the final nHAp product.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Oxide is a chemical component found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Oxide is a chemical component that remains very low at around 0.01% regardless of treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009</data>
