<node id="Rostov Region">
  <data key="d0">Rostov Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Rostov Region is a geographic area situated in the southwest of the Russian Federation. It has served as a primary location for several scientific investigations, particularly those focused on soil science and environmental monitoring. Notably, the region is the designated study area for research on Haplic Chernozem soils. Within this context, scientists have also conducted extensive monitoring of heavy metal accumulation and migration processes within the local soil systems.

Beyond its significance in pedological and environmental research, the Rostov Region has been utilized as a geographic area for analyzing historical and contemporary climate patterns. These combined studies underscore the region's value as a key site for understanding soil composition, tracking environmental contamination, and examining climatic evolution in southern Russia.&lt;SEP&gt;The geographic area in South-European facies where the field experiments and soil analysis took place.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rostov Region is a geographic area in southwest Russia where Haplic Chernozem is spread.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rostov Region is the geographic area whose Chernozems soil state and monitoring problems were analyzed in a 2019 study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-010</data>
