<node id="Australia">
  <data key="d0">Australia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Australia serves as the focal geographic region and national context for a comprehensive phosphorus flow analysis, food system study, and associated sustainability analysis. Operating at the national scale, the country encompasses the phosphorus cycles, sectoral flows, and data models central to the research. Agricultural and mineral statistics reports were conducted and published within this region, establishing it as the primary focus for evaluating resource dependencies and environmental impacts.

Economically and agriculturally, Australia is characterized by naturally phosphorus-deficient soils, which render its farming and food systems heavily reliant on imported phosphate fertilizers and phosphorus. Despite this critical dependency, the nation functions as a major exporter of phosphorus-intensive agricultural commodities and operates as a net food exporter. This export-oriented model means that most of Australia’s food and fiber production leaves the country, resulting in the overseas generation of associated organic waste. Concurrently, Australia is identified as a producer of phosphate rock, though it remains a net importer of processed phosphorus, a dynamic that reflects variations in domestic processing capabilities and industrial output.

In terms of industrial and environmental research, Australia has been a key location for investigating phosphogypsum utilization and the natural radioactivity of industrial byproducts. Phosphogypsum samples from the region have been analyzed for Th-228 activities, and the country appears in relevant datasets for radioactive isotope measurements. On mapping visualizations, Australia is typically shaded grey to indicate either a lack of data or negligible domestic phosphogypsum production. Given these dynamics, phosphorus scarcity and the development of sustainable management strategies have emerged as significant research and policy priorities within the country. Additionally, Australia has demonstrated active engagement in agricultural science by hosting the 17th ASA Conference on subsoil manuring.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia is a location where phosphogypsum samples were analyzed for radionuclide content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
