<node id="Biogeosystem Technique">
  <data key="d0">Biogeosystem Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Biogeosystem Technique is a methodological paradigm designed to address global water scarcity and optimize matter flow within the biosphere. Functioning as the foundational framework for chemical soil engineering, it introduces a transcendental approach to refining soil amelioration and remediation theories. The methodology specifically enables the environmentally safe application of phosphogypsum and serves as the core basis for intrasoil milling chemical soil-biological engineering technology. By integrating these principles, it provides a systematic approach to large-scale soil management and resource optimization.

Distinct from its role as an engineering methodology, Biogeosystem Technique is also the title of an academic journal. This publication disseminates scientific research focused on the aggregation of natural disperse formations and organic matter. The journal operates as a scholarly platform for advancing theoretical and practical knowledge related to biogeosystemic concepts and soil engineering applications, thereby supporting the broader scientific community studying these environmental and agricultural processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000</data>
