<node id="USA">
  <data key="d0">USA</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States of America (USA) is a sovereign nation that serves as a significant geographic hub for critical mineral resources and advanced technological enterprises. Geologically, the country hosts major phosphate rock deposits, particularly in North Carolina and Florida, and encompasses the Black Hills Region study site. As a primary producer of phosphogypsum—a byproduct of phosphate processing—the USA contributes substantially to worldwide production statistics, with the material's extraction and storage governed by specific national conditions. The nation is frequently referenced in scientific research concerning phosphate rock activity concentrations and phosphogypsum trace elements, having served as the geographical location for sample analyses that revealed distinct chemical ranges for key components.

In the commercial and technological sectors, the USA is the recognized country of origin and operational base for several prominent scientific and technological firms. This includes analytical instrument manufacturers ThermoFisher and Agilent, measurement technology manufacturer Quantachrome, and software company StatSoft. Collectively, these attributes establish the USA's dual prominence as a central location for both phosphate-related material production and the development of advanced analytical instrumentation and software.&lt;SEP&gt;The country where the 1981 treatise was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haplic Chernozem">
  <data key="d0">Haplic Chernozem</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Haplic Chernozem is a world-famous South-European facies soil type primarily situated in the northern Rostov Region of South Russia. This soil is characterized by distinct physical and chemical properties, although it has notably experienced significant degradation over time. Its unique composition and regional prevalence have made it a subject of considerable scientific interest and environmental management efforts.

In contemporary research, Haplic Chernozem is frequently employed as the primary substrate for model experiments focused on phosphogypsum application and remediation. These studies utilize the soil to evaluate environmental interventions, specifically analyzing shifts in macro-ion content and investigating the various chemical forms of cadmium within the treated substrate. Consequently, Haplic Chernozem serves as a critical reference point for understanding soil remediation techniques and heavy metal behavior in degraded agricultural environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil type of South-European facies in the Rostov Region where the research was conducted.&lt;SEP&gt;Haplic Chernozem is a world-famous soil type that serves as a reservoir for phosphogypsum utilization but shows signs of degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Haplic Chernozem is a soil type studied in the experiment, characterized by specific physical and chemical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil type subjected to chemical reclamation and phosphogypsum application in the model experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-011</data>
