<node id="Eq. (4)">
  <data key="d0">Eq. (4)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation that was excluded from the model due to the negligible impact of cadmium on ionic strength.&lt;SEP&gt;An equation used to substitute the total concentration value of Cd^2+ in the water extract.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical equation that was excluded from the model due to the negligible impact of cadmium on ionic strength.&lt;SEP&gt;An equation used to substitute the total concentration value of Cd^2+ in the water extract.&lt;SEP&gt;Eq. (4) is the formula describing the experimental dependence of total detection efficiency on photon energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791312524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 3">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 3 serves as a generic figure label employed across numerous distinct scientific studies and analytical contexts rather than representing a single unified dataset. In soil chemistry and environmental assessments, it visualizes macro-ion and hydroxyl ion (OH⁻) activity in soil solutions following phosphogypsum treatment via the ION-3 model, tracks cumulative phosphogypsum volume over time, monitors its generation and utilization rates in China over the past decade, and quantifies proportional environmental impacts of various industrial processes and material flows for comparative ecological footprint analyses. Within chemical engineering and structural applications, the figure illustrates the effects of agitation time on phosphogypsum leaching using TBP-TOPO in kerosene, details how acidity, time, phase ratio, and temperature impact rare earth element stripping efficiency, and depicts the failure mode of PGEF. Microbiological and ecological research utilizes it to map microbial diversity, community composition, and species overlap across composting samples.

In material science and nanoparticle characterization, Fig. 3 presents comprehensive physical and structural data, including X-ray diffraction (XRD) patterns, density, porosity, linear shrinkage, water absorption, and thermogravimetric measurements for phosphogypsum in both pellet and powder forms. It displays Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy (FT-IR) spectra of samples before and after calcination at 1000 °C, compares hydroxyapatite synthesized via hydrothermal and microwave methods, and provides a schematic of phosphate fertilizer production routes. Advanced microscopy and phase analysis are frequently featured, including scanning electron microscopy (SEM) images revealing the tabular crystalline morphology of raw phosphogypsum grains at 500x and 450x magnification, XRD patterns detailing the phase composition of PPG and prepared hydroxyapatite samples, and energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (EDS) mapping for 20HPA-HAP composites as well as elemental abundance and distribution in phosphogypsum samples. Additionally, it includes UDM plots for synthesized hydroxyapatite nanoparticles and transmission electron microscopy (TEM) alongside high-resolution TEM (HR-TEM) data detailing the internal structure, lattice fringes, diffraction patterns, and microstructural evolution of porous HA microspheres.

Beyond materials and environmental studies, Fig. 3 is also used to display XRD patterns comparing commercial and synthetic potassium sulfate, and to present unconfined compressive strength test results for soils stabilized with cement, fly ash, and phosphogypsum. In process and utility analysis, the label illustrates the technological process of Scenario 3, depicts the aggregated utility values of four criteria along with their distribution characteristics, and shows the utility performance of phosphogypsum recycling technologies across four dimensions, including their respective utility values and distributions. Collectively, these varied applications underscore the label’s broad utility across chemistry, materials science, environmental analysis, microbiology, geotechnical engineering, and industrial process evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 illustrates phosphate budget inputs and outputs for individual sectors, measured in kt/a of P.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 is a visual illustration showing the gray, lumpy wet appearance of the PG sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 displays the TEM morphology of the as-prepared nHAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 contains TEM images that visually document the short rod-like crystal structure of nHAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 is a diagram illustrating the distribution of magmatic and sedimentary phosphogypsum in a sum of REE versus Sr plot.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 3 is a graphical representation showing the effect of PG replacement on mortar tensile strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-01