<node id="Vadose Zone">
  <data key="d0">Vadose Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The unsaturated soil layer above the groundwater table that acts as a sink for carbonates.&lt;SEP&gt;The subsurface zone between the soil surface and groundwater, from which cadmium migration is reduced.&lt;SEP&gt;The unsaturated soil layer above the groundwater table that acts as a sink for carbonates.&lt;SEP&gt;The subsurface zone between the soil surface and groundwater, from which cadmium migration is reduced.&lt;SEP&gt;The unsaturated soil layer below the surface that acts as a sink for carbonates and salts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-006</data>
