<node id="Fig. 7">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 7 is not a single, unified scientific entity but rather a generic figure label employed across numerous distinct publications, meaning its content and purpose vary significantly depending on the specific study. In environmental and soil chemistry research, it illustrates the percentage of active cadmium in soil solution relative to total cadmium content. Within phosphogypsum processing literature, it appears in multiple contexts: depicting dynamic cerium and calcium concentration variations during hydrochloric acid leaching, outlining the Boren-Haber reaction cycle for catalytic decomposition, showing carbonate solution conversion procedures, presenting powder diffractograms of raw versus thermally treated samples, classifying the setting time and hardening rates of hydraulic binders, and tracking compressive strength variations in phosphogypsum cement mortar across different curing ages in air and water. In materials science and engineering, it frequently plots mechanical properties like compressive and bending strength against sodium chloride content, examines competing cations and adsorption-desorption uptake percentages, details the production and construction technology of PGEF, and classifies mix areas based on torque measurements at ninety curing days. In synthetic chemistry and pharmaceutical research, it serves as a flowchart for the proposed synthesis route of nHA production and illustrates the Halder-Wagner method analysis for synthesized HAp nanoparticles.

For analytical characterization, Fig. 7 presents XPS survey and high-resolution spectra for elemental analysis, FTIR spectra comparing pure HAp, pure drugs, and drug-loaded HAp samples, FTIR spectra evaluating Brij-93 surfactant against materials synthesized at varying concentrations, and wavelengths of spectral lines alongside concentration decreases of major elements. Additionally, it functions as a composite figure for photoelectrochemical performance measurements, including LSV, transient responses, and impedance analysis, as well as illustrating photocurrent density stability, photoluminescence spectra, and Mott-Schottky plots. Given these divergent applications, Fig. 7 must be interpreted contextually as a standard figure identifier across independent studies covering soil analysis, chemical leaching, mechanical testing, adsorption behavior, material synthesis, and spectroscopic characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 is a visual diagram illustrating the emergy flow components of Scenario 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 depicts the preparation workflow for the phosphogypsum-based self-leveling mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 illustrates the preparation process of PBSLM.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 is a figure showing particle size distribution for hydrothermal treatment with simultaneous shaking and varying milling media.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 is a figure showing the size distributions of HA samples for comparison across different milling conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 shows the effect of purified PG replacement on the compressive strength of mortars cured in dry conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
