<node id="Soil">
  <data key="d0">Soil</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil is a fundamental natural, terrestrial, and geological substrate that functions as a dynamic physical and biological matrix and a critical environmental compartment. Serving as the primary foundation for agricultural and ecological systems, it facilitates chemical mixing, root growth, microbial activity, nutrient cycling, and plant development. As a geological material, Soil contains uranium concentrations and radionuclide activity levels that vary by parent material, acts as the largest source of background environmental radon with a baseline emanation fraction of 20%, and features Radium-226 concentrations that dictate its suitability for agricultural and residential use. It also serves as a natural medium for cation and anion leaching, uranium series radionuclide behavior, plant uptake, and leaching into groundwater systems. Due to its complex physicochemical properties, Soil is extensively utilized as a natural reference medium for comparative trace element analysis, chemical concentration baselines, and scientific evaluations of heavy metal accumulation, serving as the basis for ecological risk and pollution standard assessments.

Soil is highly vulnerable to environmental contamination and readily accumulates fluorides and potentially toxic elements from atmospheric deposition and industrial activities. It frequently receives phosphogypsum via stack deposition or stockpile seepage, where phosphogypsum pollutants accumulate and undergo leaching migration, releasing toxic gases and polluted water that disrupt soil functioning. This accumulation often triggers soil acidification, altered chemical balance, reduced organic matter, and compromised structural integrity, prompting batch incubation studies to monitor shifts in element speciation and pH. Conversely, phosphogypsum is also intentionally applied to Soil to improve its physico-chemical properties, treat acidity, and support plant growth, highlighting a dual role that depends on management practices. In agricultural contexts, phosphorus mobility within Soil occurs primarily through erosion and leaching processes.

Given its critical role, Soil is a primary focus for pollution research and agricultural management. Passivation and remediation technologies are deployed to immobilize accumulated contaminants, while agricultural amendments such as biofertilizers and straw are applied to actively enhance porosity, density, structural stability, fertility, and nutrient availability. Fertilizers, including phosphorus-based applications, are routinely introduced to increase nutrient supply and boost crop yield. Additionally, Soil functions as the base material for preparing adobe samples and stabilizer mixtures, where it is frequently evaluated and stabilized with various additives like cement and phosphogypsum in engineering studies. Ultimately, Soil operates as a complex environmental medium where ecological health, agricultural productivity, and pollution control intersect.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is the medium in which lead forms and phosphogypsum are analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is the natural substrate where lead concentration and soil solution dynamics are analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is the material interacted with and milled by the subsoil rotary device.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-005</data>
