<node id="Chemical Soil Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Soil Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique that improves soil geophysical structure and architecture simultaneously with phosphogypsum application.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that improves soil geophysical structure and architecture simultaneously with phosphogypsum application.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical soil engineering is a high-level technological process aimed at simultaneously decreasing soil contamination and achieving amelioration goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical soil engineering is a high-level approach aimed at providing stable, environmentally safe fertile soil evolution.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology applied to improve soil reclamation, remediation, and fertility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-008</data>
