<node id="Florida">
  <data key="d0">Florida</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Florida is a U.S. state and geographic region that functions as a major global hub for phosphate rock mining and wet-process phosphoric acid production. As the primary domestic source of phosphogypsum, a processing byproduct, the state generates over 30 million tons annually, which is predominantly stored in large industrial stacks and ponds. The naturally occurring phosphorites in the region contain radioactive elements, resulting in phosphogypsum with high activity concentrations averaging 1000 Bq kg⁻¹. Comprehensive scientific analyses have characterized the material’s chemical composition, revealing monoclinic crystals, varying Radon-222 flux rates, and measurable activities of uranium-238 and radium-226. Additionally, polonium-210 has been found in abundant quantities in groundwater aquifers beneath mined lands. While Florida’s phosphogypsum exhibits lower rare earth element concentrations than Brazilian sources and lower overall isotope levels compared to South African deposits, it remains a focal point for research into rare earth recovery and gypsum upgrading, highlighted by a notable 2017 study utilizing chelating polymers and acidic extracts.

Due to its massive industrial scale and inherent radioactivity, phosphogypsum disposal in Florida presents significant environmental and industrial challenges, with the material’s radiological profile limiting its broader commercial applications. Consequently, the state has emerged as a critical center for environmental radiochemistry, nuclide migration studies, and radioecological assessments. Researchers have extensively evaluated radionuclide migration from phosphogypsum stacks into surface aquifers, alongside comprehensive monitoring of radon emissions and airborne particulate matter near storage sites. Multiple studies have collected and analyzed phosphogypsum samples, with Florida identified as one of four key geographic locations for assessing elemental concentrations, leaching characteristics, storage hazards, and broader environmental impacts, with particular attention paid to central and northern stockpiles. Rigorous scientific evaluations also address potential soil amendments and develop comprehensive environmental management strategies to mitigate radiological and chemical risks.

The state’s dual role as a leading phosphate producer and a hub for environmental research is further underscored by the presence of the Florida Institute of Phosphate Research and the regular hosting of specialized scientific symposia. These institutions and events facilitate ongoing policy-driven and academic efforts to address the complex management of phosphogypsum, balancing global industrial demand with the imperative to monitor and mitigate the radiological and ecological impacts of phosphate processing byproducts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-00