<node id="Hydrochloric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Hydrochloric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrochloric acid is a strong, corrosive inorganic mineral acid with extensive applications across analytical, industrial, and research domains. In laboratory and analytical settings, it is commonly prepared as a 0.01 M solution for titrating carbonate and bicarbonate anions, adjusting the pH of standard solutions and buffer mixtures, and calibrating simulated body fluids to a precise pH of 7.40. It also serves as a specified chemical reagent in standardized gypsum analysis procedures. Industrially, hydrochloric acid functions as a critical reagent in purification processes, the wet-process production of phosphoric acid, and various leaching operations. It is frequently employed as a chemical wash to remove impurities from phosphogypsum and dissolves the material during initial preparation stages.

Modern research heavily utilizes hydrochloric acid for leaching and recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum and phosphate rocks. It effectively dissolves the gypsum matrix and often demonstrates superior performance compared to sulfuric acid. However, its extraction efficiency is constrained by calcium sulfate solubility limits, yielding moderate results in direct leaching that can be enhanced through two-step processes. The long-term viability of hydrochloric acid in this application presents conflicting findings: while it proves highly effective under single-pass or optimized conditions, other evaluations indicate it may be impractical for sustained cyclic leaching, making its success highly dependent on specific experimental parameters and operational modes.

Beyond rare earth extraction, hydrochloric acid supports diverse chemical and experimental applications. It dissolves eggshell powder to facilitate calcium hydroxide formation and is used in leaching experiments to study the dissolution behavior of gypsum and phosphogypsum. In solubility research, it is tested at concentrations up to 5 M or 6 M, either alone or combined with calcium chloride and potassium chloride across varying temperatures. It also acts as a chemical parameter in preparing alpha-hemihydrate gypsum whiskers and manages soluble phosphofluorine during the low-temperature calcination of phosphogypsum. In geotechnical and construction contexts, it functions as an acidic solution that triggers the dissolution of hydration products, thereby reducing the structural strength of filling bodies. Additionally, hydrochloric acid serves as an acidic medium in desorption studies to evaluate fluoride release from materials such as nHAp, typically demonstrating moderate release rates. It is also utilized alongside sulfuric acid as a corrosive agent to assess material durability and evaluate matrix resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrochloric acid is an acidic solution used in leaching experiments with calcined phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical treatment applied to PG that did not yield the best setting time reduction compared to other acids.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-00