<node id="USEPA">
  <data key="d0">USEPA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States Environmental Protection Agency (USEPA) is a federal regulatory body responsible for establishing environmental rules, safety standards, and regulatory frameworks within the United States, though it is occasionally recognized in research as an entity of international interest. A significant portion of its mandate involves managing Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material (TENORM), particularly phosphogypsum. The USEPA classifies phosphogypsum as TENORM and designates radium-226 (Ra-226) as a Group A human carcinogen. Consequently, the agency actively regulates radon emissions from phosphogypsum stacks, sets national emission standards, and established drinking water regulations for radionuclides, including specific Ra-226 limits. Due to these radioactive properties, the USEPA restricted the general use of phosphogypsum in 1992, permitting exceptions only for applications that remain below defined radium thresholds. The agency has also published reports on phosphate processes and commissioned a 1993 report addressing diffuse NORM wastes.

Beyond radioactive materials, the USEPA establishes comprehensive regulatory limits for heavy metals and trace elements. It sets standard specifications and leaching limits for heavy metals in construction materials, with regulatory thresholds that tested mixes generally meet. The agency is also widely referenced as an environmental safety assessment model for conducting human health risk assessments. In the realm of environmental science and modeling, the USEPA sponsored a workshop review focused on metals fate and transport modeling in streams and watersheds, with findings documented in a 2008 publication. Through these regulatory actions, research initiatives, and scientific publications, the USEPA maintains a continuous commitment to advancing environmental protection, public health safety, and regulatory science.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-004</data>
