<node id="Phosphate Rocks">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Rocks</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate Rocks are natural geological materials that occur as igneous or sedimentary mineral deposits. They serve as the primary raw material for conventional phosphorus fertilizer production and are essential for manufacturing phosphoric acid. In industrial processing, these rocks are digested with sulfuric acid to yield phosphoric acid, simultaneously generating phosphogypsum as a chemical byproduct.

The chemical composition and particle size of these deposits are routinely analyzed, as these characteristics directly determine the cadmium content present in the resulting phosphogypsum waste and are frequently compared against the waste material for industrial and environmental assessment. Because the rocks contain natural radioactivity, they are also evaluated for potential radiation hazards and overall radiological impact. Beyond their role in agriculture and chemical production, phosphate rocks are utilized as a geological source for uranium recovery. However, the sustained and growing global consumption of these resources has raised significant concerns regarding long-term availability and sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rocks are mineral resources that serve as a source for rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw materials that contain significant levels of strontium and rare elements, influencing phosphogypsum composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rocks are geological formations that supply contaminants like cadmium and lead to soil via fertilizers and waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate Rocks are natural mineral resources utilized in fertilizer production and evaluated as a source for uranium extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rocks are natural mineral deposits studied for uranium content and their application as agricultural fertilizers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-031</data>
