<node id="Ukraine">
  <data key="d0">Ukraine</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Ukraine is a country situated in Eastern Europe, occupying the left and central regions of the referenced map and containing major cities such as Kyiv and Poltava. It functions as the primary geographic focus for satellite mapping initiatives and associated study sites. Within these cartographic and logistical frameworks, Ukraine is identified as a potential source location for phosphogypsum, with a specific production facility clearly marked on the map.

As a major global producer, Ukraine contributes substantially to worldwide phosphogypsum statistics, generating approximately 10.0 million metric tons annually. This industrial output has prompted environmental research within the country to evaluate the impact of phosphogypsum disposal on local soil ecosystems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
