</node>
<node id="Milling Cutters">
  <data key="d0">Milling Cutters</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Components that provide a fine aggregate structure to initially compacted soil and feed soil into a container.&lt;SEP&gt;Components that provide a fine aggregate structure to initially compacted soil and feed soil into a container.&lt;SEP&gt;The milling cutters are rotating components that break down compacted soil into a fine-aggregate structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plant">
  <data key="d0">Plant</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Plants are biological organisms that absorb cadmium ions from the soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Organisms that benefit from improved soil health, higher resistivity to pathogens, and better environmental quality of biological production.&lt;SEP&gt;Plants are biological organisms that absorb cadmium ions from the soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Organisms that benefit from improved soil health, higher resistivity to pathogens, and better environmental quality of biological production.&lt;SEP&gt;Plants are the biological target for heavy metal penetration from the soil.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792343567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pathogens">
  <data key="d0">Pathogens</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Disease-causing agents against which plants develop higher resistivity due to improved soil conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease-causing agents against which plants develop higher resistivity due to improved soil conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Technology">
  <data key="d0">Standard Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard technology refers to conventional agricultural practices like plowing that fail to ensure multilevel soil structure and fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard technology refers to conventional agricultural practices like plowing that fail to ensure multilevel soil structure and fertility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amendments">
  <data key="d0">Amendments</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Amendments are soil treatments that can introduce heavy metals into the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Amendments are applied materials, such as pulp or granular matter, used to improve soil conditions and provide nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;Amendments are soil treatments that can introduce heavy metals into the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Amendments are applied materials, such as pulp or granular matter, used to improve soil conditions and provide nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;Amendments are materials applied to soil for physical improvement, which may also introduce contaminants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soil Porous System">
  <data key="d0">Soil Porous System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The soil porous system is a structural feature whose architecture is critical for soil stability, nutrient transfer, and plant growth.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil porous system is a structural feature whose architecture is critical for soil stability, nutrient transfer, and plant growth.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil porous system is a natural structure that is often dead-ended and is addressed by the new milling technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-008</data>
