  <data key="d2">A chemical compound used in fertilizers that was analyzed for radioactivity content and associated health risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound used in fertilizers that was analyzed for radioactivity content and associated health risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound referenced in the measurement of chloride ion concentration relative to DAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium phosphate is an end product obtained after the drying process in certain hydroxyapatite synthesis methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium phosphate is a fertilizer-grade raw material mixed with phosphogypsum powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium phosphate is a compound formed during phosphogypsum hydration that is insoluble in water but soluble in acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium Phosphate can enter the gypsum structure and form a solid solution through ion substitution.</data>
