<node id="Nickel">
  <data key="d0">Nickel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nickel is a chemical element classified as both a transition metal and a heavy metal, extensively studied across environmental, geological, and industrial domains. Geologically, it is characteristically depleted in phosphorites relative to average crustal abundances and frequently associates with organic matter. Ecologically, it is often investigated alongside cadmium and lead due to its phytotoxicity and extraction potential. In industrial applications, nickel is a notable trace element found in phosphogypsum and AZ31B, where its concentration is systematically documented in micrograms per gram (often less than 1) and parts per million across various material samples. It is routinely quantified using techniques such as LA-ICP-MS and appears in analytical tabular data with associated numerical values.

In phosphogypsum-amended soils, nickel acts as a contaminant contributing to moderate pollution and posing environmental and public health risks, though its mobility in seepage waters is typically constrained by natural buffering processes. Its levels are actively monitored for environmental safety during product processing and against established regulatory thresholds. While some contexts note that concentrations align with US-EPA limits, others indicate no specific US-EPA limit is established for these applications. Concentrations in phosphogypsum solutions are recorded in milligrams per liter during leaching toxicity assessments like the Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure, and levels in phosphogypsum generally remain below the rare effect concentration. During extraction, nickel often co-occurs with rare earth elements, necessitating separation via specific ionic liquid extraction methods.

In chemical engineering and materials science, nickel serves multiple advanced functions. It acts as a key component in compound oxygen carriers, particularly when combined with phosphogypsum or iron to effectively lower reaction temperatures. It also functions as a metal dopant within hydroxyapatite structures to modify photocatalytic properties, a modification that notably slows the degradation rate of 17α-methyltestosterone compared to undoped variants. Beyond material engineering, nickel is a primary target for environmental remediation via adsorption using hydroxyapatite-based composites, with research by M. Ferri and R. Foroutan detailing its rapid ion exchange and adsorption mechanisms. Collectively, these attributes highlight nickel’s multifaceted role in ecological monitoring, industrial byproduct management, and advanced material engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a trace metal element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a heavy metal found in phosphogypsum, primarily in fine particle fractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a heavy metal and trace element detected in phosphate ore and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a trace metal found in Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A metal transferred from phosphate rock to phosphogypsum and released into the estuary, estimated at 232 tons.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured across the sampled locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
