  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A large white area adjacent to the ponds, identified as a phosphogypsum stack or industrial storage silos.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum stack is an industrial waste storage area documented in a field photograph.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum Stack is a waste storage structure that serves as a primary source of environmental contamination for surrounding groundwater systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum Stack is an industrial structure from which airborne radioactivity emissions are monitored.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum stacks are industrial structures studied for the natural-convective transport of radon-222 into open air.</data>
