  <data key="d5">1792345598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Phosphogypsum Waste Utilization Technology">
  <data key="d0">Standard Phosphogypsum Waste Utilization Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard phosphogypsum waste utilization technology is a conventional method that increases soil contaminant levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard phosphogypsum waste utilization technology is a conventional method that increases soil contaminant levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contaminants">
  <data key="d0">Contaminants</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Contaminants are harmful substances in soil whose spread is reduced by intra-soil passivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants are harmful substances in soil whose spread is reduced by intra-soil passivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Substances originating from phosphogypsum that may leach into groundwater or contact soil materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants are pollutants present in gas, liquid, and solid phases that hydroxyapatite helps remove during remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants such as strontium ions favor the formation of isomorphous phases with radium sulfate, enhancing radium incorporation.&lt;SEP&gt;Substances, including heavy metals and radionuclides, present in phosphogypsum that pose health risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792298677</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soil Health">
  <data key="d0">Soil Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil health is a condition deteriorated by cadmium pollution and eolian/water transfer in the ecosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil health is a condition deteriorated by cadmium pollution and eolian/water transfer in the ecosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pesticides">
  <data key="d0">Pesticides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pesticides are agricultural inputs that serve as a source of heavy metals in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Pesticides are agricultural inputs that serve as a source of heavy metals in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Pesticides are an industrial source of nitrobenzene discharge into effluents.&lt;SEP&gt;Pesticides are substances applied to soil that can introduce potentially hazardous heavy metals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nutrients">
  <data key="d0">Nutrients</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nutrients are agricultural inputs that contribute heavy metals to the environment and biological production.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutrients are agricultural inputs that contribute heavy metals to the environment and biological production.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutrients available for plant uptake are enhanced by the release of phosphogypsum biofertilizer into the soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutrients are soil amendments that may contain heavy metals and contribute to soil contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soil Mechanical Processing">
  <data key="d0">Soil Mechanical Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil mechanical processing is a technique combined with amendment application for waste recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil mechanical processing is a technique combined with amendment application for waste recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil mechanical processing is a technique used to loosen soil structure and mix amendments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-013</data>
