<node id="Lime Milk">
  <data key="d0">Lime Milk</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime Milk is a chemical solution and washing agent specifically utilized in the treatment and processing of phosphogypsum. It functions primarily as a neutralizing agent for acid residues present in phosphogypsum sludge, carefully adjusting the mixture to a target pH range of 5.0 to 5.3. During the washing phase of the phosphogypsum treatment process, Lime Milk is mixed with the raw material to effectively neutralize and remove both water-soluble and water-insoluble impurities, thereby purifying the substrate for subsequent industrial use.

Beyond its purification capabilities, Lime Milk serves to chemically activate the treated phosphogypsum, rendering it suitable for construction material manufacturing. This activated phosphogypsum is predominantly employed in the production of non-sintering cement. The resulting cement demonstrates significantly improved performance characteristics, specifically exhibiting higher long-term strength when directly compared to conventional cement produced from natural gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Runoff">
  <data key="d0">Surface Runoff</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;A pathway through which high phosphorus concentration leachates are discharged into the Yangchang River.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological process that transports heavy metal complexes from land to surface water and the ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a concern related to phosphogypsum storage sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological pathway through which pollutants migrate rapidly in mountainous regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological process that transports pollutants from sludge ponds to surrounding environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground Water">
  <data key="d0">Ground Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground water is an underground water resource and aquifer system that functions as a vital environmental medium and compartment. It serves as a natural solvent, receiving leaching and seepage from surrounding geological materials and facilitating the transport of uranium-thorium series radioisotopes from solid matrices into the subsurface. In specific contexts, such as those documented by Pulhani, it acts as a leaching agent for radium-226 and uranium-238 within vertisol soils. As a fundamental natural resource, ground water provides essential potable water to human populations.

Despite its ecological and human importance, ground water is frequently vulnerable to contamination from both natural and anthropogenic sources. It has been extensively documented as polluted by runoff originating from phosphogypsum sludge ponds and open sludge ponds associated with chemical plants. Furthermore, aquifer systems containing ground water are actively studied for the presence of natural radioisotopes and barium contamination. Given its critical role in public health and environmental stability, ground water quality is rigorously monitored and evaluated against established regulatory benchmarks, including the GB/T 14848-2017 standard.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lead Ion">
  <data key="d0">Lead Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead ion (Pb²⁺) is a toxic heavy metal pollutant that poses significant environmental and chemical hazards. It is notably found at substantial concentrations in industrial byproducts such as phosphogypsum. In geochemical and environmental assessments, the free, uncomplexed concentration of the lead ion serves as a primary variable in solubility equations, while its thermodynamic stability constants are routinely applied to calculate its distribution within soil solutions. Chemically, the lead ion exhibits a strong affinity for calcium sites, enabling it to displace calcium ions within the calcium silicate hydrate (C-S-H) matrix through ion exchange processes.

Due to its toxicity and mobility in various matrices, targeted remediation strategies have been developed to capture and remove it effectively. Specifically, nano-structured pig bone hydroxyapatite and three-dimensionally ordered macroporous hydroxyapatite materials have been engineered as specialized adsorbents. These hydroxyapatite-based systems are explicitly designed to target the lead ion, leveraging its chemical properties to sequester it from contaminated environments and mitigate its hazardous impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
