<node id="Sulfur">
  <data key="d0">Sulfur</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfur is a fundamental chemical element (S) that maintains atomic balance across chemical reactions and serves critical roles across industrial, geological, agricultural, and environmental domains. It is routinely detected and quantified in samples using analytical techniques such as X-ray fluorescence (XRF), scanning electron microscopy with energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (SEM-EDS), and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), which record its weight percentages and chemical states. Spectroscopically, sulfur is classified as a volatile species identifiable by a distinct peak around 2.3 keV. In specific analyzed samples, it acts as a dominant element that contributes to gypsum-based compositions, often covering nearly the entire surface area and frequently exhibiting the highest mass fraction among major constituents.

Industrially, sulfur functions as a primary raw material input for sulfuric acid production systems. It is also a major component of phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct derived from sulfuric acid, where it combines with calcium and serves as a key target for economic valorization. During material processing, sulfur exhibits dynamic behavior: it is actively tracked in slag with mass fractions below 1.0 wt%, targeted for removal during desulfurization, and recovered with over 97.44 wt% efficiency. This recovered sulfur is efficiently recycled via carbothermal reduction smelting for sulfuric acid manufacturing. In the thermal processing of phosphogypsum, sulfur serves as a primary decomposition product and a focal point in thermodynamic studies, while it can also be effectively captured from syngas mixtures by oxygen carriers. Additionally, sulfur is a fundamental component of potassium sulfate, comprising 18.34 wt% of its composition.

Agriculturally, sulfur functions as an essential plant nutrient, supplied to soils through dedicated products like ammonium sulfate and low-grade fertilizer components such as phosphogypsum. Its mobility and reactivity are evidenced by concentration decreases of approximately 13% in leached samples compared to raw materials. In emergy analysis contexts, sulfur contributes varying percentages to total system inputs, specifically 4.57% to the overall system, 4.89% in Scenario 1, 4.74% in Scenario 2, and 1.59% in Scenario 3. Across these diverse applications, the precise presence, distribution, and concentration of sulfur remain vital for material characterization, resource utilization, and agricultural supplementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is a product formed in the reduction reactions of calcium sulfate and calcium sulfide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
