<node id="Stability Constant">
  <data key="d0">Stability Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stability constant is an equilibrium parameter used to quantify the formation of cadmium complexes with various anions.&lt;SEP&gt;A coefficient representing the formation strength of lead complexes, such as the monocarbonate lead complex.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermodynamic parameter representing the equilibrium of complex formation, such as the term $\frac{10^7}{5.73}$ for the monocarbonate lead complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-023</data>
