<node id="SiO2">
  <data key="d0">SiO2</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">SiO2, chemically known as silicon dioxide, is a fundamental chemical compound and the definitive chemical formula for quartz. It is a widely distributed substance found in various industrial and geological materials, including cement clinker and granulated slag. In compositional analyses, silicon dioxide is frequently identified as a variable chemical component and a major species within phosphogypsum (PG). It is also recognized as a significant impurity in this material, with its presence consistently documented in data tables that provide specific numerical concentration ranges.

Beyond its natural and industrial occurrences, SiO2 serves several specialized functional roles in chemical and materials processing. It is utilized as an inert carrier material designed to inhibit grain growth during the CLG process. Additionally, silicon dioxide functions as a traditional catalyst support in environmental chemistry applications, where it is routinely evaluated and compared against apatite carriers in studies focused on DeNOx activity. These diverse applications highlight its versatility as both a structural component and a functional material in various scientific and engineering contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;SiO2 is a chemical compound present in the slag system, influencing quaternary acidity and melting temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;SiO2 is an additive used in the reductive decomposition of waste gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A major element compound present in varying concentrations across all analyzed samples.&lt;SEP&gt;SiO2 is a chemical compound contributing to the total composition of Soma fly ash.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon dioxide is a major chemical component measured in percentage.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon dioxide, one of the primary oxides measured in the chemical composition of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
