<node id="Na2O">
  <data key="d0">Na2O</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Na2O, chemically known as sodium oxide, is a chemical compound that functions as a minor constituent in cement clinker and is also measured as a chemical component in phosphogypsum samples. In laboratory and analytical settings, it is routinely quantified alongside other oxides, particularly K2O, utilizing specific weighing and dissolution procedures to ensure accurate compositional analysis.

When recorded in analytical datasets, Na2O concentrations are typically expressed in weight percent and appear in concentration tables that document both average values, such as 29313.21 ppm, and associated numerical concentration ranges. In certain statistical charts or data presentations, the compound may also appear as a chemical label at the top, which can sometimes serve as a title or indicate a typographical error. Across these varied reporting contexts, Na2O remains a consistently tracked metric in chemical analysis and material characterization studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium oxide is a major chemical component measured in percentage.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium oxide, a chemical compound included in the compositional analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Na2O is a chemical compound whose concentration is recorded in the compositional analysis data.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound showing variable concentrations across the analyzed samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-004</data>
