<node id="Tricalcium Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Tricalcium Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A phosphate compound whose solubility was determined in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound with the formula Ca3(PO4)2.&lt;SEP&gt;Tricalcium Phosphate is a decomposition phase of hydroxyapatite that forms at temperatures above 800 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Tricalcium phosphate is an insoluble calcium phosphate complex formed during the acidic attack of PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Tricalcium phosphate is an insoluble solid product formed from calcium and phosphate ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Tricalcium Phosphate is a crystalline phase formed during the conversion of amorphous calcium phosphate in hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tricalcium phosphate is a chemical phase that was not detected by XRD analysis in the studied samples.</data>
