  <data key="d2">A fluoride compound whose solubility was determined in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium hexafluorosilicate (Na₂SiF₆) is a chemical compound identified by diffraction peaks in the XRD analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound identified by diffraction peaks labeled N at approximately 18°, 35°, and 55°.&lt;SEP&gt;An insoluble fluoride compound that promotes tabular-shaped crystal formation with reduced internal cohesion.&lt;SEP&gt;An inorganic compound that adheres to the surface of gypsum crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Hexafluorosilicate is a water-soluble fluoride impurity found in Phosphogypsum.</data>
