  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical constituent found in granulated blast furnace slag.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(II) oxide is an intermediate compound in the oxygen release pathway of iron within composite oxygen carriers.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound whose molar ratio is included in the calculation of M_eta.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(II) oxide is a product formed from the reduction of iron(III) oxide by carbon.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate compound formed from iron(III) oxide reduction, participating in subsequent slag formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(II) oxide is an oxide component present in the initial phosphogypsum mixture.</data>
