</node>
<node id="Purified Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Purified Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Purified phosphogypsum is a processed gypsum alternative tested in Portland slag cement and gypsum plaster formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Purified Phosphogypsum is phosphogypsum treated with aqueous citric acid and washed to remove impurities, resulting in improved physical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790961463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mineral Selenite Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Mineral Selenite Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mineral selenite gypsum is a mineral gypsum variant assessed for its properties in Portland slag cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral Selenite Gypsum is a natural gypsum material used as a standard or alternative to purified phosphogypsum in cement manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790961463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Portland Slag Cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland Slag Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Portland Slag Cement is a cementitious binder and construction material primarily produced through the intergrinding of granulated slag, cement clinker, and gypsum. As a fundamental building material, its baseline composition and manufacturing process establish its core structural and binding capabilities.

The physical, engineering, and overall performance characteristics of Portland Slag Cement are notably influenced by the incorporation of phosphogypsum, which can be processed and added in various forms. When purified phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material during manufacture, the resulting cement successfully complies with standard requirements for critical metrics such as autoclave expansion and heat of hydration. Additionally, the addition of phosphogypsum samples or thermally treated phosphogypsum has been documented to modify and influence the material's physical and engineering properties. These findings highlight phosphogypsum's versatility as an additive that can be integrated into Portland Slag Cement production while maintaining adherence to established performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binding material whose properties are influenced by thermally treated phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binding material used in the development of a new CCM formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binder material used in cementitious composites alongside phosphogypsum and fly ash.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a construction material whose properties are influenced by thermally treated phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland Slag Cement is a blended cement whose hydraulic properties and strength are improved by incorporating thermally treated phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cement whose properties are influenced by the addition of thermally treated phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792482756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Citric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Citric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqueous citric acid is a solution used to measure solubility and purify phosphogypsum by reacting with impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous Citric Acid is a chemical solution used to treat phosphogypsum for purification by removing impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous citric acid is the specific form of citric acid used to treat phosphogypsum samples, with optimal concentrations varying by sample type.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous citric acid is used to treat phosphogypsum, significantly reducing its retardation effect on cement setting time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
