<node id="Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d0">Compressive Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Compressive Strength is a fundamental mechanical property that quantifies a material's maximum load-bearing capacity under compression before failure, serving as a critical indicator of structural integrity and resistance to crushing. It is typically measured in megapascals (MPa) using universal testing machines on cylindrical or cubic specimens according to standardized methods. This property is extensively evaluated across engineering, construction, and biomedical fields to assess the performance of diverse materials, including cement, concrete, mortar, bricks, tiles, blocks, plaster, cemented paste backfill, and specialized systems like composite bone cements. Evaluation is routinely conducted at specific curing intervals—2 hours, 24 hours, 1, 3, 7, and 28 days—and is frequently analyzed alongside fluidity and flexural strength.

The property exhibits a linear relationship with material density and inversely correlates with water absorption and permeability. It is heavily influenced by material formulation, processing techniques, environmental conditioning, curing duration, temperature, and additive dosages. A prominent factor in cementitious and mortar systems is the incorporation of phosphogypsum (PG). While higher replacement levels of untreated PG generally reduce compressive strength, this relationship is non-linear and often peaks at low replacement thresholds (approximately 10% to 12% in concrete and mortar, and 7.5% for Plaster of Paris). The detrimental effects of PG can be effectively mitigated or reversed through purification, ball-milling, calcination, thermal pretreatment, autoclaving, citric acid treatment, and elevated curing temperatures. Additionally, chemical activators such as superplasticizers, sodium hydroxide, quicklime, cement, and silica fume consistently enhance strength, while moisture reduction also contributes to improvements.

In specific applications, compressive strength behaves according to distinct parameters. In brick manufacturing, it is directly governed by press-forming pressure and PG content, with any post-sulfate curing reductions effectively offset by PG. Adobe and stabilized lime mortar systems demonstrate increased strength with higher stabilizer or gypsum additions. In composite bone cements, strength rises with longer incubation periods but declines with elevated sodium chloride concentrations. Ultimately, achieving optimal compressive strength demands precise control over curing parameters, strategic material substitutions, and the engineering of dense, robust network structures supported by targeted mineral compositions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-003</data>
