<node id="Alkalis">
  <data key="d0">Alkalis</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkalis are chemical impurities and contaminants that constitute a notable component of phosphogypsum composition, typically represented by the chemical formula Na2O + K2O. These substances are inherently present in phosphogypsum but require careful management due to their potential to compromise material safety and industrial viability. During initial physical separation processes, such as hydrocyclone treatment, alkalis are observed to migrate and accumulate at lower levels within the underflow fraction.

To transform phosphogypsum into a usable industrial resource, alkalis must be strictly limited and effectively removed. This purification is essential for ensuring safe application and rendering the material suitable for manufacturing cement and plaster. Various treatment methods are employed to achieve this reduction, including standard purification processes, citric acid treatment, and fluidized calcination. Through these targeted interventions, alkalis are successfully extracted, thereby enhancing the quality and commercial applicability of the processed phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792483993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
