  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluoride Ion">
  <data key="d0">Fluoride Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluoride Ion is a negatively charged chemical species that reacts with calcium to form precipitates.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ion is a chemical component often found in phosphogypsum waste, requiring immobilization to prevent environmental contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride Ion is an anion capable of replacing hydroxyl ions in the apatite crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions react with cement particles to form protective coats that influence setting time.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ion (F⁻) is an ion that can replace hydroxyl ions in C-S-H.&lt;SEP&gt;The adsorbate species whose adsorption amount and equilibrium concentration were measured in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318011</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precipitation Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Precipitation Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Precipitation Reaction describes the chemical process where soluble ions combine to form an insoluble solid.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation reaction is a process step combining adjusted pH and ammonium hydrogen phosphate to form a translucent colloid.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation reaction is a chemical process where aqueous ions combine to form an insoluble solid.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation reaction is a classification for the chemical process where an acid reacts with a base to form a solid product.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791749368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrolysis Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Hydrolysis Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrolysis Reaction describes the chemical breakdown of polyphosphates through reaction with hydroxide ions.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrolysis reaction describes the chemical breakdown of triphosphate into phosphate and water using hydroxide ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791984470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphate Fertilizer Production">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Fertilizer Production</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate Fertilizer Production is a specialized industrial process dedicated to manufacturing agricultural fertilizers derived from phosphate rock. Central to this operation is the chemical treatment of phosphate minerals, typically through acidulation, which facilitates the extraction of phosphoric acid for fertilizer formulation. A defining characteristic of this manufacturing activity is the inherent and consistent generation of phosphogypsum, a gypsum-rich solid residue that serves as a major chemical byproduct and waste material throughout the production lifecycle. The management and disposal of phosphogypsum represent critical operational and environmental considerations, directly tied to the scale and methodology of the manufacturing process. Notably, Phosphate Fertilizer Production has been identified as a primary driver behind the significant increase in phosphogypsum generation observed in China.

In addition to its chemical outputs, the process consumes significant fossil energy. From a systems and environmental accounting perspective, Phosphate Fertilizer Production is frequently evaluated in conjunction with phosphogypsum disposal practices to conduct integrated system assessments. It also serves as the defined accounting boundary for tracking greenhouse gas emissions, encompassing the entire lifecycle from raw material extraction and processing through to the final disposal of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate fertilizer production is the industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate Fertilizer Production is an industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a chemical byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial sector that generates phosphogypsum as a primary byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate fertilizer production is the industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
