<node id="Portland cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A hydraulic cement produced by intergrinding cement clinker with impure phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a common type of cement whose properties are analyzed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is the primary cementitious material in traditional cement-based self-leveling mortar, though its high price limits large-scale application.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a binding material whose hydration process is affected by phosphogypsum and soluble additives.&lt;SEP&gt;A common type of cement whose setting and mechanical properties are affected by phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a type of cement mixed with purified phosphogypsum instead of natural gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
