<node id="Calcium phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate is a compound formed as a protective coating on cement grains due to phosphogypsum impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate forms inactive protective coats on cement particle surfaces, contributing to extended setting times.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791362752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium fluoride">
  <data key="d0">Calcium fluoride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium fluoride is a compound formed as a protective coating on cement grains due to phosphogypsum impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium fluoride takes the role of fluoride capture at neutral and alkaline conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium fluoride forms inactive protective coats on cement particle surfaces, contributing to extended setting times.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791362752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Setting time">
  <data key="d0">Setting time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting time is a physical property tested for in the produced cements.&lt;SEP&gt;Setting time is a key property of cement that is considerably retarded when phosphogypsum is used.&lt;SEP&gt;Setting time refers to the duration required for cementitious materials to transition from a fresh state to a hardened state.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of cement pastes measured as initial and final times using the Vicat apparatus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compressive strength">
  <data key="d0">Compressive strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Compressive strength is a physical property tested for in the produced cements.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property of cement that is reduced when phosphogypsum is used.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property of bioactive carbonate apatite cement that was enhanced via incorporation of silica calcium phosphate composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a measured property used to evaluate and compare the performance of different concrete variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property metric measuring the load-bearing capacity of self-leveling mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property of mortars determined using cubic specimens molded according to ASTM C109.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fineness">
  <data key="d0">Fineness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fineness is a physical property measured in m²/kg (Blaine) for the produced cements and plaster.&lt;SEP&gt;Fineness is a physical property of cement measured in square meters per kilogram.&lt;SEP&gt;Fineness is a particle size property measured using the Blaine method to assess the quality of Portland slag cement.&lt;SEP&gt;A particle size measurement metric specified for calcined PG and PG in various studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Fineness refers to the specific surface area of OPC and PPC listed in Table 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
