<node id="Radioactive Elements">
  <data key="d0">Radioactive Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radioactive Elements are naturally occurring trace impurities found within phosphogypsum and its surrounding environment. Prominent examples include uranium, thorium, radium, radium-226 (Ra-226), lead-210 (Pb-210), and polonium-210 (Po-210). Their concentrations vary geographically, with notably lower levels observed in Chinese phosphate mines and phosphogypsum sources, which establishes more favorable conditions for the safe industrial utilization of this byproduct.

These elements function as persistent and hazardous contaminants that pose significant threats to ecological stability and human health. When released from phosphogypsum, they readily contaminate soil and groundwater, disrupt plant growth, and cause widespread environmental pollution. Human exposure occurs through inhalation, oral ingestion, or direct skin contact, allowing the radioactive materials to be absorbed into the body and result in substantial physiological damage.

Due to their persistent hazards, radioactive elements necessitate rigorous environmental monitoring, systematic removal, fixation, and harmless treatment protocols. Mitigation strategies, such as citric acid treatment, can effectively reduce their concentrations. However, their presence continues to severely hinder the broader industrial utilization and market recognition of phosphogypsum, as stringent safety standards and regulatory concerns limit its commercial application in many regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Trace radioactive elements present in phosphogypsum that pose potential environmental risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Radioactive elements including uranium and thorium are impurities found in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001</data>
