  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uranium-238">
  <data key="d0">Uranium-238</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uranium-238 is a naturally occurring radioactive isotope of uranium and the foundational parent nuclide of the U-238 decay series. It is naturally abundant in sedimentary phosphates and phosphate rocks, where it accumulates as a primary radionuclide in phosphogypsum waste. In undisturbed geological environments, Uranium-238 maintains radioactive equilibrium with its decay products, particularly Radium-226 and Lead-210; however, this equilibrium is frequently disrupted in phosphogypsum and related matrices. Consequently, it serves as a baseline radionuclide for isotopic ratio analysis alongside Uranium-234 and Uranium-235, with its activity often calculated using conversion factors derived from Uranium-235 (typically multiplied by 21.73). Activity ratios relative to Radium-226 and Lead-210 generally remain below unity but can reach unity under specific measurement or environmental conditions. The continuous decay of Uranium-238 generates Lead-210, a common contaminant in phosphogypsum leachate, as well as radium.

Chemically, Uranium-238 exhibits high mobility in the U(VI) oxidation state, allowing it to dissolve and migrate into surrounding water bodies, particularly under saline conditions. Following long-term phosphogypsum amendments, the isotope accumulates in soils, posing ecological and health risks due to its persistence and potential to accumulate in human tissues through multiple exposure pathways. Its concentration in phosphogypsum varies significantly by geographic origin and physical fraction, with measured levels ranging from approximately 9.0 Bq/kg in coarse fractions to 164 ± 12.5 Bq/kg in bulk samples. It is routinely monitored within phosphogypsum analysis, LCI data for PG disposal, and environmental inventories, where it is measured in becquerels, including specific readings such as 143 Bq in high-population contexts and various activity levels documented in scientific studies.

Due to these environmental and health risks, Uranium-238 requires removal from phosphogypsum to meet safety standards and is routinely tracked during leaching procedures. It can be effectively extracted and stripped from phosphogypsum using suitable organic compounds and organic extractants. However, extraction and stripping efficiencies vary considerably depending on sample type and process parameters. Developed procedures have reported efficiencies reaching 83.4% and 80.3% for specific samples (PG-Se and PG-AT), while in other experimental contexts, Uranium-238 consistently demonstrates the lowest extraction efficiency among target radionuclides, typically ranging from 45% to 60%. Stripping efficiency generally rises steadily over time, plateauing at approximately 49%, while overall removal efficiency increases up to two hours of agitation before declining. Continuous monitoring of Uranium-238’s concentration, mobility, and decay products remains essential for effective phosphogypsum management, environmental assessment, and public health protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 is a naturally occurring radioactive isotope contributing to the radioactivity of phosphate ores.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 is a radionuclide measured in phosphogypsum samples across various global locations.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 is a radioactive isotope that concentrates in elemental phosphorus, phosphoric acid scale, and phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
