<node id="Hydrothermal Pre-Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Pre-Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal pre-treatment is a technique applied to phosphogypsum to induce gypsum re-crystallization and release rare earth elements locked in the lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal Pre-Treatment is a technique involving dehydration that causes gypsum re-crystallization and releases encapsulated rare earth elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Nitric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitric Acid is a strong mineral and inorganic acid widely utilized across industrial, research, and analytical applications. In sample preparation and chemical analysis, it is added to powder and solid samples to facilitate acid digestion, adjust the initial pH of mixed solutions, and prepare materials for chemical composition analysis. It is formally incorporated into the SW-846 testing procedure and serves as a diluted acidic medium for solubility studies of phosphogypsum, synthetic gypsum, and calcium sulfate dihydrate, with solubility measurements peaking at concentrations between 22% and 25% by weight. Additionally, it is employed to maintain the solution pH above 9 during hydrothermal synthesis processes.

A primary application of Nitric Acid lies in the extraction and recovery of rare earth elements, particularly lanthanides, from phosphate by-products such as phosphogypsum and phosphohemihydrate. It effectively dissolves calcium carbonate to generate calcium nitrate solutions, which yield rare earth nitrate leachates or synthetic feed solutions that mimic phosphogypsum composition. In leaching and conventional recovery techniques, it achieves recovery rates of up to 85 percent. Compared to sulfuric acid, it demonstrates superior leaching efficiency, though it requires an additional circulation system and is less efficient than hydrochloric acid. It is also integral to the nitrophosphate process for rare earth extraction, a method that notably circumvents phosphogypsum by-product formation. Beyond rare earths, Nitric Acid is used to leach radium-226 and lead-210 from phosphogypsum, and in uranium processing under oxidizing conditions, it maintains 90% to 95% of uranium in the liquid phase. It also functions as an alternative reagent in the wet process for phosphoric acid production.

In solvent extraction and separation workflows, Nitric Acid acts as an acidified aqueous stripping agent to recover rare earth elements from loaded ionic liquids. It faintly acidifies water to prevent rare earth hydrolysis during stripping, evaluates how acidity influences ion recovery, and adjusts the pH of various solutions. It has also been tested as a salting-out agent during extraction processes, though it typically functions as an acid component in nitrate-nitric acid mixtures that yield a negligible salting-out effect. Collectively, these diverse applications underscore Nitric Acid's critical role in metal and isotope extraction, solubility analysis, and industrial chemical processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical reagent specified in the standard for use in gypsum analysis procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical agent used alongside sodium nitrate to remove fluoride and lanthanides from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric acid is a chemical reagent combined with sulphuric acid for phosphogypsum treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-01