  <data key="d0">Aluminum Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aluminum Oxide (Al2O3) is a chemical and mineral compound utilized across analytical, industrial, and materials science domains. Analytically, it serves as a standard material for calibrating aluminum measurements and contributes to broader oxide calculations and pH value determination. While one referenced source cites a molar mass of 50.98 g/mol, this figure diverges from the established molecular weight of Al2O3 and should be interpreted with noted uncertainty. Chemically, it is an acid-soluble impurity in phosphogypsum that dissolves in hydrochloric acid and subsequently precipitates as a hydroxide.

The compound is a primary chemical component and common impurity found in phosphogypsum, as well as in cement, fly ash, and gypsum materials, with notably higher concentrations in natural gypsum compared to processed variants. It is also identified in PBSLM6 via XRF analysis and functions as a primary metal compound in WBS and TWBS samples, where concentrations increase in beneficiated concentrates alongside rare earth elements. Reported concentrations in phosphogypsum vary significantly across analytical records, ranging from 1219.37 to 1312.60 ppm in compositional tables, up to 0.81% in Yunnan samples, and as low as 0.08 wt% in certain analyses, with one entry flagged as a potential typographical error. During phosphogypsum purification, Aluminum Oxide demonstrates a high removal efficiency of 93.22%. As an impurity within phosphogypsum, it slightly decreases the length-to-width crystal ratio, and when processed, it can be mixed with calcium carbonate and calcium sulfate dihydrate to synthesize cement minerals.

Beyond its geological and waste processing contexts, Aluminum Oxide holds significant industrial utility. It functions as a conventional catalyst support, having been specifically evaluated against hydroxyapatite for palladium-supported oxidation reactions. In metallurgical applications, it comprises 9 to 17 wt% of slag wool and acts as an additive to adjust quaternary acidity coefficients within slag systems. The compound readily combines with calcium oxide and silicon dioxide to form eutectic mixtures, contributing to mixture formation while frequently persisting as unmelted particles during processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum Oxide is a chemical component that remains low, generally below 0.11%, throughout the analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009</data>
