<node id="Scanning Electron Microscope">
  <data key="d0">Scanning Electron Microscope</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Scanning Electron Microscope is a sophisticated imaging instrument and microscopy technique designed to capture high-magnification, grayscale micrographs of material surfaces. Functioning as a critical diagnostic and analytical tool, it is widely applied across multiple scientific disciplines to visualize and examine microstructural characteristics, surface topography, particle morphology, and granular material structures, often resolving features at the nanoscale. The device operates by generating detailed visual representations of diverse samples, enabling researchers to characterize physical properties with high precision.

In practice, the Scanning Electron Microscope is extensively utilized to assess the distinct particle morphology and spatial distribution of rare earth elements, examine mineral phases, and detect trace elements within various matrices. It is specifically employed to analyze phosphogypsum particles, composites, and bulk samples, frequently capturing images at magnifications such as 5,000x. Beyond these applications, the instrument effectively renders detailed views of irregular, chunky particles with rough surfaces, observes crust structures in soil research, and analyzes the microstructure of bone cement samples. To achieve these accurate visualizations, the system typically operates under controlled technical parameters, such as a 15 kV accelerating voltage, ensuring reliable characterization of complex material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscope is an imaging instrument used to capture the grayscale micrograph revealing the surface morphology of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is a high-magnification imaging device used to capture grayscale micrographs of surface morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is used to examine the texture and morphology of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is an imaging device used to analyze the particulate matter morphology in the provided visual data.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-magnification imaging device used to analyze the microscopic morphology of phosphogypsum platelets.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscope is the imaging device used to capture the surface morphology of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019</data>
