<node id="Yttrium">
  <data key="d0">Yttrium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Yttrium is a chemical element classified as a rare earth element (REE), defined alongside the lanthanides and scandium, and typically positioned after them in the periodic table due to shared chemical similarities. Recognized as a critical REE by the European Commission, yttrium occurs naturally as a trace element enriched in sedimentary phosphate rocks. It is predominantly found within fluorapatite and apatite crystal structures, where it substitutes for calcium, and is also present in gypsum and fluorite. The aqueous geochemistry and speciation of yttrium in natural waters were comprehensively reviewed in 1990.

In industrial phosphate processing, particularly the wet process, yttrium is heavily concentrated in phosphogypsum (PG), with approximately 41% transferring from phosphate rock to this byproduct. It constitutes a major component of both wet and dried PG, accounting for over 80% of the total rare earth elements present. The element is homogeneously dispersed across the surfaces of PG and beneficiated concentrates, with its concentration and enrichment systematically documented in matrices such as WBS and TWBS. Measured concentrations in PG include values like 144 ± 38, alongside 39 ppm and 56.6 ppm in fluorite. Its presence in PG and associated reaction products is routinely characterized using Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass-Spectrometry (ICP-MS), and its elemental deportment is explicitly depicted in scientific graphical studies.

Due to its substantial presence in industrial byproducts, yttrium is closely monitored for environmental and economic implications, particularly regarding its mobility from PG stacks. It is actively targeted for recovery through multiple extraction methodologies. Chemical leaching using a 1.0 mol/L citric acid solution demonstrates a selectivity of 40.7% and can successfully reduce detected radionuclide forms within PG. Alternative extraction processes have reported recovery rates as high as 91.2%, while two-step bioleaching techniques achieve an extraction rate of 62%. This dual role underscores yttrium’s significance in both critical resource recovery and industrial waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Yttrium is a rare earth element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Yttrium is an element typically found in the fine fraction of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Yttrium is a trace metal found in Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Yttrium is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured across the sampled locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
