</node>
<node id="Lanthanum">
  <data key="d0">Lanthanum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lanthanum is a light rare earth chemical element and metal ion that initiates the sequence of increasing atomic numbers within the referenced dataset, while also contributing significantly to the total rare earth content of phosphate rock and phosphorites. It occurs naturally as a common impurity that is notably enriched relative to shale. During industrial acidulation processes, lanthanum is transferred from phosphate rock into phosphogypsum, where it becomes highly prevalent and often dominates the elemental composition of dried phosphogypsum. The element is homogeneously dispersed across the surfaces of both phosphogypsum and beneficiated concentrates, with regional concentration variations evident; for example, analyses of Idaho phosphogypsum report a mean concentration of 81 mg/kg, while Brazilian phosphogypsum exhibits significantly higher levels than Florida phosphogypsum. As a trace element in phosphogypsum, lanthanum is routinely characterized using Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass-Spectrometry and identified analytically by a small spectral peak appearing just after calcium at approximately 4.0 keV. Quantitative tracking of its concentration and enrichment is standard practice, with measurements actively taken across various test specimens, including WBS and TWBS samples, and data routinely cataloged with associated concentration values in analytical datasets.

Recognized as a valuable resource, lanthanum is actively recovered from various sources through diverse metallurgical and chemical processes. It demonstrates high leaching selectivity of 81.8% when treated with a 1.0 mol/L citric acid solution and can be effectively recovered via bioleaching, achieving a reported extraction rate of 58% in two-step processes. In solvent extraction operations, lanthanum is specifically isolated from nitrate leach solutions and phosphogypsum leachates using ionic liquids. In this nitrate medium, lanthanum ions form pentakis anionic complexes that are efficiently extracted by the ionic liquid and subsequently stripped using faintly acidified water. Research indicates that its extraction efficiency remains constant at 99% across pH values ranging from 1 to 6, even in the presence of ammonium nitrate. Furthermore, the stripping efficiency of lanthanum is systematically monitored across varying aqueous-to-organic phase ratios, underscoring its targeted recovery, optimization, and consistent assessment in modern rare earth processing workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanthanum is a trace chemical element present in phosphogypsum with a measured concentration of 86 ± 19.&lt;SEP&gt;A detected radionuclide in phosphogypsum that can be successfully reduced through citric acid leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare earth element present in phosphogypsum, with concentrations of 32.5 ppm and 14 ppm in fluorite.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanthanum is a rare earth element whose elemental deportment is depicted in Fig. 5.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanthanum is a rare earth element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008</data>
