<node id="Neodymium">
  <data key="d0">Neodymium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Neodymium is a light rare earth element and chemical metal ion formally classified as a critical rare earth resource by the European Commission and Seredin. Geologically, it is notably enriched in the Phosphoria Formation relative to shale and contributes significantly to the total rare earth content of phosphate rock. In industrial byproduct streams, particularly phosphogypsum, neodymium dominates the elemental composition of dried samples and is homogeneously dispersed across the surface of beneficiated concentrates. It is routinely quantified in WBS and TWBS samples, with analytical studies in Idaho phosphogypsum reporting a mean concentration of 36 mg/kg. Spectroscopically, neodymium is reliably identified through distinct signatures, producing two characteristic peaks at approximately 5.2 keV and 6.5 keV, with the 6.5 keV peak serving as a primary detection marker.

In resource recovery and processing applications, neodymium is frequently targeted for extraction from nitrate leach solutions and phosphogypsum leachate. Experimental leaching studies have reported a recovery rate of 42.8%, while two-step bioleaching processes have demonstrated an extraction rate of 98%. Advanced separation techniques utilizing ionic liquids have proven highly effective for selectively extracting the element from nitrate media. Research indicates that extraction efficiency remains constant at 95% across pH values ranging from 1 to 6, and its behavior is studied in the presence of ammonium nitrate. During ionic liquid extraction, neodymium forms pentakis anionic complexes and is co-extracted alongside lanthanum and cerium. Once transferred into the ionic liquid phase, the metal ion is subsequently stripped using faintly acidified water, with optimal stripping efficiency achieved at an A/O phase ratio of 1/3. Collectively, these properties highlight neodymium’s consistent measurability in environmental and processing matrices and its significance as a recoverable critical resource.&lt;SEP&gt;A detected radionuclide in phosphogypsum that can be successfully reduced through citric acid leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Neodymium is a rare earth element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008</data>
