<node id="Particle Morphology">
  <data key="d0">Particle Morphology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Particle morphology describes the physical shape and arrangement of crystals and clusters in phosphogypsum and concentrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle Morphology refers to the physical shape characteristics of the particles, including spherical, plate-like, and rod-like forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle morphology refers to the texture and orientation of HAp particles, which influences protein adsorption amounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle morphology refers to the physical shape and structure of the particles, compared between the two micrographs.&lt;SEP&gt;A visual characteristic of the phosphogypsum sample describing the size, shape, and arrangement of its granular particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-019</data>
