<node id="Red Mud">
  <data key="d0">Red Mud</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Red Mud is an alkaline, aluminate-rich industrial and mining residue primarily generated as a waste byproduct during alumina and aluminum production. Its chemical composition is characterized by significant concentrations of iron oxide (Fe2O3), aluminum oxide (Al2O3), silicon dioxide (SiO2), and other compounds. Historically dismissed as waste, Red Mud has become a major focus of research and comprehensive utilization strategies, particularly in China, driven by its potential for valorization and environmentally sustainable reuse. A central application involves resource recovery, where the material is processed to selectively extract valuable metals, including iron, aluminum, rare earth elements (REEs), and scandium.

In the construction and materials sectors, Red Mud demonstrates versatile functional properties and is actively incorporated into high-strength composite formulations. It is widely utilized to develop low-carbon and green cementitious materials, where it reacts with calcium sulfates to form ettringite, thereby enhancing mixture densification and facilitating the creation of vertical barriers. The residue also serves as a key modifier in phosphogypsum-based composite cementitious materials, improving their safety and performance. Furthermore, Red Mud is frequently recycled alongside phosphogypsum to engineer advanced geotechnical and environmental containment solutions. When combined with phosphogypsum and fly ash, it forms effective liners for hazardous waste disposal. Its environmental remediation capabilities are further enhanced when mixed with phosphogypsum and kaolin, significantly boosting its adsorption capacity for arsenic.

While predominantly recognized as an alumina production byproduct, Red Mud has also been evaluated in specific environmental impact studies as a secondary gypsum byproduct, assessed alongside phosphogypsum and natural gypsum. Despite this contextual classification variance, the material remains a critical subject of industrial symbiosis and circular economy initiatives, bridging waste management with resource recovery and sustainable construction technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Red mud is an industrial residue whose arsenic sorption capacity is increased by phosphogypsum addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Red mud is an industrial waste material investigated for its capacity to sorb toxic heavy metals like arsenic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-032</data>
