<node id="Oxalic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Oxalic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxalic acid is an organic chemical reagent widely employed in metallurgical and industrial applications, particularly for resource recovery and material treatment. In rare earth element processing, it serves as a highly effective precipitating agent, selectively recovering these elements from red mud, accumulated leaching solutions, and stripping solutions by forming rare earth oxalate compounds. It is also utilized in bioleaching operations to lower pH and facilitate broader metal extraction. Beyond rare earth recovery, oxalic acid is extensively studied in gypsum-related chemistry, where it is routinely tested alongside other acids to evaluate the solubility of synthetic gypsum.

In the context of phosphogypsum waste management, oxalic acid is prepared and applied as an acidic leaching reagent to treat the material. While it is utilized as one of four chemical agents aimed at removing hazardous and radioactive constituents from phosphogypsum, the leaching process selectively dissolves other elements, which consequently increases the relative proportion and total concentration of radionuclides in the treated residue, reaching approximately 0.62 wt%. This treatment yields the highest radionuclide content among comparable methods and primarily produces gypsum and disodium catena-disilicate. Despite its effectiveness in these chemical transformations, oxalic acid is noted to be less effective than citric acid for this specific leaching application.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid is a chemical solution used in washing treatments to considerably reduce soluble phosphorus pentoxide in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013</data>
