<node id="Scandium">
  <data key="d0">Scandium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Scandium is a chemical element classified as a rare earth element (REE), formally included in the REE definition alongside the lanthanides and yttrium. Recognized as a critical metal, it naturally occurs in significant concentrations within fluorapatite found in sedimentary phosphate rock. Additionally, it is selectively extracted from industrial residues such as red mud.

In analytical and environmental studies, Scandium is measured for its concentration, enrichment, and variable levels across various sample types, including WBS and TWBS samples. It is specifically analyzed as a trace element in phosphogypsum minerals using LA-ICP-MS, with results routinely documented in data tables alongside associated concentration values. The mobility and migration of Scandium from phosphogypsum stacks are closely tracked alongside yttrium and other REEs. This monitoring is conducted to evaluate both the environmental consequences of its movement and the economic potential of its recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006</data>
