<node id="Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concentration is a multifaceted scientific and industrial concept that functions both as a quantitative measurement parameter and a processing operation across chemistry, materials science, and hydrometallurgy. Fundamentally, it represents the amount of solute per unit volume of solution or the abundance of specific elements, isotopes, and radioactive materials within samples, reactants, and final products. This metric is commonly expressed in parts per million (ppm), mass percentage, or becquerels per kilogram (Bq/kg), and is frequently tracked before and after treatment processes, often accompanied by standard deviations to ensure measurement precision.

In practical and industrial applications, concentration serves as a critical variable that dictates solution strength, optimizes processing efficiency, and enables precise compositional control. For instance, it determines the strength of chemical solutions like citric acid for treatment outcomes, acts as an independent variable for testing sulfuric acid levels across three distinct percentages in the second figure, and quantifies phosphorus content in manure for agricultural calculations. In hydrometallurgical and purification contexts, concentration influences key processes such as quartz removal, compound solubilization, and the enhancement of material purity, notably in the purification of phosphoric acid following gypsum removal. It also defines the mass percentage of slurry in CPGFM formulations and measures sulfate group amounts in samples, as indicated by dip depths.

Beyond its role in chemical and industrial processing, concentration significantly impacts material properties and experimental outcomes. It is a fundamental parameter in mathematical formulas, often representing titrants or standard solutions, and directly influences crystal growth by affecting density and size, though temperature typically exerts a stronger effect on overall crystal shape. Collectively, these diverse applications underscore concentration as an essential variable for controlling chemical interactions, refining material formulations, and ensuring accurate quantitative analysis across a wide range of scientific and engineering disciplines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792405761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Agitation Speed">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Agitation Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A controlled hydrometallurgical parameter during the agitation of hydrofluoric acid and WBS.&lt;SEP&gt;A key hydrometallurgical parameter affecting the efficiency of the quartz removal process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
