<node id="Slurry">
  <data key="d0">Slurry</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mixture of hydrofluoric acid and treated solid (WBS) agitated during the hydrometallurgical treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Slurry is the mixture of Phosphogypsum and leachant during the leaching process, noted for its energy-intensive heating requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Slurry is the physical state of phosphogypsum before it undergoes dewatering.&lt;SEP&gt;Slurry is the fluid mixture formed from the PG-H2O mixture before reagent addition.&lt;SEP&gt;The slurry is a mixture of the sample and anhydrous ethanol used for electrode coating.&lt;SEP&gt;The slurry is a mixture of the sample and anhydrous ethanol used for electrode coating.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-003</data>
