  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A procedure performed on the stored solid to determine its elemental composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical analysis is a procedure detailing the weight percentage and trace concentrations of components in a phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Analysis is a procedure used to monitor and determine the elemental composition of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic procedure used to determine the chemical composition and properties of gypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical analysis is used to determine the composition of PG oxides before and after calcination at different temperatures.</data>
