<node id="Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid is an industrial chemical produced from phosphate rock, containing dissolved rare earth elements suitable for extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet-process phosphoric acid is a production method frequently referenced in studies regarding purification, material selection, and byproduct utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid is an industrial chemical produced via phosphate mining, known to contain precipitated impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical production process that generates phosphogypsum as a major byproduct through the reaction of phosphate rock and sulfuric acid.</data>
