  <data key="d0">Seredin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A researcher who devised a categorization system classifying rare earth elements into critical and excessive groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Seredin is a researcher who devised a novel categorization of Rare Earth Elements into critical, non-critical, and excessive groups based on market dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical REEs">
  <data key="d0">Critical REEs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical REEs are a subset of Rare Earth Elements deemed highly valuable due to high concentration and strong market demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-critical REEs">
  <data key="d0">Non-critical REEs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-critical REEs are a subset of Rare Earth Elements with moderate market value and supply-demand balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Excessive REEs">
  <data key="d0">Excessive REEs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive REEs are a subset of Rare Earth Elements present in high quantities but with lower economic priority.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outlook Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Outlook Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A metric used to evaluate the economic potential and outlook of rare earth element resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Outlook Coefficient is a calculated metric used for resource evaluation, representing the ratio of critical Rare Earth Elements to excessive Rare Earth Elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-ray Diffraction">
  <data key="d0">X-ray Diffraction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray Diffraction is a fundamental analytical and scientific technique primarily utilized for the structural characterization, mineralogical analysis, and crystalline phase identification of diverse natural and synthetic materials. The method operates by measuring X-ray diffraction intensities to generate diffractograms, which plot signal intensity against the diffraction angle and are commonly visualized as three-dimensional stacked line plots. By comparing these generated patterns against standard reference databases, X-ray Diffraction accurately identifies, quantifies, and compares the crystal structures of different materials, determines phase purity, and assesses overall material composition and relative quality.

Through the interpretation of diffraction data, the technique calculates critical crystallographic and microstructural parameters, including lattice and interplanar spacings, crystallinity levels, crystalline domain sizes, crystallite dimensions, particle size, material strain, texture, and peak broadening. It is also employed to qualitatively assess crystallinity, estimate crystalline domain sizes, and detect lattice strain, particularly in specialized applications such as hydroxyapatite samples. Furthermore, X-ray Diffraction effectively tracks mineralogical evolution and structural changes over time, such as determining crystalline phases in the calcium sulfate system during heating and calcination, as well as identifying specific minerals like α-quartz, trace element compounds, and synthesized products.

The technique is widely applied across a broad spectrum of matrices, with notable emphasis on phosphogypsum, hydroxyapatite powders, ammonium sulfate, brick samples, eggshells, set cement composites, and beneficiated solids. While it serves as a robust, standard tool in both research and industrial settings for verifying structural properties and chemical characteristics, it possesses a defined sensitivity limitation, detecting rare earth elements only above a threshold of 10,000 ppm. To achieve more comprehensive characterization and overcome this constraint, X-ray Diffraction is frequently integrated into multi-analytical approaches alongside complementary techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction is an analytical technique used to identify the chemical composition of hydration products.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical technique used to identify and characterize the crystalline compounds in calcined PG.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray Diffraction is an analytical technique used to observe the mineralogical transformation of phosphogypsum components during heat treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-01