<node id="European Commission">
  <data key="d0">European Commission</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">European Commission is a regulatory body that classified certain rare earth elements as critical metals.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulatory body that established directives limiting indoor radiation exposure from building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is a regulatory body that established a 1.0 mSv per annum dose criterion and activity concentration index for phosphogypsum bulk application.&lt;SEP&gt;A governing body that issued directives on radiation protection and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A regulatory body whose guidelines influence the environmental assessment and management of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is a governing body that published directives and handbooks related to environmental safety and life cycle assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission provided funding for the ERA-MIN3 action under the Horizon 2020 Program.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792402124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States Geological Survey">
  <data key="d0">United States Geological Survey</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">United States Geological Survey is an agency that estimates global phosphate rock reserves and mining volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Geological Survey is the organization that provided the database for worldwide phosphate ore excavation data.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific agency that collected and published water-quality and hydrogeologic data for phosphate disposal sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Geological Survey developed the Phreeqc program used for geochemical modeling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-017</data>
