  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A co-product generated during phosphate rock treatment that is explored for future valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorosilicic acid is a chemical recovered from wet phosphoric acid production and analyzed using potentiometric titration.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorosilicic acid is a chemical compound formed from the hydrolysis of silicon tetrafluoride and recovered via water absorption using scrubbers.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorosilicic acid is formed when silicon tetrafluoride undergoes hydrolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorosilicic acid is a chemical compound mentioned in the initial list of acids relevant to the processing context.&lt;SEP&gt;An acid compound that adheres to the surface of gypsum crystals.</data>
