<node id="Reactor">
  <data key="d0">Reactor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A reactor is processing equipment at risk of erosion-corrosion damage from quartz impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Experimental vessel where microbial fermentation and material decomposition occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactor is the experimental vessel where the chemical reactions and phase separations occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The equipment used for synthesis where higher temperature and longer synthesis time were applied.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791857346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Chloride">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride is a versatile chemical compound widely recognized as dietary salt, with extensive applications across biomedical, industrial, and analytical fields. In biomedical engineering, it serves as a critical additive in composite bone cement formulations, where its variable weight percentage and phase proportion are utilized to adjust setting time, enhance mechanical strength, increase porosity, and improve bioactivity and ionic supersaturation. Beyond medicine, sodium chloride plays a pivotal role in industrial processing, particularly in the treatment of phosphogypsum. As a salt solution, it significantly enhances the solubility of phosphogypsum compared to pure water, facilitating the washing of pre-treated material to solubilize water-soluble impurities. It is also investigated at an optimal concentration of 25 g L⁻¹, with its high solubility attributed to ionic strength effects. In this process, it acts as a chloride salt reagent that reacts with gypsum to form sodium sulfate, ultimately aiding in the production of rare earth concentrates.

In laboratory and analytical settings, sodium chloride is utilized as a primary reagent dissolved in deionized water to prepare simulated body fluid, where it constitutes the most abundant component at a concentration of 112.00 mmol L⁻¹. It also functions as an analytical-grade compound serving as a grinding medium for plant sample preparation and as a standard solution for vitamin C quantification. Furthermore, it acts as a reference standard in diffraction pattern analyses, with its characteristic peaks typically identified and marked with asterisks in experimental data.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is a chemical substance that causes microcrack expansion and reduces hydration products in the filling body.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical compound used to prepare solutions with varying concentrations for the zeta potential analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is a chemical component included in the experimental buffer mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792261046</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Carbonate">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Carbonate</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium carbonate is an inorganic alkaline compound and chemical reagent widely utilized in industrial processing, particularly for the sequential treatment and valorization of phosphogypsum. Applied as an aqueous or carbonated solution under basic conditions, it functions as a primary leaching and washing agent. Its core mechanism involves driving chemical phase conversions of calcium sulfate dihydrate, which can yield calcium carbonate (calcite) and sodium sulfate, or transform gypsum into calcium sulfate hemihydrate and lanthanum silicate depending on specific process parameters. This chemical transformation effectively solubilizes water-soluble impurities and decomposes insoluble radium compounds, thereby mitigating contamination within the phosphogypsum matrix.

In radiological management, sodium carbonate plays a critical role in radionuclide control and isotope recovery. The treatment reduces the total radionuclide concentration in the solid phosphogypsum to approximately 0.600 wt%. Concurrently, the leaching process transfers radionuclides into the solution, which can increase their relative proportion in the liquid phase. This alkaline leachate is subsequently employed as a stripping agent to recover extracted isotopes and remove radioactive materials from organic extractants. To optimize material recovery, sodium carbonate is often synergistically combined with sodium chloride or other salt solutions. This combination significantly enhances the enrichment and extraction of valuable components, particularly rare earth elements, from phosphogypsum residues, ultimately yielding concentrated rare earth products.

From an operational standpoint, utilizing sodium carbonate for phosphogypsum conversion offers distinct efficiency advantages over alternative reagents like sodium hydroxide. It requires lower energy demand, making it a more sustainable and cost-effective option for large-scale chemical processing. Through its multifaceted capabilities in phase conversion, impurity removal, radionuclide mitigation, and rare earth enrichment, sodium carbonate serves as a versatile and essential agent in modern industrial byproduct valorization and chemical reagent applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Carbonate is a chemical additive mixed with sodium thiosulfate to stabilize the solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006</data>
