<node id="Resin-In-Leach Process">
  <data key="d0">Resin-In-Leach Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The resin-in-leach process is a hydrometallurgical technique used to recover rare earth elements from phosphogypsum using specific resins and eluents.&lt;SEP&gt;Resin-in-leach process is a recovery technique involving the selection of specific resins, leaching agents, and eluents to extract rare earth elements.</data>
