</node>
<node id="J. Hazard. Mater.">
  <data key="d0">J. Hazard. Mater.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Journal of Hazardous Materials (abbreviated as J. Hazard. Mater.) is a peer-reviewed academic and scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on hazardous materials, environmental hazards, and waste management. It serves as a key resource for studies focused on the treatment, characterization, and safe application of industrial byproducts and waste streams, with a strong emphasis on environmental remediation and pollution control. The journal's editorial scope encompasses a wide range of topics, including the assessment of binders and solid waste, investigations into hazardous substances like fly ash, soil stabilization techniques, and the chemistry and applications of synthetic hydroxyapatite, particularly for contaminant removal and heavy metal adsorption.

A substantial portion of the journal's literature is dedicated to phosphogypsum, documenting its radiological and chemical characterization, ecotoxicity, and various treatment and valorization methods. Notable publications include a 2009 study on phosphogypsum stack radioactive characterization, a 2021 study on the radiological and structural characterization of phosphogypsum for brick production, and research on metal-rich phosphogypsum. The journal has also featured studies on phosphate rock, the utilization of phosphogypsum for fluoride removal, the effect of phosphorus in phosphogypsum-based cemented backfill, lanthanide leaching, nanoparticle synthesis, and methods for increasing arsenic sorption on red mud using phosphogypsum. Beyond phosphogypsum, the journal has published multiple studies on sulfurisation gypsum, arsenic leaching dynamics, metal-bearing sludge characterization, and the broader use of industrial byproducts in environmental remediation. Collectively, these publications highlight the journal's commitment to advancing scientific understanding and developing mitigation strategies for hazardous materials and industrial waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-028</data>
