<node id="Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry">
  <data key="d0">Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An analytical technique used to assess the concentration of rare earth elements and minerals in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical instrument used for qualitative and quantitative detection of heavy metals and rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry is an analytical technique used to measure concentrations of multiple elements in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry is a high-sensitivity technique used to detect and quantify trace elements in samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry is a laboratory technique employed to determine the concentration of trace elements in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry is used to determine the concentration of trace elements in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inductively Coupled Plasma Optical Emission Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">Inductively Coupled Plasma Optical Emission Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An analytical technique used alongside mass spectrometry for mineral assessment in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy is utilized to analyze the chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Inductively Coupled Plasma Optical Emission Spectroscopy is one of the analytical methods applied to phosphogypsum samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphoric Ores">
  <data key="d0">Phosphoric Ores</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The raw ores processed to generate phosphogypsum, strongly influencing its chemical characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790984452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Europium">
  <data key="d0">Europium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Europium is a chemical element classified as a rare earth element and is recognized as a critical rare earth element according to the categorization by Seredin. It is frequently encountered in industrial byproducts, particularly phosphogypsum, where it constitutes a considerable proportion in dried forms. Specific analyses of Idaho phosphogypsum have recorded a mean Europium concentration of 1.2 mg/kg, and its concentration and enrichment levels have been systematically measured and recorded in data tables across various sample sets, including WBS and TWBS samples.

Research into Europium has also focused on its chemical behavior and potential recovery. Its location and stability within calcium sulfate matrices have been extensively investigated to optimize extraction processes from phosphogypsum waste. These studies aim to improve the feasibility of recovering Europium from such waste streams, with reported extraction efforts achieving a recovery rate of approximately 50%. Consequently, Europium is actively targeted for recovery due to its critical status and measurable presence in these industrial materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a Rare Earth Element used as a model to study surface association with phosphate and sulfate ions.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare earth element used as a model to demonstrate that REEs are found on the surface of gypsum crystals as a secondary phase.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare earth element studied for its location and stability in calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a rare earth element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792401441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terbium">
  <data key="d0">Terbium</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Terbium is a chemical element whose concentration and enrichment were measured in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A critical rare earth element categorized by Seredin, found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Terbium is a rare earth element measured in WBS and TWBS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Terbium is a critical rare earth element present in a considerable proportion in dried PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Terbium is a rare earth element analyzed in Idaho phosphogypsum with a mean concentration of 1 mg/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;Terbium is a rare earth element found in phosphogypsum phases, notably in fluorite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
