<node id="Ytterbium">
  <data key="d0">Ytterbium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical element used as a dopant with Erbium to facilitate calcium fluoride crystallization at lower temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element measured in WBS and TWBS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element with a concentration below the detection limit in the analyzed sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element enriched in phosphorites relative to shale.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element analyzed in Idaho phosphogypsum with a mean concentration of 2.8 mg/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare earth element targeted for extraction with a reported recovery rate of 83.7%.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is present only as trace amounts, visible as very faint, sparse dots.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
