<node id="Samarium">
  <data key="d0">Samarium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Samarium is a rare earth chemical element that has been extensively analyzed and targeted for recovery in various industrial and research contexts. Its concentration and enrichment have been measured across multiple sample types, including WBS and TWBS samples, as well as in a provided data table where concentrations are recorded in parts per million (ppm). Specific analyses of Idaho phosphogypsum have identified Samarium within its phases, reporting a mean concentration of 5.4 mg/kg, while other assessments indicate phase concentrations ranging between 100 and an unspecified upper limit.

In terms of resource recovery, Samarium is selectively targeted for extraction, particularly from phosphogypsum leachate. Research by Hoogerstraete and Binnemans has previously investigated its extraction process and complex formation, supporting recovery efforts that have achieved a reported extraction rate of 73.2%. These combined analytical and metallurgical studies highlight Samarium's presence in industrial byproducts and the ongoing efforts to quantify and recover it efficiently.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792401441</data>
