<node id="Sol-Gel Method">
  <data key="d0">Sol-Gel Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sol-Gel Method is a wet-chemical technique used for the fabrication of materials starting from a chemical solution precursor.&lt;SEP&gt;Sol-gel method is a conventional method proposed for producing synthetic nano-hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Sol-gel method is one of the synthesis routes used to prepare hydroxyapatite powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Sol-gel is a chemical technique employed to synthesize hydroxyapatite crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Sol-Gel Method is a wet-chemical technique for preparing nanostructure hydroxyapatite powder with controlled properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microwave Irradiation">
  <data key="d0">Microwave Irradiation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Microwave irradiation is a rapid material processing and synthesis technique that relies on the in situ conversion of microwave energy into heat through rapid volumetric heating. This method significantly accelerates chemical reactions and shortens synthesis durations by employing substantially faster heating rates. The intense thermal energy promotes accelerated particle nucleation, which directly influences material morphology and consistently yields smaller particle sizes.

The technique is applied across a variety of material preparation and processing contexts. It is frequently utilized to rapidly synthesize nanostructures and prepare hydroxyapatite powders from biogenic calcium sources, often alongside or evaluated in comparison to the hydrothermal method. In other applications, microwave irradiation serves as a targeted treatment for colloids, typically followed by a cooling phase. Additionally, it functions as a specialized heating process that creates pores within phosphogypsum matrices, thereby facilitating improved lixiviant infiltration.

Operational parameters for microwave irradiation are adaptable to specific experimental requirements. Synthesis protocols may be conducted at temperatures around 80°C with a controlled heating rate of 5°C/min, with treatment durations ranging from one minute to thirty-six minutes. Despite these variable conditions, the fundamental mechanism remains consistent, leveraging rapid thermal conversion to enhance reaction kinetics, control structural properties, and optimize material preparation across diverse scientific applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Microwave irradiation is the energy application technique used to prepare and synthesize the nHAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Microwave Irradiation is a rapid processing technique applied to synthesize hydroxyapatite nanostructures and analyze their thermal stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317876</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
