<node id="Fuel">
  <data key="d0">Fuel</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuel is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to advancing research across the fields of energy, fuels, and chemical processing. The publication serves as a comprehensive platform for scholarly work, consistently featuring studies that explore innovative methodologies and material behaviors relevant to modern energy systems.

The journal's extensive publication record covers a diverse range of specialized topics. It has featured research on the mineralogical characterization of coal waste alongside studies focused on the recovery of rare earth elements from similar waste streams. Significant attention is given to advanced combustion and gasification technologies, including chemical looping gasification of lignite for syngas generation, chemical looping combustion of sulfur paste, and broader investigations into gasification and energy systems. Furthermore, Fuel publishes work on fuel preparation and chemical processing techniques. The journal's scope also extends to catalytic and geochemical studies, as demonstrated by its publication of research on the oxidative coupling of methane over hydroxyapatite catalysts and investigations into sulphate behavior resulting from gypsum dissolution. Collectively, these contributions underscore the journal's broad academic reach and commitment to publishing high-impact research in fuel science and related disciplines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791593235</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
