<node id="Crystalline Structure">
  <data key="d0">Crystalline Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystalline structure refers to the ordered atomic arrangement of materials analyzed via XRD patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline structure describes the consistent atomic arrangement of the material across different samples and treatment times.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline Structure refers to the hexagonal arrangement and P63/m space group identified in hydroxyapatite and natural bone samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline structure is the structural arrangement of the material, which influences peak position and intensity variations.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline structure describes the rhombic and orthorhombic shapes and prismatic arrangement of Phosphogypsum crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792480197</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diffraction Angle">
  <data key="d0">Diffraction Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffraction Angle serves as the fundamental horizontal axis variable in X-ray Diffraction (XRD) pattern analysis, representing the specific angle in degrees at which X-ray scattering and diffraction occur. It functions as the primary scale for plotting and interpreting XRD graphs, charts, and patterns.

While the unit of measurement is consistently degrees, the operational range varies depending on the specific experimental setup or dataset. Typical ranges span from 10 to 80 degrees, with some specific charts utilizing narrower intervals such as 15 to 80 degrees or 20 to 55 degrees. Beyond its role as a graphical axis, the Diffraction Angle is a critical geometric parameter utilized in trigonometric calculations. It directly facilitates the quantitative relationship between diffraction peak broadening and material strain, making it essential for structural and mechanical analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement metric in degrees representing the X-axis scale for the XRD pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffraction angle is a metric measured in degrees representing the angle on the horizontal axis.&lt;SEP&gt;The X-axis parameter in the XRD pattern, measured in degrees (2θ), ranging from approximately 5 to 70.&lt;SEP&gt;X-axis parameter measured in degrees, ranging from 20 to 60.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
