<node id="UNSCEAR">
  <data key="d0">UNSCEAR</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United Nations Scientific Committee on the Effects of Atomic Radiation (UNSCEAR) is an international body established to assess radiological risks and formulate global safety standards. Serving as a foundational resource for worldwide radiation protection and environmental monitoring, the committee provides essential guidelines and conversion factors for calculating absorbed dose rates. It is widely recognized for determining the annual effective dose equivalent from natural background radiation and is frequently cited as a primary source for ionizing radiation data in emission standards reports.

A core function of UNSCEAR involves establishing standardized benchmarks and exposure limits. The committee has set worldwide average activity concentration benchmarks for naturally occurring radionuclides, specifically uranium, thorium, and potassium-40. It has also formally recommended a safe dose level of 55 nGy/h for workers exposed to gamma radiation. Furthermore, UNSCEAR establishes recommended worldwide radiation exposure limits, notably publishing a 2000 report that recommended a limit of 2.4 mSv/year.

Throughout its operational history, UNSCEAR has disseminated its scientific findings through numerous authoritative publications. Key reports include a 1977 assessment on natural radioactivity, comprehensive evaluations on the sources and effects of ionizing radiation released in 1993 and 2000, and a dedicated 2000 report focusing on natural radiation exposure. The committee has also specifically documented the distribution of radium within the human body. Collectively, these standardized metrics and rigorous scientific assessments continue to underpin global regulatory frameworks and environmental monitoring practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792482495</data>
