</node>
<node id="Activity Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Activity Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Activity concentration represents the measured radioactivity levels of radionuclides in becquerels per kilogram.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity concentration is the measured quantity of radioactivity per unit mass, expressed in Bq/kg for the uranium isotopes.&lt;SEP&gt;The measured quantity of a specific isotope in a sample, expressed in Bq·kg.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity concentration is a quantitative measurement of radionuclide presence, estimated using specific emission lines and correction formulas.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity concentration is a quantitative metric measured in Bq kg^-1 to assess the level of natural radionuclides in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity concentration is a quantitative metric measured in Bq kg^-1 used to assess radioactive isotope levels in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity concentration measures the radioactivity of isotopes per unit mass, expressed in Bq kg⁻¹.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791312327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulphate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Sulphate is the predominant chemical compound found in raw phosphogypsum, a byproduct generated during the industrial production of phosphoric acid. It is directly responsible for the formation of phosphogypsum crystals and serves as the primary constituent in phosphogypsum precursor materials. Spectroscopic and diffraction analyses consistently identify it as the main phase composition of phosphogypsum waste, confirming its central role in both the chemical manufacturing process and the resulting solid byproduct.

Quantitative assessments reveal that Calcium Sulphate accounts for approximately 88.46% to 92% of the raw phosphogypsum's composition. The slight variation in these percentages reflects differences in sample sources, processing conditions, or analytical methodologies rather than fundamental discrepancies. Overall, Calcium Sulphate remains the majority chemical compound in phosphogypsum waste, defining its chemical profile and influencing its handling and potential utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792190776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IR Measurements">
  <data key="d0">IR Measurements</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">IR measurements are analytical techniques used to verify the phase composition of phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;IR measurements are spectroscopic techniques used to evaluate the chemical composition of phosphogypsum waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008</data>
