<node id="Enrichment Factor">
  <data key="d0">Enrichment Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enrichment Factor (EF) is a metric used to quantify the concentration of elements or radionuclides in samples compared to a natural background.&lt;SEP&gt;Enrichment Factor is a standard ratio or specific index used to model radionuclide migration or leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;The Enrichment Factor is a quantitative parameter used to evaluate isotope fractionation by comparing activities in different material fractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Enrichment Factor is a calculated metric comparing isotope activity in fractionated material to that in non-fractionated bulk material.&lt;SEP&gt;Enrichment Factor is a metric used to quantify the concentration of isotopes like lead-210 and radium-226 in specific phosphogypsum fractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Enrichment Factor is a metric calculated to quantify the concentration of specific substances in a fraction relative to the total sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791313927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
