<node id="Journal of Environmental Radioactivity">
  <data key="d0">Journal of Environmental Radioactivity</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Journal of Environmental Radioactivity is a scientific and academic publication dedicated to advancing research in environmental radiochemistry and the study of naturally occurring radioactive materials. The journal serves as a primary venue for scholarly work examining radionuclide flow, migration, and the radiological impacts of NORM contamination, including specific assessments of TE-NORM waste. It provides a comprehensive platform for evaluating the environmental and radiological dynamics of radioactive substances across various industrial and ecological contexts.

A significant portion of the journal's published research focuses on phosphogypsum, covering its natural radioactivity, radiological implications in agricultural settings, and the environmental consequences of its recycling and disposal. Notable studies featured in the publication include a 2014 investigation into radioactive characterization near phosphogypsum disposal sites, as well as research by El Afifi and Awwad addressing TE-NORM waste management. Additionally, the journal regularly disseminates findings on radon emanation and exhalation rates associated with phosphogypsum processing, alongside broader investigations into natural radioactivity in phosphates and related nuclide migration patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
