<node id="Rutherford, P.M.">
  <data key="d0">Rutherford, P.M.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rutherford, P.M. is a researcher and author whose scientific work primarily focuses on the environmental and chemical characteristics of phosphogypsum. Throughout their career, Rutherford, P.M. has published multiple studies examining the radioactivity, elemental composition, and broader environmental impacts of this industrial byproduct. Their research establishes a comprehensive understanding of how phosphogypsum interacts with and affects surrounding ecosystems, highlighting the necessity of rigorous environmental monitoring and assessment.

A significant portion of Rutherford, P.M.'s investigations centers on the heterogeneous distribution of various substances within phosphogypsum. Specifically, their work details the spatial and compositional variability of radionuclides, barium, strontium, fluoride, and trace elements. Notably, Rutherford, P.M. co-authored a 1994 study that assessed the environmental impacts of phosphogypsum, followed by a 1996 publication that specifically analyzed the heterogeneous distribution of radionuclides, barium, and strontium within the material. Collectively, these contributions position Rutherford, P.M. as a key investigator in understanding the complex geochemical and environmental properties of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018</data>
