<node id="Limestone">
  <data key="d0">Limestone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Limestone is a naturally occurring alkaline mineral that exists primarily as a solid form of calcium carbonate. It serves as a fundamental raw material in the construction industry and building materials sector, frequently utilized due to natural weathering processes. In industrial applications, limestone functions as a supplementary cementitious material and is calcined as the primary feedstock for quicklime production through traditional carbonate calcination. It is also actively employed as a substitution component in mortar mixes blended with slag, as well as in solidification and stabilization procedures.

A significant portion of limestone's modern utility involves its integration with industrial byproducts, particularly phosphogypsum (PG) and steel slag. In composite mixtures designed for cement and mortar manufacturing, limestone interacts with PG and steel slag to modify material properties and meet production standards, provided its dosage is carefully regulated. Research indicates that limestone influences setting time variations in PG-steel slag-slag-limestone blends and constitutes exactly 10% of sodium hydroxide-modified phosphogypsum mixtures. Furthermore, the incorporation of phosphogypsum into limestone significantly alters its thermal properties, raising its decarbonation temperature from 750°C to 900°C. Conversely, the expanded industrial adoption of phosphogypsum in Portland cement production has a notable market effect by reducing the overall quarrying demand for natural limestone.&lt;SEP&gt;Limestone is a type of fine aggregate used in the experimental mortar mixes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modified Quartz">
  <data key="d0">Modified Quartz</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Modified quartz is an alternative binder additive that physically optimizes aggregate gradation and enhances mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified Quartz is a supplementary cementitious material adopted in solidification and stabilization processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791021476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silica Fume">
  <data key="d0">Silica Fume</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silica Fume is a silica-rich supplementary cementitious material and mineral additive characterized by a silicon dioxide content exceeding 97%, with commercial sources including Gongyi Baichuan Environmental Protection Engineering Co., Ltd. Primarily utilized as an admixture in concrete and cementitious systems, it is typically incorporated at dosages ranging from 0% to 9%. In self-compacting concrete, it serves as a substitute additive that promotes calcium silicate hydrate formation, thereby enhancing later-age strength development, durability, and weathering resistance. It is also widely adopted in solidification and stabilization processes, as well as in the production of ternary concrete blends combining phosphogypsum and slag to achieve tailored flexural behavior.

Within phosphogypsum-based systems and PGCM formulations, Silica Fume is frequently blended with cement and quicklime. It actively participates in hydration reactions, increasing dissolution rates and strength coefficients while generating internal gels that improve compactness, resist water erosion, and significantly boost antifreeze and frost resistance performance. These properties also contribute to improved later-stage compressive strength. However, the material exhibits complex chemical interactions: its hydration products can be susceptible to decomposition in aqueous environments, which may contribute to crack elongation. Additionally, when reacting with quicklime, Silica Fume increases quicklime consumption and can negatively impact sample length growth. Furthermore, certain particles may remain unreacted during hydration, though they still contribute to gel polymerization and overall matrix compactness. Overall, Silica Fume functions as a multifunctional admixture that substantially modifies the mechanical, durability, and hydration characteristics of advanced cementitious composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Silica fume is a fine powder additive used to improve compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Fine powder used in ternary blended concrete alongside phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Silica fume is an additive combined with calcined PG to enhance the hydraulic and mechanical properties of cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013</data>
