<node id="OPC">
  <data key="d0">OPC</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">OPC is a typical solidification and stabilization agent used in PG mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland Cement, a traditional binder whose use in PG-based mixtures faces challenges regarding GHG emissions and durability.&lt;SEP&gt;OPC (Ordinary Portland Cement) is a standard cement type used in mortars, which Plaster Of Paris substitutes in the studied mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;OPC is Ordinary Portland Cement used as a baseline material in mortar mixes, which is replaced by PG in varying percentages.&lt;SEP&gt;OPC is the primary cementitious material in the mortar mixes, partially substituted by PG.&lt;SEP&gt;OPC is a primary cement binder used in mortar mixes, serving as a baseline for strength comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-003</data>
