<node id="Sustainable Development">
  <data key="d0">Sustainable Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sustainable Development is a long-term environmental and economic goal that serves as a core framework and guiding principle for broad ecological and industrial initiatives. It functions as the overarching objective that circular economy strategies and waste crisis management systems aim to achieve. In the energy sector, this principle drives the transition away from fossil fuels by promoting the substitution of conventional energy sources with renewable alternatives such as biodiesel. By prioritizing ecological balance alongside economic growth, it establishes a foundational standard for evaluating and directing large-scale resource management efforts.

In practical applications, Sustainable Development acts as a critical requirement and primary motivation for the comprehensive utilization and commercial valorization of industrial byproducts, particularly phosphogypsum. It strongly aligns with national green economy policies, notably within China's industrial economy, where it supports targeted research, resource optimization, and the development of beneficial applications for waste materials. Through these integrated efforts, the concept bridges policy objectives, industrial innovation, and environmental stewardship to address contemporary resource and ecological challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable Development is the long-term goal of the PG recycling industry, balancing environmental, economic, and social performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A development approach aimed at balancing environmental, economic, and social needs, linked to circular economy strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable development is the ultimate goal of the system under study, promoted by considering diverse performance indicators simultaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable development is a goal advanced through the implementation of circular economy practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792407841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Sustainability">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Sustainability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental sustainability is one of the three overlapping pillars of sustainability represented in the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental sustainability is a goal enhanced through effective food loss and waste management practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental sustainability is a key perspective for evaluating the integrated system of fertilizer production and disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;A key factor emphasized for improvement in Scenarios 1 and 4, and highest in Scenario 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental sustainability is a key objective improved by adjusting resource structures in the scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792222852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
