<node id="Cement Industry">
  <data key="d0">Cement Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cement Industry is a major industrial sector that functions as the primary market for Portland cement and is actively targeted by decarbonization goals and net zero greenhouse gas emissions mitigation strategies. As a significant consumer of industrial byproducts, the sector plays a crucial role in sustainable waste management by recycling a substantial portion of generated phosphogypsum.

The industry extensively incorporates phosphogypsum into the production of various cement types, specifically utilizing phosphogypsum groups 3 and 4, which are otherwise unsuitable for plasterboard manufacturing. In these applications, phosphogypsum serves multiple functional purposes: it acts as a direct replacement for natural gypsum in setting regulator roles, helps lower clinkerization temperatures, and allows for the adjustment of Portland cement properties. Additionally, the sector operates as a key application domain for phosphogypsum-derived products, particularly those utilizing calcium carbonate, thereby integrating waste recovery with advanced material engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;The cement industry utilizes phosphogypsum as a setting regulator, though impurities can delay setting time and reduce strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792486856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concrete">
  <data key="d0">Concrete</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Concrete is a versatile, cement-based composite construction and surfacing material widely utilized in commercial and conventional building applications. Its standard formulation incorporates Portland cement and gypsum, with the latter serving to prevent flash setting. In contemporary material science research, concrete is extensively studied as a primary matrix for evaluating the effects of substituting traditional cement with phosphogypsum at varying concentrations and percentages. Investigations, including those conducted by Smadi et al., examine multiple phosphogypsum variants such as standard, untreated, thermally treated, calcined, and recycled forms, alongside alternative compounds like Plaster of Paris. The incorporation of phosphogypsum systematically modifies concrete's fundamental characteristics, with researchers closely analyzing its impact on mechanical properties, compressive strength, tensile strength, flexural strength, permeability, workability, durability, and overall structural integrity. Notably, the addition of phosphogypsum is observed to extend both the initial and final setting times of the material.

Beyond its structural applications, concrete serves as a practical surfacing alternative to asphalt and is frequently benchmarked against materials like PGEF for comparative cost and weight analyses. Furthermore, due to its established baseline properties, concrete functions as a critical reference standard in research for evaluating the radioactivity levels of phosphogypsum and assessing the performance of modified cementitious systems. It consistently appears as the primary construction material in experimental charts and graphs, where its compressive and flexural strengths are systematically measured to validate compositional adjustments and optimize engineering performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
