<node id="Calcium Aluminate Cement">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Aluminate Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium aluminate cement is a specialized cementitious material manufactured from limestone and bauxite, functioning as an alternative binder that delivers high early mechanical strength and low CO emissions. In geotechnical and mining engineering, it is extensively utilized in cemented paste backfill systems, where it supplies the necessary aluminate for ettringite formation. It is also specifically deployed in backfill applications designed for fluoride immobilization and is recognized for its role in enhancing overall soil strength.

A significant area of industrial application and academic research involves the interaction between calcium aluminate cement and phosphogypsum, which is formally listed as a key utilization pathway for this industrial byproduct within the cement sector. When phosphogypsum is incorporated into the cement matrix, it significantly influences the material's hydration kinetics, phase composition, and strength development. Experimental testing reveals that compressive strength exhibits variations depending on the specific phosphogypsum replacement levels employed. Despite these dosage-dependent fluctuations, controlled phosphogypsum addition has been consistently shown to modify hydration products and, in optimized mixtures, enhance both the compressive strength of the cementitious matrix and the mechanical stability of the surrounding soil, underscoring its utility in sustainable construction and waste valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium aluminate cement is an aluminate material used to immobilize fluorine under torrential rainfall.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium aluminate cement is a specialized binder used to create backfill mixtures capable of immobilizing fluorides under heavy rainfall.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium aluminate cement is a base material for self-leveling mortar whose properties are affected by calcium sulfate type and dosage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
