  <data key="d0">Soil Stabilization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil stabilization is a geotechnical application that utilizes phosphogypsum to improve ground properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical method where phosphogypsum is applied to improve soil properties and stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Engineering method modifying locally available soil properties to improve its performance for construction.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical process involving the addition of materials like cement or industrial byproducts to improve soil engineering properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil stabilization is a technique involving the application of phosphogypsum to improve soil properties and infiltration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
