  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Malladrite is a fluoride mineral found in phosphogypsum that contributes to fluorine leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Malladrite is a blue mineral layer found within the soil precipitation sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;Malladrite is a chemical compound identified as part of the mineral composition in the referenced studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Malladrite is a compound formed when fluoride ions combine with alkaline elements.</data>
