<node id="Y. Wang">
  <data key="d0">Y. Wang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Y. Wang is a scholarly designation associated with multiple distinct researchers whose contributions span geotechnical engineering, mineral processing, environmental materials, and biomedical nanotechnology. One research profile focuses on mining and geotechnical applications, encompassing the review of multi-field performance and numerical simulation of cemented paste backfill, alongside co-authoring investigations into the synergistic leaching of potassium and phosphorus from potassium feldspar and phosphogypsum. A separate research trajectory addresses environmental remediation through the synthesis of phosphate-embedded calcium alginate beads specifically engineered for the sorption of lead and cadmium.

Another distinct profile centers on biomedical and nanomaterial development. This body of work includes the surfactant-assisted synthesis of hydroxyapatite particles and the design of rod-shaped hydroxyapatite structures utilized as drug carriers, notably detailed in a 2014 study published in Applied Surface Science. Additionally, this research strand features the development of multifunctional melanin-like nanoparticles tailored for bone-targeted chemo-photothermal therapy. Publication records also attribute co-authorship of reference 55 in Materials Letters (2006) to this name. Given the breadth and divergence of these scientific domains, the descriptions collectively represent separate individuals sharing the same academic name, each advancing specialized methodologies within their respective fields.&lt;SEP&gt;Y. Wang is a researcher who investigated the enhanced adsorption of fluoride onto nanosized hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spain">
  <data key="d0">Spain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Spain is a country located in southwestern Europe that serves as a major global producer and manager of phosphogypsum, generating approximately 2.5 million tons annually and accounting for 10.84% of global production and reserves. The nation hosts extensive phosphogypsum deposits and stockpile sites, primarily utilizing stockpiling methods while conducting limited research into applications such as fertilizers and soil amendments. Within Spain, the Huelva region and the Tinto-Odiel estuarine system, which extends into the Gulf of Cadiz, are particularly significant as primary locations for studying phosphogypsum geochemistry, historical trace metal toxicity, and severe radionuclide contamination. Scientific and environmental assessments of Spanish phosphogypsum have systematically analyzed its chemical composition, including mean weight percentages of various chemical oxides with specific datasets indicating approximately 46 percent, alongside evaluations of impurities and radiological profiles. Spain is notably recognized in environmental scientific literature for phosphogypsum that exhibits significantly higher radionuclide levels compared to global averages, making it a focal point for radioecological studies and sample analysis.

The country also contains a large Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material waste disposal site that has been evaluated for preliminary restoration efforts, with radioecological studies conducted on both estuarine systems and these waste repositories. Research within the region indicates that geogenic weathering is the dominant factor influencing trace pollutant distribution. Additionally, recycled gypsum has been assessed within Spain as a potential replacement for natural gypsum in cement production. As the base location for numerous associated research institutions and authors, Spain is frequently cited in data tables and scientific publications, contributing significantly to the global body of phosphogypsum research and serving as a critical geographic reference for understanding the material's chemical, radiological, and environmental characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-004</data>
