<node id="X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy is a technique used to determine potential binding mechanisms of F and P in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A method characterized by high sensitivity, ultra-trace detection limits, and stability, used to analyze phosphogypsum chemical composition.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used to determine the chemical state of elements on a material's surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-023</data>
