  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphate Ore">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Ore</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate ore is a natural geological raw material and mineral resource that serves as a foundational industrial input for the production of phosphoric acid. It is processed through multiple industrial pathways, including the wet process and the kiln process, where it is decomposed using strong mineral acids—most commonly sulfuric acid—or subjected to high-temperature heating in electric furnaces. In specific processing variations, the ore may also be dissolved in phosphoric acid or treated with treated mother liquid derived from rare earth recovery. The extraction and processing of phosphate ore are formally categorized in industrial statistics charts and are governed by waste management classifications due to the substantial generation of phosphogypsum as a processing byproduct.

The inherent geological and chemical characteristics of phosphate ore, including its mineralogical makeup, natural compositional variations, and crystal structure substitutions, fundamentally dictate the properties of the resulting phosphogypsum. Specifically, the ore's composition, combined with processing variables such as sulfuric acid concentration, determines the byproduct's color, chemical profile, and overall mineralogical traits. Notably, phosphate ore acts as the primary natural geological source of fluorine within the phosphogypsum waste stream. Consequently, the specific geological and compositional attributes of phosphate ore directly shape both industrial handling procedures and the environmental management strategies required for its processing byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate Ore is the raw material whose composition and quality strongly influence the characteristics of resulting Phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792487352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guizhou">
  <data key="d0">Guizhou</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Guizhou is a province in China recognized for its significant geological and industrial contributions, particularly in mineral processing and resource management. The region is notably endowed with deposits of refractory collophanite, which are extensively utilized in mineral processing research and associated flotation applications. In addition to its mineral wealth, Guizhou plays a pivotal role in the national phosphogypsum sector, contributing substantially to China's total phosphogypsum production. To address the environmental and industrial implications of this output, the provincial government has actively implemented specific policies and official opinions aimed at promoting the comprehensive utilization of phosphogypsum.

These targeted efforts have yielded remarkable results, with Guizhou achieving a comprehensive utilization rate of 99.22% for phosphogypsum. Consequently, the province has become a focal point for academic and industrial research, frequently featured in studies analyzing the phosphogypsum recycling industry and profiling prominent recycling companies. Furthermore, Guizhou is consistently represented in aggregate data distributions regarding phosphogypsum usage, underscoring its status as a key region for monitoring and advancing sustainable mineral processing and waste recycling practices in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Guizhou is the province containing Guiyang and Guizhou University.&lt;SEP&gt;Guizhou is a Chinese province where PG samples were collected and chemically analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;Guizhou is a key province targeted for large-scale phosphogypsum projects and demonstration projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Guizhou is a Chinese province where CPGB technology has been adopted by large-scale mines.&lt;SEP&gt;Guizhou is a Chinese province with prevalent PG generation that enforces strict recycling policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011</data>
