<node id="Smadi et al.">
  <data key="d0">Smadi et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Smadi et al. conducted research on the effects of varying calcination temperatures on PG-CPB mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Smadi et al. calcined phosphogypsum at temperatures ranging from 170 to 950 degrees Celsius for 3 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Smadi et al. investigated calcination temperatures ranging from 170 to 950 C for phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Smadi et al. documented progressive strength declines in mortars when cement is fully replaced with phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Smadi et al. are researchers who linked soundness expansion to the formation of ettringite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008</data>
