<node id="Pyrophosphate">
  <data key="d0">Pyrophosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyrophosphate is a water-insoluble and harmless substance formed from soluble phosphate during calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrophosphate is a calcium orthophosphate family member with a calcium-to-phosphorus ratio of 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrophosphate is an inert compound formed during the high-temperature calcination of phosphogypsum for polymer applications.</data>
