<node id="Fossil Fuels">
  <data key="d0">Fossil Fuels</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fossil Fuels are traditional, natural energy sources primarily composed of gas and diesel, representing rapidly depleting energy reservoirs that are increasingly contrasted with sustainable alternatives like hydrogen and biodiesel, which aim to substitute them. In industrial and analytical contexts, these resources are utilized for applications such as heating in calcination processes. They are systematically tracked for consumption and potential savings across various scenarios and are formally categorized as a resource category measured alongside minerals in standardized assessment methods.

Environmentally, Fossil Fuels are the dominant source category responsible for the majority of carbon emissions and elevated greenhouse gas outputs in analyzed scenarios. Their significant environmental impact is frequently highlighted in data visualizations, where they are explicitly listed as an environmental impact category and associated with the color olive green in chart legends.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
