<node id="Unconfined Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d0">Unconfined Compressive Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Unconfined Compressive Strength is a fundamental mechanical and physical property metric, typically measured in megapascals (MPa), that quantifies the maximum axial stress a material can withstand under compression without lateral confinement. It is primarily determined through standardized laboratory test methods that evaluate the load-bearing capacity and structural integrity of various materials. As a quantitative indicator, it serves as a critical parameter for assessing the mechanical performance, stabilization effectiveness, and strength evolution of both untreated and treated substances.

In geotechnical and construction applications, Unconfined Compressive Strength is extensively utilized to evaluate the stabilization and load-bearing capacity of untreated and treated soils, as well as stabilized soil mixes. The property is highly sensitive to material composition and curing conditions, with its values directly reflecting the effectiveness of soil stabilization techniques. Furthermore, it is applied to assess the mechanical performance of specialized filling bodies, such as the CPGFM filling body, where it tracks strength development during the curing process.

The magnitude of Unconfined Compressive Strength is significantly influenced by the incorporation of various additives and chemical components. The property increases with higher percentages of fly ash, phosphogypsum, or modified quartz, and it varies predictably with calcium hydroxide content. Consequently, Unconfined Compressive Strength functions as a versatile and essential metric for optimizing material formulations, monitoring curing progress, and ensuring the structural reliability of engineered soils and industrial byproduct-based construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-008</data>
