<node id="Fig. 8">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 8 functions as a generic figure label utilized across numerous independent scientific publications rather than representing a single unified subject. Its content is entirely context-dependent, varying significantly across research domains such as mineral processing, biomaterials, mechanical engineering, and environmental modeling. In studies focused on phosphogypsum processing and characterization, Fig. 8 depicts a three-step schematic for rare earth element extraction from recycled phosphogypsum, shows undissolved particles remaining after gypsum matrix dissolution with dilute hydrochloric acid, outlines the Boren-Haber reaction cycle for catalytic decomposition, illustrates the phosphogypsum conversion procedure using a chloride solution, and presents infrared spectra comparing the material before and after thermal treatment.

Within biomaterials and hydroxyapatite research, the figure displays scanning electron microscopy micrographs revealing morphological changes in hydroxyapatite materials with varying surfactant concentrations, shows rod-like crystals indicative of preferential hydroxyapatite crystalline growth, and presents SSM plots for synthesized hydroxyapatite nanoparticles. It also illustrates composite bone cement micrographs following immersion in simulated body fluid solution, schematically represents the photocatalytic mechanism of titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite under simulated solar irradiation, and details the release profiles of bovine serum albumin and lysozyme from hydroxyapatite samples alongside corresponding Higuchi plots.

In mechanical testing and materials engineering contexts, Fig. 8 documents compressive strength observations, diametric compression strength and elastic modulus measurements following various curing periods, and tracks length variations in PGCM specimens across different curing ages. Additionally, in environmental and systems analysis, the label is used to present a visual diagram of emergy flow components for Scenario 3. Collectively, these descriptions confirm that Fig. 8 serves as a standardized reference identifier tailored to specific experimental processes, material characterizations, kinetic analyses, and performance evaluations across diverse scientific literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 is a figure exhibiting the flexural strength of modified phosphogypsum specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 is a graphical representation presenting the 2-hour bending strength results of MPG samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A graphical illustration showing the adsorption isotherms of fluoride at various temperatures obtained via non-linear regression.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 is a figure displaying representative scanning electron microscopy images of HA particles at increasing magnifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 illustrates the effect of purified PG replacement on the flexural strength of mortars with NS after moist curing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503863</data>
