<node id="Density">
  <data key="d0">Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Density is a fundamental physical property representing mass per unit volume, typically quantified in grams per cubic centimeter (g/cm³). As a core metric in material science, quality control, and engineering, it is routinely measured during material analysis using instruments such as a helium pycnometer. The specific value of density varies significantly across different material systems and is heavily influenced by compositional ratios, synthesis parameters, and processing conditions.

In the context of nanopowders and nano-hydroxyapatite, density serves as a critical physical characteristic that correlates directly with particle diameter. Synthesized nanopowder samples typically exhibit densities ranging from 2.86 to 3.04 g/cm³, with values modulated by synthesis time and pressure. When applied to phosphogypsum, density acts as a defining trait that dictates transportation logistics and application methodologies. The intrinsic density of phosphogypsum increases when subjected to higher calcination temperatures. Furthermore, when phosphogypsum is incorporated into various matrices, its impact on density is application-dependent: it generally reduces the overall density of cement paste and phosphogypsum-polymer composites, yet increases the density of bricks at specific substitution rates.

Beyond construction materials, density is evaluated across diverse specialized fields. In biomedical applications like composite bone cement, density exhibits a slight decrease as sodium chloride concentration rises, while simultaneously maintaining a linear relationship with compressive strength, making it a reliable indicator of mechanical performance. Conversely, in other porous or composite systems, a decline in density often correlates with reduced compressive strength and increased water absorption. Additionally, density functions as a standard quality analysis parameter in biodiesel production, serving as a key metric for ensuring fuel specification and batch consistency. Collectively, these varied manifestations underscore density's versatility as a foundational analytical parameter across engineering, materials science, and industrial quality assurance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011</data>
