<node id="Yangtze River">
  <data key="d0">Yangtze River</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yangtze River is a major waterway in China that serves as a critical geographic and economic hub, particularly in relation to phosphogypsum management and environmental regulation. It provides essential water transportation advantages and waterway connectivity, offering significant market access for Hubei’s phosphogypsum recycling industry. The river’s ecosystem faces notable environmental challenges, primarily due to total phosphorus pollution originating from phosphogypsum. Consequently, numerous phosphogypsum tailings ponds are situated near the Yangtze River and its tributaries, making the region a primary focus for regulatory oversight and remedial actions.

In response to these ecological pressures, the Yangtze River was designated as a priority for protection and restoration under a national action plan implemented in December 2018. Sustainable phosphogypsum recycling practices are anticipated to play a key role in improving the river’s environmental conditions over time. The river basin also encompasses significant regional infrastructure, including the nearby Hongfeng Reservoir. Through integrated regulatory measures and industry adaptation, the Yangtze River remains central to balancing industrial activity with long-term ecological preservation in China.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791610304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
