<node id="Aqueous Phase">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Aqueous Phase is a water-based liquid medium that serves as a fundamental component across materials science, geochemistry, and chemical processing applications. Within porous materials and structural frameworks, it functions as the liquid that fills internal pores and constitutes the water channels, often depicted in visualizations as a light blue area representing these pathways. Chemically, it acts as a dynamic solvent that hosts dissolved species and facilitates ion transport. It actively receives dissolved ions released from the dissolution of other phases under lower pH conditions, maintaining a reactive environment for various chemical interactions.

In reaction and extraction systems, the Aqueous Phase operates as the primary liquid component where specific chemical processes occur. It serves as the reaction mixture for phenomena such as ammonium sulfate formation and the measurement of radium distribution coefficients against gypsum. Furthermore, it is integral to solvent extraction and stripping processes, where it is combined with an organic phase or organic ionic liquid, typically in a 2:1 ratio. During these operations, the Aqueous Phase carries dissolved metal ions, including lanthanum (La), cerium (Ce), and neodymium (Nd), and ultimately contains the stripped rare earth elements that have been successfully separated from the organic phase. Collectively, these roles define the Aqueous Phase as a versatile, polar liquid medium essential for ion distribution, chemical reactions, and phase separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cementitious Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Cementitious Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cementitious matrix is a solid phase material that forms the structural backbone of the porous medium.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cementitious Matrix immobilizes heavy metal ions, preventing their detection in leachates.&lt;SEP&gt;A grey structural area in the diagram representing the solid base of the material.&lt;SEP&gt;The grey structural matrix in which micro and macro cracks form to facilitate ion migration.</data>
