<node id="Fertilizer Industry">
  <data key="d0">Fertilizer Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The fertilizer industry is the commercial sector responsible for producing phosphoric acid and fertilizers.&lt;SEP&gt;The fertilizer industry is the industrial sector responsible for processing phosphate rock and generating phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The fertilizer industry is an application domain for products formed from PG, utilizing ammonium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fertilizer Industry is a key stakeholder affected by Phosphogypsum stacks and alternative management methods.&lt;SEP&gt;The fertilizer industry is the industrial sector that produces large quantities of phosphogypsum as a by-product.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fertilizer Industry is the industrial source of phosphogypsum, a co-product utilized in the novel synthesis approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-013</data>
