</node>
<node id="Waste Management">
  <data key="d0">Waste Management</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Waste management addresses the challenge of handling and repurposing phosphogypsum byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste management encompasses the strategies and technologies for handling and utilizing Phosphogypsum effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;A process applied to PCR, PBG, and PSC where Wastewater and Solid waste are listed as 100% reused.&lt;SEP&gt;An academic journal that published research on leaching behavior and pollutant release from phosphogypsum stockpiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal publishing proposals for evaluating the viability of gypsum waste in ceramic block production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792456417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydration Products">
  <data key="d0">Hydration Products</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration Products are chemical and cementitious compounds generated during the curing and hydration reactions of materials, particularly those involving cement and silica fume. These solid compounds fundamentally alter the internal structure of composite systems such as PGCM by bonding aggregates, filling internal pores, and increasing the overall compactness and volume of the matrix. This structural densification directly enhances the consolidation, mechanical strength, and water-resistant properties of the resulting material.

Chemically, Hydration Products serve as active interfaces for ion management. Their solid surfaces adsorb ions, form stable chemical bonds with harmful substances, and facilitate ion exchange processes, which collectively determine the leaching behavior of toxic elements. The progressive evolution of these compounds under erosion conditions further elucidates the influence mechanisms of various incorporated admixtures. In schematic diagrams of material hydration, these products are conventionally represented as blue diamonds containing the letter 'F', denoting their formation and structural significance during the reaction phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydration products are chemical compounds formed during curing that strengthen binder matrices and improve mechanical behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydration products are the chemical compounds formed when cement and phosphogypsum react with water.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydration products are the chemical compounds formed during the hydration process of cement, such as ettringite and calcium-silicate hydrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503863</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
