<node id="pH Value">
  <data key="d0">pH Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pH Value is a fundamental chemical parameter used to quantify the acidity or alkalinity of various substances and environments. In industrial and environmental applications, it serves as a critical metric for phosphogypsum (PG) and its processed variants, such as MPG. During natural weathering, PG typically exhibits a pH ranging from strongly acidic (below 3) to neutral (approximately 6). The pH of phosphogypsum samples is routinely measured during washing processes and is observed to increase as calcination temperatures rise. Following high-efficiency calcination, MPG generally stabilizes at a weakly acidic or alkaline state. Beyond solid materials, pH Value is also employed as a measured feature to indicate the acidity or alkalinity of water across different geographical regions.

In chemical and metallurgical contexts, pH Value functions as a dynamic indicator of reaction conditions and material stability. It reflects the acidity of the reaction environment and can decrease if phosphoric acid is introduced too rapidly. The parameter is also critical for maintaining the stability of calcium fluoride, as stability significantly decreases when pH levels exceed 10. Furthermore, in slag chemistry, pH Value is recognized as a distinct chemical property influenced by iron oxide content and can be determined using specific calculation equations. Collectively, these applications demonstrate that pH Value is a versatile analytical tool essential for monitoring environmental quality, optimizing industrial processing, and ensuring chemical stability across diverse material systems.&lt;SEP&gt;pH value is a measure of acidity for phosphogypsum, initially around 1 and increasing to 2.5-6 over time.&lt;SEP&gt;pH value is a chemical property of PG that increases with calcination temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
