<node id="Carbon Capture">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Capture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon capture refers to the process of capturing atmospheric carbon dioxide, which phosphogypsum-based backfill can facilitate.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon capture is an environmental application of phosphogypsum for capturing carbon emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon Capture is an application utilizing calcium sulfide, a decomposition product of PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon capture is a high-value technology for phosphogypsum that has seen research progress but has not yet reached industrial-scale production.</data>
