<node id="Data Table">
  <data key="d0">Data Table</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Data Table is a structured layout utilized across multiple scientific and analytical domains to organize and present quantitative information. In one specific application, it details the concentration of various rare earth element oxides, quantified in weight percentage. This version lists the rare earth elements in ascending order of atomic number and analyzes their distribution across different chemical components. A closely related instance functions as a structured summary that quantifies the weight percentage of each detected element, while another layout presents both quantitative weight and atomic percentages for the same detected elements.

Beyond elemental composition, the Data Table is employed to present comparative contaminant levels alongside established guidelines from multiple regulatory bodies. In spectroscopic and thermodynamic contexts, it organizes spectral peak positions and their corresponding vibrational attributions to facilitate comparative analysis. It also presents chemical species alongside their standard enthalpies of formation for both reactants and products. Furthermore, the Data Table serves as a structured compilation of experimental results, specifically detailing solubility measurements conducted under various conditions. Together, these distinct instances highlight the Data Table's adaptability as a foundational tool for structuring, quantifying, and comparing diverse scientific and regulatory datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured table presenting experimental data on phosphogypsum properties, organized into four columns and six rows.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured layout presenting the weight percentages of chemical oxides and elements in phosphogypsum across two sections.&lt;SEP&gt;The Data Table is a structured presentation of volume percentages across regions for various reaction and milling times.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
