  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Japan">
  <data key="d0">Japan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Japan is a sovereign nation and geographic region recognized for its strategic resource management, technological innovations, and significant role in international trade and policy. In the field of scientific instrumentation, Japan is the country of origin for the Rigaku X-ray diffractometer and the D/max-3BPEX-P96 powder X-ray diffractometer, and it is home to the company Jeol. Driven by inherent supply risks, the nation has officially classified rare earth elements as strategic resources.

In industrial chemistry and resource utilization, Japan pioneered research on phosphogypsum in the 1970s. Due to naturally gypsum-devoid volcanic soil and a consequent lack of domestic gypsum resources, the country economically recovers approximately three million tons of phosphogypsum annually. Japan currently achieves a 100 percent comprehensive utilization rate for this byproduct and stands as the only nation where phosphogypsum recovery for plaster manufacturing is profitable. The country primarily utilizes the material to produce gypsum construction products that offset domestic shortages, while the hemihydrate process for phosphoric acid production remains relatively widespread within its chemical manufacturing sector.

Geographically situated in North Asia, Japan serves as a primary destination for Australian agricultural exports. Furthermore, the nation has been featured in international policy assessments, notably the 2019 comparative policy evaluation of new energy vehicle development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792364185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Union">
  <data key="d0">European Union</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Union is a political and economic union that operates as a pivotal regional entity in addressing critical resource and material management challenges. It has officially classified rare earth elements as strategic materials due to significant supply risks. Furthermore, the Union actively addresses the gypsum supply gap by promoting the industrial utilization of phosphogypsum, a byproduct that requires careful handling and regulatory oversight.

To ensure environmental and public safety, the European Union has established comprehensive regulations and legislation governing phosphogypsum and related waste materials. These frameworks mandate specific hazard categorization standards for phosphogypsum and strictly regulate hazardous substances contained within it, such as radium-226. The Union also sets precise regulatory standards and activity concentration limits for radionuclides in both phosphogypsum applications and general waste materials, ensuring that industrial byproducts are managed safely.

In addition to its regulatory and strategic roles, the European Union functions as a primary funding body that supports scientific research programs focused on these material challenges. By financing studies related to phosphogypsum utilization and radionuclide management, the Union facilitates the development of sustainable practices for managing industrial waste and mitigating resource supply risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union is an international destination for Australian food and agricultural exports.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union is a destination region for Australian food and agricultural exports.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union discontinued the use of phosphogypsum in building materials in 1992.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792487011</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
