  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">H2SO4 (sulfuric acid) is a chemical leachant used in the acid leaching process to dissolve the gypsum matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;H2SO4 is a chemical compound produced using SO3 derived from PG thermal decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid, a chemical compound mentioned in the introductory equation.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound with a density of 1.84 g/cm³ and a concentration range of 95% to 98%.</data>
