<node id="Barium">
  <data key="d0">Barium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Barium is an alkaline earth chemical element that frequently occurs as a trace component or patchy impurity within various geological and industrial materials, exhibiting a notably heterogeneous distribution. It is particularly prominent in phosphogypsum by-products, where it is consistently measured at approximately 0.54 wt% in dried samples across multiple studies, including those of South African deposits, though it is depleted in phosphorite deposits relative to typical crustal abundances. Chemically, barium demonstrates poor solubility and primarily precipitates as barium sulfate within the phosphogypsum crystal lattice. This insoluble sulfate phase co-precipitates or co-crystallizes with radium, including the radioisotope Ra-226, to form sulfate compounds and solid solutions. This behavior is highly significant in uranium mining environments, where it contributes to the formation of (Ba, Ra) sulfate sludges, and in waste management systems, where it critically influences radium nucleation, solubility, and overall mobility.

In experimental and analytical contexts, barium (Ba2+) is routinely introduced as an ion in synthetic solutions for extraction experiments, where its extraction efficiency has been observed to be higher than that of radium. When subjected to leaching processes, barium acts as a major element with low mobility, showing a decreasing release rate over time and a slight decrease in concentration in leached samples. Its leaching concentrations typically remain below 10 µg/L. Spectroscopic analysis can detect barium via characteristic peaks at approximately 230 and 232 nm. Due to its widespread presence and low removal rate, barium is routinely analyzed alongside radionuclides and strontium in phosphogypsum leachates and monitored during groundwater assessments.

Given its environmental distribution and potential health implications, barium is subject to regulatory oversight. While chemically classified as an alkaline earth element, it is frequently monitored in industrial and environmental frameworks alongside heavy metals, with its concentration in phosphogypsum solutions tracked against established limits. Regulatory standards include a World Health Organization guideline value of 0.1 mg/L for drinking water quality, reflecting the need to manage its mobility and exposure in both natural and engineered systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Barium is a trace metal element measured in the provided data table with concentrations in ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Barium is an element found in phosphogypsum, typically located in the residual phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Barium is an element whose heterogeneous distribution in phosphogypsum by-product is analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;A water-soluble metal released from phosphogypsum into the estuary, estimated at 6509 tons.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element found in phosphogypsum by-products, contributing to its environmental composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Barium is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured across the sampled locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
