</node>
<node id="Fig. 10">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 10 is a figure label that appears across multiple independent studies, each utilizing it to represent distinct experimental data. In the context of phosphogypsum (PG) and modified phosphogypsum (MPG), Fig. 10 illustrates the leaching efficiency of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum across multiple cycles. It also depicts the existence patterns of fluorine (F) and phosphorus (P) elements within PG at different temperatures during the CLG process. Additionally, this figure presents the softening coefficient of modified phosphogypsum across varying temperatures, alongside corresponding softening coefficient test results for MPG samples. In related cementitious applications, Fig. 10 is used to visualize the damage mechanism of PGCM following freeze-thaw cycle experiments.

In studies involving hydroxyapatite (HAp), Fig. 10 serves a different purpose. It provides a graphical representation of the optical band gap values for five distinct HAp sample variations. Complementing this data, the figure also displays scanning electron microscopy (SEM) images of dried hydroxyapatite and calcined samples subjected to various temperatures.

Finally, in environmental or adsorption research contexts, Fig. 10 illustrates the change in solution pH during the fluoride adsorption process. Collectively, these descriptions indicate that the label Fig. 10 is not unique to a single dataset but is independently assigned to diverse figures across different scientific publications, each detailing specific material properties, chemical behaviors, or physical mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 10 demonstrates the effect of replacing OPC with calcined washed and unwashed PG on compressive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
