<node id="XRD Pattern">
  <data key="d0">XRD Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The XRD Pattern is a specialized analytical data representation and diffraction pattern utilized to characterize the structural and compositional properties of various materials. Visually, it is typically presented as a two-dimensional or stacked line graph that plots diffraction intensity or signal intensity against the diffraction angle. This graphical format serves as a fundamental tool for identifying crystalline structures, determining crystallite size, and measuring lattice spacing within analyzed samples.

In practical applications, the XRD Pattern is employed to analyze the phase structure and crystalline phase composition of specific materials, including slag and initial Phosphogypsum samples. Furthermore, it provides critical analytical data that can confirm the formation of particular compounds under specific thermal conditions, such as verifying the synthesis of calcium silicate at 1200 °C. By integrating these analytical capabilities, the XRD Pattern functions as a comprehensive diagnostic resource for material science and chemical analysis across multiple sample types.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific chart displaying sharp peaks at various angles, indicating a crystalline structure and phase composition.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement result showing that hydroxyapatite remains the main phase composition after fluoride adsorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
