<node id="Neutralization">
  <data key="d0">Neutralization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Neutralization is a pretreatment technique developed for the purification of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a chemical treatment process used to safely handle PG modifiers and byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a laboratory-scale purification method. Neutralization removes impurities from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a laboratory-scale purification technology for phosphogypsum that requires further research for industrial scalability.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a pre-treatment process applied to electroplating wastewater to adjust pH levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a chemical treatment method used to adjust the composition of phosphogypsum for specific end uses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-006</data>
