<node id="Ball Milling">
  <data key="d0">Ball Milling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ball milling is a mechanical grinding and processing technique primarily utilized to reduce particle size, control material fineness, and refine particle size distribution. By breaking apart clumps and reducing particulate aggregation, the process effectively increases pore volume and specific surface area, thereby enhancing the overall physical and chemical characteristics of the target materials. This technique can be implemented in both dry and wet configurations, and it is applied under either ex situ or in situ conditions depending on the specific processing requirements.

In industrial and materials science applications, ball milling serves as a critical pretreatment and modification method for phosphogypsum and phosphorous building gypsum. It is employed to purify these materials, grind them into fine powders, and improve their compatibility and performance when integrated into polymer-based composites. Additionally, the technique is utilized in analytical and research contexts involving hydroxyapatite samples, where it is systematically evaluated under both ex situ and in situ conditions to assess its impact on material structure and properties, often serving as a controlled variable in experimental designs. Overall, ball milling functions as a versatile mechanical processing tool that optimizes powder characteristics for diverse material products and scientific analyses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006</data>
