<node id="NaCl">
  <data key="d0">NaCl</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride (NaCl) is a versatile chemical compound utilized across diverse scientific, industrial, and experimental applications. In biomaterials science, it serves as a critical modifier and porogen within composite bone cements, where its concentration precisely regulates phase composition, setting duration, and physical characteristics. By promoting a highly porous microstructure, NaCl enhances surface properties, grain growth, mechanical performance, and biological integration of the cement. In interface and electrochemical studies, NaCl forms the solution interface for hydroxyapatite samples, specifically HAP1 and HAP2, enabling the measurement of electrochemical properties and zeta potential. It is also employed in general experimental setups, including testing reactions with calcium carbonate and preparing standard solutions or reagents.

Beyond materials science, NaCl plays a fundamental role in biological and chemical systems. It acts as a salinity component and control solution in culture media to maintain optimal osmotic and ionic conditions for biological assays. In aqueous environments, NaCl adjusts solution ionic strength and influences metal ion interactions, demonstrating minimal impact on lead (Pb(II)) removal while exhibiting slight competitive behavior for copper (Cu(II)) and zinc (Zn(II)) ions at elevated concentrations. Industrially, NaCl is utilized in dietary solutions designed to treat phosphogypsum for the production of rare earths concentrate. Collectively, these applications underscore NaCl’s multifaceted utility as a structural regulator, electrochemical medium, biological buffer, and processing agent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792261913</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAP">
  <data key="d0">HAP</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite (HAP) is a versatile calcium phosphate compound and mineral that serves as a foundational material across biomedical, environmental, and composite applications. Chemically, it typically crystallizes in a hexagonal structure, though its physical state can vary from nanocrystalline powder to amorphous calcium phosphate depending on synthesis conditions. The material is predominantly prepared through hydrothermal methods that enable controlled nucleation and self-assembly, with phosphogypsum (PG) waste frequently utilized as a sustainable calcium source. Depending on the specific preparation parameters, HAP exhibits diverse morphologies, including agglomerates, hierarchical microparticles, hierarchical microspheres, and nanoparticles. Its structural integrity and crystalline nature are rigorously validated using X-ray diffraction and various spectroscopic techniques.

In biomedical contexts, HAP functions as a critical biomaterial integrated into composite bone cements, where it actively reinforces the structural matrix. It also serves as a foundational substrate for hydrothermal deposition and surface functionalization, including the attachment of calcium sulfide crystals and AL molecules. Beyond healthcare, HAP is extensively employed as an adsorbent for capturing heavy metal ions from aqueous solutions. It is commonly utilized as an undoped baseline material to benchmark the performance of advanced composites, such as the 20HPA-HAP composite. Furthermore, HAP nanoparticles are homogeneously grown onto biochar sheets to create HAP-BC composites, which demonstrate significantly enhanced heavy metal adsorption capabilities compared to standalone hydroxyapatite. Collectively, these attributes establish HAP as a multifunctional, hydrothermally synthesized calcium phosphate material with well-documented structural, biomedical, and environmental utility.&lt;SEP&gt;An abbreviation for hydroxyapatite, the primary product in the chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a powder material analyzed for its structural and chemical properties before and after heat treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a calcium phosphate compound and a major component of bone mineral.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a calcium phosphate phase identified in the experimental samples.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a chemical compound referenced in the spectroscopic data table with associated numerical peak values.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a calcium phosphate material synthesized and analyzed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-004</data>
