<node id="Sodium Chloride (NaCl)">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride (NaCl)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical compound added to the composite bone cement to modify its physical and functional properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference compound used in the XRD pattern analysis, identified by ICDD No. 01-078-0751.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is used to adjust the ionic strength of the solution and to introduce sodium ions for competitive adsorption studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A chloride salt whose solution properties and optimal concentration significantly impact phosphogypsum solubility.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Chloride is a chemical compound prepared to create a standard solution in Section 5.62.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-007</data>
