<node id="Calcium Sulfide (CaS)">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfide (CaS)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A base material component of the composite bone cement.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical phase identified by black circles in the diffraction graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfide is a chemical compound produced by the carbon reduction of calcium sulfate and subsequently oxidized by unreacted calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound produced during the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;An intermediate product formed during phosphogypsum decomposition, with production decreasing as coal size increases.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound identified as Peak 3 in the chart.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792363048</data>
