<node id="EDS">
  <data key="d0">EDS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">EDS, formally known as Energy Dispersive X-ray Spectroscopy (and occasionally referenced as Electron Dispersive Spectroscopy), is an analytical technique and system utilized for chemical microanalysis, imaging, and elemental analysis. Typically integrated as an attachment to Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM), the method enables the precise determination of elemental composition at specific microscopic spots. Beyond basic identification, EDS facilitates the detailed examination of element distribution and migration patterns within materials, making it a fundamental tool for microscale chemical characterization.

In practical applications, EDS is extensively employed to verify the successful synthesis and structural integration of various compounds. Researchers utilize the technique to confirm the production of hydroxyapatite (HAP), calcium sulfide (CaS), and sodium chloride (NaCl), as well as to validate the successful incorporation of HPA into HAP matrices. Furthermore, EDS is applied to analyze the elemental composition of specialized materials such as PBSLM6. By providing accurate compositional data at the microscopic level, EDS remains a critical instrument for material verification and chemical structure analysis across scientific disciplines.&lt;SEP&gt;EDS is an analytical method used to examine PG, though it does not detect the presence of phosphorus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792405227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEM">
  <data key="d0">SEM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) is a high-resolution microscopic imaging and analytical technique that operates by scanning a focused electron beam across a sample's surface. This methodology enables the detailed visualization and characterization of physical structures, morphologies, and microstructural features across diverse scientific and industrial domains. By revealing surface topography, particle architecture, distribution, and arrangement, alongside internal characteristics such as fracture surfaces, grain size, porosity, and internal hydration products, SEM serves as a fundamental and indispensable tool for microscopic characterization. It provides critical insights into structural evolution and morphological transformations, making it highly effective for validating the average nanocrystal size and morphology of synthesized products, as well as for analyzing and observing particle morphology and distribution.

In practical applications, SEM is extensively utilized to image the morphology, agglomeration, and porous structure of dried and calcined hydroxyapatite samples. The technique characterizes synthetic hydroxyapatite as randomly distributed platelets and bone ash as homogenous nanoparticles, while also assessing the architecture, dimensions, and aspect ratios of hydroxyapatite nanoparticles, including peeled and rod-shaped structures. Researchers employ SEM to monitor morphological changes under varying experimental conditions, such as stirring, and to examine the surface morphology of hydroxyapatite and HPA-HAP composites. Beyond biomaterials, the technique studies the microstructures and element distribution of polished slag sections, investigates the microstructure of samples like PGI-1.4 reduced at 1250 °C, evaluates the physical structure of PG and Ni/PG carriers, and analyzes internal hydration products within PGCM. Additionally, SEM is routinely applied to examine the microstructures of ceramic bodies, cementing its role as a vital analytical method for understanding material properties at the microscale.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM is an imaging technique used to observe the surface morphology of PBSLM6.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM is an analytical technique used alongside XRD to examine decomposition products.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning electron microscopy is used to characterize particle morphology, aggregation, and size distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM is a characterization technique used to visually compare samples prepared with In Situ Milling against Ex Situ Milling.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscopy is an analytical technique used alongside XRD and dry particle sizing to characterize hydroxyapatite samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
