<node id="Bending Strength">
  <data key="d0">Bending Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical property investigated using a universal testing machine and ASTM guidelines to assess fracture resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Bending Strength is a mechanical property that decreases alongside compressive strength with higher NaCl content.&lt;SEP&gt;Bending strength ($\sigma_f$) is a mechanical property measured in MPa, exhibiting an exponential relationship with porosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Bending strength is a mechanical property that reaches its maximum value when phosphogypsum content is 75%.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property of MPG evaluated at 2 hours, with results presented in graphical form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastic Modulus">
  <data key="d0">Elastic Modulus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Elastic Modulus is a fundamental mechanical property that quantifies a material's stiffness. It is typically expressed in megapascals (MPa) and can be determined through empirical equations or direct mechanical testing. In engineering and materials science, particularly concerning road construction and stabilized mixes, this parameter is critical for evaluating performance and conditioning pavement use. The testing process often involves measuring the property at specific curing intervals, such as 7, 90, and 360 days, to track stiffness development over time.

The value of the Elastic Modulus, frequently denoted as the E value, is significantly influenced by material composition and physical characteristics. It exhibits an exponential relationship with grain size and tends to decrease as the concentration of sodium chloride (NaCl) additives increases. In specific applications like the P12 Mix, the addition of CM significantly enhances stiffness, with measurements reaching 2864 MPa at just 7 days of curing. Overall, Elastic Modulus serves as a vital metric for assessing how material formulations and curing conditions affect structural rigidity and long-term durability in civil engineering contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
