<node id="Brushite">
  <data key="d0">Brushite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brushite, chemically identified as dicalcium phosphate dihydrate, calcium hydrogen phosphate dihydrate, or calcium hydrogen orthophosphate dihydrate, is a monoclinic calcium phosphate mineral whose crystal structure closely resembles that of gypsum. It frequently occurs as a secondary crystalline or mixed phase within various cementitious systems, particularly forming as a by-product during the acidic attack of phosphogypsum or in composite bone cements and pastes incorporating waste river sludge and hemihydrate phosphogypsum. The mineral is also found in natural settings, such as bat guano deposits in Romanian caves, and can appear as a product following the drying phase of specific synthesis processes.

Analytically, brushite is routinely identified and characterized using X-ray diffraction, neutron diffraction, and infrared spectroscopy, which reveals distinct characteristic absorption bands. Functionally, it serves as a critical precursor in calcium phosphate phase transformations, undergoing hydrolysis to produce hydroxyapatite, and is utilized to optimize fluoride adsorption in aqueous solutions. Thermally, brushite exhibits a defined stability limit beginning around 700 °C, but undergoes dehydration at approximately 150 °C to transform into monetite, with some observations noting a transitional mixture of brushite and monetite during this process. These combined chemical, structural, and thermal properties establish brushite as a significant indicator phase in the analysis of advanced cement composites, phosphogypsum-based materials, and calcium phosphate systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024</data>
