<node id="Weight Loss">
  <data key="d0">Weight Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measured property indicating the percentage of cement paste lost after immersion in Ringer's solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight Loss is the percentage reduction in mass during PG decomposition, used to measure reaction progress.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured property of bricks subjected to temperature cycles, indicating material stability.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured parameter in thermogravimetric analysis representing the evaporation of surface and structural water.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss is the measured reduction in sample mass from TGA, used as a variable in calculating product purity.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss is a durability metric measured after freeze/thaw cycles, which is reduced by adding polypropene fibers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
