<node id="Particle Size">
  <data key="d0">Particle Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Particle Size is a fundamental physical dimension and quantitative metric that represents the diameter, spatial extent, or coarseness of individual particles, agglomerates, crystallites, or nanoparticles within a given material. As a critical physical parameter, it significantly influences the functional, chemical, and processing behaviors of various substances, directly dictating reaction kinetics, separation efficiency, structural properties, adsorption efficiency, and overall material performance. Its measurement and control are essential across multiple scientific and industrial domains, with evaluation methods including sieve retention percentages, electrophoresis for dispersions, and transmission electron microscopy (TEM). In graphical representations and scientific chart distributions, it is frequently plotted as a horizontal axis metric measured in millimeters on a logarithmic scale.

The specific characteristics and impacts of Particle Size vary considerably depending on the material context. In cement components, it directly governs the material's setting time. For phosphogypsum, it serves as a key physical characteristic that evolves during milling, directly impacting material performance and governing impurity content and removal rates. The majority of phosphogypsum particles typically concentrate between 0.04 and 0.075 millimeters, with experimental samples often characterized as less than 63 micrometers, while target specifications frequently aim for a d50 range between 50 and 100 micrometers. In hydroxyapatite applications, Particle Size is a critical parameter controlled by synthesis conditions and actively modified by milling techniques. It dictates adsorption efficiency, where smaller dimensions yield superior performance. Observed dimensions vary by method and synthesis: nanocrystals generally measure between 10 and 25 nanometers in diameter and 75 to 150 nanometers in length; synthesized nanoparticles typically range from 18.4 to 35 nanometers or 6 to 30 nanometers; TEM observations record dimensions of 20 to 60 nanometers; and general particulates or agglomerates range from 10 to 30 nanometers to over 50 nanometers.

Beyond these specific applications, Particle Size plays a decisive role in other domains. In soil and stabilizer systems, it affects the reduction in dry unit weight. When applied to rare earth element-bearing minerals and general raw materials, it determines bioleaching effectiveness and overall leaching efficiency. In microscopic analyses, it denotes the diameter of individual agglomerates or crystallites, which may range from 0.1 to 0.3 micrometers. Across all these contexts, precise characterization and control of Particle Size remain vital for optimizing material processing, enhancing functional outcomes, and tailoring synthesized crystal or nanoparticle properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical characteristic of phosphogypsum samples analyzed to determine its effect on leachability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007</data>
