<node id="Ethanol">
  <data key="d0">Ethanol</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethanol is a versatile chemical compound extensively utilized across materials science, chemical research, and analytical preparation protocols. Primarily functioning as a solvent and washing agent, it is routinely employed to purify synthesis products and precipitates, often in combination with deionized or distilled water. This washing process effectively removes impurities, side products, and specific residual substances, including polyvinyl alcohol (PVA) from hydroxyapatite (HAP) powders, Brij-93 surfactant residues, and organic contaminants from chicken eggshells when boiled with distilled water. Additionally, ethanol serves as a cleaning solvent for FTO substrates and is applied after distilled water rinses to ensure thorough purification of synthesized powders.

Beyond its purification roles, ethanol supports advanced materials characterization and specialized research applications. It acts as a dispersion medium for the ultrasonic treatment of powders, including HAP and gypsum samples, to prepare sonicated suspensions prior to Field Emission Scanning Electron Microscopy (FESEM) and standard SEM analysis. In geotechnical and cementitious studies, ethanol functions as a displacement liquid for determining the bulk density and porosity of cement samples, particularly when water is utilized as the setting liquid. Furthermore, ethanol is integrated into catalytic investigations to examine reactivity over HAP-based catalysts, aiding in the elucidation of acid-base selectivity mechanisms.

In synthetic chemistry, ethanol also serves as a direct reactant, notably in a one-step process to synthesize potassium sulfate from PG. Through these diverse applications ranging from impurity removal and microscopy sample preparation to density testing and catalytic research, ethanol remains a critical reagent for both fundamental chemical research and practical materials processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol is used as a washing agent to remove impurities from the synthesized HAp samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol is a solvent used alongside deionized water to wash the precipitate during nanosized hydroxyapatite preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol acts as a solvent in which nHAp nanoparticles demonstrate easy dispersion properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317876</data>
