<node id="Simulated Body Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Simulated Body Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Simulated body fluid is a standardized solution used to evaluate the in vitro bioactivity and apatite-forming ability of biomaterials.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated body fluid is the medium used to evaluate protein adsorption and release profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated Body Fluid is a chemical solution prepared by dissolving specific reagents in deionized water and buffering to pH 7.40, used to simulate human body fluid for protein adsorption studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated body fluid is the evaluation medium used to assess protein adsorption amounts and release profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated body fluid is a chemical solution used as a medium for calcium phosphate mediated gene delivery systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-009</data>
