<node id="Mortar">
  <data key="d0">Mortar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortar refers to two distinct concepts in scientific and engineering literature. In laboratory settings, it functions as a physical grinding tool specifically designed to pulverize thermally decomposed bone samples and desiccated hydroxyapatite products into finer particles during hydroxyapatite synthesis.

In construction and materials engineering, Mortar is a cementitious building material that serves as a secondary or alternative construction medium, frequently analyzed alongside concrete. Its composition typically involves a mixture of cement or clinker, fine aggregates, water, and binders such as β-building gypsum powder recovered via PBG technology, Plaster Of Paris, and calcium hydroxide. A significant focus of modern research involves incorporating phosphogypsum as a partial replacement or supplementary additive, often in dehydrated forms or combined with anhydrite, to alter its behavior and optimize performance. Extensive studies evaluate the mechanical and chemical properties of these phosphogypsum-enhanced Mortar mixtures, assessing compressive, flexural, and tensile strengths under various curing conditions, alongside acid corrosion resistance and microstructural evolution. Key research objectives center on optimizing setting time and hardening properties by adjusting phosphogypsum replacement ratios and integrating supplementary materials, thereby enhancing the material's overall durability, performance characteristics, and suitability for construction applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502969</data>
