<node id="P-Value">
  <data key="d0">P-Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">P-Value is a statistical measure from ANOVA indicating the significance of the relationship between compressive strength and density.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric indicating statistical significance, with highly significant results marked as p &lt; 0.001.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791142009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulfate (CaSO4)">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate (CaSO4)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulfate is a resorbable component used in composite bone cements to modulate setting time and bioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is the primary chemical compound in phosphogypsum that undergoes decomposition in PSC technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a precursor phase in phosphogypsum that hydrolyzes into calcium hydroxide under high pH and temperature conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a primary reactant that undergoes reduction by carbon and oxidizes calcium sulfide.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary reactant in the phosphogypsum decomposition process that reacts with carbon to form intermediate and final products.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound identified as Peak 1 in the chart, corresponding to gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792363048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nanohydroxyapatite (nHAP)">
  <data key="d0">Nanohydroxyapatite (nHAP)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanohydroxyapatite is a nanostructured form of hydroxyapatite extensively researched in restorative dentistry for its enhanced biomaterial properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyapatite–calcium sulfate composite bone cement">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite–calcium sulfate composite bone cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A composite bone cement combining hydroxyapatite and calcium sulfate, developed to improve bioactivity, injectability, and mechanical properties for bone repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium chloride (NaCl)">
  <data key="d0">Sodium chloride (NaCl)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride is used as a cationic substitution additive in hydroxyapatite and beta-tricalcium phosphate composites to enhance mechanical strength and bioactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silk fibroin">
  <data key="d0">Silk fibroin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silk fibroin is a natural protein material combined with hydroxyapatite to create composite scaffolds for bone tissue repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-tricalcium phosphate (b-TCP)">
  <data key="d0">Beta-tricalcium phosphate (b-TCP)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-tricalcium phosphate is a calcium phosphate ceramic used in scaffold compositions, often modified with additives like sodium chloride to improve dissolution control and bioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-tricalcium phosphate is a phase detected with low intensity in the synthetic hydroxyapatite particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792176766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coprecipitation">
  <data key="d0">Coprecipitation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Coprecipitation is a chemical synthesis technique used to produce hydroxyapatite and related biomaterials.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a common mechanism where trace components form isomorphous crystals and incorporate into the crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a mechanism by which foreign ions are incorporated into phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a previously utilized technique for synthesizing hydroxyapatite, often resulting in agglomeration or uncontrolled particle sizes.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a chemical synthesis technique used to produce hydroxyapatite, noted for potential issues with particle size control.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a synthesis technique for hydroxyapatite that can result in agglomeration and uncontrolled particle size.&lt;SEP&gt;Coprecipitation is a chemical synthesis method previously used to produce hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791626951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sol–gel">
  <data key="d0">Sol–gel</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sol–gel is a wet-chemical synthesis method utilized for fabricating hydroxyapatite biomaterials with controlled properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
