<node id="SBF">
  <data key="d0">SBF</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">SBF (Simulated Body Fluid) is a solution used in vitro to study the interaction with biomaterials like hydroxyapatite composites.&lt;SEP&gt;SBF is the abbreviation for Simulated Body Fluid, the chemical solution used in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;SBF is a simulated body fluid solution used as a dispersant to suspend HAp particles and measure zeta potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated Body Fluid, a pH 7.4 solution used for in vitro release testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated body fluid serving as the physiological medium for testing protein release profiles at 37°C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007</data>
