<node id="Chem. Mater.">
  <data key="d0">Chem. Mater.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemistry of Materials, commonly abbreviated as Chem. Mater., is a scientific journal dedicated to the field of materials chemistry. Over its publication history, the journal has featured a diverse range of research focusing on the synthesis, characterization, and application of various advanced materials. Notable studies published in the journal include a 2022 investigation into hydroxyapatite/calcium sulfate cements, as well as research detailing the hydrothermal crystallization of hydroxyapatite films. The journal has also documented work on nanomaterials, specifically the preparation and growth mechanisms of gold nanorods, alongside investigations into the microstructures of poly(silsesquioxane)s.

In the realm of biomedical and drug delivery applications, Chemistry of Materials published a 2004 study examining the release of ibuprofen from silica matrices. Additionally, the journal has served as a platform for scholarly contributions from various researchers, including a 2003 paper co-authored by S. Bose and research authored by Onuma and Ito. Through these varied publications, the journal continues to serve as a key resource for advancements in materials science and chemistry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017</data>
