<node id="Incubation">
  <data key="d0">Incubation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Incubation is an experimental procedure involving holding samples for predetermined periods to assess mechanical and structural changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEM Technique">
  <data key="d0">SEM Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM Technique is a microscopy method used to analyze the surface structure and apatite formation on composite bone cement samples after SBF immersion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kokubo et al.">
  <data key="d0">Kokubo et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kokubo et al. are researchers who first introduced the SBF Solution for analyzing surface structure changes in bioactive glass ceramics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Tissue-Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Bone Tissue-Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone Tissue-Engineering is a medical field focused on developing biomaterials for repairing or regenerating bone structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Blood Plasma">
  <data key="d0">Human Blood Plasma</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Human Blood Plasma is a biological fluid whose inorganic ion concentration serves as the basis for formulating SBF Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Falcon Tubes">
  <data key="d0">Falcon Tubes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Falcon Tubes are laboratory containers used to hold SBF solution for immersing composite bone cement samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Bath">
  <data key="d0">Water Bath</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Bath is an experimental apparatus used to maintain SBF solution at a constant temperature of 37°C during sample immersion.&lt;SEP&gt;A water bath is a heating apparatus used to maintain constant temperature during the reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791749076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bioactive Glasses">
  <data key="d0">Bioactive Glasses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bioactive Glasses are a class of biomaterials extensively studied for their bone tissue-engineering applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glass Ceramics">
  <data key="d0">Glass Ceramics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glass Ceramics are a class of biomaterials extensively studied for their bone tissue-engineering applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Glass Ceramics represent a high-value application for phosphogypsum valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Glass ceramics are advanced materials that utilize phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microstructure">
  <data key="d0">Microstructure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microstructure refers to the internal structural arrangement of composite bone cement, which correlates with its mechanical performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal structure of the material, specifically a porous matrix of aggregated needle-like crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;The dense, regular, and interlock microstructure formed by calcium sulfate dihydrate in PGEF.&lt;SEP&gt;Microstructure is the internal physical arrangement of phosphogypsum that becomes improved and densified after citric acid treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal arrangement of the material, revealed as agglomerated irregular particles with a cauliflower-like structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Microstructure refers to the internal structural arrangement of the material, which is influenced by macroscopic properties and calcination conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal structure of the matrix, which becomes denser due to ettringite formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792456251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SBF Test">
  <data key="d0">SBF Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SBF Test is a widely recognized experimental method for characterizing the in vitro bioactivity of various biomaterials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SBF Immersion Test">
  <data key="d0">SBF Immersion Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SBF Immersion Test is a standardized in vitro testing method that uses SBF solution to evaluate biomaterial bioactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Vivo Animal Models">
  <data key="d0">In Vivo Animal Models</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">In Vivo Animal Models are experimental models used to accurately predict biomaterial performance in the human body, though they are more expensive.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone-binding Abilities">
  <data key="d0">Bone-binding Abilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone-binding Abilities refer to the capacity of a biomaterial to attach to bone, evaluated by the formation of an apatite layer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apatite Layer">
  <data key="d0">Apatite Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Apatite Layer is a bone-like mineral deposit that forms on biomaterial surfaces, serving as a prerequisite for evaluating bone-binding abilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Performances">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Performances</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical Performances refer to the physical strength and durability properties of composite bone cement, which are influenced by microstructure and NaCl content.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical Performances refer to the high strength and load-bearing capabilities required for road pavement materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
