<node id="Emergy Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Emergy Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergy analysis is an evaluation method used to assess the environmental performance of phosphate fertilizer production and phosphogypsum disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergy analysis is a methodological approach used to evaluate the environmental sustainability and energy-use efficiency of industrial systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergy Analysis is a quantitative approach used to assign value to environmental efforts and artificial investments in production systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A methodological approach used to assess the synergistic effects and sustainability of the integrated system.&lt;SEP&gt;A sustainability evaluation methodology used to assess energy flows and ecological compensation criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergy Analysis is a method used to evaluate the sustainability of ecosystems and industrial processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002</data>
