<node id="J. Environ. Chem. Eng.">
  <data key="d0">J. Environ. Chem. Eng.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">J. Environ. Chem. Eng. is a scientific and academic journal dedicated to publishing research in environmental and chemical engineering. The publication features a diverse range of studies, with a notable focus on phosphorus-related industrial processes and waste valorization. Specifically, it has published research on advanced oxidation technologies utilized in phosphoric acid production, as well as innovative methods for impurity removal from phosphogypsum. The journal serves as a key platform for researchers investigating sustainable chemical processes and industrial waste management.

A significant portion of the journal's published work centers on hydroxyapatite, including studies on its hydrothermal synthesis from waste materials, adsorption kinetics, adsorption isotherms, and the development of organophosphonate-modified hydroxyapatites. Notably, it published prominent 2018 research detailing the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite from waste. Furthermore, J. Environ. Chem. Eng. is recognized for disseminating multiple highly cited studies on water treatment applications and fundamental adsorption mechanisms, solidifying its reputation as a vital resource for environmental remediation and materials science research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-016</data>
