  <data key="d0">CaCl2</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CaCl2 is a compound produced via a new reaction pathway for PG decomposition facilitated by Cl elements.&lt;SEP&gt;CaCl2 is a compound formed during PG impregnation and ion exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;CaCl2 is a chemical compound dissolved in aqueous solution to provide calcium ions for the reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium chloride, a product formed during the KCl and calcium carbonate reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-013</data>
