<node id="R2">
  <data key="d0">R2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">R2 denotes two distinct concepts depending on the analytical context. In chemical engineering and materials processing, R2 refers to a specific reaction step and its corresponding chemical equation that describes the transformation of calcium sulfate (CaSO4) complex salts. This reaction is a critical component in the formation and transformation of these salts during phosphogypsum (PG) impregnation. Specifically, the R2 reaction equation represents the dehydration process that converts hemihydrate into anhydrite III.

In environmental and resource assessment modeling, R2 functions as a quantitative metric and indicator. It measures comprehensive energy consumption within the resource dimension and contributes 1.77% to result variation in sensitivity analyses. Furthermore, R2 tracks the impact of pollutant emissions across four distinct analytical scenarios. The metric demonstrates a consistent downward trend in subsequent scenarios, with utilization scenarios recording an 11.78% decrease in pollutant emissions compared to Scenario 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223613</data>
