<node id="Wollastonite">
  <data key="d0">Wollastonite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Wollastonite is a calcium silicate mineral identified as a solid product in the phosphogypsum reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A pink segment in the product stack that disappears when the PG to lignite ratio exceeds 0.2.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a mineral phase that carbonate clays have the potential to generate during the brick baking process.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical phase labeled "W" in the legend, corresponding to a peak in the cluster between 28 and 32 degrees.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a standard material used for calibrating Si and Ca measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a natural mineral containing major cations Ca2+ and Mg2+, used as a raw material for CO2 carbonation.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a calcium silicate mineral studied for its aqueous carbonation mechanisms as a CO2 sequestration process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792123048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FeS Solid">
  <data key="d0">FeS Solid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">FeS solid is an iron sulfide compound formed as a solid product during the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A teal top layer that forms in the product stack at higher ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
