<node id="Molar Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Molar Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Molar ratio represents the quantitative proportion of phosphogypsum to lignite in the reaction system.&lt;SEP&gt;The ratio of Phosphogypsum to Lignite, ranging from 0.1 to 1.0, which influences product composition and total molar amount.&lt;SEP&gt;Molar ratio represents the proportion of organophosphate to total phosphorus, ranging from 0% to 30% in the prepared samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Molar Ratio is a factor affecting the synergism of the TBP-TOPO leaching process.&lt;SEP&gt;Molar Ratio is a chemical proportion used to compute the mass ratio of HAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Molar Ratio refers to the Ca to P ratio of approximately 1.66 in nHAp, indicating high purity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003</data>
