  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791090726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grain Boundary">
  <data key="d0">Grain Boundary</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The grain boundary is the interface where grain growth occurs and is subject to drag forces and resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Grain boundaries are interfaces between different crystalline grains in a material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GOC">
  <data key="d0">GOC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GOC represents the particle radius of the oxygen carrier, a key variable in the growth kinetics equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791090726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygencarrying Performance">
  <data key="d0">Oxygencarrying Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygencarrying performance refers to the cyclic stability and efficiency of the oxygen carrier, influenced by SiO2 addition.</data>
