<node id="Hydrogen Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A phosphate ion shown with a central yellow sphere bonded to four red spheres and a hydrogen sphere.&lt;SEP&gt;A phosphor impurity in PG composition that contributes to increased setting times.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Phosphate is a chemical additive introduced into the reaction media to provide necessary phosphorus for synthetic hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Phosphate is a chemical species that undergoes condensation in calcium-deficient HAP during heat treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Phosphate undergoes condensation at 600-775°C to form Calcium Pyrophosphate and Water.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Phosphate ions replace sulfate ions in the gypsum structure due to similar size, mass, and charge.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-011</data>
