<node id="Chemical Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical Treatment is a specialized purification and pretreatment process primarily applied to phosphogypsum to modify its physical, chemical, and morphological properties. This procedure serves as a critical preparatory step designed to remove impurities and enhance the material's viability for use in building and construction applications. By altering the inherent characteristics of phosphogypsum, Chemical Treatment transforms it from a waste byproduct into a resource suitable for industrial and structural purposes.

The process employs a combination of acids, alkalis, and salts to carefully adjust the pH levels of the material. This chemical manipulation facilitates the precipitation and removal of soluble contaminants, specifically fluorine and phosphorus. Additionally, Chemical Treatment addresses radiological concerns by disrupting radioactive equilibrium and reducing radionuclide concentrations, thereby modifying the chemical structure to meet safety and quality standards for construction use.

Beyond chemical purification, Chemical Treatment fundamentally alters the physical morphology of phosphogypsum, converting its typical crystalline plate structure into more desirable globular or granular forms. While the procedure is most extensively documented in the context of phosphogypsum processing, the underlying principles also apply to other materials containing radionuclides where disrupting radioactive equilibrium is necessary. Ultimately, Chemical Treatment functions as a comprehensive modification strategy that integrates impurity removal, radiological mitigation, and structural reformation to enable sustainable industrial applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
