<node id="Yangtze River Economic Belt">
  <data key="d0">Yangtze River Economic Belt</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yangtze River Economic Belt is a major ecological and economic development zone in China that serves as a critical geographic region for phosphate resource exploitation and heavy chemical industry operations. It contains a high concentration of phosphogypsum storage facilities, making the management, distribution, and utilization of this industrial byproduct a central focus of regional environmental policy.

Consequently, the region is extensively studied and analyzed for total phosphorus pollution, treatment characteristics, and the environmental management of the Three Phosphorus Industry. Proper handling of phosphogypsum and other pollutants is deemed crucial for the region's high-quality development, as improper disposal significantly impacts its ecological integrity. The Yangtze River Economic Belt remains a primary area for conducting risk assessments and implementing comprehensive environmental management strategies to balance industrial growth with ecological protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Regional economic zone analyzed for surface water quality and correlation during the 13th five-year plan period.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792225377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yangtze Three Gorges Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">Yangtze Three Gorges Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yangtze Three Gorges Reservoir is a location where nitrogen and phosphorus loads were analyzed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-019</data>
