<node id="Phosphorite">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorite is a phosphate ore that may remain incompletely decomposed in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorite is a sedimentary rock rich in phosphate minerals, characterized by significant trace element enrichment relative to shale.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorite is a phosphate rock where Radium is likely co-precipitated with Barium or Strontium.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorite is a mineral subjected to carbothermic reduction with micronutrient-bearing cosolvents for slag activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
