<node id="Coal">
  <data key="d0">Coal</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Coal is a non-renewable solid fossil fuel that functions as a critical energy source, fundamental raw material, and primary carbon substrate across diverse industrial, experimental, and chemical processing applications. Explicitly tracked in energy consumption tables, it serves as a central component in the PBG and PSC technology processes and scenarios. Within these frameworks, coal operates as a direct energy source, a core chemical feedstock, and a reducing agent—comparable to coke or charcoal—that is added to mixtures to facilitate reactions, such as in phosphogypsum decomposition and phosphate fertilizer production. Furthermore, it acts as a key substrate for advanced research, including chemical looping gasification and combustion experiments.

Quantitatively, coal contributes approximately 1.95% to 2.09% of the total emergy input across various system evaluations, specifically accounting for 2.09% in Scenario 1 and 2.02% in Scenario 2. Despite this relatively modest emergy share, it is identified as the primary fossil fuel source and the largest contributor to carbon emissions within the production system. Coal significantly drives carbon emissions across Scenarios 1, 2, and 3, accounting for the vast majority of combustion-related emissions. Consequently, optimizing the structural utilization of coal is strongly recommended to reduce carbon emission intensity, particularly in Scenario 3.

The extensive industrial and experimental utility of coal carries substantial environmental consequences, directly contributing to notable ecological impacts measured by indicators such as Fossil Depletion Potential (FDP) and Global Warming Potential (GWP). As a vital carbon-based material bridging energy production, chemical processing, and experimental research, coal necessitates careful management of its environmental footprint to mitigate its significant ecological and carbon emission impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is mixed with phosphogypsum in experiments to analyze decomposition processes and reaction mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is a reactant mixed with phosphogypsum for thermal decomposition experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
