<node id="Cement Retarders">
  <data key="d0">Cement Retarders</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement Retarders are industrial additives and conventional construction materials primarily utilized in the building sector. Historically produced using natural gypsum, contemporary manufacturing increasingly relies on recycled phosphogypsum (PG) as the primary raw material, with some formulations also incorporating Anhydrite III or combining PG with lime. This production shift is largely driven by small-scale integrated companies that merge phosphogypsum generation with recycling operations. In specific manufacturing contexts, such as Scenario 4, the process utilizes PG and lime in optimized ratios to maintain sustainability and alter emergy input proportions.

Economically, Cement Retarders are classified as low-value-added products. Their commercial distribution is heavily constrained by transportation costs, typically limiting the sales radius to within 100 kilometers of the production facility. In China, they currently represent a dominant, yet low-value, application and recycling technology for phosphogypsum. Due to these economic limitations, some industry perspectives recommend a gradual reduction in their reliance, even as they remain a primary utilization pathway for this industrial byproduct.

From an environmental and technical standpoint, Cement Retarders serve as a critical bridge between conventional construction standards and circular economy initiatives. The substitution rate of phosphogypsum in these formulations is a pivotal variable that significantly influences Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) outcomes, making it a key sensitivity factor for evaluating phosphogypsum cement recycling (PCR) technology. By repurposing industrial waste into functional building materials, they play an essential role in sustainable construction practices despite their current low-value categorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement retarders are construction applications where phosphogypsum is utilized.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000</data>
