  <data key="d2">FeS is an iron sulfide compound produced in Step 2 and used to reduce CaSO4 in Step 3.&lt;SEP&gt;FeS is a monosulfide compound whose sulfur species exhibit binding energies between 161.0 and 161.1 eV.</data>
