<node id="Phosphate Mines">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Mines</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate mines are the source locations for clay by-products and phosphogypsum utilized in sustainable construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial sites identified as a primary source of total phosphorus pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate mines are industrial sites that apply PG produced by chemical plants for underground goaf backfill.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate mines in China contain low levels of radioactive elements, serving as the primary source of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-010</data>
