<node id="TG Analysis">
  <data key="d0">TG Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TG Analysis is a thermal measurement technique used to evaluate the properties of compound oxygen carriers.&lt;SEP&gt;TG Analysis is an experimental procedure utilizing graphite powder as a carbon source and nitrogen gas as a sweep gas.&lt;SEP&gt;TG Analysis is a thermal analysis method that tracks mass changes in phosphogypsum as temperature increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric analysis is conducted to determine the calcination temperature range of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792294020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cerium Dioxide">
  <data key="d0">Cerium Dioxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cerium dioxide is loaded onto the surface of PG, hindering calcium sulfate reactions and requiring higher energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerium dioxide is a metal oxide combined with hydroxyapatite to support gold catalysts for formaldehyde oxidation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
