  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dehydration behaviour describes the chemical changes and impurity shifts phosphogypsum undergoes during calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration behaviour refers to the thermal decomposition and water loss characteristics of phosphogypsum during calcination.</data>
