<node id="Phosphorus Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The natural process involving the release, transport, deposition, and tectonic movement of phosphorus, which is disrupted by phosphogypsum dumping.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural biogeochemical process disrupted by phosphogypsum accumulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The phosphorus cycle is the biogeochemical system analyzed for waste generation and recycling trends in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Cycle is a biogeochemical process describing the movement of phosphorus through ecosystems, a central theme in multiple cited works.</data>
