<node id="Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid Production">
  <data key="d0">Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid Production</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet-Process Phosphoric Acid Production is a manufacturing method that uses concentrated sulfuric acid to decompose phosphate rock, resulting in significant phosphogypsum emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet-process phosphoric acid production is an industrial method that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet-process phosphoric acid production is the industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a primary byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet-process phosphoric acid production is a chemical manufacturing process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct through the reaction of phosphate rock with sulfuric acid.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003</data>
