<node id="Heavy Metal Elements">
  <data key="d0">Heavy Metal Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heavy metal elements in phosphogypsum are analyzed using techniques such as X-ray fluorescence and ICP-MS.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants associated with phosphogypsum that can cause soil and water anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metal elements originate from phosphate rock and pose risks of chronic poisoning and kidney failure if they enter the food chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metal elements are trace impurities in phosphogypsum that pose threats to environmental and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy Metal Elements are chemical components with strong migration and transformation abilities that transfer to nature and eventually enter the human body via the food chain.&lt;SEP&gt;A category of toxic elements including Cr, As, Hg, and Cd detected in MPG at elevated temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-005</data>
