<node id="Mercury">
  <data key="d0">Mercury</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mercury (Hg) is a chemical element and heavy metal that also functions as a trace element in geological contexts, notably exhibiting depletion in phosphorites relative to shale. Naturally occurring as a toxic impurity in phosphogypsum (PG), its presence and concentration vary by region, with documented levels such as 0.06 mg/kg in PG and 0.01% by weight in specific samples. During the conversion of PG to processed phosphogypsum (MPG), mercury forms substitutional solid solutions with calcium and iron, experiences an approximately 83% reduction in concentration, and is detected at processing temperatures of 185°C and 190°C, raising potential safety concerns. Analytical studies identify mercury throughout the sample matrix with a uniform speckled distribution and multiple spectral peaks between 10 and 15 keV, with concentration data routinely tabulated for leaching toxicity and ecological risk assessments.

In environmental and industrial settings, mercury is recognized as a hazardous pollutant that frequently leaches into groundwater, particularly from phosphogypsum stockpiles and stacks. It is classified as highly contaminating under standards such as those in Quebec, with Tunisian phosphogypsum showing notably high concentrations. Due to its severe health risks, including neuronal damage and neurodegenerative diseases, mercury is subject to stringent regulatory oversight, including a World Health Organization (WHO) guideline of 0.001 mg/L and a water quality limit of 0.002 mg/L, alongside monitoring in fertilizers per Chinese standard GB/T23349. It is explicitly monitored in data analysis using units of µg/L and is often studied alongside other contaminants to assess threats to ecological systems and public safety.

To mitigate these ecological and public health risks, mercury is actively targeted for removal or adsorption using hydroxyapatite-based composites and magnetic composites. Low-temperature calcination has been shown to completely eliminate mercury from MPG, while specific treatments like PBSLM6 have demonstrated zero leaching concentrations. The element is consistently analyzed for its ecological risk in both PG and MPG, with leaching detection results and concentration metrics providing critical data for safety evaluations and regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;A toxic heavy metal present in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a chemical element studied for its sources and dispersion in estuarine systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a trace metal found in Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured, with notably high levels recorded in Tunisian samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
