<node id="Iron Oxides">
  <data key="d0">Iron Oxides</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron oxides are impurities present in the runoff, giving it a distinct orange or rust color.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron oxides are additive components in the phosphogypsum ingredient system used to meet slag wool production requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron oxides are materials utilized collaboratively to construct a low eutectic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Compounds contained in MPG whose reductive dissolution during initial hydration contributes to an increase in cadmium levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron oxides are compounds present in MPG whose dissolution during hydration increases cadmium content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-030</data>
