<node id="Airborne Particulate Matter">
  <data key="d0">Airborne Particulate Matter</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Airborne Particulate Matter is environmental material in Beijing showing seasonal variation in oxidative potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Airborne particulate matter originates from phosphogypsum piles via wind erosion or operations and is a potential source of radioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Airborne Particulate Matter is an environmental pollutant tracked in proximity to phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-021</data>
