</node>
<node id="Beijing">
  <data key="d0">Beijing</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Beijing, the capital city of China, serves as a prominent political, academic, and environmental research hub. It is the headquarters of the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology and hosts a wide array of academic and research institutions, including the University of Science and Technology Beijing, Beijing University of Technology, and the Institute of Agricultural Resources and Regional Planning. The city also functions as a major publishing center, housing China Environment Publishing Group and serving as the publication location for Geology Press, which published the groundwater quality standard.

In addition to its institutional and publishing roles, Beijing is a focal point for environmental and scientific investigations. Research conducted within the city has examined the seasonal oxidative potential variations of airborne particulate matter and assessed heavy metal contamination in soils from a coal-mine brownfield. The city further supports scholarly work as the site of Wang, C.'s research and the location of various authors' affiliated research institutions, highlighting its central role in multidisciplinary academic and technical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Beijing is the geographic location of the Metallurgical Industry Press.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792364185</data>
