<node id="Table 4">
  <data key="d0">Table 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 4 functions as a generic, context-dependent placeholder label widely utilized across independent scientific publications rather than denoting a single static dataset. Its specific content is entirely dictated by the research domain, serving as a versatile analytical repository for diverse experimental and comparative data. In environmental and materials research focusing on phosphogypsum, Table 4 comprehensively documents chemical, radiological, and physical properties, including heavy metal concentrations, trace element mass content, activity ratios, enrichment factors, and radionuclide ratios. It also details structural and mineralogical analyses via X-ray diffraction, rare earth element leaching methodologies, and trace element concentrations measured through LA-ICP-MS. In applied environmental studies, it compares microbial growth metrics, summarizes construction material performance such as phosphogypsum-based mortar replacement and compressive strength, and presents Life Cycle Inventory data for road construction applications.

In geotechnical engineering, Table 4 reports maximum dry unit weight and optimum moisture content for soils amended with fly ash and fly ash-phosphogypsum, alongside experimental results from compaction and Atterberg limit tests on stabilized soils. Ecological and regulatory contexts utilize it to list acceptable concentrations and ecological service requirements for various air and water pollutants across multiple scenarios. Within biomedical and materials science, the table shifts focus to hydroxyapatite research, presenting adsorption results for Bovine Serum Albumin and LSZ on rod-shaped surfaces, quantitative metrics for synthesized powders including density, specific surface area, roughness, and particle size, and thermodynamic parameters for fluoride adsorption onto nano-hydroxyapatite derived from phosphogypsum.

Furthermore, Table 4 frequently encapsulates hydrogeochemical modeling outputs, presenting water-soluble lead (Pb^2+) concentrations and mole fractions in soil water extracts, calculated values from the ION-2 model, and lead concentrations under varying phosphogypsum doses. Across all disciplines, it also commonly outlines foundational experimental frameworks, design criteria, and quality monitoring parameters. Collectively, these varied applications demonstrate that Table 4 is a highly adaptable analytical placeholder tailored to report specialized findings ranging from elemental and radionuclide profiling to microbiological comparisons, construction performance metrics, surface adsorption studies, and hydrogeochemical modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 contains calculated Gibbs free energy and enthalpy values for specific chemical reactions at various temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 lists the beginning temperatures of possible reactions based on thermodynamic calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;A table detailing strict chemical and physical specifications for phosphogypsum intended for use in the plaster industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 presents the calculated crystallite sizes and lattice strain for each hydroxyapatite sample type.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 provides the results of the compound composition of PG determined after calcination using X-ray diffraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 documents the X-ray diffraction results for PG calcined at different temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-004</data>
