<node id="Manganese">
  <data key="d0">Manganese</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Manganese is a transition metal and chemical element that functions across geological, environmental, and materials science domains. In geological contexts, it is generally classified as a trace element and is notably depleted in phosphorites relative to average crustal abundances. Within phosphogypsum matrices, however, it acts as a major chemical species and metallic oxide impurity. It is detected in variable concentrations within phosphogypsum samples, typically exhibiting mass fractions between 0.010% and 0.080%, and is routinely quantified using analytical techniques such as LA-ICP-MS. Due to its prevalence, the concentration of manganese in phosphogypsum solutions is actively monitored against established environmental regulatory limits.

From an environmental and water quality perspective, manganese is regulated as a heavy metal. Regulatory frameworks enforce a specific concentration limit of 0.05 mg/L, while the World Health Organization provides a guideline value of 50 mg/L. Environmental remediation strategies frequently target manganese for removal from aqueous systems. It can be susceptible to elimination through simple water washing, and it is commonly extracted using ion-exchange resins like Dowex 50W-x8. However, treatment efficacy is highly dependent on the specific substrate, with certain conditions yielding a 0% removal rate.

In materials chemistry, manganese serves diverse functional roles. It is present as a trace element in the AZ31B alloy. When incorporated into hydroxyapatite structures as a substituent, it increases the material's solubility and consequently reduces its overall stability. Conversely, when deployed as a supported metal catalyst, manganese demonstrates improved toluene conversion efficiency compared to traditional alumina-supported catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;Manganese is a chemical element whose concentration in phosphogypsum was measured across the sampled locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
