<node id="OH-">
  <data key="d0">OH-</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">OH- is the chemical formula representing the hydroxide ion.&lt;SEP&gt;OH- is a hydroxide ion that attaches to Ca9(PO4)6 clusters during reflux to facilitate HA growth.&lt;SEP&gt;OH- refers to hydroxide ions whose data are reported in literature regarding relevant functional groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxide ions are reactants in the formation of HAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-005</data>
