<node id="Composting Process">
  <data key="d0">Composting Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Composting Process is the experimental procedure during which microbial population changes and soil treatments were monitored.&lt;SEP&gt;Composting Process is a biological decomposition cycle characterized by distinct temperature phases and microbial activity.&lt;SEP&gt;A biological decomposition procedure where temperature and moisture are controlled to promote microbial growth and fermentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological decomposition method where temperature and microbial reproduction are closely linked.&lt;SEP&gt;The composting process involves microbial activity that alters the physicochemical properties of the waste mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;A biological treatment method studied for its response to phosphogypsum addition regarding physico-chemical properties and microbial diversity.&lt;SEP&gt;Composting process involves adding phosphogypsum to alter physico-chemical properties and microbial diversity in compost tea.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792094244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microorganisms">
  <data key="d0">Microorganisms</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil-dwelling organisms whose available living space is reflected by soil porosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological agents whose growth and propagation are promoted by high temperatures and optimal moisture during composting.&lt;SEP&gt;Living organisms whose growth and propagation require proper hydration and specific environmental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological agents that decompose particulate organic matter into finer forms, supporting rhizosphere expansion and aggregate stabilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
