<node id="Soil Porosity">
  <data key="d0">Soil Porosity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A soil property reflecting the living space available to microorganisms and water holding capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical soil property improved by biofertilizer addition, facilitating plant growth and nutrient transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical soil property controlling water and gas flow, improved by straw addition and microbial-plant interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil porosity is improved by biofertilizer application, making the soil less susceptible to consolidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil porosity is a physical property modelled across soil organic matter and land-use continua.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil porosity is a physical property of soil that correlates with radon exhalation values from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
