<node id="60 °C">
  <data key="d0">60 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">60 °C is the temperature setting used by the Constant-Temperature Water Bath during chlorophyll extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;60 °C is the elevated temperature condition that significantly promotes the release of elements by increasing phosphogypsum solubility.&lt;SEP&gt;60 °C denotes an elevated experimental condition that increases the chemical species release rate and solubility of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013</data>
