<node id="Hydrogen Ions">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Ions formed from the dissociation of potassium bisulfate in solution, which decompose in an alkaline medium.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen ions represent the acidic environment required for dissolution and are released as a byproduct of manganese phosphate formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen ions are exchanged ions in acidic soils whose amounts are reduced by phosphogypsum conjugate products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-012</data>
