<node id="Gamma Radiation">
  <data key="d0">Gamma Radiation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma Radiation is a form of external, aerial radioactive exposure primarily originating from phosphogypsum storage stacks and gypsum stacks. This radiation is emitted directly from these facilities due to the presence of Radium-226 and its subsequent decay products. Characterized by a small quality factor, the absorbed dose of Gamma Radiation typically equals the equivalent dose in humans. As a direct exposure risk, it poses potential hazards to both humans and animals. To manage this risk, Gamma Radiation levels are routinely measured, often expressed as a safety metric in millisieverts per year (mSv y-1), to evaluate radiological exposure against established public dose limits.

In industrial applications, particularly during brick sintering, phosphogypsum is incorporated into construction materials, resulting in external Gamma Radiation emitted by the finished bricks. When phosphogypsum is utilized at concentrations up to 30%, the resulting external radiation exposure is reduced to less than one mS. This demonstrates that while Gamma Radiation presents a direct radiological hazard during storage and handling, its emission can be effectively quantified and mitigated through regulated industrial practices and controlled material composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma radiation is a form of external exposure originating from radionuclides in phosphogypsum building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma radiation is a form of ionizing radiation emitted by phosphogypsum stacks, causing locally elevated radiation levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792487517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
