<node id="Acidulation Process">
  <data key="d0">Acidulation Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The acidulation process is a chemical procedure used to extract phosphoric acid from phosphate rock.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidulation is the chemical process used to extract phosphoric acid from phosphate rock, affecting uranium partitioning.&lt;SEP&gt;The acidulation process converts phosphate rock, forming HF and other compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;The acidulation process involves reacting phosphate rock with sulfuric acid to produce phosphoric acid and phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
