<node id="SENES">
  <data key="d0">SENES</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SENES is a research organization that has conducted extensive environmental and geochemical assessments across North America, with a particular focus on Ontario, Alberta, Florida, and Canada. A significant portion of its work involves the characterization of phosphogypsum, where it has reported scientific data on particle density, bulk density, and vertical hydraulic conductivity. The organization has also evaluated the chemical properties of the material, specifically citing the pH levels of aged and leached phosphogypsum. Furthermore, SENES conducted detailed leachate studies utilizing phosphogypsum samples sourced from both inactive and active industrial stacks in Ontario and Alberta.

Beyond phosphogypsum analysis, SENES has investigated groundwater quality and radioactive emissions. The entity has documented instances of elevated radium concentrations in groundwater systems and measured radon-222 exhalation rates alongside ambient concentrations at stacks located in Ontario and Alberta. In terms of regional synthesis, SENES summarized field studies conducted in Florida and reviewed groundwater investigations in Alberta. The organization also contributed to public health and environmental monitoring by discussing fluoride monitoring programs across Canada and reporting on seasonal variations in fluoridation levels. Through these diverse initiatives, SENES has provided critical data for hydrogeological and environmental contaminant assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792487517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
