<node id="Central Florida">
  <data key="d0">Central Florida</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Central Florida is a sub-region of Florida that functions as a major geographic and industrial hub for phosphate operations, particularly concerning phosphogypsum management. The area features operational stacks built on limestone bedrock with phosphatic clay deposits and is home to key industrial facilities, including the AMAX Phosphate Inc. and USS Agri-Chemicals Plant. These installations serve as primary sites for phosphogypsum storage and phosphate industry waste disposal, which have prompted comprehensive environmental hazard assessments.

In scientific and environmental research, Central Florida is widely utilized as a baseline and reference region for geochemical and radiological studies. It is recognized as a geographical source of phosphogypsum characterized by distinct trace metal concentrations, and it served as the origin for samples analyzed by Rutherford et al. The region is specifically referenced for radium-226 (Ra-226) measurements and acts as a comparative baseline for evaluating trace element levels in South African phosphogypsum. Additionally, Central Florida has been the focus of extensive investigations into the hydrogeology and water quality of phosphate waste disposal sites, as well as radiological hazard and emission analyses conducted by Roessler and Guidry on phosphogypsum stacks. Together, these attributes establish Central Florida as a critical reference area for assessing the environmental and geochemical impacts of phosphate industry activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792479872</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alberta">
  <data key="d0">Alberta</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Alberta is a Canadian province that functions as a notable geographic region for environmental monitoring and industrial research. The province has implemented specific maximum air quality guidelines targeting fluoridation levels to safeguard public and environmental health. Within its boundaries, Alberta hosts active phosphogypsum stacks managed by fertilizer manufacturers, which are constructed on glacial till and contain water-filled ponds.

Extensive scientific investigations have been conducted across the province to evaluate the radioactivity and chemical characteristics of phosphogypsum. Research efforts have specifically analyzed soil interactions with phosphogypsum leachate and explored decommissioning strategies for phosphogypsum tailings. Furthermore, Alberta is referenced in scientific datasets for radioactive isotope measurements, encompassing the analysis of radionuclide activities in phosphogypsum samples, some of which trace their origin to Idaho. Collectively, these studies position Alberta as a critical location for assessing the environmental impact, chemical behavior, and regulatory management of phosphogypsum and related radioactive materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a region where phosphogypsum was studied for its radioactivity and chemical characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a geographical source of Phosphogypsum with lower concentrations of certain trace metals compared to Central Florida.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a region where the radioactivity and chemical characteristics of phosphogypsum were investigated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
