<node id="Phosphogypsum Stacks">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Stacks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum stacks are large, man-made industrial structures and waste accumulations where phosphogypsum is deposited using acidic process water. These facilities function as extensive storage sites for industrial byproducts and are typically constructed as large piles or mounds. Documented instances of these structures are found in various locations, including central Florida and on salt marshes in Huelva, Spain.

Due to their environmental and health implications, these stacks have been extensively monitored and investigated for radon exhalation rates, radioactive exposure levels, and airborne particulate emissions. The waste material emits radon-222 and gamma radiation, making the stacks notable sources of radon exhalation. Radiation exposure levels fluctuate depending on environmental factors such as surface covering and moisture content.

Phosphogypsum stacks pose significant environmental and occupational risks. They are highly susceptible to leaching, which can lead to groundwater contamination, and contribute to atmospheric pollution through the emission of airborne particulates. These characteristics underscore the potential occupational hazards associated with the sites and highlight the need for careful management to mitigate risks to workers and surrounding ecosystems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792485749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. E.P.A.">
  <data key="d0">U.S. E.P.A.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A regulatory body that issued a final ruling requiring phosphogypsum to be placed in stacks or mines.&lt;SEP&gt;A regulatory agency that adopted exposure limits based on risk assessments of phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory agency that adopted a limit on Rn-222 emissions from phosphogypsum stacks based on risk assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. E.P.A. is a regulatory agency that established concentration limits for Ra-226 in phosphogypsum intended for agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory body that adopted an upper limit on Radon-222 emissions from phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
