<node id="As">
  <data key="d0">As</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">As (Arsenic) is a chemical element classified as both a trace element and a hazardous heavy metal. Its concentration is routinely measured, monitored, and reported across various analytical and geochemical datasets. In these records, including the first table and broader tabular datasets, As is consistently listed with specified contaminant levels and associated numerical measurements, with concentrations typically expressed in parts per million (ppm) or milligrams per liter (mg/L). For example, analytical data has recorded its presence in PBSLM at a concentration of 0.0 mg/L.

The element is notably detected in phosphogypsum (PG), other PG variants, MPG samples, and terrestrial materials. It is actively monitored during spike recovery tests to validate analytical procedures. Due to its hazardous properties, the presence of arsenic in these environmental and industrial matrices is closely tracked, particularly because it contributes to significant carcinogenic risks. Overall, As is a well-documented chemical element whose distribution, concentration, and health implications are systematically recorded across multiple scientific and industrial contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-015</data>
