<node id="Air">
  <data key="d0">Air</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Air serves as a multifaceted medium across various scientific and industrial applications. In environmental and radiochemical contexts, it acts as the gaseous phase utilized in partition coefficient measurements for Radon-222 solubility. Additionally, air functions as a collection medium where ejected Thorium-234 atoms accumulate during radioactive decay processes. It also interacts with industrial byproducts, serving as an environmental medium that becomes contaminated by impurities leaching from phosphogypsum, while simultaneously acting as the surrounding fluid medium that facilitates natural convection and heat transfer around the same material.

From a thermal and processing standpoint, air is employed as a rapid cooling medium for samples immediately following a melting process. In combustion applications, it operates as a necessary combustion component, working in conjunction with natural gas within burner systems to sustain efficient fuel oxidation.

Within emergy analysis and sustainability assessments, air is recognized as a local renewable resource and natural input. It consistently contributes to total emergy inputs across different modeled scenarios, accounting for 2.79% in Scenario 1, 2.70% in Scenario 2, and 2.60% in a generalized Total Input calculation. Furthermore, air serves as the primary origin or source for R1 and is utilized as a local renewable input in Scenario 2, where its inclusion actively contributes to improved overall sustainability metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Factor Q">
  <data key="d0">Quality Factor Q</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A parameter indicating radiation quality, small for gamma radiation and X-rays, intermediate for neutrons, and high for alpha particles.</data>
