<node id="Singh">
  <data key="d0">Singh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Singh is a researcher whose work primarily centers on the chemical properties, impurity management, and treatment of phosphogypsum, alongside its diverse industrial and agricultural applications. A significant portion of Singh’s research investigates the detrimental effects of soluble phosphorus and fluorine compounds on the hydration and solidification processes of phosphogypsum and gypsum-based materials. Specifically, Singh demonstrated that soluble phosphorus pentoxide hinders the hydration of hemihydrate phosphogypsum by forming an insoluble calcium phosphate coating, which delays solidification and alters crystal morphology. Additionally, Singh established a harmful influence ranking of various fluorides on the setting time, strength, and overall performance of gypsum and filling bodies.

To mitigate these impurity-related challenges, Singh pioneered the systematic treatment of phosphogypsum using aqueous citric acid solutions, notably documenting this approach in 2002. This treatment effectively converts problematic phosphate and fluoride impurities into water-soluble compounds, thereby removing impurities, augmenting material strength, and shortening setting times. Singh also explored purification through ammonium hydroxide, wet sieving, and calcination. Regarding calcination, Singh asserted that optimal mechanical properties are achieved at 1000 °C, while also conducting studies at 800 °C and later examining the material's properties in collaboration with Garg.

Beyond chemical processing, Singh investigated the broader applications of phosphogypsum. In agriculture, Singh highlighted the viability of properly processed phosphogypsum as a nutrient source for plant nutrition. In construction materials, Singh manufactured cement by intergrinding clinker with phosphogypsum or selenite gypsum, measuring associated declines in compressive strength. Singh also prepared mixtures of calcined phosphogypsum and slag with various chemical additives, notably in 1995, to measure soundness expansion and observe prolonged setting times at higher calcined phosphogypsum ratios. Furthermore, Singh co-authored studies on the effect of curing temperature on phosphogypsum mixtures and investigated its use in polymer flooring compositions. Additionally, Singh was cited alongside Kashem regarding iron oxide dissolution mechanisms and, together with Khan, suggested a method for determining the adsorption equilibrium constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
