<node id="U(VI)">
  <data key="d0">U(VI)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">U(VI) is an oxidation state of uranium that may be adsorbed onto apatite crystal surfaces as the uranyl ion.&lt;SEP&gt;U(VI) is a uranium oxidation state that is highly soluble and mobile, dominating under oxidizing conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;U(VI) is a highly mobile chemical form of uranium found in phosphogypsum, posing a significant environmental contamination risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A highly mobile form of uranium in the environment, raising environmental concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
