  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ionizing radiation is a subject of study regarding its sources and biological effects, as documented by UNSCEAR.&lt;SEP&gt;Ionizing radiation is a health hazard associated with chronic exposure to radionuclides in phosphogypsum building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of energy whose sources and biological effects were comprehensively reviewed by UNSCEAR.&lt;SEP&gt;Ionizing radiation is a hazard addressed by safety standards and dosimetric assessments related to phosphogypsum handling.</data>
