<node id="Lead (Pb)">
  <data key="d0">Lead (Pb)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead (Pb) is a chemical element and heavy metal ion that functions as a dangerous pollutant and contaminant within environmental systems. It disperses throughout the ecosphere primarily through eolian and water transfer mechanisms. In soil solutions, Lead's chemical speciation, activity, and forms are predominantly bound to associates. Scientific studies frequently calculate and analyze its equilibrium concentration, water-soluble forms, solubility, and complexation in aqueous solutions. Chemically, Lead exhibits the lowest adsorption capacity among tested metals.

Due to its hazardous nature, Lead is subject to strict regulatory limits in drinking water standards established by the U.S., Canada, the EEC, and the WHO. It is also systematically tracked in environmental inventory data, with measured quantities recorded at 2.13 x 10^-3 kg in high population contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-004</data>
