  <data key="d0">Clay Minerals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Clay minerals are substrates where U(IV) may be adsorbed or exist as a chemically-complexed phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Clay minerals are substances with which U(VI) can be complexed in phosphate structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Impurities indicated by the presence of SiO2, Al2O3, and alkali oxides in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Clay Minerals are soil components whose susceptibility to lime is influenced by particle size and crystallinity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003</data>
