<node id="Rainwater">
  <data key="d0">Rainwater</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Rainwater infiltrates through inactive stacks, causing long-term downward leaching that contributes to groundwater contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Rainwater is a natural solvent used by Haridasan for leaching radium-226 from phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Rainwater is an environmental pathway through which PG enters the ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Rainwater is an environmental pathway through which PG and heavy metals enter the natural environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Rainwater combines with process waters in phosphogypsum stacks to form hydraulic heads that drive water infiltration.&lt;SEP&gt;Rainwater is a natural leachant used in studies to assess radium mobilization from phosphogypsum under weather conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792485464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
