  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfur dioxide is a byproduct of PSC technology that is further utilized to manufacture sulfuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur Dioxide is a chemical compound whose concentration is quantified using the standardized Sodium Thiosulfate solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur dioxide is a gaseous byproduct released during the oxidation of calcium sulfide by unreacted calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur dioxide is an air pollutant that utilizes most of the ecological services provided by the atmospheric environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound whose production decreases with increased reaction temperature.</data>
