  <data key="d2">An environmental impact metric where PCR technology emits more than natural gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Particulate matter formation potential is an environmental damage indicator assessing particulate matter emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Particulate Matter Formation Potential (PMFP) measures particulate matter emissions, where PCR Technology shows higher emissions than natural gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Particulate Matter Formation Potential is an environmental impact metric that decreases as PSC Technology proportions increase.&lt;SEP&gt;Particulate Matter Formation Potential (PMFP) is an environmental impact category evaluated in the analysis.</data>
