<node id="PMFP">
  <data key="d0">PMFP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Particulate Matter Formation Potential is an environmental impact category that exhibited higher variability in the PCR and PBG technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;PMFP represents particulate matter formation potential that decreases with increased PSC technology usage.&lt;SEP&gt;PMFP is an environmental impact indicator measuring particulate matter formation potential.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010</data>
