<node id="Calcium Carbide Residue">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Carbide Residue</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">An industrial alkaline waste identified as a feasible substitute for quicklime in PCR technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electricity">
  <data key="d0">Electricity</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Electricity is a fundamental energy resource and the consumed form of electric power that functions as a critical raw material and energy input across multiple production processes. It is formally cataloged in energy consumption tables and quantified as a measured metric recorded in kilowatt-hours. This energy source is actively utilized and tracked across the PCR, PBG, and PSC scenarios, where it serves as a foundational input for all three processes.

Within environmental impact analyses, electricity is consistently monitored due to its substantial ecological and health-related consequences. Its consumption directly contributes to human health impacts, ecological toxicity, and overall toxicity potentials. Furthermore, electricity is a major driver of carbon emissions in these production scenarios. It ranks as the third-largest contributor to emission trends overall, and its rapid increase in consumption is specifically identified as the primary factor behind the elevated carbon emission index observed in Scenario 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792222852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Building Gypsum Powder">
  <data key="d0">Building Gypsum Powder</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A material whose substitution in PBG technology can completely offset environmental burdens.&lt;SEP&gt;Building gypsum powder is the finished product obtained after milling, used for sale or as a raw material for gypsum blocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Building gypsum powder is the final packaged product from the powder production line.&lt;SEP&gt;A final powder product obtained after packaging Hemihydrate Gypsum Powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Building gypsum powder is a reference material checked during the sieving process to ensure quality standards are met.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792294454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Warming Potential">
  <data key="d0">Global Warming Potential</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global Warming Potential is an environmental impact category where PSC Technology demonstrates the smallest impact, reducing emissions by 13.3 percent.&lt;SEP&gt;An environmental impact metric dominated by carbon dioxide emissions from coal combustion and coke reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Global Warming Potential is an environmental impact category that exhibited higher variability in the PCR and PBG technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Global Warming Potential is an environmental impact indicator measuring greenhouse gas emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Global Warming Potential (GWP) is a key environmental impact category measured in the comparative analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Global warming potential is a primary indicator affecting phosphogypsum chemical transformation sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791593795</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ozone Depletion Potential">
  <data key="d0">Ozone Depletion Potential</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An environmental impact metric significantly influenced by quicklime consumption in PCR technology and electricity use in others.&lt;SEP&gt;Ozone Depletion Potential (ODP) is an environmental impact category where PSC Technology significantly reduces emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Ozone Depletion Potential is an environmental impact indicator measuring ozone-depleting substances.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity Analysis is a technique used to determine how variations in input parameters affect life cycle assessment results and identify sensitive factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A method identifying parameters like lime consumption and cement retarder substitution rates that significantly affect LCA results.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation technique used to assess how variations in assumptions like transportation distance affect results.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique conducted to evaluate the impact of uncertain parameters like Phosphogypsum dose, stack height, and transport distance.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity analysis is a method used to assess the effect of distance assumptions on LCA results.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity analysis is a procedural evaluation testing how parameter variations affect environmental scores.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity analysis is a technique used to evaluate how changes in main input parameters affect emergy-based indicator results.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792222593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chen, B.">
  <data key="d0">Chen, B.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A researcher cited in previous studies confirming the feasibility of using calcium carbide residue.&lt;SEP&gt;Chen, B. is a co-author of a 2022 study on the harmless treatment and directional stabilization of toxic substances in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who co-developed and optimized phosphogypsum-based geopolymer cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792177100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wu">
  <data key="d0">Wu</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wu is a researcher whose work primarily focuses on the utilization, treatment, and environmental management of industrial byproducts and solid waste, with a particular emphasis on phosphogypsum and calcium carbide residue. In the context of phosphogypsum, Wu has investigated its stable accompanying minerals and the origins of its toxic substances. To address these challenges, Wu et al. (2022b) identified calcination as an effective pretreatment technology, while also co-creating schematic diagrams that illustrate how toxic metal ions can be immobilized using CPGFM backfill. Furthermore, Wu has developed new phosphogypsum-based building materials designed to provide high structural strength while maintaining environmental protection standards.

Beyond phosphogypsum applications, Wu’s research extends to calcium carbide residue, where their work has been cited to confirm the feasibility of its practical utilization. In materials science, Wu reported that mesoporous hydroxyapatite synthesized using cetyltrimethyl ammonium bromide achieves the highest bovine serum albumin loading capacity. On a broader environmental management level, Wu is recognized for establishing a comprehensive solid waste evaluation system aimed at reducing pollution and enhancing recycling efficiency. Collectively, these contributions highlight Wu’s expertise in transforming hazardous industrial waste into valuable resources through advanced material synthesis, chemical immobilization, and systematic waste management frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcination Process">
  <data key="d0">Calcination Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A thermal process stage in PSC technology that accounts for approximately 60% of total coal use.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination Process is a heat treatment procedure applied to HAP at specific temperatures to induce phase transformations.</data>
