<node id="CO2 Sequestration">
  <data key="d0">CO2 Sequestration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CO2 Sequestration is the process of capturing and storing carbon dioxide to mitigate carbon emissions. In the context of industrial by-products, it is explored as an environmental application and a novel valorization route for phosphogypsum. This approach utilizes modified mineral carbonation, wherein phosphogypsum is chemically altered to react with and permanently store carbon dioxide. Through this mechanism, the material functions as an active medium for carbon capture and storage, transforming a waste stream into a functional resource.

Despite its clear environmental benefits and potential for sustainable utilization, CO2 sequestration currently represents the phosphogypsum application with the lowest volume of scientific literature. Research continues to propose phosphogypsum valorization as a targeted strategy for carbon mitigation, highlighting the need for expanded studies to fully develop, optimize, and validate this waste-to-resource pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012</data>
