</node>
<node id="Thermal Stability">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Stability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal Stability is a critical characteristic determining catalyst lifetime and material suitability for high-temperature applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal stability is a material property that hydroxyapatite enhances for supported gold nanoparticles, preventing degradation at high temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of materials analyzed through heating processes to observe mass loss and decomposition patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098909</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sintering">
  <data key="d0">Sintering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sintering is a process that converts hydroxyapatite into β-Tricalcium Phosphate, increasing calcium and phosphate ion availability for protein binding.&lt;SEP&gt;Sintering is a catalyst degradation process that hydroxyapatite's phosphate and hydroxyl groups help prevent.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal process indicated by necking among coalesced particles in heat-treated powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Sintering is a high-temperature process used to decompose phosphogypsum and red mud for metal extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Sintering is a thermal treatment applied to HA samples to improve crystallinity by incorporating amorphous surface atoms into the lattice.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acidic Centers">
  <data key="d0">Acidic Centers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acidic centers are surface features on hydroxyapatite that facilitate electrophilic attack of adsorbed oxygen, boosting oxidation activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen Activation">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Activation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen activation is a chemical process facilitated by electrons trapped in hydroxyapatite's vacancies, crucial for oxidation reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ha">
  <data key="d0">Ha</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ha is a researcher who investigated palladium-loaded hydroxyapatite for methane oxidation applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boukha">
  <data key="d0">Boukha</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Boukha is a researcher who validated the efficiency of palladium-loaded hydroxyapatite in methane oxidation reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Boukha is a researcher who studied cobalt-supported hydroxyapatite for 1,2-dichloroethane oxidation and gold-supported hydroxyapatite for CO elimination.&lt;SEP&gt;Boukha is a researcher who conducted studies on the applicability of hydroxyapatite supported gold in CO elimination processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wang">
  <data key="d0">Wang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wang is a researcher whose work spans materials science, catalysis, and environmental engineering, with a strong focus on industrial byproduct valorization and sustainable processing. In the field of catalysis, Wang reported that hydroxyapatite enhances the thermal stability of gold against sintering and conducted studies on the applicability of hydroxyapatite-supported gold in carbon monoxide elimination processes.

Wang’s research extensively covers geopolymer and cementitious systems, particularly those utilizing phosphogypsum. Wang investigated the production of geopolymer cement using beta-hemihydrate phosphogypsum, slag, fly ash, and an alkali activator, demonstrating that the resulting cement yields a non-crystalline geopolymer system known as CeSeH Gels. Further studies documented how the strength of CPGFM varies with different phosphogypsum and alkaline activator contents, while also highlighting the beneficial encapsulation of toxic elements through the interlacing of AFt and C-S-H gels during solidification.

Beyond material synthesis, Wang co-investigated a coupled process for potassium extraction and carbon dioxide mineralization. Wang also contributed to literature on the sustainable development of the phosphogypsum recycling industry and was cited regarding PGEF applications and environmental safety standards. Collectively, these contributions underscore Wang’s expertise in developing eco-friendly material processing techniques, advancing catalytic technologies, and ensuring environmental safety in industrial applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang is a researcher who investigated the impact of waste reuse on the sustainability of municipal solid waste incineration systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang is a researcher cited for dividing purchased inputs into renewable and nonrenewable resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Researcher cited for providing industrial solid waste land occupation data.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang confirmed that phosphogypsum could be used as a substitute for natural gypsum in self-leveling mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang is a researcher whose previous studies informed the examination of heavy metals in PG.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher cited regarding the ecological hazards of heavy metals in MPG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-015</data>
