<node id="Huang">
  <data key="d0">Huang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Huang is a researcher whose work spans environmental chemistry, materials science, and resource valorization. In the field of catalysis and gas treatment, Huang investigated hydroxyapatite-based materials, demonstrating that surface hydroxyls and the inherent basicity of hydroxyapatite significantly enhance nitrous oxide decomposition. Additionally, Huang conducted studies utilizing hydroxyapatite-supported gold catalysts specifically designed for carbon monoxide elimination processes.

A substantial portion of Huang’s research focuses on the valorization and application of phosphogypsum. Huang co-authored key references on phosphogypsum valorization processes and provided critical heavy metal concentration data for Chinese phosphogypsum solutions. Experimental work by Huang involved soaking phosphogypsum in a 4% citric acid solution, which resulted in increased compressive strength and improved microstructural densification. Furthermore, Huang studied the environmental benefits of phosphogypsum, particularly its capacity to reduce soil salinity and enhance overall soil fertility.

Beyond materials and environmental applications, Huang has contributed to resource sustainability and economic analysis. Huang emphasized the urgent need to produce potash fertilizer directly from K-feldspar to mitigate the depletion of soluble potassium reserves. In the realm of industrial and financial metrics, Huang is also cited as a reference source for net profit margin on sales and exposure risk metrics, highlighting a multidisciplinary approach that bridges laboratory research with practical economic and risk assessment frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Huang is a researcher who prepared concrete mixtures using pretreated PG and slag.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who manufactured binder materials with PG and slag, observing longer setting times with increased PG content.&lt;SEP&gt;Huang depicted higher expansion in specimens in 2010 manufactured from PG-steel slag-slag-limestone mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Huang is a researcher who studied the modification of phosphogypsum mixtures using sodium hydroxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
