  <data key="d2">Fish scales are animal waste sources successfully used to derive hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Fish scales are a waste material used as a source for preparing hydroxyapatite for selenite adsorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eggshells">
  <data key="d0">Eggshells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Eggshells are a natural, calcium-rich biogenic waste material derived from animals, primarily composed of calcite. Functioning as a valuable precursor, they are widely utilized as a starting source for the extraction and synthesis of hydroxyapatite and related calcium phosphate materials. From these eggshells, hydroxyapatite crystals can be successfully obtained through various processing methods.

Due to their chemical composition and inherent properties, eggshells serve as a referenced natural source material specifically for preparing hydroxyapatite for use as a bone graft material. Their role as a sustainable, biogenic waste product makes them an effective and economical foundation for biomedical applications requiring calcium phosphate derivatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792425629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mussel Shells">
  <data key="d0">Mussel Shells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mussel shells are biogenic waste products utilized as a source for hydroxyapatite extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Biogenic product derived from waste, utilized as a source for hydroxyapatite extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mussel shells are animal waste sources successfully used to derive hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthetic Hydroxyapatite (s-HAp) is a chemically engineered, manufactured form of the hydroxyapatite compound, characterized by higher purity and a specific surface area that surpasses naturally sourced materials. Produced as a nano-scale material, it is primarily synthesized from phosphogypsum using hydrothermal methods. The manufacturing process yields a purified solid product that is finalized through filtration and drying stages.

Designed to closely mimic natural bone ash, Synthetic Hydroxyapatite functions as a commercial and industrial substitute for bone ash in various applications. It is widely utilized as a bone substitute material in biomedical contexts. Additionally, its nano-scale properties make it a subject of study for defluoridation chemistry and equilibrium properties, underscoring its potential in environmental remediation and water treatment applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792425962</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Natural Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural hydroxyapatite is derived from bioresources and differs from synthetic forms due to lower purity, higher substitution, and lower specific surface area.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural hydroxyapatite is a biomineral extracted from Corbicula moltkiana freshwater clam shells for synthesis purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Hydroxyapatite is the dominant structure in natural bone ash after calcination, serving as a benchmark for synthetic particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791559146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca/P Value">
  <data key="d0">Ca/P Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ca/P value is a chemical ratio in hydroxyapatite that is influenced by alterations in compound purity and substitutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P value is a chemical ratio in hydroxyapatite that influences its purity and remediation efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Remediation">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Remediation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Remediation is a dedicated ecological application field focused on eliminating and mitigating pollution across air, water, and soil environments. This domain serves as a critical context for developing and implementing strategies that purify contaminated natural resources, with a specific emphasis on treating polluted wastewater and soil. By targeting multiple environmental matrices, the field aims to restore ecological balance and reduce the overall footprint of anthropogenic contaminants.

Within this application area, hydroxyapatite plays a central role due to its versatile chemical properties. The material is extensively utilized for its strong adsorption and sorption capacities, which effectively capture and remove pollutants from various media. Furthermore, synthesized and sustainable forms of hydroxyapatite function as advanced photocatalysts, enabling the light-driven degradation of persistent contaminants. Together, these mechanisms establish Environmental Remediation as a comprehensive framework for evaluating and deploying hydroxyapatite-based treatments to achieve sustainable pollution control and ecological restoration.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental remediation is an application area for sustainable photocatalysts derived from the synthesized Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Titanium Dioxide (TiO2)">
  <data key="d0">Titanium Dioxide (TiO2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Titanium dioxide is a photocatalyst that presents low adsorption ability and high electron-hole recombination but shows superior activity when combined with hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyapatite (Hap)">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite (Hap)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite is a material combined with titanium dioxide to form composites that enhance photocatalytic activity and reduce toxic intermediate production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silver Phosphate (Ag3PO4)">
  <data key="d0">Silver Phosphate (Ag3PO4)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silver phosphate is a compound coupled with hydroxyapatite to form a composite that improves photodegradation activity tenfold compared to the pure compound.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diclofenac (DCF)">
  <data key="d0">Diclofenac (DCF)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Diclofenac is a pharmaceutical compound effectively photodegraded by multiphasic hydroxyapatite–titanium dioxide material, reducing water toxicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluoxetine">
  <data key="d0">Fluoxetine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluoxetine is a micropollutant degraded with 100% maximum efficiency by the hydroxyapatite–titanium dioxide photocatalyst.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ofloxacin">
  <data key="d0">Ofloxacin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ofloxacin is an antibiotic photodegraded by zinc oxide-hydroxyapatite nanocomposites, which show greater activity than the oxide phase alone.&lt;SEP&gt;Ofloxacin is an antibiotic pollutant whose removal kinetics are evaluated using hydroxyapatite-based composite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ciprofloxacin">
  <data key="d0">Ciprofloxacin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ciprofloxacin is an antibiotic photodegraded by zinc oxide-hydroxyapatite nanocomposites.&lt;SEP&gt;Ciprofloxacin is an antibiotic pollutant whose removal kinetics are evaluated using hydroxyapatite-based composite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pentachlorophenol">
  <data key="d0">Pentachlorophenol</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pentachlorophenol is an organic pollutant efficiently photodegraded over titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composite.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound degraded by titania/hydroxyapatite composite photocatalysts with mosaic structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Formaldehyde">
  <data key="d0">Formaldehyde</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Formaldehyde is a carcinogenic volatile organic compound targeted for catalytic oxidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is an organic pollutant efficiently photodegraded over titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is a volatile organic compound whose catalytic oxidation was investigated over organic molecule-modified hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is a volatile organic compound oxidized by hydroxyapatite-stabilized gold nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;A compound combusted at room temperature using hydroxyapatite foam as a catalyst.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetaldehyde">
  <data key="d0">Acetaldehyde</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaldehyde is the dehydrogenation product of ethanol primarily produced over hydroxyapatite catalysts with high Ca/P Ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaldehyde is a compound decomposed photocatalytically by chromium(III)-doped titanium-hydroxyapatite particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitric Oxide (NO)">
  <data key="d0">Nitric Oxide (NO)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitric oxide is a gas produced during fuel combustion that is harmful to health and the environment, and is removed by titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen Dioxide (NO2)">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Dioxide (NO2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen dioxide is a harmful gas whose production as a toxic intermediate is considerably lessened over titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methylene Blue">
  <data key="d0">Methylene Blue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Methylene Blue is a dye efficiently degraded by hydroxyapatite acting as a photocatalyst under UV irradiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Methylene Blue is a synthetic dye and organic pollutant whose photodegradation is effectively enhanced by the TiO2/Hap composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Methylene blue is an organic dye whose photodegradation activity increased by 50% when titanium dioxide was combined with hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rhodamine B">
  <data key="d0">Rhodamine B</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Rhodamine B is a synthetic dye and organic pollutant whose degradation is studied using the TiO2/Hap composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodamine B is an organic dye photodegraded by silver phosphate-hydroxyapatite composites and iron(III)-substituted hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photocatalytic Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Photocatalytic Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Photocatalytic Degradation is the process of breaking down organic pollutants using light-activated catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is a process used to break down organic pollutants and pharmaceuticals using modified hydroxyapatite materials and composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is an environmental remediation process that breaks down organic pollutants like dyes using composite materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is a process studied for breaking down gaseous formaldehyde using hydroxyapatite-based catalysts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photocatalytic NOx Removal">
  <data key="d0">Photocatalytic NOx Removal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Photocatalytic NOx removal is a process utilizing modified hydroxyapatite materials to remove nitric oxides produced during fuel combustion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
