  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">BSA protein is a biological molecule studied for its release kinetics from hollow hydroxyapatite microspheres into polymer networks.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA Protein is a biological molecule studied for its adsorption and release behavior on hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA protein is a biomolecule whose adsorption and release dynamics were studied on hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA protein is studied for its adsorption and release behavior on hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA Protein is a negatively charged acidic protein whose adsorption on hydroxyapatite crystalline planes was investigated.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA Protein is an acidic protein studied for its adsorption behavior on hydroxyapatite surfaces.</data>
