<node id="Calcium Phosphates">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Phosphates constitute a broad chemical family and class of minerals that encompass compounds such as hydroxyapatite (HA). Recognized for their inherent biocompatibility and significant biological and medical relevance, this family is extensively characterized across foundational scientific literature. The materials exhibit notable physicochemical properties, including high thermal stability, distinct crystallization behaviors, and measurable electrochemical activity, making them subjects of rigorous analysis in solid-state chemistry.

The synthesis of Calcium Phosphates is highly tunable and typically relies on precipitation-based methods, where critical parameters such as pH and temperature dictate the final material structure. Advanced modified precipitation routes are frequently employed to enhance thermal stability, while sustainable raw materials, including chicken eggshells, are utilized as cost-effective precursors. Due to their tailored bioceramic nature and biocompatibility, Calcium Phosphates are widely applied in regenerative medicine and are extensively documented for their precipitation mechanisms and clinical significance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792406917</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
