</node>
<node id="Cadmium Ions">
  <data key="d0">Cadmium Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cadmium Ions are metal cations that preferentially occupy Ca(II) sites in the apatite structure due to higher electronegativity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadmium ions are toxic heavy metal pollutants in aqueous solutions that cause severe health problems and are targeted for removal by the developed adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metal ions present in wastewater that are targeted for removal by the adsorbents.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metal ions targeted for removal from wastewater using the HPA-HAP composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadmium Ions are heavy metal ions targeted for removal from aqueous solutions and wastewater using various adsorbents.&lt;SEP&gt;Metal ions (Cd²⁺) that exhibit significantly higher adsorption capacity than cobalt ions across tested doping levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791652804</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strontium Ions">
  <data key="d0">Strontium Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Strontium Ions are metal cations that preferentially occupy Ca(II) sites in the apatite structure due to a larger ionic radius.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791247038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lead Ions">
  <data key="d0">Lead Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead ions (Pb2+) are toxic heavy metal cations that function as significant environmental contaminants. Chemically characterized by a larger ionic radius and higher electronegativity compared to calcium, these ions preferentially occupy Ca(II) sites within apatite crystal structures. In aqueous environments, they chemically react with hydroxylapatite granules and exhibit strong affinity for various adsorbent materials.

Due to their toxicity and persistence, lead ions are a primary target for removal from wastewater and other aqueous solutions. Remediation strategies frequently employ hydroxyapatite-based technologies, including nano-materials, powders, granules, composites, and chemically modified variants. Additionally, environmental studies have demonstrated the effective adsorption of lead ions by biochar and hydroxyapatite-biochar nanocomposites. Through these chemical reactions and adsorption mechanisms, hydroxyapatite and its advanced composites serve as critical agents in mitigating heavy metal contamination in water systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead ions are Pb2+ ions whose thermodynamics in Haplic Chernozem soil solution are modeled to justify environmentally safe phosphogypsum recycling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonate Anions">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Anions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate Anions are anionic substitutes that replace hydroxide ions in the apatite lattice to enhance its acidity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791247038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
