<node id="Heterogeneous Catalysis">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous Catalysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heterogeneous catalysis is a scientific field where hydroxyapatite has been previously studied, though not the focus of this review.&lt;SEP&gt;Heterogeneous Catalysis is a field where solid catalysts' acid-base properties play a key role in driving catalytic performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Heterogeneous Catalysis is a field where the acid-base properties of solid catalysts drive the activity and selectivity of chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Heterogeneous catalysis involves using solid catalysts, such as hydroxyapatite-supported materials, to drive chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Heterogeneous catalysis is a chemical application domain where hydroxyapatite is utilized due to its structural properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791655882</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FTIR">
  <data key="d0">FTIR</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR), occasionally referred to as Fourier Transformed-Infrared Spectroscopy, is a fundamental spectroscopic and analytical technique that measures the absorption of infrared light to identify specific chemical bonds, molecular vibrations, and functional groups. By providing detailed insights into the chemical composition and structural properties of diverse inorganic and organic materials, FTIR serves as an indispensable tool across materials science and biomedical research. The method is routinely applied to evaluate complex substances, analyze protein structures, confirm the successful loading or binding of biomolecules onto material surfaces, investigate chemical interactions between adsorbents and adsorbed metal ions, and examine the spectra of specific compounds such as the Brij-93 surfactant.

A primary application of FTIR involves the comprehensive characterization of hydroxyapatite (HAp) and apatite-based systems, including synthesized HAp samples and carbonated hydroxyapatite powders. The technique verifies crystal structures, distinguishes specific HAp phases through characteristic phosphate (PO4) and hydroxyl (OH) ion peaks, and detects organic functional groups within the HAp matrix. It is specifically utilized to confirm the presence of oxygen vacancies on the O-H group of HAp and to study ion accommodation mechanisms, such as carbonate ion substitution within apatite crystal lattices. Furthermore, FTIR results regarding these structural features have been shown to align consistently with X-ray diffraction (XRD) findings, including observations on the inhibitory effects of HPA on crystal growth.

Beyond apatite materials, FTIR is extensively employed to analyze calcium carbonate and related compounds. It identifies chemical bonds and vibration modes within calcium carbonate and its associated impurities, and facilitates the detailed analysis and comparison of synthetic versus commercial calcium carbonate samples. Through these diverse analytical capabilities, FTIR remains a versatile and essential method for verifying chemical structures, confirming specific bonds, and elucidating the physicochemical properties of a wide range of inorganic and organic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic method using Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy to analyze molecular structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic method used to analyze the chemical composition and identify impurities in MPG.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy used to reinvestigate the molecular spectra of synthetic brushite.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR is a characterization technique used to identify the addition of A and B Type Carbonated Substituted HA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
