  <data key="d2">Fluoroapatite is a thermodynamically stable apatite variant where the Y site is occupied by fluoride ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoroapatite is a fluorine-substituted apatite powder subjected to thermal analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoroapatite is a fluorine-substituted calcium phosphate compound studied alongside hydroxyapatite for conversion and oxidation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A calcium phosphate material compared with hydroxyapatite for catalytic activity in butan-2-ol conversion and methane oxidation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-025</data>
