<node id="Biomedical Applications">
  <data key="d0">Biomedical Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biomedical Applications are a primary field where hydroxyapatite's thermal and chemical stability makes it an attractive material.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomedical Applications represent potential uses for nano-hydroxyapatite that require effective purification methods to remove phosphogypsum-based impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomedical Applications are potential uses for the powders involving the adsorption of proteins and cells on their surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;The intended use of synthesized hydroxyapatite nanostructures in medical and therapeutic contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Fields where Hydroxyapatite is commonly utilized due to its properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary field of use for Hydroxyapatite due to its biocompatibility and ceramic properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomedical applications represent a primary field where hydroxyapatite is utilized due to its properties as a calcium phosphate ceramic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
