<node id="Heat Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Heat Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat Treatment is a post-synthesis thermal processing step primarily applied to hydroxyapatite powders and related samples to systematically modify their physical, structural, and chemical properties. The procedure typically involves heating the materials at 900 °C for specified durations, most frequently three hours, although one record cites a negative temperature value that is likely a typographical error. This controlled thermal exposure fundamentally alters the material's crystalline architecture by increasing both crystallite size and the overall degree of crystallinity. These structural advancements are corroborated by an increased intensity of characteristic spectroscopic peaks, confirming the successful sintering and stabilization of the hydroxyapatite matrix.

In addition to crystalline modifications, the thermal process significantly impacts the material's surface and pore characteristics. Heating at 900 °C induces pore collapse and widens the pore size distribution, effectively shifting the structural framework from purely mesoporous to a combined meso- and macroporous configuration. This restructuring concurrently reduces the overall surface area while directly enhancing the material's functional performance. Specifically, the treatment optimizes adsorption characteristics at low pressures and substantially improves adsorption capacity for both acidic and basic proteins. Consequently, Heat Treatment serves as a critical evaluation and optimization parameter for tailoring hydroxyapatite powders, with its precise effects on crystal morphology, size, and surface properties being carefully controlled to meet specific application requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat Treatment is a calcination process applied to phosphogypsum to enhance its cementing value and mechanical performance in mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat treatment is a process involving heating phosphogypsum at specific temperatures to enhance its performance as a replacement material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
