<node id="Teeth">
  <data key="d0">Teeth</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Teeth are biological structures and human hard tissues that function as natural sources of hydroxyapatite crystals. Primarily composed of apatites and hydroxyapatite, this mineral serves as the main structural component throughout the tissue, with particularly high concentrations localized in the enamel layer. The mineral makeup of teeth is fundamentally similar to that of bone, establishing a consistent biological framework across hard human tissues.

This hydroxyapatite-rich composition is directly responsible for the structural hardness and strength characteristic of teeth. In addition to their natural physiological role, the properties of this mineral have been adapted for clinical use, with synthetic hydroxyapatite derived from or modeled after dental structures being extensively utilized for various dental applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792001842</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
