<node id="Apatites">
  <data key="d0">Apatites</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Apatites are a mineral group with the general formula Me10(XO4)6Y2 that crystallize in the hexagonal system.&lt;SEP&gt;Apatites are a group of natural calcium phosphate minerals with a general stoichiometry close to Ca10(PO4)6Y2.&lt;SEP&gt;Apatites are naturally occurring phosphate minerals studied for their structure, properties, and applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-031</data>
