<node id="Catalysis">
  <data key="d0">Catalysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalysis is a field of application for hydroxyapatite, where it functions as a catalyst, photocatalyst, or active phase support.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical process where hydroxyapatite acts as a catalyst, photocatalyst, or active phase support to improve reaction performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Catalysis is a vital environmental application of hydroxyapatite that accelerates chemical reactions like biodiesel synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791247343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hexagonal Crystal System">
  <data key="d0">Hexagonal Crystal System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The crystallographic structure classification for hydroxyapatite, characterized by specific lattice parameters and space group P63/m.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002</data>
