  <data key="d5">1791900752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P63/m Space Group">
  <data key="d0">P63/m Space Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The P63/m space group defines the crystallographic symmetry of the hexagonal system in which hydroxyapatite crystallizes.&lt;SEP&gt;P63/m Space Group is the specific crystallographic symmetry group identified in the hydroxyapatite particles.&lt;SEP&gt;P63/m Space Group is the specific crystallographic space group defining the hexagonal structure of the synthesized hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lattice Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Lattice Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Lattice parameters are the approximate structural measurements for hydroxyapatite, with a = 9.37 Å and c = 6.88 Å.&lt;SEP&gt;Lattice parameters a = 9.423 Å and c = 6.883 Å characterize the crystal structure of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Lattice parameters (a = 9.987 Å, c = 7.33 Å) define the unit cell dimensions of hexagonal pyromorphite.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural measurements characterizing the crystal structure of the synthesized HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural metrics calculated from XRD data to describe the geometric dimensions of the HAp crystal unit cell.&lt;SEP&gt;Lattice Parameters are structural measurements determined by XRD analysis for synthesized hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Lattice parameters include the a and c dimensions and their ratio, which are measured via XRD analysis to characterize hydroxyapatite crystallinity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca(I) Ions">
  <data key="d0">Ca(I) Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ca(I) ions are a specific type of calcium ion that borders the first channel in the hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
