<node id="Kumar">
  <data key="d0">Kumar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kumar, a researcher in materials science and environmental engineering, has conducted extensive work on sustainable construction materials and brick manufacturing. In a 2002 study, Kumar investigated the use of calcined phosphogypsum combined with fly ash and lime binders to produce bricks. By manufacturing bricks with varying percentages of calcined phosphogypsum, the research demonstrated that adjusting the phosphogypsum content directly influences material density. Additionally, higher concentrations of calcined phosphogypsum were found to reduce water absorption while significantly improving the compressive strength of the bricks, particularly when subjected to heat curing. Building on this work, Kumar also noted that hollow blocks could serve as a practical and effective substitute for traditional hollow concrete blocks and clay bricks.

In a separate area of research focused on catalysis and environmental remediation, Kumar explored advanced catalyst formulations. The study demonstrated that well-dispersed silver oxide supported on apatite carriers yields optimal DeNOx activity among the tested catalysts. Together, these findings underscore Kumar’s contributions to both the development of eco-friendly building materials and the optimization of catalytic processes for nitrogen oxide reduction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lin">
  <data key="d0">Lin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lin is a researcher whose academic contributions span materials science, environmental chemistry, and geotechnical engineering, with a pronounced emphasis on phosphogypsum utilization and advanced composite development. In the field of phosphogypsum applications, Lin has conducted extensive investigations into its chemical behavior and structural modifications. This includes employing X-ray absorption spectroscopy to examine uranium speciation within phosphogypsum, optimizing parameters to efficiently synthesize alpha-hemihydrate gypsum whiskers from the material, and co-investigating the impact of sodium hydroxide on phosphogypsum-based mixtures. Lin also co-authored research on the setting time variations of phosphogypsum-steel slag-slag-limestone mixtures and co-conducted a 2010 study analyzing the expansion of phosphogypsum-based cementitious specimens.

Beyond phosphogypsum research, Lin has contributed to the development of a polyaniline/HPA/ZrO2/epoxy composite coating specifically engineered for marine metal protection. In environmental catalysis, Lin verified the advantages of hydroxyapatite basicity for nitrous oxide decomposition, identifying RhOx/Hap as the most active catalyst. Additionally, Lin’s scholarly work encompasses the synthesis of multilevel heterogeneous soil architectures. Collectively, these diverse projects demonstrate Lin’s expertise in sustainable material processing, corrosion mitigation, and environmental remediation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452838</data>
