<node id="Carbonate Groups">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate groups are surface components that enrich hydroxyapatite when copper acetate is used, negatively impacting SCR activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate groups are chemical functional groups identified by absorption dips around 1600 cm⁻¹ representing asymmetric stretching.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical groups detected via FT-IR spectroscopy, suggesting the presence of c-HAp impurities in synthetic hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate groups are chemical structures detected in portlandite samples, indicated by specific absorption bands in the FTIR spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical groups whose presence reveals a possible carbonated hydroxyapatite structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate groups are chemical bonds detected in the spectrum, indicating possible impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-003</data>
