<node id="Sorption">
  <data key="d0">Sorption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An efficient and economical technique for immobilizing pollutants using hydroxyapatite as a sorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Sorption is a chemical process where rare earth elements bind to ion exchange resins during phosphogypsum treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Sorption is a mechanism studied for fluoride in soil interacting with phosphogypsum leachate and for arsenic on red mud.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423470</data>
