  <data key="d0">Pb2+</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pb2+ is a divalent cation that can substitute for Ca2+ in apatite structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Pb2+ is the water-soluble and free-form lead ion whose low concentration in soil reduces adverse effects on plants.&lt;SEP&gt;Pb2+ (lead ions) are reduced in mobility and bioavailability due to the soil-root biogeochemical barrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Pb2+ refers to lead ions, which undergo passivation processes in the studied plant organogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-014</data>
