<node id="Thermochim. Acta">
  <data key="d0">Thermochim. Acta</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermochim. Acta is a scientific journal dedicated to thermochimical research and thermal analysis. It primarily publishes studies that utilize thermogravimetric analysis and kinetic evaluations to investigate the thermal properties and decomposition behaviors of various chemical compounds and mineral materials. The journal maintains a strong focus on advancing understanding in thermal chemistry through rigorous experimental and analytical reporting.

The publication has featured a diverse range of specific studies, including research on the thermal decomposition of hexahydrated nickel iron citrate and kinetic analyses of calcium carbonate decomposition. It has also published extensive work on phosphogypsum, covering its thermal behavior, a two-step decomposition approach, and thermogravimetric analyses of reactions involving both gypsum and phosphogypsum. Additionally, the journal disseminated a notable 2001 study examining the temperature effects on hydroxyapatite properties.

As a recognized academic resource, Thermochim. Acta is frequently cited in scientific reference lists, underscoring its role as a credible and influential venue for disseminating peer-reviewed research in the field of thermal analysis and thermochimistry.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermochim. Acta is the academic journal that published the 1997 study on the thermal behavior of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033</data>
