<node id="HAp">
  <data key="d0">HAp</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp, the standard abbreviation for hydroxyapatite, is a synthesized nanocrystalline ceramic material extensively investigated across materials science, biomaterials, and chemical engineering. It is typically produced via hydrothermal conversion, often starting from PPG, where it crystallizes as the final phase after 15 hours at a pH of 11. The material's structural evolution and final morphology are significantly influenced by the shape transformation of CC, while its growth can be precisely regulated through the addition of CTAB and citrate. Structurally, HAp predominantly forms rod-shaped particles, nanorods, or microcrystals featuring specialized hierarchical architectures and mesoporous characteristics. It is rigorously characterized by its crystalline structure, specific [Ca]/[P] ratio, chemical composition, textural properties, and functional groups.

In research and practical applications, HAp serves as a versatile target and unmodified baseline material. Its unique physicochemical and semiconductor properties, including distinct flat band potentials and efficient charge separation capabilities, make it highly suitable for photocatalytic applications, where it is often utilized as a pristine semiconductor sample. Simultaneously, its biocompatible surface and mesoporous nature allow it to function effectively as a biomaterial substrate for protein adsorption and as a targeted drug delivery carrier. Consequently, HAp remains a foundational and highly regulated nanomaterial in both biomedical engineering and advanced photocatalytic studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
