<node id="Citrate">
  <data key="d0">Citrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Citrate is a bioorganic micromolecule used as an additive to regulate the nucleation and crystal growth of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrate is a molecule that chelates calcium ions, provides nucleation sites for HAp, and modifies crystal aggregation modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrate is a chelating agent that controls calcium ion release and promotes the orderly self-assembly of HAp building blocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrate is a chemical compound used synergistically with CTAB to control the morphology of hydroxyapatite microcrystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrate is a chemical compound used synergistically with CTAB to control the morphology of hydroxyapatite microcrystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
