<node id="Trisodium Citrate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Trisodium Citrate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Trisodium citrate dihydrate is a chemical reagent dissolved to form the precursor solution for hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Trisodium citrate dihydrate is a chemical used alongside CTAB to synthesize 3D hierarchical superstructures of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Trisodium citrate dihydrate is a chemical used alongside CTAB to synthesize 3D hierarchical superstructures of Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Nitrate Tetrahydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Nitrate Tetrahydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium nitrate tetrahydrate is a chemical reagent and primary calcium precursor utilized across various synthesis and preparation methodologies. Functioning as a key calcium source, it is typically dissolved in distilled water to generate a calcium salt solution that supplies essential calcium ions for subsequent reactions. In specific protocols, the compound may be dehydrated through heating to prepare a synthetic calcium nitrate solution tailored for extraction trials.

This versatile starting material plays a central role in multiple advanced synthesis routes, including the NoSurf synthesis method, precipitation techniques, microwave-assisted synthesis, and hydrothermal preparation processes. Notably, it is extensively employed as a fundamental reactant in the production of hydroxyapatite, serving both in solution-based synthesis and in the fabrication of hydroxyapatite powder. Overall, calcium nitrate tetrahydrate acts as a critical chemical starting material that initiates and facilitates diverse material synthesis and extraction procedures by delivering controlled calcium ion concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydrated form of calcium nitrate (Ca(NO3)2 · 4H2O) used as a chemical precursor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792262255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammonium Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Ammonium Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonium phosphate is a chemical reagent dissolved to provide phosphate ions for hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Phosphate is a class of phosphate fertilizer products derived from phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Phosphate is a chemical compound dissolved in water to react with calcium chloride for nanocomposite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium phosphate is a chemical precursor dissolved to initiate the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Phosphate is a chemical compound represented as (NH4)2HPO4, likely used in synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792262255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guangzhou Chemical Corporation">
  <data key="d0">Guangzhou Chemical Corporation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Guangzhou Chemical Corporation is the supplier of analytically pure chemicals used in the experimental preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomineralization">
  <data key="d0">Biomineralization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biomineralization is a natural process involving the assembly of biomacromolecules that inspired the study's synthetic approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomineralization is a rapid process exhibited by eggshell-derived hydroxyapatite upon contact with human tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomineralization is a biological process where nano-HAp's cytophilicity and biological activity play a significant role.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791855082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Precipitation">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Precipitation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical precipitation is a chemical-processing route used to synthesize hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;A method applied to remove heavy metals from the environment, noted for potential drawbacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical precipitation is the primary removal mechanism responsible for Pb(II) uptake by HAP-BC.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Precipitation is a synthesis procedure involving solution-based solid formation, utilized for producing nano hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Precipitation is a pre-treatment process applied to electroplating wastewater before analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791653869</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
