</node>
<node id="Tooth Enamel">
  <data key="d0">Tooth Enamel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Tooth enamel is a natural biological structure where citrate plays a role in apatite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tooth enamel is a biological material whose self-organized microstructure and crystallites are studied and mimicked using hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Tooth Enamel is a biological material whose microstructure is mimicked by hydroxyapatite crystallites.&lt;SEP&gt;Tooth enamel is the hard outer layer of teeth, whose crystalline structure closely resembles that of HAp Type 6.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
