</node>
<node id="O-H Stretching">
  <data key="d0">O-H Stretching</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A broad, shallow dip around 3400–3500 cm⁻¹ in Curve A, characteristic of water or hydroxyl groups.&lt;SEP&gt;O-H Stretching is a vibrational mode in the high wavenumber region associated with hydroxyl groups and water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfate Groups">
  <data key="d0">Sulfate Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical groups responsible for a significant, broad absorption feature around 1000–1100 cm⁻¹ across all spectral curves.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate groups are chemical components used as a reference denominator to normalize the carbonate signal in the calibration equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate Groups are chemical groups characteristic of PPG that are absent in the synthesized HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate Groups are chemical groups characteristic of PPG that are absent in the synthesized HAp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792190541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonate Ions">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate ions are chemical species (CO3 2-) that originate from the dissociation of carbonic acid and readily react with divalent cations to form solid precipitates. In various material and environmental contexts, they function as atmospheric components or trace impurities that significantly influence the chemical composition of target structures. Within crystalline frameworks, particularly apatite and hydroxyapatite lattices, carbonate ions frequently substitute for phosphate or hydroxyl groups during synthesis. This substitution occurs both within the bulk lattice and on the surfaces of synthesized powders, with adsorption being notably enhanced on surfactant-produced powders due to their increased surface area.

Analytically, carbonate ions are routinely quantified as a percentage impurity in samples such as phosphogypsum, utilizing derived calibration equations for precise measurement. Spectroscopically, they manifest as a distinct chemical group exhibiting two vibrational modes within the sample structure. Their asymmetric stretching vibrations are particularly characteristic, becoming increasingly sharp and distinct under specific analytical conditions, such as those documented in curves E and F. Together, these properties define their behavior across synthesis, structural integration, and analytical characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions are adsorbed onto the surface of Hydroxyapatite, with adsorption capacity increased by the presence of CTAB.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate Ions partially substitute phosphate groups in the Hydroxyapatite lattice due to atmospheric carbon dioxide capture.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions are adsorbed onto the surface of Hydroxyapatite, with adsorption capacity increased by the presence of CTAB.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate Ions partially substitute phosphate groups in the Hydroxyapatite lattice due to atmospheric carbon dioxide capture.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions are ligands that form complexes with lead, contributing to the KasPb calculation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792343567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
