<node id="Grinding">
  <data key="d0">Grinding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Grinding is a mechanical and physical treatment process that serves distinct purposes across different industrial and chemical applications. In the context of rare earth element recovery, grinding is applied to phosphogypsum as a physicochemical pre-treatment and physical preparation method. This operation reduces particle size, optimizes particle size distribution, and enhances leaching efficiency and rare earth element recovery prior to extraction. Specific implementations involve mechanically processing dried phosphogypsum using an electromagnetic pulverizer for approximately three minutes to increase the concentration of rare earth elements before extraction.

In the broader context of chemical phosphoric acid production, grinding refers to the mechanical step used to finely process feed rock. This operation is widely recognized as the most energy-intensive stage of the chemical phosphoric acid manufacturing process. Additionally, in certain material processing workflows, grinding functions as a post-calcination step designed to produce the final desired powder form. Across all applications, grinding fundamentally acts as a size-reduction and physical modification technique essential for optimizing material properties and downstream chemical recovery or production efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Grinding is a mechanical processing step whose duration is reduced when processing phosphogypsum-modified clinker.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
