<node id="pH 11">
  <data key="d0">pH 11</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pH 11 is the target acidity level reached by adding ammonium hydroxide during the reaction phase.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 11 is a synthesis parameter that produced hydroxyapatite powders with higher carbonation compared to pH 9.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 11 is the alkaline condition required to provide sufficient hydroxide ions for the complete hydrolysis of calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 11 is the alkaline medium condition required for obtaining phase-pure hydroxyapatite during synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 11 is the alkaline condition maintained during the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkaline pH condition required for complete hydrolysis of CaSO₄ and formation of HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 11 represents an experimental condition corresponding to a highly alkaline sample analyzed in the X-ray diffraction study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-010</data>
