<node id="Nano-Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Nano-Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Nano-Hydroxyapatite is a synthesized material with high crystallinity and a calcium-phosphate structure, explored for wastewater treatment, biomedical applications, and as an alternative phosphorus fertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;Nano-hydroxyapatite is a nanomaterial studied for its high adsorption capacity toward dissolved heavy metals and mixed metallic ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nano-Hydroxyapatite is a material whose crystal structure is compared to Phosphogypsum using X-ray Diffraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Product sample labeled nHAp, displaying characteristic diffraction peaks confirming successful synthesis.</data>
