<node id="Tap Water">
  <data key="d0">Tap Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water used to mix with PG to obtain a homogenous slurry.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water is commonly used in the actual preparation of CPGFM, differing from experimental deionized water.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water is a solvent used throughout all steps of the preparation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water serves as the solvent used to mix with phosphogypsum during the initial preparation step.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water is a washing medium used in various phosphogypsum treatment protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water is used as a purification method for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Tap water is used to slurry treated PG before applying ultrasonic vibration in Potgieter's physical treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792483993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammonia Solution">
  <data key="d0">Ammonia Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A solution used to adjust the pH to 11 during the synthesis process.&lt;SEP&gt;An agent used for pH adjustment during the NoSurf synthesis route.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonia Solution is used to adjust the pH of the ammonium hydrogen phosphate solution to 12.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonia solution is used to adjust and maintain the pH of the synthesis solution at 10 during precipitation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonia solution is used to adjust the pH of the reaction mixture to approximately 11.0.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonia solution is used to adjust the reaction pH to 11 during the synthesis process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792003010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alkaline Medium">
  <data key="d0">Alkaline Medium</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical environment (pH:11) where high purity nHA can be obtained.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline Medium refers to the high pH environment required to obtain phase-pure Hydroxyapatite during synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;An alkaline medium is recommended as the optimal solution for dissolving and converting phosphogypsum waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019</data>
