<node id="Competitive Adsorption">
  <data key="d0">Competitive Adsorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Competitive Adsorption refers to the simultaneous sorption of multiple heavy metal ions in contaminated water.&lt;SEP&gt;Competitive adsorption refers to the simultaneous adsorption of multiple ions, studied by introducing coexisting cations into the heavy metal solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Competitive adsorption is the process studied to understand how multiple heavy metals interact with adsorbents in mixed solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Competitive adsorption refers to the simultaneous uptake of multiple metal ions by an adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Competitive Adsorption is the process where multiple heavy metal ions simultaneously compete for binding sites on the adsorbent surface.&lt;SEP&gt;Competitive adsorption describes the process where multiple substances compete for binding sites on an adsorbent surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791287728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
