<node id="Carbonate Group">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate Group is a chemical group identified by a peak at 1467 cm⁻¹ in the HAP-BC spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonate Group is a chemical substituent that partially replaces phosphate groups in the Hydroxyapatite lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate Group is a chemical component (CO3 2-) that partially substitutes phosphate groups in the HAp lattice due to atmospheric carbon dioxide entrapment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonate Group (CO3^2-) substitutes phosphate groups in HAp due to atmospheric CO2 adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonate group is an ionic species produced by urea hydrolysis that incorporates into the hydroxyapatite lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonate Group (CO3^2-) substitutes phosphate groups in HAp due to atmospheric CO2 adsorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-009</data>
