<node id="P-O Bond">
  <data key="d0">P-O Bond</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The P-O Bond is a fundamental chemical linkage that forms within phosphate groups and phosphorus pentoxide (P2O5). It serves as a critical structural component in various synthesized materials, particularly hydroxyapatite (HAp) and HAP-BC. Through Fourier-transform infrared (FTIR) spectroscopy, the P-O Bond is characterized by its distinct stretching and bending vibrations, which produce specific absorption peaks essential for material identification.

Detailed spectral analysis reveals that the bending vibration of the P-O Bond appears at a peak of 933 cm⁻¹ in the HAP-BC spectrum. Furthermore, the bond is detectable at specific binding energies within the P 2p spectra, providing complementary data on its chemical environment. Despite its structural significance in HAp, the P-O Bond is noted to exhibit notably diminished spectral intensity in this matrix. Collectively, these spectroscopic features highlight the P-O Bond's vital role in the chemical and structural analysis of phosphate-based compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792188341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
