<node id="Freundlich Constant">
  <data key="d0">Freundlich Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Freundlich Constant (K_F) is a parameter derived from the Freundlich isotherm model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Freundlich constant is an indicator of adsorption capacity in the Freundlich adsorption isotherm model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intercept">
  <data key="d0">Intercept</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The intercept of the plotted line is used to determine the Freundlich constant K_F.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slope">
  <data key="d0">Slope</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The slope of the plotted line is used to determine the parameter n.&lt;SEP&gt;Slope refers to the geometric extension of the subbase layer outward beyond the upper pavement layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The slope is a mathematical property of the linear regression line that is directly proportional to the activation energy.&lt;SEP&gt;The slope refers to the gradient of a plotted line used to determine activation energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792363903</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isoelectric Point">
  <data key="d0">Isoelectric Point</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The isoelectric point represents the zero potential level on the zeta potential graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adsorbate">
  <data key="d0">Adsorbate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The adsorbate is the substance being adsorbed by the adsorbent at equilibrium.&lt;SEP&gt;The target substance that is removed from the solution by the adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbate refers to the substance being removed from a solution, such as Fluoride or heavy metals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pollutant">
  <data key="d0">Pollutant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The pollutant is the substance removed from water by the phosphogypsum adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;A target substance dissolved in a solution that is removed by an adsorbent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equilibrium is the state at which the amount of adsorbate adsorbed per unit mass is measured.&lt;SEP&gt;Equilibrium shifts under lower pH conditions, promoting the dissolution of phases.&lt;SEP&gt;The state reached after 40 minutes of contact time where extraction efficiency no longer increases with duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Equilibrium represents the state where adsorption capacity plateaus and no further net uptake occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Equilibrium is the chemical state of the solution relative to atmospheric CO2 or soil carbonates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792345946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adsorption Intensity">
  <data key="d0">Adsorption Intensity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorption intensity relates to the surface heterogeneity and is represented by the parameter n.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015</data>
