</node>
<node id="Langmuir Isotherm">
  <data key="d0">Langmuir Isotherm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Langmuir Isotherm is a mathematical model used to describe monolayer adsorption processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical model used to describe monolayer adsorption and calculate adsorption constants for HAP-BC.&lt;SEP&gt;An equilibrium model describing adsorption relationships, represented by a non-linear equation involving maximum adsorption and an adsorption constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318011</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freundlich Isotherm">
  <data key="d0">Freundlich Isotherm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Freundlich Isotherm is a mathematical model used to describe multilayer adsorption processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical model used to describe multilayer adsorption and calculate adsorption constants for HAP-BC.&lt;SEP&gt;An equilibrium model tested to accurately fit experimental adsorption data for process design.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical model for adsorption equilibrium written in non-linear form, characterized by constants K_F and n_F.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monolayer Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Monolayer Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monolayer Coverage is a process where ions form a single layer on an adsorbent surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009</data>
