<node id="Ca(II)">
  <data key="d0">Ca(II)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A divalent cation that reduces the removal percentage of Cu(II) and Zn(II) through competitive uptake.&lt;SEP&gt;Ca(II) is a coexisting cation in water that competes with heavy metals during the adsorption process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010</data>
