<node id="Ce">
  <data key="d0">Ce</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ce is a symbol representing the equilibrium concentration of a pollutant remaining after adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerium, a rare earth element whose extraction efficiency was measured under varying concentrations and temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ce is a rare earth element ion whose stripping efficiency from loaded ionic liquid is investigated under varying experimental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A trace element measured in parts per million in the provided analytical data.&lt;SEP&gt;Ce is a chemical element listed in a tabular dataset with associated numerical measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerium is a chemical element represented by the symbol Ce.&lt;SEP&gt;Ce is the symbol for Equilibrium Concentration in the percentage removal formula.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
