<node id="Hydroxyapatite-Biochar Nanocomposite">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite-Biochar Nanocomposite</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite-Biochar Nanocomposite is a fabricated material used as an adsorbent for heavy metal removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite-Biochar Nanocomposite is a fabricated composite material combining hydroxyapatite and biochar to enhance heavy metal adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite-biochar nanocomposite is a fabricated material combining the advantages of both components to remove lead, copper, and zinc ions.&lt;SEP&gt;A composite material combining hydroxyapatite and biochar used for competitive adsorption of metal ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791653062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pseudo-Second-Order Model">
  <data key="d0">Pseudo-Second-Order Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudo-Second-Order Model is a kinetic model that best fits the adsorption of heavy metal ions onto the nanocomposite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Langmuir Model">
  <data key="d0">Langmuir Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Langmuir Model describes the adsorption isotherm of Pb(II) onto the nanocomposite.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical model for adsorption that showed a lower correlation coefficient (above 0.77) compared to other models in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freundlich Model">
  <data key="d0">Freundlich Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Freundlich Model describes the adsorption isotherms of Cu(II) and Zn(II) onto the nanocomposite.&lt;SEP&gt;Freundlich Model is an isotherm model that better represents the adsorption process, indicating a non-monolayer adsorption mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;An isotherm model indicating that the adsorption process involves non-monolayer surface coverage.&lt;SEP&gt;Freundlich Model is a mathematical model that provides a better representation of the adsorption process than other models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Freundlich Model is a theoretical framework used to analyze adsorption equilibrium data through fitted curves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
