  <data key="d0">Type IV Isotherm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorption isotherm type indicating mesoporous structures in BC.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of adsorption isotherm exhibited by the HAp particles according to IUPAC standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV isotherm is a classification of N2 sorption isotherms indicating mesoporous features in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV isotherm is a classification of N2 sorption isotherms indicating mesoporous features in the samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010</data>
