</node>
<node id="Gas Adsorption-Desorption Isotherm">
  <data key="d0">Gas Adsorption-Desorption Isotherm</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The gas adsorption-desorption isotherm is a scientific chart used to analyze the porosity and surface area of solid materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791289149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Composites">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Composites</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum composites are solid materials analyzed for porosity and surface area using gas adsorption-desorption isotherms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791289149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Area">
  <data key="d0">Surface Area</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface Area is a fundamental physical and material property that quantifies the total exposed surface of a substance, typically expressed in square meters per gram. In materials science, it is routinely characterized using gas adsorption-desorption isotherms, with nitrogen adsorption serving as a standard technique for determining the specific surface area of powdered samples. This property is highly sensitive to a material's microstructure, particle morphology, and processing history.

The behavior of Surface Area varies significantly across different materials and conditions. In phosphogypsum fractions, it decreases as grain size increases, a relationship that directly impacts radon exhalation rates. For hydroxyapatite (HA) powders and crystals, Surface Area is markedly enhanced by the incorporation of surfactants, which can increase the value up to threefold. Conversely, thermal processing consistently reduces this property, as heat treatment leads to a substantial and significant decrease in the surface area of HA samples. These characteristics highlight Surface Area's critical role in evaluating material performance and structural modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface area is a textural property of mesoporous hydroxyapatite that influences drug adsorption and release rates.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific surface area of the synthesized HAp sample is 86.29 m^2/g.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface Area is a measurable property of the hydroxyapatite nanopowder that can be regulated using the MSS2 reactor.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface area is a material property determined using nitrogen adsorption-desorption isotherm plots.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface area of HAp on the FTO thin film electrode, a variable in the carrier density calculation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792190223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Materials Science">
  <data key="d0">Materials Science</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Materials science is the academic discipline that utilizes gas adsorption-desorption isotherms to analyze solid materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The scientific field where the "28d" curing age notation is commonly used.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials Science is the academic discipline conducting experiments to identify specimens and track mix proportions.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials science is the scientific field where nitrogen adsorption-desorption isotherm plots are commonly applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials science is a field of study that provides context for the kinetic analysis and thermal analysis of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal publishing studies on the water resistance of phosphogypsum cement pozzolanic compositions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792456417</data>
