<node id="Wet Acid Method">
  <data key="d0">Wet Acid Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The wet acid method is an industrial process for producing phosphoric acid that generates phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The wet acid method is a chemical process used in the production of phosphoric acid, which generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;The wet acid method is a chemical process used to produce phosphoric acid from phosphate rock using sulfuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;The wet acid method is a process for producing phosphoric acid from calcium phosphate ore and sulfuric acid, which generates large quantities of phosphogypsum waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001</data>
