<node id="Trace Metals">
  <data key="d0">Trace Metals</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Trace Metals are chemical and heavy metal elements that are extensively analyzed for their levels, toxicity, speciation, distribution, mobility, and bioavailability in environmental samples. Key examples include cadmium, copper, zinc, lead, and chromium. These metallic elements are characterized by their tendency to bioaccumulate within ecosystems, which subsequently leads to the pollution of water, soil, and plant systems.

In industrial contexts, Trace Metals are frequently identified as impurities within phosphogypsum. Their presence in this material poses potential dangers during storage and may significantly affect emission impacts. Because of these ecological and industrial risks, the behavior and environmental impact of Trace Metals remain a primary focus of scientific research and monitoring efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Trace metals include arsenic, silver, barium, cadmium, chromium, lead, mercury, and selenium found in Phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792479745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
