<node id="Class C Fly Ash">
  <data key="d0">Class C Fly Ash</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Class C fly ash is a material used alongside lime to stabilize phosphogypsum for potential marine applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Class C Fly Ash is a specific industrial byproduct studied for composition with phosphogypsum and cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash produced from lignite and sub-bituminous coal, possessing both pozzolanic and cementitious properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific grade of fly ash utilized alongside phosphogypsum and cement for soil stabilization.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of fly ash studied by Nalbantoglu Z for its effectiveness as a soil stabilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;Class C fly ash is a specific grade of fly ash used in cement composites for marine applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Class C fly ash is a material used in combination with phosphogypsum for stabilization and potential marine applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012</data>
