<node id="Rutherford">
  <data key="d0">Rutherford</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rutherford is a researcher whose scientific contributions center on the geochemical characterization of phosphogypsum and related mineral systems. In 1994, Rutherford conducted extensive analyses of phosphogypsum samples sourced from various global locations, providing foundational data that is frequently cited in academic footnotes. This work encompasses detailed studies on phosphogypsum fractionation, the identification of quartz and other mineral phases within the material, and the assessment of trace concentrations present in phosphogypsum.

Beyond bulk mineralogical analysis, Rutherford has elucidated specific chemical stabilization mechanisms, notably demonstrating how cerium compounds stabilize the hemihydrate sulfate structure and retard dihydrate recrystallization. The researcher's empirical findings are widely applied to estimate the leaching potential of fluoride, copper, cadmium, zinc, and chromium. Additionally, Rutherford has expanded this geochemical expertise to investigate the complexation behavior of uranium(VI) with clay minerals, underscoring a consistent focus on mineral-water interactions and environmental contaminant mobility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792485025</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al-Hwaiti">
  <data key="d0">Al-Hwaiti</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Al-Hwaiti is a researcher cited for investigations into phosphogypsum trace elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Al-Hwaiti is a researcher cited in the footnotes for contributing to the research articles on PG.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who investigated phosphogypsum amendments and found they caused contamination in soils and vegetables.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who found that phosphogypsum amendments caused contamination in soils and vegetables like tomatoes and green peppers.&lt;SEP&gt;Al-Hwaiti is a researcher whose previous studies informed the examination of heavy metals in PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Al-Hwaiti is a researcher who tested various chemical combinations, including lime water, seawater, and acids, for phosphogypsum treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
