<node id="Particle Diameter">
  <data key="d0">Particle Diameter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The horizontal axis variable on a logarithmic scale measuring particle size in nanometers.&lt;SEP&gt;The average size of the hydroxyapatite particles calculated from specific surface area and density.&lt;SEP&gt;The average size of nanoparticles calculated from SSA and density, ranging from 8 to 39 nm.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property representing the size of the nanopowder particles, measured in nanometers across different sample types.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle Diameter is a measured physical property that correlates directly with density and inversely with specific surface area.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle Diameter tracks the size change of microspheres, transitioning from small solid ACP spheres to larger core-shell HA structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
