</node>
<node id="Heat Treatment Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Heat Treatment Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat Treatment Conditions specify the temperature and duration applied to powders to alter their properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spherical Particles">
  <data key="d0">Spherical Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Spherical Particles are one of the primary morphological forms of hydroxyapatite observed in the NoSurf powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Spherical particles are smaller hydroxyapatite structures (40-60 nm) observed via FESEM in non-surfactant synthesized powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Roughly spherical or globular structures with irregular, bumpy surfaces that are densely packed and agglomerated into a porous network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plate-like Particles">
  <data key="d0">Plate-like Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plate-like Particles are large, flat morphological forms of hydroxyapatite observed in the NoSurf powder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod-like Particles">
  <data key="d0">Rod-like Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rod-like Particles are needle-shaped morphological forms of hydroxyapatite predominantly found in the Surf powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Rod-like Particles are the physical morphology of the synthesized hydroxyapatite powders, characterized by uniform dimensions and varying aspect ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791664401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallite Size">
  <data key="d0">Crystallite Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallite Size is a physical, microstructural, and structural parameter that represents the average dimension of individual crystalline domains or crystals within polycrystalline materials, nanoparticles, and synthesized powders. Typically expressed in nanometers, it is a fundamental property that directly contributes to diffraction peak broadening and correlates directly with the overall degree of crystallinity. The parameter is primarily estimated using X-ray diffraction (XRD) models and equations, most notably the Scherrer equation (also referred to as the Sahadat-Scherrer Model). Calculation methodologies involve analyzing XRD peak intercepts, accounting for lattice contraction or expansion, and utilizing the slope of plotted graphs to derive the mean particle size.

In the specific context of hydroxyapatite (HAp) powders and nanoparticles, Crystallite Size is frequently measured as a structural property along the c-axis or c direction. For instance, it has been recorded at 33.6 nm for the (002) crystallographic plane. The size exhibits distinct behavioral trends: it increases with heat treatment and expands along the c-axis when surfactants, particularly Brij-93, are incorporated during the synthesis process. Overall, Crystallite Size serves as a critical microstructural metric for characterizing the nanoscale architecture and crystalline quality of advanced materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property representing the dimensions of crystalline domains within the nanopowder, measured in nanometers.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite Size is a measured physical property indicating the dimensions of individual crystals in the nanopowder.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite Size is a physical property of the prepared samples estimated using the Scherrer equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite Size is a physical property of the prepared samples estimated using the Scherrer equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite size is a measured physical property of hydroxyapatite particles, averaging 28 nm across samples with specific values for different milling treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallinity Degree">
  <data key="d0">Crystallinity Degree</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallinity Degree is a measured structural property of hydroxyapatite powders, expressed as a percentage.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of structural order in the powders that improves with heat treatment and correlates with crystallite size.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallinity degree is a structural parameter of hydroxyapatite powders influenced by heat treatment and surfactant use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="N2 Adsorption Analysis">
  <data key="d0">N2 Adsorption Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">N2 adsorption analysis is a technique used to assess the surface properties and bioactivity of hydroxyapatite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OH- Group">
  <data key="d0">OH- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">OH- groups are chemical components within hydroxyapatite crystals whose spectral peak intensity reflects the material's crystalline state.</data>
