<node id="Bragg Angle">
  <data key="d0">Bragg Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bragg Angle is a geometric parameter representing the diffraction angle used in crystallite size calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;The diffraction angle corresponding to the position of a specific analyzed peak, used in the cosine term of the formula.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bragg Angle is a parameter representing the angle of the highest intensity diffracted peak used in the Scherrer equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bragg angle is a fundamental parameter in X-ray diffraction used to identify crystalline phases and calculate particle size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
