<node id="Scherrer Constant">
  <data key="d0">Scherrer Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A dimensionless shape factor approximated as 0.9 for spherical crystals with cubic symmetry.&lt;SEP&gt;Scherrer Constant is a parameter (usually 0.89) used in the Scherrer equation to estimate crystallite size.&lt;SEP&gt;Scherrer Constant is a parameter (usually 0.89) used in the Scherrer equation to estimate crystallite size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792190541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wavelength">
  <data key="d0">Wavelength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The wavelength of the X-ray source used during the diffraction experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Wavelength ($\lambda$) is a parameter used in Scherrer's equation for crystallite size calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;The horizontal axis measurement ranging from 208 nm to 238 nm used to identify elemental peaks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792040883</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Miller Indices">
  <data key="d0">Miller Indices</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Numerical notations used to identify specific crystal planes corresponding to diffraction peaks.&lt;SEP&gt;Miller indices are crystallographic notations used to label specific diffraction peaks in XRD analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A notation system (hkl) used to label specific diffraction peaks across all data traces.&lt;SEP&gt;Miller Indices (hkl) are used to identify specific peaks in the diffraction pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallographic notation used to annotate specific diffraction peaks for hydroxyapatite crystallographic planes.&lt;SEP&gt;Miller Indices are crystallographic notations used to describe specific faces of gypsum needles affected by lanthanides.&lt;SEP&gt;Miller indices are crystallographic plane identifiers used to label specific diffraction peaks in the reference pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Counts Per Second">
  <data key="d0">Counts Per Second</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit measuring X-ray diffraction signal intensity on the vertical axis of the chart.&lt;SEP&gt;The unit of measurement for signal intensity in the XPS spectra.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-023</data>
