<node id="PO4 3-">
  <data key="d0">PO4 3-</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PO4 3- is a tetrahedral phosphate ion that binds to CTA+ nuclei due to charge and stereochemistry complementarity.&lt;SEP&gt;PO4 3- is a phosphate ion whose bending and stretching vibrations are identified in the ATR spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;PO4 3- is the phosphate ion responsible for the strong P-O stretching vibration bands observed in the FTIR spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;PO4 3- is a phosphate ion group identified in the FTIR spectra of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Particle size">
  <data key="d0">Particle size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Particle size is a physical characteristic of the synthesized powders that is regulated by the presence of CTAB.&lt;SEP&gt;Particle size is a physical characteristic of MPG that influences setting times.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011</data>
