  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ball-Milling Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Ball-Milling Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ball-milling treatment reduces particle size, increases specific surface area, and improves fluidity and strength while lowering water requirements for phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791361860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rashad">
  <data key="d0">Rashad</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rashad calcined phosphogypsum at 850 degrees Celsius for 2 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Rashad conducted experiments determining optimal calcination temperatures for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Rashad is a researcher who calcined PG at 850 °C for 2 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Rashad is a researcher mentioned in the context of phosphogypsum calcination studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Rashad is a researcher who found that calcined phosphogypsum enhances the compressive strength of fly ash-based geopolymers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potgieter et al.">
  <data key="d0">Potgieter et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Potgieter et al. demonstrated that treating phosphogypsum-based cemented paste backfill with sulfuric acid or ammonium hydroxide reduces set retardation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791361860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wu et al.">
  <data key="d0">Wu et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wu et al. are researchers who investigated the application of calcium carbide slag for phosphogypsum neutralization.&lt;SEP&gt;Wu et al. reported that ball-milling treatment efficiently reduces phosphogypsum particle size and improves compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Wu et al. documented the forms of phosphate impurities in phosphogypsum and their release during hydration.&lt;SEP&gt;Researchers who cited decision-making trial and evaluation laboratory and life cycle assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Du et al.">
  <data key="d0">Du et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Du et al. utilized ball-milling combined with reverse flotation to eliminate microfine particles and organic materials from raw phosphogypsum ore.&lt;SEP&gt;Researchers who summarized the composition of PG, including various impurities and contaminants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001</data>
