<node id="Fine Aggregate">
  <data key="d0">Fine Aggregate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fine aggregate is a basic component mixed with PG and clinker to create mortar combinations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fine aggregate is a granular material used in mortar mixtures prepared by Abdelhadi et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Fine aggregate is a component used in mortar mixtures alongside clinker and phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Li">
  <data key="d0">Li</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Li is a researcher whose work primarily focuses on the application of phosphogypsum in cementitious materials and environmental remediation. In studies involving calcium aluminate cement, Li reported that the addition of phosphogypsum reduces cement clinker requirements and promotes phase elimination. Through X-ray diffraction analysis of hydrated samples at varying phosphogypsum concentrations, Li identified the primary minerals present in phosphogypsum slag cement. Furthermore, Li concluded that incorporating phosphogypsum with cementitious materials significantly immobilizes soluble fluorine, while also investigating fluorine re-release phenomena in CPGFM filling slurry.

Beyond cement chemistry, Li provided heavy metal concentration data for Chinese phosphogypsum solutions and explored the hydrothermal method for removing organic matter and phosphorus. Li also examined the durability of filling bodies under chemical erosion, acidic environments, and salt solutions. Li co-authored publications in the International Journal of Inorganic Materials, and Li’s 2021 research has been cited as a data source in comparative tables.&lt;SEP&gt;Li studied lime neutralization and concluded it effectively removes soluble phosphorus but has limited effects on soluble fluorine and eutectic phosphorus impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Li is a researcher who studied the effects of calcium carbide slag dosing, reaction temperature, and time on phosphogypsum modification.&lt;SEP&gt;A trace element measured in parts per million in the provided analytical data.&lt;SEP&gt;Li is a researcher who studied phosphogypsum from China in 2021.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792406487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potgieter">
  <data key="d0">Potgieter</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Potgieter found that cement containing PG exhibited lower compressive strengths at early ages compared to natural gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Potgieter is a researcher who explored phosphogypsum decomposition reacting with various forms of carbon in 1999.&lt;SEP&gt;Potgieter is a researcher who eliminated impurities from phosphogypsum using various chemical washes.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who studied chemical and physical treatments of PG incorporated into clinker to produce cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792483381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hwaiti">
  <data key="d0">Hwaiti</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Hwaiti confirmed the behavior of PG-containing cement showing lower early-age compressive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791363405</data>
