<node id="Slag">
  <data key="d0">Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Slag is a versatile industrial byproduct and waste material generated during various manufacturing and processing operations, including carbothermal reduction smelting of PGI and PGI-1.4, general chemical processing, smelting, and specifically the production of Monoammonium Phosphate (MAP). Initially formed as a molten substance, it solidifies upon cooling and is routinely characterized for its phase composition, microstructure, chemical distribution, pH, and viscosity. Chemically, slag typically comprises sulfides and sulfates, with its sulfur content fluctuating according to the carbon-to-sulfur (C/S) molar ratio and potentially retaining sulfide residues.

In construction and cementitious engineering, slag functions primarily as a supplementary cementitious material and mineral additive. It is extensively blended with binders such as ordinary Portland cement, limestone, gypsum, fly ash, slaked lime, and gypsum anhydrite to significantly enhance the mechanical properties, compressive strength, and long-term durability of concrete and mortar. When combined with pretreated or calcined phosphogypsum (PG), slag optimizes geopolymer cement formulations, refines material microstructures, and facilitates the development of cemented PG filling materials. Specific mixtures incorporating acid phosphogypsum and slaked lime are utilized in mortar production, while blends with phosphogypsum and lime enable the creation of fiber-modified mixtures. Additionally, the partial replacement of slag with phosphogypsum in binder systems influences setting time, and slag-PG concrete combinations effectively reduce chloride permeability.

Beyond structural applications, slag plays a critical role in chemical processing and sustainable resource management. It acts as a concentration medium for impurities during treatments such as phosphogypsum carbonation with ammonium acetate and is integrated into hybrid systems designed to maximize industrial waste valorization. By consistently transforming industrial byproducts into high-performance construction components and further processing them into high-value materials, slag operates as a sustainable, performance-enhancing agent that advances both structural integrity and resource efficiency in modern material synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Slag is the waste byproduct generated during the thermal process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG-Based Geopolymer Cement">
  <data key="d0">PG-Based Geopolymer Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PG-Based Geopolymer Cement is a material produced by combining PG, slag, fly ash, and alkali activator.</data>
