<node id="Softening Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Softening Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical property measured for hemihydrate phosphogypsum composite containing recycled waste glass.&lt;SEP&gt;Softening coefficient is a durability metric discussed in relation to the admixtures' effects on the materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Softening Coefficient is a metric reflecting the water resistance of phosphogypsum, which increases with temperature and indicates superior water repellency when exceeding 0.8.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured property of MPG that failed to meet the GB/T9776 Standard requirement of greater than 0.8 under 165 °C test conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-008</data>
