<node id="Natural Sand">
  <data key="d0">Natural Sand</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A material combined with phosphogypsum and cement in mortar formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Sand is a standard aggregate in concrete and mortar mixtures that can be partially substituted by Plaster Of Paris.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural sand is a natural aggregate partially replaced by PG in mortar and concrete mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural sand is a material replaced by phosphogypsum in brick manufacturing, affecting the final density.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural sand is a fine aggregate partially replaced by phosphogypsum in self-leveling mortar mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;A component in mortar mixtures partially replaced with PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural sand is a base aggregate partially replaced by PG in self-leveling mortar mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluidity">
  <data key="d0">Fluidity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A property of magnesium oxysulfate cement that decreases when combined with phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluidity is a performance metric measuring the flowability of self-leveling mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of PG products that improves due to increased internal compactness from smaller decomposition particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluidity is a physical property of PBSLM measured in millimeters, influenced by component friction and hydration cohesion.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property of the mortar measured at 0 and 30 minutes, indicating workability.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluidity is a mechanical property of PBSLM that decreases with increased MPG content and increases with decreased cement content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
