  <data key="d0">Hydration Degree</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measure of cement hydration that was found to be virtually identical between modified and unaltered PG after 28 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydration degree represents the extent of chemical reaction completion among admixtures inside PGCM, increasing with curing age.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011</data>
