<node id="Calcium Hydrogen Phosphate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Hydrogen Phosphate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A phosphor impurity in PG composition that contributes to increased setting times.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium hydrogen phosphate dihydrate is a precursor reagent used in the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Hydrogen Phosphate Dihydrate is a secondary chemical compound identified in the composition of raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound identified in the XRD pattern, commonly known as Brushite.</data>
