<node id="Mullite">
  <data key="d0">Mullite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A mineral phase that forms during the crystallization process of bricks at temperatures around 1000 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Mullite is a primary mineral component of fly ash detected in the concrete samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Mullite is a mineral phase identified by peak 2, appearing in clusters around 29°-30° and scattered between 35°-60°.&lt;SEP&gt;Mullite is an aluminum silicate compound (AlSiO9) identified in the mineralogical composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791938226</data>
