<node id="Anhydrous Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Anhydrous Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Anhydrous gypsum is a stable product formed alongside hemihydrate gypsum during the calcination of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous gypsum is a mineral phase that maintains its crystalline shape in brick samples containing Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous gypsum is produced by calcining beta-hemihydrate gypsum and is utilized as a chemical filler.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous Gypsum is the final dehydration product formed from semi-hydrated gypsum at temperatures above 195°C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301772</data>
