<node id="Hemihydrate PG">
  <data key="d0">Hemihydrate PG</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemihydrate PG is a form of phosphogypsum used as a predominant adhesion agent in cement pastes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate PG is a form of phosphogypsum containing coarse particles that negatively impacts the water retention of filling slurry.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate PG is a form of phosphogypsum resulting from the dry process, typically having larger particle sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000</data>
