  <data key="d5">1791365237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Min et al.">
  <data key="d0">Min et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Min et al. researched how soluble phosphorus and organic substances in phosphogypsum increase material gelling time.&lt;SEP&gt;Min et al. are researchers who provided chemical composition data for phosphogypsum samples in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Min et al. are researchers who considered that increasing calcium hydroxide content improves strength evolution by reducing porosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Min et al. are researchers who demonstrated the strength-enhancing effects of calcined phosphogypsum in fly ash-lime binders.&lt;SEP&gt;Min et al. are researchers who reported significant compressive strength enhancements with specific curing parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liu et al.">
  <data key="d0">Liu et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Liu et al. represents a citation used across distinct research domains, primarily encompassing materials science and methodological frameworks. In materials and environmental engineering, Liu et al. conducted extensive investigations into phosphogypsum. They provided detailed chemical composition data for phosphogypsum samples from China and compared raw and calcined forms, noting their similar chemical profiles. Their research explored pretreatment and processing techniques, demonstrating that water washing optimizes particle size distribution and reduces shear thinning, while hydrothermal processing was examined to determine how pH levels affect particle morphology and agglomeration. Additionally, they concluded that incorporating gamma alumina promotes AFt precipitation and enhances fluorine retention. Beyond technical characterization, this research group also summarized the profitability and sustainability of phosphogypsum across various industrial applications.

In a separate methodological context, Liu et al. is cited for contributions to decision-making and resource economics. These researchers are recognized for applying game theory to balance weight vectors, a mathematical approach designed to minimize deviation in multi-criteria evaluations. They are also credited with introducing the concept of emergy loss, which is framed as a mechanism for economic resource compensation within sustainability and systems analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Liu et al. are researchers cited for their findings on the correlation between modification temperature and the strength of modified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Liu et al. are researchers cited for results regarding the positive effect of calcium sulfate compounds on MPG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guiyang">
  <data key="d0">Guiyang</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Guiyang is a location where phosphogypsum samples with high sulfur trioxide content were sourced.&lt;SEP&gt;Guiyang is the city where Guizhou University is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hubei">
  <data key="d0">Hubei</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Hubei is a Chinese province that plays a significant role in the nation's phosphogypsum sector, contributing substantially to China's total phosphogypsum production. It is prominently represented in aggregate data distributions regarding phosphogypsum usage and has been a central focus of multiple studies analyzing the phosphogypsum recycling industry. These investigations frequently examine prominent companies engaged in recycling within the region and involve the collection and chemical analysis of phosphogypsum samples sourced from Hubei, which are characterized by a moderate sulfur trioxide content.

In addition to its research significance, Hubei is strategically targeted for the development of large-scale and demonstration phosphogypsum projects. The province has also actively advanced its recycling infrastructure, with CPGB technology being successfully adopted by large-scale mining operations. Through these initiatives, Hubei continues to serve as a critical hub for phosphogypsum management, technological innovation, and industrial recycling efforts in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei is a Chinese province that issued technical regulations for the safe treatment and recycling of PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recycling">
  <data key="d0">Recycling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Recycling is a waste management process identified as a risk-free and environmentally beneficial solution for phosphogypsum stockpiling.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling is a process used to repurpose phosphogypsum, though contaminants can degrade the quality of the recycled product.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of reprocessing PG into usable products and materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791451491</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treatment Methods">
  <data key="d0">Treatment Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Treatment methods are applied to phosphogypsum to remove contaminants and improve its suitability for engineering applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelling Time">
  <data key="d0">Gelling Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelling time is a material property that increases due to the presence of soluble phosphorus and organic substances in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strength Development">
  <data key="d0">Strength Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strength development refers to the process by which gypsum gains mechanical strength, which is hindered by contaminants.&lt;SEP&gt;Strength development describes the mechanical property progression of cementitious binders derived from industrial wastes over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loss on Ignition">
  <data key="d0">Loss on Ignition</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss on Ignition is a chemical analysis metric and measurement technique used to evaluate mass loss resulting from dehydration, moisture evaporation, and the removal of volatile components or impurities during heating or calcination. Expressed in weight percentages, this property serves as a key indicator of a material's volatile content and thermal stability. It is routinely documented in chemical composition tables, such as Table 1, to assess the composition and behavior of various materials, including phosphogypsum, cement, and fly ash.

When applied to phosphogypsum, Loss on Ignition provides critical insights into its thermal degradation profile. Initial measurements for phosphogypsum samples have been recorded at baseline levels of 20.8% and 14.19%, reflecting variations in sample conditions or initial moisture content. As calcination temperature increases, the metric decreases significantly. The value drops drastically during heating and typically falls below 1% at temperatures of 600°C and above, demonstrating the material's progressive dehydration and volatile release. By tracking these changes, researchers can effectively compare the thermal stability and compositional integrity of phosphogypsum against cement and fly ash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Raw Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw Phosphogypsum is an unprocessed industrial byproduct whose chemical composition closely resembles that of its calcined counterpart. In analytical and spectroscopic studies, it is consistently identified as the untreated sample corresponding to spectrum (a) and is routinely evaluated using infrared spectroscopy.

As a construction and composite material, Raw Phosphogypsum serves as a primary base material and the principal constituent of PGCM. Due to its inherently low cementitious properties, it is frequently combined with β-HPG in experimental mixtures at a fixed 60% to 40% ratio to enhance overall performance. The hydration of Raw Phosphogypsum within these composites is significantly influenced by the addition of cement and silica fume, and the material is typically cured using hemihydrate phosphogypsum to develop functional cementitious products. Despite its utility in mixtures, Raw Phosphogypsum exhibits notable mechanical vulnerabilities, as it tends to degrade and flake off when subjected to cyclic stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw Phosphogypsum is the untreated material baseline, containing no detectable sodium prior to leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw Phosphogypsum is the unprocessed industrial byproduct evaluated for compatibility with conventional road construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The unprocessed source material containing major and trace elements that contribute to impurities in the final product.&lt;SEP&gt;The unprocessed version of phosphogypsum that generally exhibits higher trace element concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw Phosphogypsum refers to the initial, untreated material state before calcination and washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcined Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Calcined Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcined phosphogypsum is a thermally treated and processed form of phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct. Through calcination, the material undergoes physical and chemical modifications while largely retaining a chemical composition similar to its raw counterpart. This thermal treatment effectively reduces water-soluble impurities and generally results in lower water absorption and permeability compared to untreated phosphogypsum.

The processing significantly alters the material's performance characteristics, notably shortening its setting time and modifying its density. These changes make calcined phosphogypsum highly valuable in construction applications, where it is utilized to enhance binder and cement properties. It is commonly blended with slag cement, fly ash, and quicklime to improve matrix compressive strength. Furthermore, the treated material helps mitigate strength degradation and actively enhances the properties of geopolymer systems, making it a versatile additive in advanced construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
