<node id="Ajam et al.">
  <data key="d0">Ajam et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Researchers who developed fired bricks using a mixture of phosphogypsum, sand, and clay.&lt;SEP&gt;Ajam et al. are researchers who documented that calcium sulfate accounts for approximately 77% of phosphogypsum's composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Ajam et al. replaced clay with fine PG in clay bricks, documenting significant compressive strength declines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brickmaking Process">
  <data key="d0">Brickmaking Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Brickmaking process is an industrial application where treated phosphogypsum is used to reduce overall energy consumption and heat requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methodical Crushing">
  <data key="d0">Methodical Crushing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Methodical crushing is a processing step recommended to eliminate the residual fluorescence effect caused by calcium sulphate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clean Gypsum Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Clean Gypsum Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clean gypsum recovery refers to the estimated 75% yield of purified gypsum achieved through the sieve technique.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009</data>
