<node id="Scanning Electron Microscope Micrograph">
  <data key="d0">Scanning Electron Microscope Micrograph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A high-magnification grayscale image revealing the dense, complex microstructure of a cementitious composite or phosphogypsum reaction product.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-magnification, black-and-white image used to visualize the surface topography and morphology of the phosphogypsum material.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-magnification grayscale image revealing the surface morphology of a material.&lt;SEP&gt;A composite scientific figure containing multiple panels of particulate matter and crystal structures under varying experimental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792407841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plate-like Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Plate-like Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plate-like crystals are the dominant feature in the micrograph, appearing as flat, irregular, overlapping scales with smooth surfaces and sharp edges.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-039</data>
