<node id="Environment">
  <data key="d0">Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Environment functions as a primary evaluation criterion and a main criteria-level dimension within an indicator system and decision hierarchy, branching directly from total utility. As one of four core dimensions, it specifically focuses on ecological and pollution impacts, serving to assess the ecological burden and environmental footprint of various technologies. In the context of phosphogypsum recycling and resource utilization, Environment operates as a performance metric where phosphogypsum-based technologies generally demonstrate relatively high performance.

Despite these technological advancements, the physical environment faces severe threats from phosphogypsum stockpiling, which introduces chemical pollution, radiation exposure, and dust release. Conversely, the implementation of phosphogypsum resource utilization methods positions the environment as a primary beneficiary of reduced pollutant impacts. Beyond industrial applications, the environment also absorbs phosphorus losses originating from the Australian food system, which are distributed across nonagricultural soil, water bodies, and landfill sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Environment is a domain potentially affected by heavy metal release from MPG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
