<node id="Surface Modification">
  <data key="d0">Surface Modification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface modification is applied to phosphogypsum to enhance its compatibility and application in materials like polyolefin.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface modification is a treatment process applied to phosphogypsum to enhance its compatibility with polyolefin composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface modification involves altering chemical and physical features to enhance biomaterial performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface modification is the process of altering HAP surface properties using AL molecules to enhance bioactivity and change composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000</data>
