<node id="Ceramic Blocks">
  <data key="d0">Ceramic Blocks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ceramic blocks are composed of clay, cement, and phosphogypsum, representing another potential application in construction.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceramic blocks are construction units produced by incorporating gypsum waste, evaluated for technical and environmental viability.&lt;SEP&gt;Building components produced by incorporating gypsum waste to evaluate technical and environmental viability.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceramic blocks are manufactured using a mixture of non-plastic clay, plastic clay, gypsum waste, and cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
