  <data key="d0">Sulphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulphate is a chemical component whose potential activating function for PG in concrete systems requires further investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulphate is a compound that can be employed as a soil conditioner.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulphate is a chemical group identified in phosphogypsum through specific absorption bands in FTIR and XRD analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound forming mobile complexes with radionuclides within phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792486704</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoclaved Aerated Concrete">
  <data key="d0">Autoclaved Aerated Concrete</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoclaved aerated concrete is a material produced through autoclaving, characterized by high tobermorite content and decomposed ettringite.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a novel construction material developed using unprocessed PG, cement, FA, and chemical additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a specialized product whose anhydrite content increases when Phosphogypsum is added to the batch.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a lightweight building material prepared using untreated phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight concrete material prepared using waste red gypsum and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight building material evaluated through dry-wet cycle testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polycarboxylate Superplasticizer">
  <data key="d0">Polycarboxylate Superplasticizer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An additive studied for its effect on the properties of phosphogypsum-based cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycarboxylate superplasticizer is a chemical additive that improves compressive strength and decreases water absorption in phosphogypsum matrices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792455412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Molecular Dynamics Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Molecular Dynamics Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A computational technique used alongside experiments to investigate the mechanical properties of phosphogypsum slag cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular dynamics simulation is a computational technique used to model the transport properties of water molecules confined between hydroxyapatite surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular dynamics simulation is a computational technique used to elucidate surface protonation mechanisms and hydrogen bonding interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317876</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermodynamic Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Thermodynamic Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
