<node id="Specific Gravity">
  <data key="d0">Specific Gravity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific gravity is a physical property of phosphogypsum that increases as calcination temperature increases.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil property measured at 2.44, representing the ratio of the density of soil solids to the density of water.&lt;SEP&gt;A density metric for phosphogypsum, measured at 2.516, falling within the standard range of 2.3-2.6.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property representing the ratio of a material's density to a reference density, measured for both samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The ratio of the density of a material to the density of water, documented for PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific gravity is a physical property of soil and stabilizers that influences the reduction in dry unit weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific gravity is a physical property of PG that increases with calcination temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003</data>
