<node id="Gypsum Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Crystals are mineral formations in the mortar microstructure whose shape and size are altered by phosphate ions and citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Microscopic crystals that precipitate and clump together during the chemical reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystals that precipitate and clump together during the chemical reaction to form agglomerates.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum crystals are mineral structures whose growth rates are influenced by lanthanide substitution and elemental radii.</data>
