<node id="Land Occupation">
  <data key="d0">Land Occupation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Land Occupation refers to the spatial footprint and land use alterations caused by the accumulation and disposal of solid waste, particularly phosphogypsum stockpiles. This phenomenon involves the significant consumption of arable and ecological land, representing a direct environmental consequence of pollutant emissions and waste management activities. In environmental accounting frameworks, it is quantified as a measurable activity within Life Cycle Inventory data specifically associated with phosphogypsum disposal.

Beyond its physical dimensions, Land Occupation serves as a resource dimension indicator assigned a weighting factor exactly half that of comprehensive energy consumption. It also captures the economic impact and financial losses resulting from solid waste landfilling and pollutant emissions. Furthermore, this metric is integral to emergy accounting systems, where it is utilized to calculate associated emergy losses, thereby linking physical land consumption to broader environmental and economic valuation models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
