<node id="Zhou et al.">
  <data key="d0">Zhou et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhou et al. is a research group that has extensively investigated the chemical characterization and industrial utilization of phosphogypsum (PG). Their foundational work includes classifying the three primary chemical forms of phosphorus within phosphogypsum and identifying a significant methodological gap: the current lack of integrated processes for the sequential synthesis of calcium sulfate whiskers and the extraction of rare earth elements. In parallel, the researchers developed and presented the Two-step Hydration Process to advance material processing techniques. Their investigations into cemented paste backfilling demonstrated that pretreating PG with water washing effectively removes impurities, thereby enhancing the mechanical strength of the final material. Furthermore, they established a direct correlation between the soluble phosphorus content in the treated PG and the compressive strength of the cemented paste fill. To optimize chemical treatment protocols, Zhou et al. also determined the ideal concentration and washing cycles required for effective citric acid application.

Beyond geotechnical applications, Zhou et al. has been prominently referenced in brick manufacturing research involving phosphogypsum. The team successfully manufactured non-fired bricks using a composite mixture of PG, lime, and sand. Through systematic experimentation, they observed and documented how varying the proportion of phosphogypsum directly influences the structural integrity and strength development of the resulting bricks. Collectively, their multidisciplinary research provides a comprehensive framework for valorizing phosphogypsum, bridging the gap between chemical processing optimization and practical construction material development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
