<node id="Gypsum Waste">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum waste is a recycled material proposed for incorporation into ceramic block production to evaluate technical and environmental viability.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum waste is an industrial byproduct processed to recover elemental sulphur and convert calcium sulphide to calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum waste is incorporated into ceramic block production to evaluate technical and environmental viability.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum waste is an industrial byproduct utilized for calcium carbonate particle production and CO2 fixation.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum waste is combined with clay and cement to manufacture ceramic blocks with a compressive strength of 4.64 MPa.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum waste is a byproduct incorporated into ceramic block production to evaluate technical and environmental viability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
