  <data key="d2">IFA is an international government agency investigated as part of the phosphogypsum research scope.&lt;SEP&gt;The abbreviation for the International Fertilizer Association, which published a 2020 report on recycling rates.&lt;SEP&gt;IFA is a cited data source for fertiliser sector information.&lt;SEP&gt;IFA organized the Global Safety Summit and published the PG Handbook referenced in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;IFA is an organization cited in literature reviewing zero-waste strategies for phosphogypsum utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;The IFA is an organization that initiated the Phosphogypsum Leadership Innovation Partnership.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003</data>
