<node id="US-EPA">
  <data key="d0">US-EPA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">US-EPA is an international government agency investigated as part of the phosphogypsum research scope.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory body whose leaching thresholds are used to evaluate the safety of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory body that established the concentration limits for trace elements in the TCLP test.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Environmental Protection Agency, which establishes regulatory limits for leachable contaminants.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Environmental Protection Agency, which published EPA-1311 and a reference document on hazardous waste characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Environmental Protection Agency, which sets regulatory limits for chemical contaminants.&lt;SEP&gt;The US-EPA establishes regulatory limits for chemical elements in environmental samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
