<node id="Tinto River">
  <data key="d0">Tinto River</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tinto River is a waterway in Spain whose salt marshes were studied for their capacity to mitigate contamination from PG landfills.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tinto River is a river in Spain transporting sulfates, metals, and metalloids to the Huelva Estuary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tinto River is an estuarine system in SW Spain where phosphogypsum impact and natural attenuation processes are assessed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tinto River forms an estuary with the Odiel River, receiving contaminated effluents from phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007</data>
