<node id="Yang">
  <data key="d0">Yang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Yang is a researcher whose work primarily focuses on the valorization, processing, and application of phosphogypsum, alongside related materials science investigations. In 2013, Yang examined the use of sulfur as an alternative reducing agent for phosphogypsum decomposition. Subsequent research explored various physical and chemical techniques to enhance phosphogypsum utilization, including the investigation of hydrodynamic separation and flotation methods to increase rare earth element concentration within the material. Yang also documented the self-hardening characteristics of hemihydrate phosphogypsum during its hydration conversion and investigated hydrothermal methods for modifying phosphogypsum crystal growth. Furthermore, Yang explored the practical application of phosphogypsum as a raw material for self-leveling mortar and proposed integrating phosphate fertilizer production with phosphogypsum reuse systems to improve overall resource efficiency.

Beyond phosphogypsum applications, Yang's research extends to advanced adsorbent synthesis, specifically utilizing HPA as a mixed linker and surface modifier to prepare defective UiO-66-NH2 adsorbents. Additionally, Yang's 2020 study is frequently cited as a data source in comparative scientific tables. Collectively, these contributions highlight a sustained research effort dedicated to transforming industrial byproducts into valuable materials and optimizing sustainable chemical processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang highlighted potential safety risks associated with heavy metals in low-temperature calcined phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang is a researcher who prepared self-leveling mortar mixtures with varying PG contents.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang is a researcher who calcined phosphogypsum at 500 °C for 4 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang prepared a 2016 self-leveling mortar mixture containing cement, PG, and natural sand to study shrinkage.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang is a researcher who exposed phosphogypsum to low and high autoclave conditions to evaluate brick manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
