<node id="Sedimentary Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d0">Sedimentary Phosphate Rock</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sedimentary phosphate rock contains lower concentrations of rare earth elements compared to igneous phosphate rock.&lt;SEP&gt;Sedimentary phosphate rock is the raw material processed at the Huelva industrial complex to produce phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sedimentary Phosphate Rock is the geological source material for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A geological matrix primarily composed of fluorapatite, serving as a source for rare earth elements in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sedimentary phosphate rock is a type of phosphate ore processed to produce phosphogypsum with higher silicon dioxide concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-006</data>
