  <data key="d0">Common Ion Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The common ion effect is a chemical phenomenon that explains the low solubility of phosphogypsum under normal conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Common ion effect denotes a chemical phenomenon responsible for the low solubility of phosphogypsum under normal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019</data>
