  <data key="d5">1792362329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reductive Decomposition">
  <data key="d0">Reductive Decomposition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reductive decomposition is a process exploring the conversion of phosphogypsum to sulfur dioxide using reducing gases and carbon forms, limited by high temperature requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Reductive decomposition is a method used to break down phosphogypsum with high-sulfur-concentration coal to produce SO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Reductive decomposition is a chemical process used to break down phosphogypsum and waste gypsum into valuable components like sulfur dioxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
