  <data key="d0">K2SO4</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">K2SO4 is the target potassium compound generated during the extraction process from K-feldspar.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium sulfate, a chemical compound mentioned in the introductory equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium sulfate, a product formed during the KOH and calcium carbonate reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;K2SO4 is the chemical formula for potassium sulphate, a stable co-product generated during the dispersion and carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium sulfate, a chemical compound used to activate anhydrate phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020</data>
