<node id="Seawater">
  <data key="d0">Seawater</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Seawater is a saline environment that significantly enhances Phosphogypsum solubility and facilitates the migration of uranium into adjacent marine areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Seawater is a natural water body mixed with phosphogypsum leachates to study the behavior of heavy metals and radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;Seawater is a medium used in combination with lime water and sulphuric acid for phosphogypsum treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Seawater is a high-salinity solution that enhances the solubility of phosphogypsum and facilitates uranium migration to adjacent seas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
