<node id="Monetite">
  <data key="d0">Monetite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Monetite is a semi-hydrated calcium phosphate mineral with the chemical formula CaHPO4. It is characterized as an insoluble compound that typically forms through the thermal dehydration or calcination of brushite. This transformation occurs when brushite loses its structural water at temperatures ranging from approximately 150°C to 250°C. Additionally, Monetite can be generated during the acidic attack of PG and is frequently identified as a stable product following the drying phase of various synthesis procedures.

In materials science and chemical research, Monetite is routinely characterized alongside brushite to analyze crystallization dynamics and phase transformations. It is specifically recognized by its median width during the synthesis and characterization of hydroxyapatite. As a key semi-hydrated phase in calcium phosphate chemistry, Monetite plays a significant role in understanding the intermediate stages of phosphate mineral formation and thermal processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792402834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cryolite">
  <data key="d0">Cryolite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryolite is a fluoride compound that precipitates when high concentrations of dissolved aluminum and fluorine are present in PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Cryolite is a fluorine precipitate that forms under conditions of high dissolved aluminum concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
