  <data key="d2">Chukhrovite is a complex fluoride compound that can form when fluorine co-crystallizes with other elements in PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Chukhrovite is a synthetic mineral compound with a defined crystal structure involving calcium, aluminum, silicon, sulfate, fluoride, and water.&lt;SEP&gt;Chukhrovite is a mineral that precipitates when alkali concentration is low and aluminum is present.</data>
