<node id="Adsorption Process">
  <data key="d0">Adsorption Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorption processes are mechanisms that fix uranium compounds on the exterior surfaces of mineral structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption Process is the mechanism by which heavy metal ions bind to adsorbent surfaces, influenced by pH and surface charge.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption Process refers to the mechanism by which heavy metal ions adhere to the surface of adsorbents, identified as a non-monolayer mechanism in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorption Process refers to the mechanism by which substances adhere to a surface, identified as non-simple monolayer adsorption in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;The overall mechanism involving boundary layer diffusion, intraparticle diffusion, and equilibrium stages, analyzed through kinetic and isotherm models.&lt;SEP&gt;The mechanism by which fluoride ions bind to the surface of nHAp derived from PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792317345</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
