<node id="Natural Radionuclides">
  <data key="d0">Natural Radionuclides</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural radionuclides are radioactive elements whose migration and fractionation are key concerns in phosphogypsum research.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural radionuclides are radioactive elements found in the environment, often extracted or mobilized during phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Radionuclides are radioactive impurities in phosphogypsum that contribute to its high toxicity and environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural radionuclides are radioactive elements whose environmental fate is tracked alongside heavy metals in phosphogypsum treatment studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029</data>
