  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nuclide Migration refers to the movement of radioactive elements through environmental systems, particularly studied in the context of Florida phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclide migration refers to the movement of radioactive isotopes in the environment, particularly studied in Florida phosphogypsum.</data>
