<node id="Environmental Radiochemistry">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Radiochemistry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Radiochemistry is the scientific discipline examining radionuclide migration and the environmental impact of radioactive materials like those in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental radiochemistry is the scientific field studying the behavior of radioactive substances in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental radiochemistry involves modeling the behavior and migration of radionuclides in ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental radiochemistry is the scientific field examining nuclide migration and radioactive contamination from industrial byproducts like phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007</data>
