  <data key="d2">EPMA is a microanalysis technique used alongside LA-ICPMS to study REE vectors in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;EPMA is a microanalytical technique used to determine the detailed chemical composition of minerals in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A microanalytical technique used to determine that rare earth elements are mostly found in the fluorine phase.&lt;SEP&gt;EPMA denotes an analytical method used to identify mineral phases such as gypsum, quartz, and fluorine in phosphogypsum.</data>
