<node id="PG Recycling Technologies">
  <data key="d0">PG Recycling Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PG Recycling Technologies refers to the technical processes and industrial methods dedicated to the production, modification, and non-hazardous treatment of phosphogypsum, with a primary focus on its recycling. This entity encompasses a specific set of fifteen industrialized technologies that have been systematically analyzed in recent studies. These technologies represent a distinct collection of specialized processes designed to transform phosphogypsum waste into valuable resources through various engineered approaches.

The assessment of PG Recycling Technologies relies on a multi-dimensional indicator system that evaluates comprehensive utility performance across four critical criteria: resource efficiency, environmental impact, economic viability, and social implications. While research frameworks apply this structured, multi-criteria evaluation to each of the fifteen technologies, the broader field currently suffers from inconsistent evaluation standards. This lack of uniformity complicates comparative analysis and hinders standardized industrial implementation, highlighting the need for harmonized assessment protocols to fully leverage the sustainable potential of these recycling methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
