<node id="PVA">
  <data key="d0">PVA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">PVA is a polymer used to peel and prepare HAP samples for spectroscopic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyvinyl alcohol used as a mounting medium to peel and prepare HAP layers for SEM imaging.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a water-soluble polymer used to successfully separate the HAP layer from the substrate without altering particle morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a polymer structure whose characteristic vibrations decreased after washing, indicating its removal from the sample.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a polymer used to peel the Hydroxyapatite layer without causing distinct morphological changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PO3- Group">
  <data key="d0">PO3- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The PO3- group is a chemical moiety whose vibrations increased after washing, signaling the effective removal of PVA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water/Ethanol Mixture">
  <data key="d0">Water/Ethanol Mixture</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The water/ethanol mixture is a solvent treatment used to wash the sample, successfully removing almost all PVA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AL Molecules">
  <data key="d0">AL Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AL molecules are bisphosphonate compounds containing one hydroxyl group and two phosphate groups that bind to HAP.&lt;SEP&gt;AL molecules are organic compounds containing -NH2 groups that bind to HAP surfaces to alter chemical and physical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;AL Molecules are functional compounds used to modify the surface of Hydroxyapatite powders, confirmed by chemical shifts in spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Phosphate Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate crystals are crystalline structures to which AL molecules exhibit high affinity due to their chemical composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate crystals are synthesized with controlled size and shape for various biomedical and material science applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XPS Spectra">
  <data key="d0">XPS Spectra</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS spectra are analytical measurements used to determine binding energies and elemental assignments for HAP, HAP-AL, and pure AL samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
