<node id="XPS">
  <data key="d0">XPS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS is an analytical technique used to study the surface composition of functionalized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, a surface characterization technique employed for hydroxyapatite and calcium phosphates.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy used to detect elemental composition and confirm the capture of heavy metal ions.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS is an analytical method used to obtain full survey and high-resolution spectra for chemical bonding analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical technique used to determine the chemical states of sulfur and iron elements on sample surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS is employed to investigate the valence states of iron and sulfur in the slag samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS is an analytical method used to obtain full survey and high-resolution spectra for chemical bonding analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010</data>
