</node>
<node id="Alendronate (AL)">
  <data key="d0">Alendronate (AL)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Alendronate is a molecule used to functionalize hydroxyapatite powders for biomaterial applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Alendronate is an amino-bisphosphonate molecule with specific side groups that improve surface interactions and binding affinity with HAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zoledronate (ZOL)">
  <data key="d0">Zoledronate (ZOL)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Zoledronate is an amino-bisphosphonate compound noted for its electrostatic interactions and hydrogen bonding with calcium minerals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NTA">
  <data key="d0">NTA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">NTA is a chemical compound that selectively coordinates to Ca2+ ions, influencing HAP crystal growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrilotriacetic acid is an organic additive used to promote the fabrication of hierarchical HAP microparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;NTA is a tripodal tetradentate ligand that coordinates with calcium ions to form an intermediate complex during the reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;NTA is a tetradentate chelating agent used to control the crystal growth of Hydroxyapatite during synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fourier Transform Infrared (FTIR) Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">Fourier Transform Infrared (FTIR) Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">FTIR spectroscopy is used to confirm the surface modification of HAP with AL molecules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Deposition">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Deposition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal Deposition is the process used to deposit HAP on a substrate in the presence of calcium and phosphate precursors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammonium Dihydrogen Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Ammonium Dihydrogen Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonium Dihydrogen Phosphate is a chemical precursor used in the hydrothermal deposition of HAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyvinyl Alcohol (PVA)">
  <data key="d0">Polyvinyl Alcohol (PVA)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">PVA is a reagent used to successfully peel the deposited hydroxyapatite layer without morphological changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyvinyl Alcohol is a water-soluble polymer used to peel the as-deposited HAP layer to obtain powders.&lt;SEP&gt;A polymer used as an alternative peeling agent for hydroxyapatite layers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sigma-Aldrich">
  <data key="d0">Sigma-Aldrich</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sigma-Aldrich is a supplier of chemicals such as Calcium Chloride and Ammonium Dihydrogen Phosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical supplier that provided NTA, Fluoromount, alendronate sodium, and FTO glass.&lt;SEP&gt;Sigma-Aldrich is the supplier that provided key chemical reagents and surfactants for the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Sigma-Aldrich is the supplier from which potassium dihydrogen phosphate, sodium hydroxide, and Brij-93 were obtained.&lt;SEP&gt;A supplier of P123 surfactant used in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;A supplier of P123 surfactant used in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Sigma-Aldrich provided the reagent grade hydroxyapatite used as an initial standard for FT-IR measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
