<node id="Hydrothermal method">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal method is a synthesis technique used to prepare hierarchical HAP structures at various temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal method combines moderate temperatures with high pressures to prepare nanocrystalline hydroxyapatite with controlled size and morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal method is a synthesis technique using high temperature and pressure to influence crystal shape.&lt;SEP&gt;A general synthetic approach for obtaining hydroxyapatite microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
