  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to measure weight loss and dehydroxylation behavior of HAP microparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric analysis, the specific thermal treatment method applied to the phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to study the material, with a maximum temperature of 980°C.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is a thermal analysis method used to quantify calcium carbonate formation by measuring weight loss corresponding to carbon dioxide decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to measure mass loss and determine decomposition temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric analysis used to study phosphogypsum decomposition with coal.</data>
