  <data key="d0">JCPDS No. 96-900-1234</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">JCPDS No. 96-900-1234 is the standard reference card used to match the X-ray diffraction peaks of the synthesized Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="100 °C">
  <data key="d0">100 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">100 °C is the temperature threshold below which Hydroxyapatite exhibits low stability and crystallinity.&lt;SEP&gt;100 °C is a synthesis temperature at which nanocrystalline hydroxyapatite forms alongside impurity phases.&lt;SEP&gt;100 °C is the temperature maintained during the oven-drying phase of the synthesis process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427797</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="120 °C">
  <data key="d0">120 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">120 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S1.&lt;SEP&gt;120 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature yielding plate-like structures with irregular shapes.&lt;SEP&gt;120 °C is the temperature at which the hydrothermal treatment was conducted to synthesize the hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;120 °C is a specific reaction temperature applied during the material synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;A reaction temperature condition used during the synthesis process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792261759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="150 °C">
  <data key="d0">150 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">150 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S2.&lt;SEP&gt;150 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature where needle-like rods self-assemble into microparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;150 °C is a synthesis temperature at which quartz impurities dissolve, leaving calcium hydroxide as a side phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791628323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="165 °C">
  <data key="d0">165 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">165 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S3.&lt;SEP&gt;165 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature producing uniform flower-like hierarchical microparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="180 °C">
  <data key="d0">180 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">180 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Samples S4 through S8.&lt;SEP&gt;180 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature yielding larger flower-like hierarchical microparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;A treatment temperature applied to MPG that results in clustered crystals with surface damage and cracks.&lt;SEP&gt;180 °C is a specific calcination temperature used in the experimental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792299232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="400 °C">
  <data key="d0">400 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">400 °C is the temperature used for thermal treatment of HAP samples.&lt;SEP&gt;400 °C is the thermal treatment temperature applied for 30 minutes to evaluate morphological changes.&lt;SEP&gt;400 °C is the specific temperature parameter applied during high thermal post-treatment to affect nanoparticle shape.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="16 Hours">
  <data key="d0">16 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">16 Hours is an insufficient duration for hydrothermal deposition, resulting in no observed precipitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="20 Hours">
  <data key="d0">20 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">20 Hours is an insufficient duration for hydrothermal deposition, resulting in no observed precipitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plate-like Structures">
  <data key="d0">Plate-like Structures</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Plate-like Structures are the irregular morphological features formed at 120 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Plate-like structures are morphological formations in the s-HAp sample created by the agglomeration of spherical particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Plate-like Structures are agglomerated forms of S-HAp particles observed on the surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792177351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle-like Rods">
  <data key="d0">Needle-like Rods</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle-like Rods are the primary structural components that self-assemble at 150 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FTO">
  <data key="d0">FTO</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FTO is the substrate material on which the HAP layer is initially deposited before the peeling process.&lt;SEP&gt;FTO is a metal substrate used for the hydrothermal deposition and growth of hierarchical Hydroxyapatite structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XPS Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">XPS Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS Spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to measure binding energies and detect chemical shifts indicating successful functionalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
