  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM images capture microscopic morphology to evaluate particle aggregation and structural changes after peeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Microscopic visualizations revealing the morphological characteristics and particle size distribution of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM images are microscopic visualizations used to document the morphology of calcium sulfate dihydrate crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM images visually document the structural characteristics of CPGFM filling bodies at varying pH levels.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM images are microscopic visualizations used to analyze the surface morphology of synthesized HAp.</data>
