<node id="Blast Furnace Slag">
  <data key="d0">Blast Furnace Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Blast furnace slag is an industrial byproduct and solid waste characterized by a chemical composition rich in calcium, silica, alumina, and magnesium oxide, alongside iron oxides that directly influence its pH and viscosity. This versatile material is widely integrated into the construction industry, where it serves as a key component to partially replace clinker during the production of composite cement. Additionally, its specific mineral profile is utilized to meet composition requirements for slag wool, and researchers are actively investigating modified forms of the waste for advanced slag fiber production.

Beyond conventional building applications, blast furnace slag plays a significant role in environmental remediation and sustainable resource utilization. Its high calcium content makes it an effective source material for carbon dioxide fixation through carbonation processes, offering a pathway for greenhouse gas sequestration. Furthermore, the material is employed as a foundational raw material for synthesizing hydroxyapatite-zeolite composites, demonstrating its adaptability across diverse ecological and high-value industrial applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Blast furnace slag is an industrial byproduct mixed with phosphogypsum and clinker to produce specialized cement types.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792484618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
