<node id="TEM">
  <data key="d0">TEM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) is a high-resolution imaging and analytical characterization technique widely utilized to investigate the physical, structural, morphological, and internal microstructural properties of diverse synthesized materials. Frequently employed in conjunction with Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM), TEM provides detailed visual data that enables researchers to examine a wide range of samples, including nanoparticles, nanopowders, microspheres, and dried particles. The technique is particularly valued for its ability to measure precise nanorod dimensions, determine average particle size and diameter, assess overall morphology, and characterize particle size distributions. Additionally, TEM serves as a critical tool for analyzing phase and structure transformations within various compounds.

In the specific context of hydroxyapatite (HAp) and its nanohydroxyapatite (nHAp) variants, TEM plays an essential role in revealing internal structural details and confirming distinct crystalline characteristics. By analyzing these synthesized compounds, the technique successfully verifies the hexagonal crystalline structure and the P63/m space group of the particles. It is also specifically applied to observe the rod-like microstructure of dried hydroxyapatite particles and to examine the morphology and crystal structure of nHAp nanoparticles. Through these targeted applications, TEM facilitates a comprehensive understanding of the material properties, physical architecture, and microstructural evolution of the studied samples, making it an indispensable analytical tool in materials science and nanotechnology research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
