<node id="Sulfate Group">
  <data key="d0">Sulfate Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sulfate Group is a chemical moiety and component defined by the SO₄²⁻ formula and S-O bonding structure. It is routinely identified and analyzed through infrared (IR) and Fourier-transform infrared (FT-IR) spectroscopy, serving as a fundamental reference in the analytical characterization of various prepared chemical compounds.

Spectrally, the group is distinguished by characteristic vibrational signatures, including strong asymmetric stretching, bending, and symmetric deformation vibrations. These properties manifest as prominent absorption bands typically ranging from 1000 to 1100 cm⁻¹, with a specific asymmetric stretching peak frequently observed at 1095 cm⁻¹. Chemically, the Sulfate Group is highly characteristic of gypsum, as well as its hemi-hydrate and anhydrous forms, and functions as a core component within calcium sulfate compounds and ammonium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;The sulfate group is a chemical component characterized by a spectral dip around 872 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;The sulfate group is a chemical component with a higher relative concentration in the dotted black line sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427289</data>
