<node id="Bovine Serum Albumin (BSA)">
  <data key="d0">Bovine Serum Albumin (BSA)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bovine Serum Albumin (BSA) is a protein whose adsorption and loading amount on HAp were measured using UV and TG results.&lt;SEP&gt;Bovine serum albumin (BSA) is a negatively charged protein used to test the drug loading and release capacity of rod-shaped Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Bovine serum albumin (BSA) is a negatively charged protein used to test the drug loading and release capacity of rod-shaped Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001</data>
