<node id="FTIR Spectrum">
  <data key="d0">FTIR Spectrum</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FTIR Spectrum is a scientific graph plotting light transmittance against wavenumber to identify chemical bonds and functional groups.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectrum is a spectroscopic dataset used to reveal molecular vibrations, adsorbed water, and carbonate substitution in hydroxyapatite powders.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific chart used in chemistry to identify substances based on molecular vibrations, plotting light transmission against frequency.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic data representation showing vibrational bands of chemical groups like nitrate and water within the ionic liquid.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectrum is the graphical representation of infrared absorption data used to identify molecular vibrations and chemical compositions.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectrum is a line graph representing Fourier Transform Infrared spectroscopy data, displaying multiple spectral lines for different samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The FTIR Spectrum is a composite graph displaying infrared spectral ranges used to characterize the chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photon Energy">
  <data key="d0">Photon Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Photon energy is a measured parameter plotted on the x-axis of EDS spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon Energy serves as the horizontal axis metric for the EDS spectrum, representing X-ray energy in kilo-electron volts.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon energy, hv, is calculated using Planck's constant and wavelength, and is used to determine band gap energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon energy, hv, is calculated using Planck's constant and wavelength, and is used to determine band gap energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Counts">
  <data key="d0">Counts</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Counts serves as the vertical axis metric for the EDS spectrum, representing the intensity of detected X-rays.&lt;SEP&gt;Counts represent the frequency or number of occurrences plotted on the vertical axis of the histogram.&lt;SEP&gt;Counts represent the intensity of the X-ray diffraction signal on the Y-axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792364328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="O-H Stretching Vibrations">
  <data key="d0">O-H Stretching Vibrations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O-H stretching vibrations are chemical bond vibrations typically associated with water or hydroxyl groups in the 3000–3600 cm⁻¹ region.&lt;SEP&gt;O-H Stretching Vibrations are molecular motions associated with water molecules, appearing as a broad absorption feature.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical bond vibration labeled at approximately 3352.90 cm⁻¹, attributed to adsorbed water or hydroxyl groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792123793</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H-O-H Bending Vibrations">
  <data key="d0">H-O-H Bending Vibrations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">H-O-H bending vibrations are chemical bond vibrations associated with water, identified at the 1635 cm⁻¹ peak.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791486667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S-O Stretching Vibrations">
  <data key="d0">S-O Stretching Vibrations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">S-O stretching vibrations are characteristic chemical bond vibrations in sulfate groups, identified at the 1092 cm⁻¹ peak.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791486667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="K-Alpha Lines">
  <data key="d0">K-Alpha Lines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">K-alpha lines are specific energy emission lines where phosphorus appears in the EDS spectrum.</data>
