  <data key="d0">FTIR Spectra</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d2">FTIR spectra were recorded for pure HAp to compare with drug-loaded samples.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR spectra are analytical data representations used to identify chemical bonds and functional groups in hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrared spectroscopy data used to analyze the extraction mechanism and molecular interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectra is spectral data showing absorption bands that confirm the absence of sulfate groups and presence of phosphate groups in HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectra is spectral data showing absorption bands that confirm the absence of sulfate groups and presence of phosphate groups in HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectra are analytical data used to compare structural influences and identify specific chemical groups within the material.</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
