<node id="Heating Rate">
  <data key="d0">Heating Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Heating Rate is a fundamental experimental and process parameter defined as the rate at which temperature increases during thermal analysis, decomposition, or synthesis experiments. Quantitatively measured in degrees Celsius per minute or degrees Celsius per hour, it is conventionally denoted by the symbol β. As a controlled temperature increase speed, it serves as a critical variable in thermogravimetric analysis and kinetic studies, where it is frequently represented on the vertical axis of kinetic analysis plots. The heating rate directly governs the thermal exposure of samples, making it indispensable for calculating kinetic parameters and characterizing material behavior under varying thermal conditions.

In practical applications, the heating rate significantly influences experimental outcomes and material transformations. It affects the temperature and timing of phosphogypsum dehydration, modulates sample transformation during thermogravimetric analysis, and determines the quantity of intermediate calcium sulfide produced during decomposition. In synthesis contexts, it acts as a decisive process variable that differs across methods, directly controlling particle growth and nucleation speed. Standardized protocols often specify exact heating rates to ensure reproducibility, such as 10 °C/min for the thermogravimetric analysis of dried hydroxyapatite and general thermal analysis, 5 °C/min alongside a target temperature of 200 °C, and 15 °C/min for specific decomposition processes. By carefully adjusting this parameter, researchers can precisely manipulate reaction kinetics, optimize synthesis pathways, and accurately interpret thermogravimetric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Heating rate is a controlled experimental parameter set at 30°C/min during the clinker production tests by Kacimi et al.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
