<node id="Nitrogen Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen Atmosphere is a gaseous environment used during thermal treatment to determine that the gas has no effect on the phosphogypsum reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen atmosphere is a specific sintering condition used in Xiao and coworkers' three-step metal recovery method.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen Atmosphere is the inert gaseous environment used during thermogravimetric studies to prevent oxidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen Atmosphere serves as the controlled environment for the heating process.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen Atmosphere is the inert environment used during the decomposition and analysis of phosphogypsum.</data>
