<node id="Water Molecules">
  <data key="d0">Water Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Molecules are present in the raw sample and contribute to specific absorption features in the spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Water Molecules penetrate the PGCM matrix during the immersion stage and seep out during the drying stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Water molecules are present in the analyzed samples, contributing to O H stretching and bending vibration bands in the spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecules interconnected by molecular bonds and connected to sulfate ions via hydrogen bonds within the crystal structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H-O-H Bending Vibration">
  <data key="d0">H-O-H Bending Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A molecular vibration corresponding to the bending motion of water molecules, detected at a specific wavenumber.&lt;SEP&gt;H-O-H Bending Vibration is a molecular motion of water molecules observed around 1630 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;H-O-H bending vibration is the molecular vibration of water molecules observed around 1630 cm⁻¹.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asymmetric Stretching Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Asymmetric Stretching Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asymmetric Stretching Vibration is a vibrational mode of the sulfate ion observed around 1150–1170 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;Asymmetric stretching vibration corresponds to the sharp, strong peak around 1100 cm⁻¹ in the sulfate ion spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Asymmetric stretching vibration is the molecular vibration of the sulfate ion responsible for the dominant peak.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symmetric Stretching Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Symmetric Stretching Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symmetric Stretching Vibration is a vibrational mode of the sulfate ion identified in the spectral attribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dehydration Process">
  <data key="d0">Dehydration Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dehydration Process involves heating the sample to remove crystallization water and convert dihydrate to anhydrite forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration process is a thermal process applied to synthetic PG that triggers phase transformations at specific temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792406487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
