<node id="Hexagonal Structure">
  <data key="d0">Hexagonal Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hexagonal structure refers to the crystal lattice form of anhydrite III.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hexagonal Structure describes the crystallographic lattice arrangement of the synthesized Hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexagonal Structure is the crystallographic lattice structure exhibited by all synthesized hydroxyapatite types.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexagonal structure describes the crystalline morphology of the hydroxyapatite nanoparticles derived from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-010</data>
