</node>
<node id="Curing Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Curing Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Curing Conditions refer to the controlled environment of 20±2°C and 50±5% relative humidity applied after initial natural curing.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing conditions refer to controlled temperature and humidity environments applied to specimens to optimize material performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing conditions refer to the environmental settings (water or air at 20°C) used to harden construction specimens over a specified duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental states (Air or Moist) that influence the compressive strength of material samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baking Process">
  <data key="d0">Baking Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Baking Process is a drying procedure conducted at 40±2°C until specimen mass stabilizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
