  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791515834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry-Wet Cycle Test">
  <data key="d0">Dry-Wet Cycle Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deterioration experiment used to evaluate the weathering performance of the cementitious materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791515834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Resistance Test">
  <data key="d0">Water Resistance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A long-term performance experiment used to explore the water resistance of the cementitious materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791515834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Length Shrinkage Test">
  <data key="d0">Length Shrinkage Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A long-term performance experiment used to summarize the length shrinkage law of the cementitious materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure to measure dimensional changes in specimens over various curing periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791515834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RPG">
  <data key="d0">RPG</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RPG is an abbreviation for raw phosphogypsum, noted for its low cementitious property.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791515834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blank Control Group">
  <data key="d0">Blank Control Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The blank control group is a comparison group without quicklime, cement, or silica fume.&lt;SEP&gt;The blank control group serves as a baseline for comparing the compressive strength of PGCM specimens cured in water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solvation Rate">
  <data key="d0">Solvation Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solvation rate is a parameter determined for specimens after freeze-thaw and wet-dry cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Term Soaking In Water">
  <data key="d0">Long-Term Soaking In Water</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-term soaking in water is a curing method used to determine the compressive strength of samples at specified ages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freeze-thaw Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Freeze-thaw Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Freeze-thaw Cycle is an environmental testing condition that causes significant damage to PGCM as the number of cycles increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry-wet Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Dry-wet Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry-wet Cycle is an environmental testing condition that results in less damage to PGCM compared to freeze-thaw cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Curing in Water">
  <data key="d0">Curing in Water</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Curing in water is a maintenance condition that provides a water-filled environment to accelerate cement hydration and improve compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing in Water is a condition that yields more significant compressive strength improvements from admixtures compared to air curing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Curing in Air">
  <data key="d0">Curing in Air</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Curing in air is a maintenance condition where specimens are exposed to air, leading to slower hydration and varying compressive strength outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing in Air is a baseline curing condition for PGCM samples, showing lower strength improvements from admixtures than water curing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Silicate Hydrate Gel">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Silicate Hydrate Gel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium silicate hydrate gel is a primary hydration product that bonds to phosphogypsum particles to form an adhesive layer.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Silicate Hydrate Gel is a hydration product in PGCM that enhances interfacial adhesion and mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium silicate hydrate gel is a flocculent hydration product formed during the curing of filling materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791723719</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
