<node id="Chemical Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The chemical reaction during which gypsum crystals precipitate and form agglomerates.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical reaction is the process involving the conversion of gypsum into hydroxyapatite, analyzed using enthalpy values.&lt;SEP&gt;The process where gypsum and phosphoric acid react to form hydroxyapatite, sulfuric acid, and water, enabling phosphogypsum valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;The chemical reaction involves the conversion of specific reactants into products, analyzed for thermodynamic properties.</data>
