<node id="Curing Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Curing Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A controlled environmental parameter maintained at 20 ± 2 °C during long-term water resistance testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing temperature influences the generation of hydration products and inversely affects fluoride leaching rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing temperature is a variable investigated for its effect on the unconfined compressive strength of phosphogypsum specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing temperature is a process parameter elevated from room temperature to 40-85°C to accelerate hydration and improve strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relative Humidity">
