  <data key="d5">1791529642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Human Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Human tissue is the biological environment where hydroxyapatite exhibits rapid biomineralization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sinterability">
  <data key="d0">Sinterability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sinterability is a superior property of hydroxyapatite derived from chicken eggshells.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure is a synthesis parameter in the hydrothermal method, reaching up to 100 KPa.&lt;SEP&gt;Pressure is a controlled operating parameter of the MSS2 reactor, reaching up to 6 MPa.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791857078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microwave Energy">
  <data key="d0">Microwave Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microwave energy is converted in situ into heat during microwave irradiation synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heat">
  <data key="d0">Heat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat is generated in situ from microwave energy, enabling rapid solution volume treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal energy generated by phosphogypsum due to residual radioactivity or chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat is a minor source of carbon emissions, ranking fourth in the emission contribution trend.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792226716</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precursor Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Precursor Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Precursor solutions containing calcium hydroxide and phosphoric acid are mixed to synthesize hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aging Process">
  <data key="d0">Aging Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The aging process involves storing the precursor solution at 80°C under magnetic stirring for 2 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eggshell Powder">
  <data key="d0">Eggshell Powder</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Eggshell powder is the fine particulate material produced by grinding dried chicken eggshells.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystal Size">
  <data key="d0">Crystal Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystal size is a physical parameter estimated for hydroxyapatite powders and documented in experimental results.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal size is a quantitative measurement of hydroxyapatite crystallite dimensions, which increases with longer synthesis times.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal size refers to the 28 nm dimension of nHAp calculated from the XRD diffraction peak using the Scherrer equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Bone Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone hydroxyapatite serves as a biological reference standard with a typical Ca/P ratio between 1.5 and 1.85 and crystallites in the 20–40 nm range.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Hydroxyapatite is the natural biological reference material that the synthesized hydroxyapatite mimics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791529777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyapatite Samples">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite Samples</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite samples are synthesized materials evaluated for crystal size, carbonate content, and Ca/P ratio using various analytical methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite Samples (HAP1, HAP2, HAP3) are material samples analyzed to study thermal behavior and modification with BSA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791748680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type B Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Type B Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Type B hydroxyapatite is a structural classification defined by carbonate ion substitution from the ambient atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Type B Hydroxyapatite is a specific variant of hydroxyapatite formed when phosphate ions are substituted by carbonate ions during synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003</data>
