<node id="pH 9">
  <data key="d0">pH 9</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pH 9 is a synthesis parameter that produced hydroxyapatite powders with lower carbonation compared to pH 11.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 9 represents an experimental condition corresponding to an alkaline sample analyzed in the X-ray diffraction study.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkaline pH condition maintained during the chemical reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 9 is the adjusted alkaline condition used to precipitate metal ions as hydroxides.</data>
