<node id="Activation Energy">
  <data key="d0">Activation Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation energy is a type of energy value that Ei likely represents in the context of molecular transitions.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation energy is the minimum energy required for the reorganization of Posner's clusters into HA crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation Energy is a kinetic parameter measured in kJ/mol, evaluated across various reaction models.&lt;SEP&gt;A kinetic parameter calculated using various methods, representing the energy barrier for the phosphogypsum decomposition reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation Energy is a kinetic parameter measured in kilojoules per mole, calculated at various heating rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation Energy is a reaction parameter representing the energy required for decomposition or dehydration, calculated from the plot's slope.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation energy ($E_a$) is a chemical parameter representing the energy required for decomposition or dehydration reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792363202</data>
