<node id="Nanowires">
  <data key="d0">Nanowires</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanowires are a type of nanostructure similar to nanorods, appearing as elongated structures within the aggregated sample cluster.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Equation">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration Equation is a mathematical formula used to calculate the exact percentage of carbonate impurity from FTIR spectral ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sample Label">
  <data key="d0">Sample Label</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sample Label is text reading MW11-36min that identifies the sample and indicates its microwave treatment duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Phase Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase Transformation is a material change process induced by microwave irradiation, leading to the observed nanostructure morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;The structural and chemical changes occurring during the reduction process, critical for understanding desulfurization efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Process illustrating the conversion from Phosphogypsum to Nano-Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrated Intensity">
  <data key="d0">Integrated Intensity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Integrated Intensity represents the area under spectral peaks, used as the numerator and denominator in the calibration equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorption Peak">
  <data key="d0">Absorption Peak</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Absorption Peak refers to specific points in the infrared spectrum at 1458 cm⁻¹ and 604 cm⁻¹ corresponding to molecular vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorption peak at 3437.8 cm^-1 corresponds to the stretching and bending vibration of H-O bonds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673877</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Parameter">
  <data key="d0">Energy Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy Parameter is a variable representing spectral intensity values at specific wavenumbers in the logarithmic ratio equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1458 cm⁻¹">
  <data key="d0">1458 cm⁻¹</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1458 cm⁻¹ is the wavenumber characteristic of the asymmetric stretching vibration of carbonate ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="604 cm⁻¹">
  <data key="d0">604 cm⁻¹</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">604 cm⁻¹ is the wavenumber characteristic of the bending vibration of sulfate groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T1">
  <data key="d0">T1</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">T1 is a temperature variable used in the logarithmic ratio equation for energy parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;T1 is a sample ID corresponding to microspheres synthesized for 1 hour of hydrothermal time.&lt;SEP&gt;PG-based subgrade materials technology, which performs best in freshwater consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;T1 is a technology in the mid-range utility group with peaks generally located between 0.55 and 0.75.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T2">
  <data key="d0">T2</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">T2 is a temperature variable used in the logarithmic ratio equation for energy parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;T2 is a sample ID corresponding to microspheres synthesized for 2 hours of hydrothermal time.&lt;SEP&gt;A PG recycling technology identified as having better performance for most indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;T2 is a technology in the mid-range utility group with peaks generally located between 0.55 and 0.75.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
