<node id="Stoichiometric Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Stoichiometric Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Stoichiometric Ratio is a chemical standard that the HT11-12h sample exceeded in calcium-to-phosphorus proportion.&lt;SEP&gt;The stoichiometric ratio refers to the ideal molar Ca/P ratio of 1.67 for HAp particles, used as a benchmark for purity.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoichiometric Ratio represents the ideal molar Ca/P ratio of 1.67 for HAp particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792177351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
