  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Hydroxide (Ca(OH)2)">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Hydroxide (Ca(OH)2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium hydroxide is an intermediate phase formed during the hydrothermal conversion of phosphogypsum, which decreases with increasing synthesis time.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound identified as Peak 4 in the chart.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792364185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rietveld Refinement">
  <data key="d0">Rietveld Refinement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A computational technique used to analyze XRD data and determine crystal structure parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Rietveld refinement is a computational technique applied to XRD data to determine precise crystal structure parameters and unit cell dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Rietveld refinement is a computational method used for analyzing powder diffraction patterns and matching crystal structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A computational method applied to XRD data to confirm crystal structure and determine unit cell parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Rietveld Refinement is a crystallographic analysis technique used to interpret powder diffraction data.&lt;SEP&gt;Rietveld Refinement is a quantitative phase analysis technique used to determine the phase percentages of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791834567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brij-93 Surfactant">
  <data key="d0">Brij-93 Surfactant</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brij-93 Surfactant is a chemical additive and surfactant compound utilized during the synthesis of hydroxyapatite (HAp), with specific applications noted in hydrothermal synthesis processes. It is extensively investigated and employed as a functional agent to regulate the crystallization, morphology, and aspect ratio of HAp crystals and particles.

The primary mechanism of Brij-93 Surfactant involves capping the surfaces of growing HAp crystals, which effectively directs and promotes unidirectional growth. By controlling particle morphology and actively preventing agglomeration during the synthesis phase, it serves as a critical tool for tailoring the structural and morphological properties of synthesized hydroxyapatite materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791626361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sphere Model">
  <data key="d0">Sphere Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The sphere model is an initial modeling approach for XRD refinement that resulted in poor fitting due to inaccurate peak broadening assumptions.&lt;SEP&gt;A modeling approach used in initial Rietveld refinement attempts that resulted in poor fitting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle-like Coherent Domains Model">
  <data key="d0">Needle-like Coherent Domains Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The needle-like coherent domains model is a refined approach that improves XRD fitting by accounting for preferential crystalline growth along the c-axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="200°C">
  <data key="d0">200°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">200°C is the constant temperature maintained during the hydrothermal synthesis process to drive phase conversion reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15 Hours">
  <data key="d0">15 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">15 hours is the synthesis duration required for the complete reaction of calcium hydroxide with phosphate anions to form stoichiometric hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;The duration of the hydrothermal synthesis process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627879</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rod-like Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Rod-like Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rod-like crystals describe the observed morphological characteristic of the synthesized hydroxyapatite, resulting from preferential growth along the c-axis.&lt;SEP&gt;Rod-like crystals are elongated crystalline structures measuring 40 nm in length and 15 nm in diameter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791857078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphate Anions">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Anions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate anions ($\mathrm{PO_4^{3-}}$) are free ions in the solution that react with calcium hydroxide to form hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate Anions are negatively charged ions on hydroxyapatite surfaces that interact with positively charged protein groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate anions are contaminants whose emissions to soil and water lack damage factors in the primary impact assessment method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791880740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Cell Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Unit Cell Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unit cell parameters ($a$, $b$, $c$) are structural dimensions determined via Rietveld refinement to characterize the hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural measurements including space group, Z value, and lattice constants determined for HAp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Convergence Factor ($R_{wp}$)">
  <data key="d0">Convergence Factor ($R_{wp}$)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The convergence factor ($R_{wp}$) is a statistical metric used in Rietveld refinement to evaluate the quality of the fit between observed and calculated XRD patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isotropic Peak Broadening">
  <data key="d0">Isotropic Peak Broadening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Isotropic peak broadening is a modeling assumption applied to XRD reflections that initially resulted in poor fitting for the hydroxyapatite sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="00l Reflections">
  <data key="d0">00l Reflections</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">00l reflections are specific XRD peaks that were observed to be significantly narrower, indicating anisotropic crystalline growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="c-axis">
  <data key="d0">c-axis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The c-axis is the crystallographic direction along which preferential growth of the hydroxyapatite crystals occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Space Group No. 176">
  <data key="d0">Space Group No. 176</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Space Group No. 176 corresponds to the $P6_3/m$ symmetry classification determined for the synthesized hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791542358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aspect Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Aspect Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspect Ratio is a quantitative metric representing the particle length to diameter ratio, ranging from 3.5 to 10-13.&lt;SEP&gt;A morphological parameter defined as the ratio of particle length to particle diameter, which increases with surfactant addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspect Ratio is a geometric measurement representing the length-to-diameter ratio of the synthesized rod-like particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative measure of particle elongation, calculated as length divided by diameter.&lt;SEP&gt;A geometric property of MPG crystal particles that decreases following calcination, indicating improved crystal quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792299232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Co-B-N-H Nanowires">
  <data key="d0">Co-B-N-H Nanowires</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-B-N-H Nanowires are a previously synthesized material compared to the current study, where Brij surfactant similarly influenced morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-B-N-H nanowires are a previously synthesized material that exhibited a similar morphological effect when using Brij surfactant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791626951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="200 °C">
  <data key="d0">200 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">200 °C is the temperature condition maintained during the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;200 °C is the specific temperature maintained during the hydrothermal synthesis process.&lt;SEP&gt;200 °C is the synthesis temperature required to obtain phase pure nanocrystalline hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;The synthesis temperature maintained during the hydrothermal conversion process.&lt;SEP&gt;The synthesis temperature required for hydrothermal preparation of HAp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15 h">
  <data key="d0">15 h</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">15 h is the duration of the hydrothermal synthesis process for the hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;15 h denotes the sufficient duration required for hydrothermal synthesis to achieve phase purity.&lt;SEP&gt;15 h is the duration used for hydrothermal synthesis at 200 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;The required synthesis duration for the complete conversion of Ca(OH)₂ into HAp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-Phase Model">
  <data key="d0">Single-Phase Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Single-Phase Model is used for structure refinement from XRD data of the Hydroxyapatite sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-Phase Model is a crystallographic analysis approach used to refine XRD data for the hydroxyapatite sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A single-phase model is used in XRD data refinement to analyze peak widths and broadening for HAp samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791626951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isotropic Peak Widths">
  <data key="d0">Isotropic Peak Widths</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Isotropic Peak Widths is an XRD refinement parameter assuming uniform peak broadening across all reflections.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791543258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anisotropic Peak Broadening">
  <data key="d0">Anisotropic Peak Broadening</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anisotropic Peak Broadening is an XRD refinement parameter accounting for direction-dependent peak widening in 00l reflections.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791543258</data>
