<node id="ICP-OES Analysis">
  <data key="d0">ICP-OES Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ICP-OES Analysis is a measurement technique used to determine the Ca/P ratio and evaluate the structural similarity of hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical technique used to determine the elemental composition and Ca/P ratio of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical technique used to determine the calcium-to-phosphorus ratio of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical technique used to determine the calcium to phosphorus ratio of synthetic hydroxyapatite and bone ash samples by mass.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-OES Analysis is an analytical technique used to determine the elemental composition and Ca/P ratio of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical method used to evaluate the calcium-to-phosphorus ratio of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-OES Analysis is a technique used to measure the calcium-to-phosphorus ratio of the samples.</data>
