<node id="Bone China">
  <data key="d0">Bone China</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone China is a specialty tableware product characterized by high mechanical strength, whiteness, and translucency, typically containing bone ash.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial application evaluated for s-HAp particles as a substitute to bone ash.&lt;SEP&gt;A ceramic product where phosphogypsum-based synthetic hydroxyapatite particles could potentially be commercially applied as a bone ash substitute.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone china is a ceramic material extensively characterized for its microstructure, fracture toughness, and formulation variations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone China is a high-strength specialty tableware product typically formulated with bone ash, clay, and fluxing materials.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial application where s-HAp particles could be evaluated as a substitute for bone ash.&lt;SEP&gt;A ceramic material extensively studied in the referenced literature for its microstructure, properties, and formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-001</data>
