<node id="Bone Ash">
  <data key="d0">Bone Ash</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A natural calcium phosphate material used as a benchmark for comparing synthetic hydroxyapatite properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Ash is a natural material derived from bones, traditionally used as a primary component in bone china formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Ash is a natural material used as a commercial benchmark for comparing synthetic hydroxyapatite particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural material compared with synthetic hydroxyapatite, showing a higher calcium to phosphorus ratio and distinct morphological features.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural sample used as a comparative reference for synthetic hydroxyapatite characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Ash is a natural material derived from bones, traditionally used as a primary component in bone china formulations.</data>
