<node id="ICP-OES">
  <data key="d0">ICP-OES</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ICP-OES is an analytical technique and instrument utilized for chemical analysis and elemental characterization across a variety of material types. It is primarily employed to determine the major, minor, and trace elemental composition of solid samples, including solid products and specific materials such as hydroxyapatite. The method is also applied to liquid and prepared specimens, such as phosphogypsum leachate and samples prepared with powder, water, and acid.

A key application of ICP-OES involves the precise determination of the calcium-to-phosphorus (Ca/P) molar ratio in hydroxyapatite and other material samples. Additionally, it serves as a critical tool for characterizing the detailed chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples. Overall, ICP-OES functions as a versatile measurement technique for assessing both the broad chemical makeup and specific elemental ratios of diverse solid and liquid specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical technique used to determine elemental composition and Ca/P ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-OES is an analytical technique used to measure the calcium-to-phosphorus ratio in hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-OES is an analytical technique used for characterizing the chemical composition of synthesized materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792177218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
