<node id="Thermodynamic Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Thermodynamic Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermodynamic analysis is the computational evaluation used to determine the feasibility and spontaneity of the reaction sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermodynamic analysis is used to construct the PGI system and determine melting characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermodynamic analysis evaluates the feasibility of the reaction sequence by calculating enthalpy changes and assessing exothermic properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermodynamic Analysis is a calculation method used to predict reaction temperatures and feasibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-004</data>
