<node id="Exothermic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Exothermic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exothermic Reaction describes the heat-releasing nature of the proposed reaction steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic reactions are thermal events indicated by downward peaks in the Differential Thermal Analysis curve.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic Reaction is a chemical process hypothesized to cause decreased stripping efficiency at elevated temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic reaction describes the energy-releasing nature of the proposed chemical steps, indicating thermodynamic spontaneity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792177532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrium Constant">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrium Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equilibrium Constant is a thermodynamic parameter reduced by increased temperature, affecting product yield.&lt;SEP&gt;The equilibrium constant is a thermodynamic parameter that decreases with temperature increases, affecting product concentration at equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-004</data>
