<node id="Conversion">
  <data key="d0">Conversion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conversion is the chemical process step where reagents are added to the slurry to produce new compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversion is a chemical process involving the reaction of Phosphogypsum and Sodium Hydroxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversion is a chemical process step where reagents are added to the slurry to synthesize new compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversion denotes the fraction of reactant transformed during the decomposition process.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversion represents the degree of phosphogypsum transformation over time in the kinetic model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-002</data>
