<node id="Table 7">
  <data key="d0">Table 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 7 refers to multiple distinct data tables found across various scientific publications, each serving a specific analytical purpose. In studies focused on phosphogypsum processing, one instance documents the average concentrations of radioelements and toxic elements during the preparation and transformation of phosphogypsum-derived compounds. Another variation addresses environmental compliance and leaching behavior by summarizing trace element leaching concentrations from Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure (TCLP) tests on raw phosphogypsum, explicitly comparing these results against United States Environmental Protection Agency (US-EPA) regulatory limits. A third context within phosphogypsum research utilizes Table 7 to illustrate the basic mechanical properties and water consumption requirements of modified phosphogypsum samples under various experimental conditions.

In materials science and crystallography applications, Table 7 presents crystalline lattice parameters and phase composition data. Specifically, it summarizes lattice parameters determined through X-ray diffraction (XRD) analysis for synthesized hydroxyapatite, providing structural insights into the material. Finally, in environmental impact assessment research, Table 7 tracks and presents the changes in pollutant emission impacts across four distinct operational scenarios. Collectively, these entries demonstrate that Table 7 functions as a recurring placeholder identifier used in different research documents to report diverse datasets ranging from geochemical concentrations and leaching tests to crystallographic parameters and emission impact analyses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 8">
  <data key="d0">Table 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 8 is a generic designation used across multiple independent scientific and engineering studies to present distinct datasets. In the context of phosphogypsum processing and material science, one instance of Table 8 documents the average concentrations of trace elements and the transfer factors of toxic elements during the preparation and transformation of phosphogypsum-derived compounds. This specific table also presents thermogravimetric analysis results, detailing specific surface areas and weight loss percentages for various hydroxyapatite samples. In geotechnical engineering applications, a separate Table 8 reports the physical properties and geotechnical characterization test results for designed soil mixes labeled E1, E2, and E3, including measurements of pH, shear strength, and Proctor compaction data.

In environmental and scenario-based analyses, another Table 8 compiles quantitative indicators across four distinct scenarios. This version specifically lists the EYR and ELR values, calculated SEI values with their corresponding change rates, and carbon emission intensity metrics. Collectively, these entries demonstrate that Table 8 serves as a standardized data presentation format across diverse research domains, ranging from chemical transformation and material characterization to geotechnical testing and environmental impact assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 8 is a data table presenting the phase composition of MPG under varying temperatures and holding times.&lt;SEP&gt;A table detailing the phase composition of MPG, highlighting hemihydrate gypsum content at 180 °C/10 h.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301054</data>
