<node id="Detergents">
  <data key="d0">Detergents</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Detergents is an industry that utilizes phosphogypsum as a valuable resource through valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Detergents are non-food uses of mined phosphorus that enter the wastewater system and are exported from the food system.&lt;SEP&gt;Detergents are products containing phosphorus produced and consumed in Australia.&lt;SEP&gt;Detergents are household and commercial cleaning products that contribute phosphorus to wastewater streams.&lt;SEP&gt;Detergents are industrial products manufactured using domestically consumed phosphate rock.&lt;SEP&gt;An input material directed into the wastewater processing unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003</data>
