  <data key="d0">Ammonium Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonium chloride is a chloride solution used to study the solubility of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chloride salt reagent added to the process to react with gypsum and form ammonium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium chloride is a chemical additive used in low-temperature calcination to reduce soluble phosphorus and fluorine content.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Chloride is a salt used in conjunction with ammonium hydroxide to prepare an alkaline buffer solution.</data>
