<node id="Light Rare Earth Elements">
  <data key="d0">Light Rare Earth Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Light rare earth elements are a classification of rare earth elements grouped by atomic mass.&lt;SEP&gt;Light rare earth elements, including lanthanum, cerium, and neodymium, are the primary components recovered in the leach liquor.&lt;SEP&gt;Light rare earth elements, ranging from Lanthanum to Samarium, constitute 60-80% of REEs in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Light Rare Earth Elements are trace elements found in Phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002</data>
