<node id="Pozzolanic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Pozzolanic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pozzolanic reaction is a chemical process activated by phosphogypsum when treating volcanic tuffs.&lt;SEP&gt;Pozzolanic reaction is a chemical process facilitated by calcium and sulfate ions released from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process involving the development of binding properties in materials under wetting and drying conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The pozzolanic reaction occurs between calcium, aluminium, and sulfates species to form calcium sulfo aluminate minerals.&lt;SEP&gt;Pozzolanic reaction is a chemical process between silicate materials and lime that is accelerated by calcined phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process accelerated by calcined phosphogypsum that enhances the mechanical strength of fly ash mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Pozzolanic reaction is a chemical process in cementitious materials that requires adequate temperature and curing period to occur effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
