<node id="Total Phosphorus Pollution">
  <data key="d0">Total Phosphorus Pollution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total phosphorus pollution is a major environmental issue in the Yangtze River, primarily caused by the phosphate industry and phosphogypsum tailings ponds.&lt;SEP&gt;Total phosphorus pollution refers to the contamination of water bodies, particularly in the Yangtze River Basin, caused by industrial and agricultural runoff.&lt;SEP&gt;An environmental issue in the Yangtze River Basin that prompted policy development and control strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791610049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Building Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Building Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Building gypsum is a high-value product manufactured from phosphogypsum for construction applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Building gypsum is a construction material produced through the calcination of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A construction material whose mechanical properties and water consumption are improved through phosphogypsum milling treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Gypsum refers to a Chinese standard that stipulates minimum compressive strength requirements for gypsum materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Building gypsum is a construction material whose setting time and strength are evaluated under the influence of various retarders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792300494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
