<node id="Phosphogypsum Tailings Ponds">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Tailings Ponds</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum tailings ponds are the largest contributors to total phosphorus emissions. Phosphogypsum tailings ponds pose major safety and environmental risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum tailings ponds are regulated facilities requiring monitoring and remediation under Yangtze River protection policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum tailings ponds are waste management sites represented in the industrial statistics chart.&lt;SEP&gt;A waste management category dealing with phosphogypsum waste storage and tailings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-014</data>
