<node id="Recrystallization Process">
  <data key="d0">Recrystallization Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The recrystallization process is a two-step method that produces alpha-hemihydrate phosphogypsum with superior cementitious properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization processes are wet process categories intended to enhance phosphorus pentoxide recovery efficiency and produce purer filter cakes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792406917</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tailings Ponds">
  <data key="d0">Tailings Ponds</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tailings ponds are storage structures used to stockpile phosphogypsum, often constructed by damming valleys or repurposing mining sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage facilities for phosphogypsum that require improved management to prevent environmental issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-009</data>
