  <data key="d2">Anhydrous gypsum type II is a high-value phosphogypsum derivative produced via calcination above 700°C, noted for enhanced water resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous gypsum type II is a form of phosphogypsum produced via the thermal process, characterized by minimal impurities and medical-grade suitability.</data>
