<node id="Gypsum Building Materials">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Building Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Building Materials are traditional construction products manufactured using processed phosphogypsum as a primary raw material. They currently serve as the main utilization pathway for this industrial byproduct, accounting for 22% of its total consumption within the construction sector. From a technical perspective, the structural integrity and quality of these materials can become unstable if the source phosphogypsum contains elevated levels of silica.

Although classified as a major and dominant application route, this pathway is also described as a secondary utilization method that typically yields low value-added products and operates within a market characterized by severe homogenized competition. In industry visualizations and charts, this specific utilization pathway is conventionally represented by the color green.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum building materials are construction products whose development trends are analyzed under carbon peak and neutralization contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792226294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
