  <data key="d0">60°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">60°C is the temperature maintained during the magnetic stirring and amalgamation of Solution A and Solution B.&lt;SEP&gt;60°C is the reaction temperature used in the chemical precipitation method.&lt;SEP&gt;60°C is the high temperature condition applied during the leaching experiments to investigate temperature effects.&lt;SEP&gt;60°C is a heating temperature used in buffer preparation and chemical reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-003</data>
