  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystal Planes are specific atomic lattice orientations in hydroxyapatite identified through XRD diffraction patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural planes within a material whose orientation and alignment are analyzed using texture coefficients.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal planes such as (211), (112), and (300) are indexed in the XRD patterns to identify the hydroxyapatite phase.</data>
