<node id="Hydration of Hemihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Hydration of Hemihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration of Hemihydrate Gypsum is the chemical process converting hemihydrate gypsum to dihydrate gypsum, represented by a specific chemical equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dissolution Crystallization Theory">
  <data key="d0">Dissolution Crystallization Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dissolution Crystallization Theory is a theoretical pathway explaining the hydration process through solubility differences and ion release.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution crystallization theory explains gypsum hydration through solubility saturation and spontaneous crystallization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792299784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Colloid Theory">
  <data key="d0">Colloid Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Colloid Theory is an alternative theoretical pathway describing the hydration process via complex compounds, hydrosols, and continuous cohesion.&lt;SEP&gt;Colloid theory describes gypsum hydration as a gel-forming process similar to cement hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792299950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dissolution Process of Hemihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Dissolution Process of Hemihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dissolution Process of Hemihydrate Gypsum is the initial step where hemihydrate gypsum releases calcium and sulfate ions into solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallization Process of Dihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Crystallization Process of Dihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallization Process of Dihydrate Gypsum is the subsequent step where dihydrate gypsum forms and disrupts the solubility equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grashof Number">
  <data key="d0">Grashof Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dimensionless number used alongside the Rayleigh and Prandtl numbers to model convection.&lt;SEP&gt;A dimensionless number in fluid dynamics that approximates the ratio of buoyancy to viscous force and determines the onset of natural convection.&lt;SEP&gt;Grashof Number is a dimensionless parameter in fluid dynamics and heat transfer used to characterize natural convection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grashof Number Equation">
  <data key="d0">Grashof Number Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Grashof Number Equation is the mathematical formula $Gr = \frac{g \beta \Delta T H^3}{v^2}$ defining the Grashof Number.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Quantities Relationship Equation">
  <data key="d0">Physical Quantities Relationship Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Quantities Relationship Equation is the mathematical formula $y = Y \times 4x^2 / L$ defining a relationship between physical variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluid Dynamics">
  <data key="d0">Fluid Dynamics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluid Dynamics is a branch of physics concerned with fluid flow, providing the theoretical context for the Grashof Number.&lt;SEP&gt;A branch of physics concerned with the flow of fluids and the forces acting on them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heat Transfer">
  <data key="d0">Heat Transfer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heat Transfer is the physical process of thermal energy exchange, closely linked to fluid dynamics in phosphogypsum applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A discipline of physics dealing with the generation, use, conversion, and exchange of thermal energy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Convection">
  <data key="d0">Natural Convection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fluid dynamics phenomenon modeled in PGEF to calculate the optimum air layer thickness.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural convection is a physical process modeled mathematically for PGEF in Fig. 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Convection is a fluid motion mechanism driven by buoyancy forces, analyzed using the Grashof Number in phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanism of heat transfer driven by buoyancy forces due to temperature differences in a fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alpha">
  <data key="d0">Alpha</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alpha is an angle between the vertical axis and the slanted blue line in the trapezoid diagram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theta">
  <data key="d0">Theta</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Theta is an angle adjacent to alpha, likely defining the spread of stress or geometry.&lt;SEP&gt;Theta represents the diffraction angle on the X-axis of the diffractogram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792364328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Hydration Equation">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Hydration Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The chemical equation CaSO4·0.5H2O + 1.5H2O → CaSO4·2H2O + X represents the hydration reaction of hemihydrate gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solubility HG &gt; DG">
  <data key="d0">Solubility HG &gt; DG</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solubility HG &gt; DG indicates that hemihydrate gypsum solubility is greater than dihydrate gypsum solubility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saturation Solubility of Hemihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Saturation Solubility of Hemihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Saturation solubility of hemihydrate gypsum is represented by a vertical dashed green line in the dissolution crystallization pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Compound">
  <data key="d0">Complex Compound</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Complex compound is an intermediate stage in the colloid theory pathway of gypsum hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrosol">
  <data key="d0">Hydrosol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrosol is a stage following the complex compound in the colloid theory pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelling Crystallization of Dihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Gelling Crystallization of Dihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelling crystallization of dihydrate gypsum is the final stage in the colloid theory pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Cohesion">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Cohesion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous cohesion describes the process linking hydrosol to the gelling crystallization of dihydrate gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixing With Water">
  <data key="d0">Mixing With Water</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixing with water is the process step that transforms hemihydrate gypsum into the hydration progress stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grashof Number Variables">
  <data key="d0">Grashof Number Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Grashof Number Variables include g, beta, Delta T, H, and v, which are components of the Grashof Number equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Variables">
  <data key="d0">Physical Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Variables include y, Y, x, and L, which are components of the linear mathematical equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PGEF">
  <data key="d0">PGEF</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PGEF is a modified phosphogypsum-based embedded filler characterized by a regular, dense, and interlocking crystalline microstructure.&lt;SEP&gt;PGEF is a modified phosphogypsum embedded filler whose stress performance, thermal insulation, and microstructure were analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;PGEF is a novel construction material prepared in the research, utilized in cast-in situ concrete hollow floor structures to reduce weight and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modified Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Modified Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Modified Phosphogypsum serves as a primary material component in the formulation of PGEF, characterized by low cost and absence of secondary contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified Phosphogypsum is a thermodynamically treated form of phosphogypsum used in construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified Phosphogypsum is a processed form of phosphogypsum used to assess environmental hazards and applied in construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified Phosphogypsum is a processed variant of phosphogypsum whose properties are enhanced through controlled calcination and drying.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified phosphogypsum is an intermediate processed material with reduced heavy metal content and no environmental safety risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792300104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polypropylene Fiber">
  <data key="d0">Polypropylene Fiber</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polypropylene Fiber is a locally sourced material used as a 0.5% mass ratio component in the filler mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;Polypropylene Fiber is incorporated as a material component in the PGEF mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
