  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration Mechanism refers to the chemical and physical processes occurring during the early hydration of the filler, studied using modern analytical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydration mechanism describes how slaked lime interacts with HPG to form calcium sulfate dihydrate crystals.</data>
