  <data key="d0">Sulfate Radical</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfate radical is a chemical species whose symmetric and asymmetric stretching vibrations are analyzed in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical group in PGEF hydration products identified by an infrared absorption peak at 1124.0 cm^-1.&lt;SEP&gt;A free radical generated through the thermal activation of potassium persulfate that contributes to organic pollutant dissipation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016</data>
