</node>
<node id="Early Strength">
  <data key="d0">Early Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Early strength is a desirable performance characteristic targeted in the development of new backfill materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Early strength is a cement property reduced by impurities such as phosphorus and fluor&lt;SEP&gt;Early strength is a mechanical property measured at 1 day, which increases from 8.1 MPa to 17.3 MPa with PG addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Early strength is a mechanical property where lime-fly ash binders typically underperform compared to phosphogypsum-enhanced binders.&lt;SEP&gt;Early strength refers to the initial mechanical strength of mortars, which is lower for phosphogypsum-cement but improves over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012</data>
