<node id="Leaching Toxicity">
  <data key="d0">Leaching Toxicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaching toxicity is an environmental metric assessed alongside compressive strength to evaluate the safety of phosphogypsum-based backfill.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Toxicity is an environmental property of solid waste measured using standardized extraction procedures involving vibration or acid solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Toxicity is an environmental risk metric evaluated to assess the chemical stability and safety of phosphogypsum-based materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching toxicity is the environmental hazard metric evaluated for phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of chemical leaching from materials, expressed in milligrams per liter (mg/L).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018</data>
