</node>
<node id="HPG">
  <data key="d0">HPG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HPG refers to three distinct but related phosphogypsum-based materials recognized in industrial processing and materials science. 

First, HPG commonly denotes hemihydrate phosphogypsum, a processed derivative of phosphogypsum utilized in specialized material production. This variant is characterized by polygonal aggregates of sheet- and plate-like crystals and is produced by adding quicklime to remove impurities and promote gelling activity. As an industrial solid waste material, it serves as an aggregate or cementitious substitute in filling mining operations. Specifically, it functions as a primary component comprising 40%–62% of the CPGFM slurry and acts as a binder in cemented phosphogypsum filling material developed by Guizhou Chanheng Group.

Second, HPG can refer to high phosphorus gypsum particles. In this context, the material's dissolution behavior and subsequent gypsum growth are significantly influenced by the addition of chemical additives, particularly slaked lime.

Third, HPG denotes high purity phosphogypsum. For this variant, the condensation process is notably accelerated through reactions involving calcium carbonate. Collectively, these distinct interpretations of HPG highlight its versatile role in phosphogypsum valorization, spanning crystallographic processing, chemical modification, and industrial application in mining backfill and specialized construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;HPG is an intermediate material in the conversion process from MPG, involving adsorption by colloidal dicalcium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792301772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
