  <data key="d0">Insoluble Fluorine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insoluble Fluorine is a chemical form in Phosphogypsum that exerts little effect on material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Insoluble fluorine is a form of fluoride present in phosphogypsum with generally less pronounced effects on cemented paste fill material.&lt;SEP&gt;Insoluble fluorine is a stable impurity form that does not participate in chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Insoluble fluorine is a chemical specification metric for phosphogypsum, required to be less than 0.6 percent.</data>
