<node id="Lan et al.">
  <data key="d0">Lan et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lan et al. are researchers who determined that increasing mixing time induces consistent crystal growth and improves material strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791720004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slaked Lime">
  <data key="d0">Slaked Lime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Slaked lime, chemically identified as calcium hydroxide, is a fundamental alkaline compound that serves as a chemical base, an industrial alkali, and a primary ingredient in traditional mortars. In materials engineering, it functions as both a chemical reactant and a physical modifier within composite systems. Its alkaline nature allows it to actively participate in and drive various chemical reactions, making it a critical stabilizing agent in industrial and construction applications.

When integrated into phosphogypsum-based composites, slaked lime reacts with inherent impurities to fundamentally alter microstructural development and enhance overall strength characteristics. It specifically enhances the hydration mechanism of high-purity phosphogypsum while simultaneously acting as an effective additive to control phosphorus migration. Additionally, when combined with cementitious materials, it improves mechanical strength and ensures reliable setting times. The compound is also formally recognized within CPGFM compositions, highlighting its essential role in optimizing the performance and stability of industrial byproduct-based construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792483876</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement Hydration Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Cement Hydration Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement hydration reaction is a chemical process accelerated by temperature, impacting the early and later strength of the composite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791720004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixing Time">
  <data key="d0">Mixing Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixing time is a processing parameter that influences crystal growth consistency and contact strength up to an optimal limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixing Time is the duration of agitation during the treatment process, which influences the reduction of soluble phosphorus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791720277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mine">
  <data key="d0">Mine</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Mine is the practical application site where slurry performance and mixing time effects require monitoring.</data>
