  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A destructive leaching testing method abbreviated as TCLP used to evaluate harmful element leaching behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure is a standardized EPA test method used to evaluate the leaching potential of hazardous substances from waste materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure is an environmental testing method used to assess contamination risks of optimal mix materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure is a testing method used to assess the contamination risk of mix materials to the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A test method to determine the mobility of hazardous contaminants in liquid waste.</data>
