<node id="Unit Weight">
  <data key="d0">Unit Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mass per unit volume of adobe specimens, which increases with phosphogypsum addition but remains below standard requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit weight is a physical property of the construction matrix affected by the addition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit weight is a physical property of construction materials that declines or increases depending on the density of the material replaced by phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit Weight is a physical property evaluated for its response to the use of PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit weight is a physical property of the matrix that is reduced when phosphogypsum is included.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450981</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adobe Walls">
  <data key="d0">Adobe Walls</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
