<node id="HAP1">
  <data key="d0">HAP1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAP1 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample characterized in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP1 is a hydroxyapatite sample with a Ca:P molar ratio of 1.66 and a point of zero charge of 6.64.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP1 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample with a BET surface area of 28 m2/g.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP1 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample synthesized by one of the three methods, exhibiting a pHpzc of 6.64.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP1 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample represented by a black line in the thermal analysis curves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAP2">
  <data key="d0">HAP2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAP2 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample characterized in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP2 is a hydroxyapatite sample with a Ca:P molar ratio of 1.65 and a point of zero charge of 6.22.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP2 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample with a BET surface area of 47 m2/g.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP2 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample synthesized by one of the three methods, exhibiting a pHpzc of 6.22.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP2 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample represented by a red line in the thermal analysis curves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAP3">
  <data key="d0">HAP3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAP3 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample characterized in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP3 is a hydroxyapatite sample with a Ca:P molar ratio of 1.64 and a point of zero charge of 6.43.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP3 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite sample with a BET surface area of 13 m2/g.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP3 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample synthesized by one of the three methods, exhibiting a pHpzc of 6.43.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP3 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample represented by a blue line in the thermal analysis curves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-ray Diffraction Analysis">
  <data key="d0">X-ray Diffraction Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray Diffraction Analysis is a technique used to determine the structural parameters and relationship between synthesis and structure of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray Diffraction Analysis is a laboratory technique applied to determine the developed cementitious compounds in the mixes.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray Diffraction Analysis is a technique applied to determine cementitious phases and explain solidification mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray Diffraction Analysis is used to examine solid raw and production materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792363202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BET Method">
  <data key="d0">BET Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The BET Method is a technique used to measure the specific surface area of hydroxyapatite samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pHpzc">
  <data key="d0">pHpzc</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pHpzc represents the point of zero charge at the hydroxyapatite/NaCl interfaces for the different samples.&lt;SEP&gt;pHpzc is a characteristic electrochemical parameter of hydroxyapatite that varies based on the synthesis method.&lt;SEP&gt;pHpzc is the point of zero charge for hydroxyapatites, noted to be similar to the pHiep of BSA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pHiep">
  <data key="d0">pHiep</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pHiep represents the isoelectric point values for the hydroxyapatite systems.&lt;SEP&gt;pHiep is the isoelectric point characterizing the diffusion layer of the electrical double layer.&lt;SEP&gt;pHiep is a characteristic electrochemical parameter for BSA adsorbed on hydroxyapatite, measured at 5.82.&lt;SEP&gt;pHiep is the isoelectric point of BSA protein, recorded as 5.82.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amide I Band">
  <data key="d0">Amide I Band</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Amide I Band is a spectral peak near 1650 cm⁻¹ resulting from C=O stretching vibrations of peptide bonds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amide II Band">
  <data key="d0">Amide II Band</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Amide II Band is a spectral peak near 1540 cm⁻¹ associated with N–H bending and C–N stretching vibrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amide III Band">
  <data key="d0">Amide III Band</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Amide III Band is a spectral peak near 1240 cm⁻¹ associated with C–N stretching and N–H bending vibrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="People Programme (Marie Curie Actions)">
  <data key="d0">People Programme (Marie Curie Actions)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The People Programme (Marie Curie Actions) provided financial support for the research under the Seventh Framework Programme.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seventh Framework Programme">
  <data key="d0">Seventh Framework Programme</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Seventh Framework Programme is a European Union funding program that supported the research via the People Programme.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca:P Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Ca:P Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ca:P ratio is a compositional parameter of hydroxyapatite that influences the adhesion of protein groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="COO- Group">
  <data key="d0">COO- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The COO- group is a protein surface group that adheres preferentially to hydroxyapatite with a higher Ca:P ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NH4+ Group">
  <data key="d0">NH4+ Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The NH4+ group is a protein group that interacts with hydroxyapatite at low Ca:P ratios, requiring higher temperatures for removal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal analysis is a characterization technique used to evaluate the synthesized hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal analysis is used to study the adherence of BSA particles to hydroxyapatite and the electrostatic forces involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal analysis is an experimental technique used to study the thermal behavior of the synthesized nano-hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792001842</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Colloidal Stability">
  <data key="d0">Colloidal Stability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Colloidal stability is an electrochemical property of hydroxyapatite influenced by the synthesis method.</data>
