  <data key="d0">Purity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A quality metric of phosphogypsum that increases after impurity removal processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Purity is a quality metric for phosphogypsum that can reach up to 99.12% through roughing reverse flotation and positive flotation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Purity is a key metric in the preparation of alpha-hemihydrate gypsum whiskers, reaching 100% under optimized conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Purity is a property of MPG assessed using the intensity of the sulfate ion fingerprint peak.&lt;SEP&gt;Purity is a measured parameter representing the percentage of the sample remaining after drying at 250 C.&lt;SEP&gt;Purity is a measured parameter in Table 2 calculated from samples dried at 250 degrees Celsius.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-007</data>
