  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">150°C is a specific calcination temperature identified as consuming the least energy for producing β-hemihydrous gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific temperature at which the calcium sulfate system was heated to determine phases via X-ray diffraction.&lt;SEP&gt;150°C is the temperature at which phosphogypsum was calcined for 2 hours to improve its mechanical properties.</data>
