<node id="Agitation Time">
  <data key="d0">Agitation Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agitation Time is a process parameter investigated from 0.5 to 8 hours, with 2 hours identified as optimal for maximum removal efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Agitation Time is a parameter fixed at 2 hours for the leaching process to ensure effective extraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBP-TOPO Concentration">
  <data key="d0">TBP-TOPO Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TBP-TOPO Concentration is a process parameter ranging from 0.05 M to 1 M, with optimal removal efficiency observed at 0.9 M.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synergistic Leaching">
  <data key="d0">Synergistic Leaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synergistic Leaching is a process utilizing the combined effect of tributyl phosphate and TOPO to improve extraction performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mass Transfer">
  <data key="d0">Mass Transfer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mass transfer is a physical process improved by the addition of tributyl phosphate to TOPO in the leaching system.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical process of moving solutes between phases, which increases with longer stirring durations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791813449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solvent Saturation">
  <data key="d0">Solvent Saturation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solvent saturation occurs when phosphogypsum particles become fully loaded with solvent, leading to a decrease in leaching efficiency over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790646</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fine Particle Size">
  <data key="d0">Fine Particle Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fine particle size is the physical state of phosphogypsum achieved through grinding, which shortens diffusion paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004</data>
