<node id="Stripping Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Stripping Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stripping Efficiency is a quantitative performance metric used to evaluate the effectiveness of extraction and recovery processes, specifically measuring the percentage of target substances successfully removed or recovered during phase separation or stripping phases. In a general chemical context, it quantifies the proportion of chemical elements, isotopes, or radionuclides extracted from organic extractants or removed during specialized procedures such as the sT Stripping Percent process. The metric serves as a critical indicator of process optimization, directly reflecting how effectively a system separates and recovers desired components from a mixture.

In specialized applications, particularly within rare earth element recovery, Stripping Efficiency is specifically assessed to evaluate the successful removal of lanthanum, cerium, and neodymium ions from loaded ionic liquids. Operational studies have demonstrated that this metric can achieve recovery rates as high as 98.5% during the stripping phase, highlighting its importance in optimizing rare earth extraction workflows. Furthermore, the efficiency is highly dependent on process parameters; it typically increases as the aqueous-to-organic (A/O) phase ratio rises, eventually stabilizing and plateauing once optimal extraction conditions are reached. Together, these characteristics establish Stripping Efficiency as a fundamental benchmark for assessing and refining separation technologies across nuclear, chemical, and materials recovery fields.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
