<node id="A/O Phase Ratio">
  <data key="d0">A/O Phase Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The volume ratio between the organic and aqueous phases, maintained at 1/1 during experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A/O phase ratio is an experimental parameter set to 1/1 between aqueous and organic phases.&lt;SEP&gt;A/O Phase Ratio is the volumetric ratio between aqueous and organic phases, found to be optimal at 1/1.&lt;SEP&gt;The A/O phase ratio represents the proportion of aqueous to organic phases used in chemical extraction experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The A/O phase ratio is a parameter representing the proportion of aqueous to organic phases, ranging from 1/3 to 3/1, which drives changes in stripping efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Schiff Base">
  <data key="d0">Schiff Base</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Schiff Base is a chemical compound utilized in solvent extraction to separate thorium(IV) from chloride media.&lt;SEP&gt;A Schiff base is a chemical compound used as an extractant for thorium(IV) in chloride solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-014</data>
