<node id="Naphthalene">
  <data key="d0">Naphthalene</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Naphthalene is an organic modifier applied during hydroxyapatite synthesis to alter crystallite size and morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene is an organic modifier that forms pore-forming structures with high surface area and volume.&lt;SEP&gt;An organic modifier added to the reaction system during synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene is an organic modifier that acts as a template to create pore structures and increase porosity in HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene serves as a template that creates pore-forming structures, increasing the surface area and porosity of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene is an organic modifier used in the hydrothermal reaction to alter the crystalline structure of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-000</data>
