<node id="Degree of Crystallinity">
  <data key="d0">Degree of Crystallinity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A quantitative measure of the ordered atomic structure within the synthesized HAp material.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric representing the proportion of crystalline regions in a material, calculated using peak height ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;Degree of crystallinity measures the proportion of crystalline material within the sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Degree of Crystallinity is a measure of structural order in the samples that increases with surfactant concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Degree of Crystallinity is a measure of structural order in the samples that increases with surfactant concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792190541</data>
