  <data key="d5">1791835756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Technique">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hydrothermal Technique is a specialized synthesis method primarily utilized for the production and structural modification of hydroxyapatite (HAp). The fundamental process involves heating precursor mixtures within sealed autoclaves under controlled thermal conditions. This approach is highly effective for deliberately altering the crystal structure of HAp, allowing for precise manipulation of its internal lattice and external morphology.

In practical applications, the technique is extensively employed to synthesize specific HAp architectures, including nanorod-shaped structures and microplates, each exhibiting controlled structural and morphological properties. These materials are frequently derived from waste phosphogypsum (PPG) and are often prepared in the presence of surfactants to guide crystal growth. By leveraging these hydrothermal conditions, the method efficiently converts phosphogypsum waste into high-value, morphologically tailored hydroxyapatite materials with customized structural characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation 24">
  <data key="d0">Equation 24</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation 24 is a mathematical formula representing the Sahadat-Scherrer Model for calculating crystallite size.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 24 is the mathematical formula for calculating the mass fraction of a hydrated compound.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792069208</data>
