<node id="HAp Type 2">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 2</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A synthesized hydroxyapatite nanopowder sample with an average particle diameter of 9.7 nm measured by SA/BET.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 2 is a hydroxyapatite sample characterized by dark field TEM imaging and particle size distribution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 2 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite sample analyzed for crystallite size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite variant with a specific surface area of 211 m²/g and high structural water content.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 2 is a material sample with a measured Calcium-to-Phosphorus ratio of 1.61 ± 0.02.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp Type 3">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 3</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A synthesized hydroxyapatite nanopowder sample with an average particle diameter of 13.7 nm measured by SA/BET.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 3 is a hydroxyapatite sample characterized by dark field TEM imaging and particle size distribution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 3 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite sample analyzed for crystallite size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite variant with a specific surface area of 149 m²/g and lower water adsorption compared to Types 1 and 2.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 3 is a material sample with a measured Calcium-to-Phosphorus ratio of 1.61 ± 0.02.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp Type 4">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 4</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A synthesized hydroxyapatite nanopowder sample with a specific surface area of 85 m²/g and a density of 3.00 g/cm³.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 4 is a hydroxyapatite sample with an average particle size of 18.4 nm and considerable diversity in nanoparticle shape and size.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 4 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite sample analyzed for crystallite size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite variant included in the ranking of total water content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp Type 1">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp Type 1 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite nanopowder engineered to serve as a direct synthetic equivalent of natural bone. Its crystalline structure is identical to that found in both human and animal bone tissue. The sample is fully crystalline and has been specifically analyzed for its crystallite size distribution.

The material is produced through a room-temperature precipitation process that does not require a reactor. This synthesis yields a nanopowder with an average particle diameter of 8.1 nm, as measured by SA/BET. HAp Type 1 exhibits a high specific surface area of 258 m²/g. Chemically, it is characterized by the greatest carbonate content and the highest a lattice parameter. Additionally, it displays a Calcium-to-Phosphorus ratio of 1.64 ± 0.02, which is the highest measured value for this variant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp Type 5">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 5</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A synthesized hydroxyapatite nanopowder sample with a specific surface area of 61 m²/g.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 5 is a hydroxyapatite sample with an average particle size of 26.9 nm and uniform crystallite shape.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 5 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite sample analyzed for crystallite size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite variant included in the ranking of total water content.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 5 is a material sample with a measured Calcium-to-Phosphorus ratio of 1.61 ± 0.02.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp Type 6">
  <data key="d0">HAp Type 6</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp Type 6 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite powder characterized by larger nanoparticle size and a crystalline structure similar to tooth enamel.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 6 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite nanopowder characterized by larger nanoparticle size and a crystalline structure similar to tooth enamel.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthesized hydroxyapatite nanopowder sample with a specific surface area of 51 m²/g, average particle diameter of 39 nm, and density of 3.04 g/cm³.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 6 is a hydroxyapatite sample with an average particle size of 35 nm and uniform crystallite shape.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 6 is a synthetic hydroxyapatite sample analyzed for crystallite size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite variant included in the ranking of total water content.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Type 6 is a material sample with a measured Calcium-to-Phosphorus ratio of 1.60 ± 0.03.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
