<node id="Potassium Ion">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium ions are byproducts that can substitute calcium ions within the hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;An ion that reacts directly with sulfate ions to synthesize potassium sulphate.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium ion is a chemical species that reacts directly with sulfate ions to form potassium sulphate.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Ion is a highly soluble impurity ion removed from the final nHAp product by washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792318458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
