  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ecotoxicity">
  <data key="d0">Ecotoxicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ecotoxicity is an environmental impact category and safety metric primarily focused on ecosystem quality, evaluated through standardized assessment methods and frequently measured alongside human toxicity. It functions as a critical indicator in environmental impact studies, particularly when assessing management scenarios, air emissions, resource consumption, and negative emissions associated with soil amendment practices. A significant portion of ecotoxicity impacts stems from these sources, with phosphogypsum and phosphogypsum-amended soil representing key areas of concern. Specifically, ecotoxicity quantifies the harmful effects of phosphogypsum on a wide range of biological organisms, including aquatic life, bacteria, invertebrates, algae, and plants. Ensuring that phosphogypsum recycling processes do not trigger adverse ecotoxicity effects is a central objective in environmental safety evaluations.

In graphical representations and impact charts, ecotoxicity is conventionally denoted by the color teal in the legend. Overall, it serves as a comprehensive metric for quantifying and mitigating the potential ecological risks posed by industrial byproducts and agricultural amendments, ensuring that developmental and recycling activities remain within safe ecological boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792456533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Material Transport">
  <data key="d0">Material Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Material transport is a process contributing to environmental burden, primarily involving lorry transport and fossil fuel consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Material transport is a process contributing to negative environmental impacts in the road construction scenario.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
