<node id="Respiratory Inorganics">
  <data key="d0">Respiratory Inorganics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Respiratory inorganics are pollutants emitted during material transport that contribute to environmental burden.&lt;SEP&gt;Respiratory Inorganics is a dominant impact category reduced through conventional gypsum and phosphoric acid savings.&lt;SEP&gt;Respiratory inorganics is an impact category associated with materials transport and clay savings.&lt;SEP&gt;Respiratory Inorganics is an environmental impact category listed in the chart's legend, associated with the color yellow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791878118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acidification/Eutrophication">
  <data key="d0">Acidification/Eutrophication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acidification and eutrophication are impact categories where Ecoindicator 99 has limitations, prompting comparison with CML 2 Baseline 2000.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidification and eutrophication are environmental impact categories evaluated in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidification and eutrophication are impact categories contributing to environmental burden from material transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidification/Eutrophication is an impact category reduced through conventional material savings.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidification/eutrophication is an impact category associated with materials transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidification/Eutrophication is an environmental impact category listed in the chart's legend, associated with the color dark blue.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791878118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Emissions">
  <data key="d0">Air Emissions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Air emissions are environmental outputs from the top surface of stacks that increase with shorter stack heights.&lt;SEP&gt;Air emissions categorize gaseous and particulate releases into the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Air emissions include dust and sulfur dioxide generated during industrial production.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Emissions are atmospheric discharges from production units that require further control.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Emissions encompass gaseous pollutants released during production that require treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Gaseous releases from the top of the sulfuric acid production system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792221470</data>
