  <data key="d0">Coesite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Coesite is a mineral detected in citric acid-leached phosphogypsum, typically used in manufacturing glass and electronics.&lt;SEP&gt;Coesite is a chemical phase identified in phosphogypsum when treated with citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Coesite is a mineral phase detected in phosphogypsum treated with citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical phase labeled "C" in the legend, corresponding to a peak in the cluster between 28 and 32 degrees.</data>
