  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicate is a chemical phase identified in phosphogypsum when treated with sodium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicate is a compound whose relative proportion increases in phosphogypsum across all leaching reagents.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicate is a chemical component present in a sample with a recorded content of 58.891%.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicate is a minor phase impurity identified in the PG sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicate is a soil amendment used alongside lime and phosphogypsum in agricultural studies.</data>
