<node id="Landfill">
  <data key="d0">Landfill</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Landfill is a common disposal method for phosphogypsum that results in leachate formation and environmental risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is a disposal site for biosolids and other waste materials containing phosphorus.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is a destination for phosphorus losses from the Australian food system.&lt;SEP&gt;A disposal site for unused biosolids.&lt;SEP&gt;A destination for food waste sent from municipal and commercial/industrial sectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005</data>
