<node id="Cement and Concrete Research">
  <data key="d0">Cement and Concrete Research</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An academic journal that published research by M. Singh and colleagues.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement and Concrete Research is a prominent journal featuring multiple studies on phosphogypsum utilization and cementitious binders.&lt;SEP&gt;A peer-reviewed journal that published a 1989 study on phosphogypsum and cement properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific journal that published investigations into the chemical and physical treatments of phosphogypsum to render it suitable as a cement set retarder.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement and Concrete Research is a journal that published research on utilizing weathered phosphogypsum as a set retarder.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific journal that published multiple studies on phosphogypsum applications in cement and concrete.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792482495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strontium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Strontium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical compound listed at 0.49 wt% in the bottom section of the phosphogypsum composition table.&lt;SEP&gt;Strontium Oxide is a minor impurity present in raw phosphogypsum, detailed in Table 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792122028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2 Theta">
  <data key="d0">2 Theta</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The horizontal axis metric in the XRD chart representing the diffraction angle in degrees, ranging from 3.00 to 87.3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791917532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gypsum Formula">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Formula</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The chemical formula CaSO4 · 2H2O, which aligns with the high concentrations of sulfur trioxide and calcium oxide in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791917532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Treatments">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Treatments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of substances including citric acid, oxalic acid, sodium carbonate, and sodium bicarbonate used to affect radionuclide concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791917532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Untreated Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Untreated Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The raw, untreated phosphogypsum material used as a baseline for comparing chemical treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Untreated Phosphogypsum is the raw form of PG that exhibits a strong retarder effect on cement setting time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphoric Acid Process">
  <data key="d0">Phosphoric Acid Process</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">The phosphoric acid manufacturing process breaks the radioactive equilibrium among radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;The industrial manufacturing process that produces PG as a by-product.&lt;SEP&gt;The phosphoric acid process is the industrial manufacturing method that generates phosphogypsum as a by-product.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503973</data>
