<node id="SM">
  <data key="d0">SM</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A 0/20 mm size fraction material added to raw PG to improve geotechnical properties and mechanical performance.&lt;SEP&gt;SM is a stabilizer material combined with PG in specific mix proportions for road applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Stabilizing additive incorporated into raw PG to enhance physicochemical and mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;SM is a mix formulation listed in Table 8 with a pH of 6.9 and specific physical test results.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the CM-PG-SM-HRB mix contributing to the material properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="L">
  <data key="d0">L</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A material added to raw PG to reduce natural moisture content and neutralize acidity.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime additive incorporated into P2 Mix to drastically improve load-bearing capacity metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;A material component used in mixture P4.&lt;SEP&gt;L represents the emergy quantification of land occupation loss due to solid waste disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;L is a component used in mortar mixes alongside NS and PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005</data>
