<node id="CBR">
  <data key="d0">CBR</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">CBR is a parameter measuring water sensitivity and bearing capacity for road layers.&lt;SEP&gt;California Bearing Ratio metric measuring load-bearing capacity, significantly improved by SM and lime additions.&lt;SEP&gt;CBR (California Bearing Ratio) is a metric listed in Table 8 for evaluating mix properties.&lt;SEP&gt;CBR is a geotechnical parameter measuring bearing capacity, which shows significant improvement with the addition of silty gravel material.&lt;SEP&gt;California Bearing Ratio, a penetration test used to evaluate subgrade and base course strength for pavements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791937342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
