<node id="Table 10">
  <data key="d0">Table 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Summary data presentation comparing the effects of SM, FA, L, CM, and HRB on mix properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A table detailing the engineering properties, including pH, CBR ratio, and modulus measurements, of designed mixes.&lt;SEP&gt;A data table listing results used to verify immediate stability specifications for pavement layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 10 presents the indicator values of the SDI and ID for the four scenarios, detailing their impact on the SEI.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 10 presents quantitative data on the heavy metal content in PG, MPG, and hydrated PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 10 is a data table documenting heavy metal leaching content in PG and MPG under various processing conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 10 is a data table presenting elemental content measurements, specifically highlighting Chromium levels after hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792299624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
