<node id="EDX Analysis">
  <data key="d0">EDX Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">EDX Analysis is an analytical method used to obtain elemental data for the prepared samples.&lt;SEP&gt;EDX Analysis is an analytical technique used to measure the atomic composition and elemental weight percentages of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical technique used to confirm the presence of oxygen vacancies.&lt;SEP&gt;EDX Analysis is an analytical method used to obtain elemental data for the prepared samples.&lt;SEP&gt;EDX Analysis is an analytical technique used to measure the atomic composition and elemental weight percentages of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical technique used to confirm the presence of oxygen vacancies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XPS Analysis">
  <data key="d0">XPS Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS Analysis is a surface-sensitive analytical and characterization technique primarily employed to determine the elemental composition, chemical state, chemical environments, oxidation states, and bonding characteristics of sample surfaces. By focusing exclusively on the outermost atomic layers, this method provides precise insights into surface-specific properties and defects. A standard operational consideration involves the frequent observation of carbon peaks, which are routinely attributed to ubiquitous surface contamination rather than intrinsic material composition.

The technique is widely applied across materials science and industrial research to address specific analytical needs. It is commonly utilized to confirm the presence of oxygen vacancies within solid materials and to characterize the surface composition of specialized samples, such as PGI-1.4 samples that have been reduced at controlled temperatures. In metallurgical and chemical contexts, XPS Analysis is instrumental in verifying the content and chemical form of sulfur in slag, as well as in elucidating the bonding characteristics and oxidation states of iron and sulfur compounds. Collectively, these applications underscore its versatility as a critical tool for detailed surface chemical profiling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792189238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Synthesis Process">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Synthesis Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal Synthesis Process is the preparation method used to produce the PPG-derived Hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal Synthesis Process is the preparation method used to produce the PPG-derived Hydroxyapatite samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008</data>
