  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P123">
  <data key="d0">P123</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">P123 is a non-ionic surfactant composed of a triblock copolymer that serves as a templating agent during the hydrothermal synthesis and modification of hydroxyapatite (HAp) samples. Frequently utilized alongside CTAB and referenced in comparative datasets such as Table 2, P123 self-assembles into larger micelles that effectively increase the surface area of the synthesized materials. As a structural director, it plays a critical role in controlling particle morphology, crystallite size, and phase formation. By guiding the assembly process, P123 successfully templates the growth of HAp into nanorod and two-dimensional flaky-crystal-like architectures while simultaneously enhancing the overall crystallinity of the modified structures.

Despite its versatility in morphological control and crystallinity enhancement, P123 exhibits distinct performance trade-offs when compared to CTAB. Evaluations indicate that P123 yields comparatively shorter nanorods and a reduced proportion of flaky structures relative to CTAB-based alternatives. These morphological differences directly correlate with a lower photoelectrochemical (PEC) efficiency, meaning that while P123 is highly effective for directing nanostructure dimensions and improving crystalline quality, its application involves a measurable compromise in electrochemical performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792187318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Band Gap">
  <data key="d0">Band Gap</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Band gap is a structural property of hydroxyapatite that influences its light absorption capability and optoelectronic performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Band Gap is a key electronic property measured for the prepared samples, indicating their semiconducting characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Band gap is a structural property of hydroxyapatite that influences its light absorption capability and optoelectronic performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Band Gap is a key electronic property measured for the prepared samples, indicating their semiconducting characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-000</data>
