  <data key="d2">IUPAC is an organization that co-funded the research project alongside UNESCO and PhosAgro.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC is an organization that co-sponsored the research grants alongside UNESCO and PhosAgro.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC is the international organization responsible for publishing the technical report on gas physisorption and surface area evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC provides the classification system used to identify type IV isotherms and type H3 hysteresis loops in the material characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC is an organization that co-funded the research project alongside UNESCO and PhosAgro.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC is an organization that co-sponsored the research grants alongside UNESCO and PhosAgro.&lt;SEP&gt;IUPAC is the international organization responsible for publishing the technical report on gas physisorption and surface area evaluation.</data>
