<node id="HAp-CTAB-3">
  <data key="d0">HAp-CTAB-3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-CTAB-3 is a specific variant of hydroxyapatite (HAp), specifically PPG-derived, that is synthesized through modification with a CTAB surfactant at a concentration of 3 wt%. Structurally, the sample forms a morphology characterized by shorter nanorods and flaky features, which typically results in slight agglomeration. This material is explicitly included in comparative data tables to assess its physical and chemical properties alongside other synthesized variants.

In terms of photoelectrochemical performance, HAp-CTAB-3 exhibits intermediate to moderate stability and photocurrent response. When evaluated for photocurrent density, it demonstrates a value of approximately 3 μA/cm². Across comparative assessments, this specific surfactant-modified hydroxyapatite variant consistently ranks second in overall photoelectrochemical efficiency, highlighting its balanced and reliable performance characteristics in experimental evaluations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792188233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp-P123-3">
  <data key="d0">HAp-P123-3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-P123-3 is a synthesized hydroxyapatite material, specifically a variant of PPG-derived HAp, that has been modified with P123 surfactant at a concentration of 3 wt%. Structurally, this sample forms shorter nanorods and exhibits a higher degree of agglomeration when compared to HAp-CTAB-3. In terms of porosity, HAp-P123-3 displays a pore volume distribution that is nearly identical to that of Pristine HAp, characterized by a gradual decline in volume as the pore diameter increases.

When evaluated for its photoelectrochemical properties, HAp-P123-3 demonstrates an intermediate photocurrent response and stability. However, it is also characterized by very low overall efficiency and activity, with measured photocurrent density reaching approximately 2 μA/cm² at 1.4 V. These combined attributes define HAp-P123-3 as a distinct surfactant-modified hydroxyapatite variant with specific morphological, porous, and photoelectrochemical behaviors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792187888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp-P123-6">
  <data key="d0">HAp-P123-6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-P123-6 is a specific variant of PPG-derived hydroxyapatite synthesized by modifying the base material with P123 surfactant at a precise concentration of 6 wt%. Structurally, this prepared sample exhibits reduced agglomeration and is characterized by a shorter nanorod morphology. In terms of porosity, it displays a lower, flatter pore volume distribution featuring a small peak within the 10–20 nm range.

When evaluated for photoelectrochemical performance, HAp-P123-6 demonstrates an intermediate photocurrent response and photoelectrochemical stability. Its photocurrent density profile is marked by an early current rise, though it achieves a lower plateau compared to CTAB-modified samples. Despite these characteristics, it records the lowest efficiency among the labeled curves in its comparative evaluations. Overall, HAp-P123-6 serves as a distinct, surfactant-modified hydroxyapatite material with defined structural and photoelectrochemical properties tailored for specific experimental assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
