</node>
<node id="Pristine HAp">
  <data key="d0">Pristine HAp</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pristine HAp is an unmodified, native hydroxyapatite material synthesized from polypropylene glycol (PPG) without the incorporation of any surfactants. It functions as a fundamental control and baseline sample within experimental datasets, explicitly listed in comparative tables to evaluate physical properties, crystallinity, and textural characteristics. Morphologically, the material exhibits an irregular, flaky particle structure accompanied by obvious agglomeration. Its textural profile is defined by a low and flat pore volume distribution, which closely resembles that of HAp-P123-3.

In functional testing, Pristine HAp serves as the reference standard for photocatalytic and electrical property evaluations, consistently demonstrating significantly lower efficiency than surfactant-modified variants. This diminished performance stems from the rapid recombination of photo-generated electrons and holes, yielding the lowest photocurrent response among tested samples. Electrically, the material displays a distinct current knee at approximately 1.0 V, followed by a steady current density increase that reaches roughly 3 μA/cm². Consequently, Pristine HAp provides a critical benchmark for quantifying the structural and photoelectrochemical improvements achieved through surfactant-assisted synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
