<node id="Band Gap Energy">
  <data key="d0">Band Gap Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Band gap energy, Eg, is a characteristic determined from the relationship between photon energy and absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy difference between conduction and valence bands, critical for determining photocatalytic redox potential alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;Band gap energy, Eg, is a characteristic determined from the relationship between photon energy and absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy difference between conduction and valence bands, critical for determining photocatalytic redox potential alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;Band gap energy is a property of semiconductor materials used in the Mulliken electronegativity equation to calculate band edge positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-012</data>
