<node id="Debye-Scherrer Equation">
  <data key="d0">Debye-Scherrer Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Debye-Scherrer equation is a mathematical formula used to calculate crystallite size and crystallinity from diffraction peak broadening.&lt;SEP&gt;Debye-Scherrer Equation is a theoretical framework compared with the Scherrer Equation for crystal analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical formula applied to X-ray diffraction data to calculate crystalline domain sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792425339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase Evolution">
  <data key="d0">Phase Evolution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase evolution describes the structural transformation from amorphous calcium phosphate to crystalline hydroxyapatite over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791984880</data>
