<node id="Hydrothermal Time">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal time refers to the duration of the reaction process, ranging from 0.5 to 15 hours, which dictates material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal time is a critical parameter that controls the morphological evolution and structural stability of the microspheres.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal Time refers to the duration of the synthesis process, ranging from 1 to 10 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal time refers to the duration of the reaction, during which urea hydrolysis gradually establishes an alkaline environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791984880</data>
