  <data key="d0">Posner's Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posner's Clusters are spherical associations that form larger structures in ACP, hindering nitrogen adsorption at early hydrothermal stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate clusters with the formula Ca9(PO4)6, considered the basic units of ACP and key to apatite nucleation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fast Fourier Transform">
  <data key="d0">Fast Fourier Transform</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast Fourier Transform is an analytical technique used to reveal that nano whiskers are crystalline HA with preferred c-axis orientation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast Fourier Transform is the computational method used to generate the diffraction pattern inset in Panel (e).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAED Pattern">
  <data key="d0">SAED Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SAED Patterns display diffraction rings assigned to HA planes and diffuse rings indicating the coexistence of ACP and HA phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEM Observations">
  <data key="d0">SEM Observations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM Observations are used to characterize surface particles, nano whiskers, and the transition from solid ACP to core-shell HA microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen Adsorption/Desorption Isotherms">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Adsorption/Desorption Isotherms</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen adsorption/desorption isotherms are measured to analyze the surface area and porosity of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;These isotherms characterize the porosity of the microspheres, exhibiting type IV curves with type H3 hysteresis loops.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core-Shell Structure">
  <data key="d0">Core-Shell Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific microstructural arrangement of the hydroxyapatite microspheres characterized by a distinct inner and outer layer.&lt;SEP&gt;The Core-Shell Structure forms after 4 h of hydrothermal treatment and characterizes the final HA microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T4">
  <data key="d0">T4</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">T4 is a sample ID corresponding to microspheres synthesized for 4 hours of hydrothermal time.&lt;SEP&gt;A PG recycling technology that exhibits poor economic performance and lower overall performance.&lt;SEP&gt;T4 is a technology in the low utility group exhibiting a multi-modal distribution with peaks around 0.35, 0.45, and 0.55.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T5">
  <data key="d0">T5</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">T5 is a sample ID corresponding to microspheres synthesized for 5 hours of hydrothermal time.&lt;SEP&gt;A PG recycling technology identified as having better performance for most indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;T5 is a technology in the high utility group with peaks around 0.6, 0.7, and 0.8.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T10">
  <data key="d0">T10</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">T10 is a sample ID corresponding to microspheres synthesized for 10 hours of hydrothermal time.&lt;SEP&gt;PG-based polymer material technology, which achieves the highest net present value.&lt;SEP&gt;T10 is a specific PG recycling technology whose ranking fluctuated significantly from 2–11 due to uncertain factors.&lt;SEP&gt;T10 is a technology in the mid-range utility group showing a distribution peaking around 0.5, 0.6, and 0.7.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slit-Shaped Pores">
  <data key="d0">Slit-Shaped Pores</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Slit-shaped pores are structural features in the microspheres attributed to self-assembled clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985846</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.344 nm">
  <data key="d0">0.344 nm</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.344 nm is the interplanar spacing of lattice fringes corresponding to the (002) planes of HA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985846</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
