<node id="ICP-MS">
  <data key="d0">ICP-MS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ICP-MS is a mass spectrometry-based analytical technique and laboratory instrument designed to quantify, analyze, and measure trace elements, elemental concentrations, and overall chemical composition. Functioning as a highly sensitive detection method, it is utilized to determine the precise contents of trace constituents and confirm the presence of impurities across diverse material matrices. The technique operates as a fundamental laboratory tool for generating detailed elemental data in scientific research and industrial analysis.

In practical applications, ICP-MS is extensively employed to characterize phosphogypsum samples and their prepared solutions, as well as to assess the chemical makeup of residual phases. It is also specifically applied to verify impurities within potassium sulphate and to analyze trace elemental profiles in broader experimental datasets. By integrating these varied use cases, ICP-MS serves as a versatile and critical analytical method for comprehensive elemental quantification and compositional verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792120308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
