<node id="LA-ICP-MS">
  <data key="d0">LA-ICP-MS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">LA-ICP-MS is a trace element analysis technique combining laser ablation with mass spectrometry.&lt;SEP&gt;Laser ablation inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry used to examine chemical species and trace elements in samples.&lt;SEP&gt;LA-ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to determine the trace element composition of minerals in phosphogypsum in ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;LA-ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to evaluate changes in the chemical composition of minerals after leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;LA-ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to measure the trace element composition of minerals in leached phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A mass spectrometry technique used alongside EPMA to analyze rare earth element distribution in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
