  <data key="d0">SEM-EDS Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM-EDS analysis is a technique used to reveal trace amounts of residual fluorapatite and map elemental distribution on gypsum surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS analysis is used to examine the microstructure and elemental composition of the PGI-1.4 sample.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS analysis is a technique used to obtain the microstructure and elemental distribution of the slag samples.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS analysis is a technique used to map elemental distribution and identify compounds like iron sulfide within the slag.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopic and spectroscopic method used to examine the morphology and composition of portlandite and potassium sulphate.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM-EDS Analysis is a microscopic and spectroscopic technique used to examine the composition and morphology of materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A semi-quantitative analytical technique used to reveal elemental concentrations in powdered materials.</data>
