<node id="Process Optimization and Mechanism Study for Sulfur Recovery from High-Silica Phosphogypsum via Carbothermal Reduction Smelting">
  <data key="d0">Process Optimization and Mechanism Study for Sulfur Recovery from High-Silica Phosphogypsum via Carbothermal Reduction Smelting</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A 2024 research article investigating sulfur recovery and value-added utilization of liquid slag from high-silica phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbothermal Reduction Smelting">
  <data key="d0">Carbothermal Reduction Smelting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbothermal reduction smelting is the experimental method used to recover sulfur and produce liquid slag from high-silica phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An innovative smelting method that enables efficient sulfur recovery and amorphous slag formation from high-silica phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbothermal Reduction Smelting is the experimental methodology involving proportioning, mixing, melting, cooling, and grinding.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbothermal Reduction Smelting is an industrial process used to obtain SO2 flue gas and slag from PGI.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbothermal reduction smelting is a process investigated for decomposing phosphogypsum and optimizing slag microstructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wet-Processed Phosphoric Acid Production">
  <data key="d0">Wet-Processed Phosphoric Acid Production</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet-processed phosphoric acid production is the industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a major byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid Slag">
  <data key="d0">Liquid Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid slag is the molten byproduct formed during carbothermal reduction smelting, composed of amorphous magnesium-calcium-aluminosilicate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kiln Ringing">
  <data key="d0">Kiln Ringing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Kiln ringing is a problematic phenomenon in traditional rotary kiln processes caused by low-melting phases wrapping phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alumina">
  <data key="d0">Alumina</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Alumina is an additive component in the phosphogypsum ingredient system used to meet slag wool production requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Alumina is a component found in industrial solid wastes like blast furnace slag and fly ash, added to meet slag wool composition requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;An additive that reacts with calcium sulfate or calcium oxide, affecting the desulfurization effect and phase composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Alumina is a material combined with silica and magnesium oxides to form eutectic mixtures that lower melting points.&lt;SEP&gt;Alumina is a chemical component in fly ash that contributes to its pozzolanic properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792141505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slag Wool">
  <data key="d0">Slag Wool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Slag wool is a high-value-added mineral fiber and manufactured material produced from the homogeneous molten phase discharged in liquid slag. The production process involves subjecting the molten slag to either centrifugal or blowing techniques to form a fibrous structure. As a target industrial material in joint preparation processes, its synthesis is governed by strict physicochemical parameters, including specific acidity, viscosity, and pH requirements. Chemically, slag wool is characterized by defined component ranges of silicon dioxide (SiO2), calcium oxide (CaO), aluminum oxide (Al2O3), and magnesium oxide (MgO), with amorphous diffraction peaks serving as its foundational structural basis.

Because slag wool serves as the primary target product, its stringent production requirements directly dictate the necessary raw material composition and slag system parameters. Consequently, the manufacturing specifications for slag wool guide the construction and compositional design of the phosphogypsum ingredient system (PGI system). This ensures that the resulting fiber product consistently meets all required industrial standards while optimizing the overall material preparation workflow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnesium Oxides">
  <data key="d0">Magnesium Oxides</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnesium oxides are additive components in the phosphogypsum ingredient system used to meet slag wool production requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;An additive that participates in side reactions during the reduction roasting process.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium oxides are oxides added to the system to form eutectic mixtures and promote material melting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional Sulfuric Acid and Cement Process">
  <data key="d0">Traditional Sulfuric Acid and Cement Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional Sulfuric Acid and Cement Process is an established industrial method for utilizing phosphogypsum that faces challenges with kiln ringing and product quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operating Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Operating Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Operating temperature is a critical experimental parameter that significantly affects the desulfurization rate and phase structure of the slag.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792096029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rotary Kiln">
  <data key="d0">Rotary Kiln</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rotary kiln is the industrial equipment used for calcination in traditional phosphogypsum processing, prone to ring formation.&lt;SEP&gt;The rotary kiln is used to dry phosphogypsum and remove free and crystal water to generate hemihydrate phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial equipment used in Scenario 2 for drying phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A kiln used for drying PG in Scenario 2, where natural gas combustion occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792221761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Ingredient (PGI) System">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Ingredient (PGI) System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The PGI system is a constructed slag system with a low eutectic point designed for phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum Ingredient (PGI) System is a constructed mixture of phosphogypsum and additives designed to meet slag wool production requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792096029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amorphous Magnesium-Calcium-Aluminosilicate">
  <data key="d0">Amorphous Magnesium-Calcium-Aluminosilicate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
