<node id="PGI-1.4">
  <data key="d0">PGI-1.4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PGI-1.4 is a specific modified phosphogypsum sample formulation and system designed for specialized material testing and compositional control. Characterized by a quaternary acidity coefficient of 1.40 and a precisely defined set of component masses, this material incorporates specific additives that fundamentally alter its properties. Notably, it features a carbon-to-sulfur (C/S) molar ratio of 0.5, alongside carefully calibrated proportions of Al2O3 and Fe2O3. Compared to standard phosphogypsum, PGI-1.4 exhibits distinct thermal characteristics, including modified decomposition rates and unique phase transformation behaviors.

The sample has been extensively utilized in laboratory settings to establish baseline compositional ratios and to conduct follow-up reduction tests. Its thermal decomposition and carbothermal reduction behaviors have been systematically analyzed across a range of temperatures and varying C/S molar ratios. Through comprehensive thermal analysis and reaction condition testing, PGI-1.4 serves as a critical reference material for evaluating how modified phosphogypsum systems respond to thermal stress and chemical reduction processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097275</data>
