<node id="TG-DTA">
  <data key="d0">TG-DTA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermogravimetric-differential thermal analysis used to measure weight loss under a nitrogen atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;TG-DTA is a thermal analysis technique used to investigate the efficiency of the carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;TG-DTA is a thermal analysis technique used to generate curves for synthetic and commercial calcium carbonate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792119971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonation Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Carbonation Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonation efficiency is a metric evaluated using TG-DTA to assess the performance of the adapted carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric defined as the ratio of experimentally formed carbonate to the theoretical carbonate amount derived from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonation efficiency is a performance metric defined as the ratio of experimentally formed carbonate to the theoretical amount based on total calcium content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792120308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
