<node id="Soil I">
  <data key="d0">Soil I</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil I is a soil sample collected in Balikesir, classified as A-7-5 and MH-type.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil I is a specific soil sample type used in the compaction and strength tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil I is a base soil material used in stabilization experiments with various additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil I is a soil type used in stabilization experiments with cement, fly ash, and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A base soil type tested with various additives to determine its mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of soil mixture analyzed for its geotechnical properties and response to various additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil I is a soil type used in compressive strength testing, showing lower strength values compared to Soil II when additives are applied.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792141505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soil II">
  <data key="d0">Soil II</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil II is a soil sample collected in Balikesir, classified as A-7-5 and CH-type.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil II is a base soil material used in stabilization experiments with various additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil II is a soil type evaluated for compaction characteristics and strength when stabilized with various additives.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific soil type analyzed in the study, showing significant strength increase with 15% cement content.&lt;SEP&gt;A second base soil type tested alongside Soil I to evaluate the effects of additives.&lt;SEP&gt;A second type of soil mixture evaluated alongside Soil I for mechanical strength and plasticity characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil II is a soil type used in compressive strength testing, generally achieving higher strength values than Soil I at higher additive percentages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792141505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C">
  <data key="d0">C</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">C is an additive used in soil stabilization mixtures at varying percentages.&lt;SEP&gt;C represents carbon, which undergoes gasification at smaller coal sizes.&lt;SEP&gt;C is an identified chemical phase present in the mixtures and reference pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Dry Density">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Dry Density</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum dry density is a key parameter measured during compaction tests to evaluate soil compaction potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum dry density is a compaction metric that decreases as fly ash content increases due to lower specific surface gravity.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured parameter indicating the highest density achievable for a soil sample during compaction.&lt;SEP&gt;The highest achievable dry density of a soil mixture under standard compaction effort.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792141666</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
