<node id="Analytic Hierarchy Process">
  <data key="d0">Analytic Hierarchy Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method used to obtain weight vectors for indicators, integrated with EWM using Game Theory.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytic Hierarchy Process is a weighting calculation technique involving structure decision hierarchy, judgment matrix construction, and consistency check.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytic Hierarchy Process is a structured decision-making technique mentioned as a related context for data analysis and weighting methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entropy Weight Method">
  <data key="d0">Entropy Weight Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Entropy Weight Method is a weighting technique integrated with AHP via GT to determine final indicator weights.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to calculate indicator weights based on entropy and information quantity variation.&lt;SEP&gt;Entropy Weight Method is a weighting calculation technique that uses data normalization, indicator proportion, and entropy calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Entropy Weight Method is a multi-criteria decision-making technique that uses normalized entropy to determine the weights of different variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Game Theory">
  <data key="d0">Game Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical framework integrated into the MCDA method for criteria weighting and ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;A conceptual framework used to balance different weight vectors and minimize deviation from ideal comprehensive weights.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Index">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency Index is a metric calculated to verify the logical consistency of the judgment matrix in AHP.&lt;SEP&gt;A calculated metric used to evaluate the consistency of a judgment matrix, derived from the maximum eigenvalue and indicator number.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A calculated metric derived from the consistency index and random index, where a value below 0.1 indicates acceptable matrix consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Index">
  <data key="d0">Random Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A reference value determined by the indicator number of criteria, used in calculating the consistency ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Judgment Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Judgment Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Judgment Matrix is a constructed matrix representing pairwise comparisons of indicators relative to upper-level indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured matrix used in AHP to represent relative importance between criteria, whose consistency is evaluated using CI and CR.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shannon">
  <data key="d0">Shannon</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A researcher cited for defining entropy as a measure of information contained in a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
