  <data key="d0">Human Body Toxicity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Human Body Toxicity is an environmental safety metric evaluated in the assessment of PG recycling technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T15">
  <data key="d0">T15</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A PG recycling technology identified as performing exceptionally well with a utility value above 0.70.&lt;SEP&gt;T15 is a specific PG recycling technology whose ranking fluctuated significantly from 1–9 due to uncertain factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology showing the highest utility values with peaks extending up to 0.85.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T12">
  <data key="d0">T12</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-production of sulfuric acid and fertilizer technology, which performs best in investment cost but poorly in other economic metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;A PG recycling technology involving the co-production of sulfuric acid and fertilizer, which underperformed with a utility value below 0.30.&lt;SEP&gt;T12 is a specific PG recycling technology whose ranking remained stable at 14–15 despite uncertain factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology exhibiting a single broad peak in utility distribution centered around 0.3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T13">
  <data key="d0">T13</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hollow-core slabs technology, which performs better in ECO2.&lt;SEP&gt;A PG recycling technology that underperformed with a utility value below 0.30.&lt;SEP&gt;T13 is a specific PG recycling technology whose ranking remained stable at 14–15 despite uncertain factors.&lt;SEP&gt;T13 is a technology in the low utility group with a distribution peak around 0.35.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Economy">
  <data key="d0">Economy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the four dimensions of the indicator system, related to economic aspects of recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Economy is a criteria-level dimension in the decision hierarchy representing economic performance indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary evaluation criterion measuring financial viability and investment returns.&lt;SEP&gt;Economy is a performance criterion where PG recycling technologies generally demonstrate lower performance, requiring targeted optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Economy is a main dimension branching from the total utility in the indicator system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Society">
  <data key="d0">Society</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the four dimensions of the indicator system, addressing social implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Society is a criteria-level dimension in the decision hierarchy representing social impact indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary evaluation criterion evaluating social impacts such as employment and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Society is a performance criterion where PG recycling technologies generally demonstrate lower performance, requiring targeted optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Society is a main dimension branching from the total utility in the indicator system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792159694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
