  <data key="d0">Risk-Averse Decision-Makers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk-Averse Decision-Makers are individuals sensitive to losses but slow to respond to interests, characterized by a risk attitude parameter less than 0.5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk-Neutral Decision-Makers">
  <data key="d0">Risk-Neutral Decision-Makers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk-Neutral Decision-Makers are individuals with a neutral risk attitude who make decisions directly based on indicator values, characterized by a risk attitude parameter equal to 0.5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logarithm Utility Functions">
  <data key="d0">Logarithm Utility Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Logarithm Utility Functions are mathematical models selected to compute the utility values of individual indicators based on risk attitudes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distance-Based Merging Rule">
  <data key="d0">Distance-Based Merging Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Distance-Based Merging Rule is a technique employed to calculate the utility value at the criteria level and the total utility value.&lt;SEP&gt;A rule used to aggregate the utility values of the four main criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792160084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solid Waste Recycling Technologies">
  <data key="d0">Solid Waste Recycling Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solid Waste Recycling Technologies are the subject of evaluation, assessed through total utility values across four dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Technologies evaluated in the study, with utility values calculated using the distance-based merging rule.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ce07008b902e3e05b9cea9315e7aa04-chunk-006</data>
