<node id="Hydrothermal Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal reaction is a synthesis process conducted at 180°C for 15 hours to produce hydroxyapatite nanorods.&lt;SEP&gt;The synthesis process evaluated across different time increments to determine the optimal duration for producing adequate hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrothermal reaction is a synthesis process where reaction time is optimized to approach the target stoichiometric ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal Reaction is a synthesis process where varying reaction times affect the volume fraction of material in targeted size regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005</data>
