<node id="Scenario 2">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 2 is a comparative emergy flow model and case study designed to evaluate a phosphogypsum (PG) reuse strategy integrated with monoammonium phosphate (MAP/MPA) production. As the second of four evaluated scenarios, it functions as a disposal and resource utilization method where PG is processed into gypsum powder and blocks for building materials. The model systematically tracks resource inputs, product emergy, and associated environmental impacts across the MAP production and PG manufacturing stages.

In terms of resource and energy dynamics, Scenario 2 relies heavily on high electricity and natural gas consumption, particularly for PG drying, supplemented by air, hydropower, and fossil fuels. This energy mix improves the overall resource structure and enhances resource efficiency. Quantitatively, it records a 21.33% increase in R1 and a 16.02% increase in FR compared to Scenario 1, while simultaneously showing reduced values for R2, LH, LL, and Total in comparative data tables. Due to the rapid escalation in electricity and fossil fuel usage, it exhibits the highest CEI value among the four scenarios. Within its environmental accounting framework, PEI contributes positively to SEI, whereas ESI exerts a negative impact.

Environmentally and economically, the scenario slightly increases production efficiency and economic benefits while delivering moderate sustainability improvements and a reduced pollution index relative to the baseline. The shift to PG reuse alters emission profiles by increasing the shares of SO2 and NOx, yet it drastically reduces dust and solid waste contributions. Consequently, Scenario 2 serves as a critical experimental condition for calculating and comparing emergy loss values for pollutants, as well as for assessing carbon emissions and synergistic effects within the MPA production system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
