  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario 3">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 3 is a phosphogypsum (PG) resource utilization and disposal strategy integrated with monoammonium phosphate (MAP/MPA) production, specifically designed to manufacture fertilizer filling materials. Evaluated as one of four comparative scenarios within an emergy flow model, it assesses resource inputs, product emergy, environmental impacts, carbon emissions, and pollutant emissions. The scenario functions as a case study analyzing the MAP production and PG manufacturing stages, serving as the optimal experimental condition for evaluating synergistic effects and life-cycle phosphorus management.

In terms of resource consumption, Scenario 3 significantly increases emergy inputs by incorporating phosphorus tailings as a renewable resource and utilizing dicalcium phosphate. This approach is marked by a tenfold increase in diesel consumption and a 26.95% rise in electricity use, which contributes to a higher Carbon Emission Index (CEI) value compared to Scenario 1. Despite these elevated energy demands, the strategy successfully recovers solid wastes and introduces phosphorus tailings into the production cycle, balancing resource efficiency with advanced pollution control.

Environmental and comparative analyses demonstrate that Scenario 3 achieves the highest sustainability and the lowest environmental load among the evaluated options. It reduces total emergy loss by 57.66%, decreases dust and solid waste contributions, and yields lower values for R2, LH, LL, and Total in comparative datasets. When benchmarked against Scenario 1, it records a 9204.21% increase in FR and a 186.03% increase in FN. Ultimately, Scenario 3 represents the most effective PG management strategy, delivering the best synergistic effect through efficient life-cycle phosphorus recovery and comprehensive emission mitigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792220571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario 4">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 4 is a production and resource utilization case study within a comparative emergy analysis framework, specifically designed to evaluate monoammonium phosphate (MAP) manufacturing integrated with phosphogypsum (PG) reuse for cement retarder production. As one of four evaluated conditions, it functions primarily as a PG disposal and recycling method that incorporates lime to facilitate cement retarder synthesis. The scenario is modeled as an emergy flow system to assess resource inputs, product emergy, and associated environmental impacts, particularly focusing on pollutant emissions, carbon output, and emergy loss values.

In terms of resource and energy metrics, Scenario 4 exhibits a shifted input profile compared to baseline and other scenarios. It records minor increases in R1, FR, and FN, alongside a 26.68% rise in electricity consumption. The addition of lime slightly elevates emergy inputs, contributing to an adjusted resource structure characterized by a declining share of renewable inputs and a growing proportion of nonrenewable resources. Consequently, the scenario demonstrates reduced values for R2, LH, LL, and Total metrics. While it successfully minimizes dust and solid waste contributions, achieves the highest total emergy loss reduction at 58.27%, and records the lowest pollutant emissions impact intensity, these localized environmental gains are offset by broader systemic drawbacks. Specifically, Scenario 4 yields the lowest Emergy Sustainability Index (ESI) and the lowest synergistic effect index, reflecting an increased overall environmental load and diminished long-term sustainability relative to alternative scenarios. Ultimately, Scenario 4 represents a trade-off where targeted pollution and waste reduction are achieved at the expense of overall resource efficiency and ecological sustainability in the MAP production system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
