<node id="ESI">
  <data key="d0">ESI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ESI measures emergy sustainability index, ranking highest in Scenario 3 and lowest in Scenario 4.&lt;SEP&gt;ESI is a data metric representing resource efficiency, which significantly influences the overall synergistic effect in each scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;An indicator with adverse or negative impacts on SEI in Scenarios 1, 2, and 4, but positive in Scenario 3.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric defined by a mathematical equation involving EYR and ELR.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792221332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EYR">
  <data key="d0">EYR</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">EYR is an indicator measuring production efficiency and economic competitiveness across different scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;EYR measures emergy yield ratio, with values close to one indicating high dependence on imported resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Economic yield ratio indicator measured across the four scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the ESI metric equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019</data>
