<node id="MAP Production Stage">
  <data key="d0">MAP Production Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MAP Production Stage encompasses the sequential processes of manufacturing monoammonium phosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAP production stage is a consistent industrial process across four scenarios, serving as the source of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAP production stage is a primary system component contributing 99.94% to the total emergy input of Scenario 1.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAP production stage is a key industrial process analyzed across all scenarios for its emergy input contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;A production phase where R1, FR, and FN account for 2.79%, 0.29%, and 96.92% of total emergy input.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAP production stage is a manufacturing phase that heavily depends on phosphate rock, liquid ammonia, and operating costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
