<node id="Carbon Emission Intensity">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Emission Intensity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon emission intensity is a key metric for evaluating the environmental performance of the integrated system.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric measuring CO2-eq per ton of MAP, used to compare environmental impact across scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon emission intensity (CEI) is a metric measuring carbon emissions, ranking lowest in Scenario 1.&lt;SEP&gt;A factor considered for reduction in Scenario 2 and lowest in Scenario 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon emission intensity is a metric targeted for reduction through energy and resource structure optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of fossil energy use that increases with certain PG reuse methods, highlighting an environmental trade-off.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-000</data>
