  <data key="d0">Concentrated Steam</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Concentrated Steam is a heat source provided by the hot blast stove for evaporation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG Reuse">
  <data key="d0">PG Reuse</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PG Reuse is a method involving the reuse of phosphogypsum to mitigate pollutant emissions and reduce emergy loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergy Loss">
  <data key="d0">Emergy Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional economic resource compensation required to eliminate negative impacts from pollutant emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Concept quantifying the environmental cost derived from land occupation and pollutant emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergy loss is a metric quantifying environmental impact, with Scenario 1 showing the highest loss and Scenarios 2-4 showing significant declines.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergy Loss is a metric quantifying environmental impact caused by pollutants and land occupation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pollutant Emissions">
  <data key="d0">Pollutant Emissions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pollutant Emissions are environmental impact factors evaluated across various disposal and production practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Pollutant Emissions are outputs from the production system that require ecological services for dilution and may cause ecological or economic losses.&lt;SEP&gt;Discharges of pollutants into air and water that cause ecological services and emergy losses.&lt;SEP&gt;Pollutant Emissions are environmental discharges whose impact is primarily driven by extra ecological services and emergy losses.&lt;SEP&gt;Emissions impact intensity, which is lowest in Scenario 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial by-products whose reduction is a primary goal of the proposed technologies and management strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
