</node>
<node id="Solid Waste Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Solid Waste Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Solid waste disposal is the operational process that necessitates land occupation and associated emergy loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid Waste Disposal is a process that leads to land occupation and associated emergy losses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydropower">
  <data key="d0">Hydropower</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydropower serves as a renewable energy source contributing to the operation costs in Scenario 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydropower is a renewable energy source contributing to FR in both the MAP production and building materials stages.&lt;SEP&gt;A renewable energy source contributing to FR in both production stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydropower is introduced in Scenario 2 to increase the share of renewable resource input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PEI">
  <data key="d0">PEI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">PEI measures pollution emission index, showing significant reductions across all PG reuse scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;PEI is a data metric representing pollution index, where lower values contribute positively to the synergistic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance indicator that contributes positively to SEI in Scenarios 2 and 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CEI">
  <data key="d0">CEI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">CEI measures carbon emission intensity, ranking lowest in Scenario 1 and highest in Scenario 2.&lt;SEP&gt;CEI is a data metric representing carbon emission index, which is minimized in high-performing scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance indicator contributing positively to SEI in Scenario 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TP Discharge">
  <data key="d0">TP Discharge</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">TP discharge represents total phosphorus released in wastewater, reduced by PG reuse methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Total phosphorus discharge in wastewater, a key pollutant reduced by resource utilization methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Imported Resources">
  <data key="d0">Imported Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Imported resources are heavily relied upon across all scenarios, leading to low economic efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG Resource Utilization Methods">
  <data key="d0">PG Resource Utilization Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PG resource utilization methods encompass the alternative production strategies evaluated in Scenarios 2, 3, and 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedures designed to reduce pollutant impacts on human health and the environment compared to PG storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Methods for repurposing PG that incur new environmental issues and require optimization to achieve synergistic effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fertilizer-Filling Material Production Stage">
  <data key="d0">Fertilizer-Filling Material Production Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The fertilizer-filling material production stage in Scenario 3 contains the largest proportion of imported renewable emergy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG Storage">
  <data key="d0">PG Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Baseline method for phosphogypsum management that serves as a comparison point for resource utilization scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;PG storage serves as the baseline method for comparing pollution emission impacts in PEI analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A storage method evaluated for its impact on the MPA production system's environmental metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;PG storage is the baseline method compared against PG reuse options for improving system synergistic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;The large-scale stockpiling of PG that requires remediation technologies to retain fluorine, phosphorus, and sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792223926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waste Gases">
  <data key="d0">Waste Gases</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Waste gases are the medium for dust emissions, which are reduced by PG reuse methods.&lt;SEP&gt;The medium through which dust emissions occur and are reduced by resource utilization methods.</data>
