<node id="FR">
  <data key="d0">FR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FR represents a renewable emergy input component derived from operation and investment costs.&lt;SEP&gt;FR represents a renewable flow input category, derived from operation costs, hydropower, and phosphorus tailings.&lt;SEP&gt;A renewable emergy flow component derived mainly from the renewable part of operation costs and hydropower.&lt;SEP&gt;FR represents a specific emergy resource category that increases significantly in Scenario 3 and is primarily derived from phosphorus tailings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792224994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FN">
  <data key="d0">FN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FN represents a nonrenewable emergy input component derived from materials and nonrenewable costs.&lt;SEP&gt;FN represents a non-renewable flow input category, derived from raw materials like phosphate rock and energy sources like natural gas.&lt;SEP&gt;A nonrenewable emergy flow component primarily derived from phosphate rock, liquid ammonia, lime, and nonrenewable operation costs.&lt;SEP&gt;FN represents an emergy resource category that declines in Scenario 3 but increases slightly in Scenario 4 due to lime input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792224994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
