<node id="Integrated System Performance Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Integrated System Performance Assessment</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1775dab65ef7445e05c5e396bcc0009b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d2">The integrated system performance assessment establishes a comprehensive indicator system to evaluate environmental performance.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792226869</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fertiliser">
  <data key="d0">Fertiliser</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fertiliser is a phosphorus-containing product that can be manufactured from recovered phosphorus waste streams.&lt;SEP&gt;An agricultural input imported into and produced in Australia, serving as a major phosphorus source.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertiliser is a manufactured agricultural product primarily derived from phosphate rock and used extensively in Australian farming.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertiliser is an industrial sector involved in phosphate budgets and the generation of phosphogypsum stockpiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertiliser is a key input in agricultural systems, with its application rates varying across cropping systems and affected by temporal factors like drought.&lt;SEP&gt;An economic sector with phosphorus losses of 20 kt/a P associated with phosphogypsum stockpiles.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector involved in phosphorus processing, characterized by temporary phosphorus losses from phosphogypsum stockpiles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Livestock">
  <data key="d0">Livestock</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A key sector covering animal production, including aquaculture, pastures, and feedlots.&lt;SEP&gt;Animals whose feed composition, manure reuse, and carcass phosphorus content are analyzed in the model.&lt;SEP&gt;Livestock is a key sector involving pastures and feedlots, responsible for manure production, loss, and recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector supported by the majority of phosphorus use in Australia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector where phosphorus is lost or recycled outside the sector, excluding manure recycled internally and abattoir waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food Production">
  <data key="d0">Food Production</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A sector covering crop and fisheries production, imports, and consumption metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;The agricultural sector encompassing crop and fisheries production, central to the phosphorus budget analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Food production is a sector generating organic waste, with some phosphorus recycled back to agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector accounting for phosphorus losses from organic waste associated with overseas exports, excluding abattoir waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organic Waste">
  <data key="d0">Organic Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A key sector comprising solid organic waste from postharvest food system activities, excluding abattoir waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste material from municipal and commercial sectors, tracked for phosphorus content and recycling potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic waste includes materials like banana peels and egg shells that can be efficiently recovered for phosphorus and other resource value.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic waste from food processing and consumption contains phosphorus that can be recirculated.&lt;SEP&gt;A material stream analyzed for data quality, containing food waste, blood and bone, and seafood waste.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector representing phosphorus flows that overlap with food production losses, with percentages calculated relative to the organic waste sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Stockpiles">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Stockpiles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum stockpiles are temporary storage sites for phosphorus from the fertiliser production process, theoretically extractable for reuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Man-made stockpiles in the fertiliser sector associated with temporary phosphorus losses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soil Erosion">
  <data key="d0">Soil Erosion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil erosion refers to phosphorus leaching from agricultural soils into non-agricultural soils, counted as an export.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil erosion is a process causing phosphorus losses to non-agricultural uses and water.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural process identified as the primary cause of phosphorus losses in the agriculture sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abattoir Waste">
  <data key="d0">Abattoir Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Abattoir waste is a type of organic waste excluded from the study due to a lack of data.&lt;SEP&gt;Abattoir waste is a type of organic waste excluded from livestock and food production loss calculations due to a lack of data.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste from slaughterhouses excluded from phosphorus recycling calculations in the livestock and food production sectors due to data limitations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manure">
  <data key="d0">Manure</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Manure is a biological and organic waste byproduct generated by the livestock sector, distinguished by its substantial phosphorus content. The phosphorus contained within livestock manure exceeds the total amount of phosphorus present in the food consumed by the entire human population. This organic material functions as a primary carrier for phosphorus, with its mass and phosphorus concentration serving as critical variables in mass balance calculations.

Within agricultural systems, manure facilitates nutrient transfer between different sectors and follows multiple pathways: it can be recycled back into farming as a fertilizer, managed outside the livestock sector, or lost to the environment. As a locally derived alternative fertilizer source, manure presents significant opportunities for phosphorus recovery and increased reuse. Expanding its utilization in agriculture can substantially reduce reliance on imported phosphate fertilizers, thereby enhancing resource sustainability and supporting circular nutrient management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mining Sector">
  <data key="d0">Mining Sector</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mining sector is a component of the food production-consumption system involved in resource extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial sector holding significant phosphate rock reserves that are currently being depleted.&lt;SEP&gt;The mining sector is an industrial area where internal recovery of phosphorus could potentially occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The mining sector is the industrial domain where circular economy operations and waste management barriers are analyzed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792406917</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crop Residues">
  <data key="d0">Crop Residues</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Crop residues are agricultural byproducts that are recirculated within the agriculture sector and excluded from food production recycling calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Crop residues are agricultural byproducts that are recirculated within the agriculture sector and excluded from phosphorus loss calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Effluent Box">
  <data key="d0">Effluent Box</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A system component that outputs water and sends one unit to the Recycled Effluent Box.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recycled Effluent Box">
  <data key="d0">Recycled Effluent Box</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A system component receiving one unit from the Effluent Box and splitting output to agriculture and non-ag soil.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Ag Soil">
  <data key="d0">Non-Ag Soil</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A destination for recycled biosolids and recycled effluent.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector receiving 0.1 units from the Recycled Effluent Box.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recycled Organics Unit">
  <data key="d0">Recycled Organics Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A research unit contributing data on fertiliser application and agricultural practices.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization cited as a data source for organic waste generation and recycling statistics.&lt;SEP&gt;The Recycled Organics Unit prepared a report on organics recycling in Australia.&lt;SEP&gt;A research organization providing reports on organic waste and recycling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyder Consulting">
  <data key="d0">Hyder Consulting</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyder Consulting is a firm that prepared a report on waste and recycling in Australia.&lt;SEP&gt;A consulting firm providing reports used for organic waste data assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-015</data>
