<node id="Australian Food System">
  <data key="d0">Australian Food System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Australian food system is characterized by naturally phosphorus-deficient soils and a heavy reliance on imported phosphorus for agricultural productivity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Australian Food System is the subject of the flow analysis, characterized by substantial phosphorus losses and inefficiencies from mine to fork.&lt;SEP&gt;The system boundary for the research, encompassing sectors from phosphate rock production to food consumption and waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The integrated network of food production, consumption, and waste management analyzed in the phosphorus budget.&lt;SEP&gt;The Australian Food System encompasses the production, consumption, and environmental impact of phosphorus within the country.&lt;SEP&gt;The Australian food system encompasses production, consumption, and waste stages where phosphorus flows are analyzed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792247941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
