<node id="Pastures">
  <data key="d0">Pastures</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Pastures are grazing lands compared with cropping systems for phosphorus loss tracking.&lt;SEP&gt;Pastures are agricultural lands in Australia where a significant portion of applied fertiliser is utilized.&lt;SEP&gt;Pastures are agricultural lands fertilised with phosphorus to support grazing livestock.&lt;SEP&gt;Pastures are grazing lands predominantly used for Australian livestock, which are phosphorus-efficient due to negligible phosphorus inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792248302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cropping Systems">
  <data key="d0">Cropping Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cropping systems are agricultural practices where phosphorus use efficiency is studied and applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Cropping systems are agricultural methods compared with pastures for phosphorus loss tracking.&lt;SEP&gt;Cropping Systems represent agricultural practices in Australia that consume a major share of applied phosphorus fertiliser.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792248563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beef">
  <data key="d0">Beef</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Beef is a phosphorus-intensive agricultural commodity, with Australia exporting 64% of its domestic production.&lt;SEP&gt;Beef is a phosphorus-intensive agricultural commodity exported from Australia.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary agricultural export contributing to phosphorus outflows from the Australian food system.&lt;SEP&gt;Beef is a major agricultural export that facilitates phosphorus transfer out of the Australian food system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-005</data>
