<node id="Livestock Sector">
  <data key="d0">Livestock Sector</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Livestock Sector represents over 60% of Australia's phosphorus demand, primarily driven by fertilized pastures and animal feed production.&lt;SEP&gt;The livestock sector encompasses animal husbandry activities that consume feed and produce manure, meat, and dairy products.&lt;SEP&gt;A sector characterized by phosphorus accumulation in manure and varying use efficiency across grazing systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The livestock sector is the largest phosphorus-demanding sector in Australia, representing 63% of total demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792248985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food/Fibre Production System">
  <data key="d0">Food/Fibre Production System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The food and fibre production system processes agricultural and livestock outputs into consumable goods and exported commodities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1b5f95e85d7bfa3b7aab581f3c82b33-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792248985</data>
