<node id="Carcinogenic Risk">
  <data key="d0">Carcinogenic Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carcinogenic risk is a component of human health risk assessment, evaluated alongside non-carcinogenic risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Carcinogenic risk is a metric used to evaluate the potential cancer-causing effects of heavy metal exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;The probability of developing cancer due to exposure to contaminants, synonymous with Total Cancer Risk in the context.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-023</data>
