<node id="Geological Accumulation Index Method">
  <data key="d0">Geological Accumulation Index Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geological Accumulation Index Method determines heavy metal pollution levels by comparing metal content to chemical background values, reflecting enrichment in sediments.&lt;SEP&gt;An assessment approach used to determine pollution levels, identifying Hg in PG as a serious pollution level while MPG shows negative indices.&lt;SEP&gt;The geological accumulation index method assesses environmental safety, indicating Cd poses a risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Geological Accumulation Index Method is an analytical technique used to assess heavy metal accumulation in MPG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-023</data>
