  <data key="d0">nHAp</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">nHAp is a synthesized adsorbent material derived from phosphogypsum used for fluoride removal.&lt;SEP&gt;nHAp is a nano-hydroxyapatite material synthesized from phosphogypsum, exhibiting a short rod-like crystal structure and high purity.&lt;SEP&gt;nHAp is a synthesized nano-hydroxyapatite material used as an efficient adsorbent for fluoride removal from aqueous solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;nHAp is a material derived from PG used as an adsorbent for fluoride ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nano-hydroxyapatite derived from waste PG, serving as the adsorbent material in the fluoride adsorption study.&lt;SEP&gt;nHAp is a material derived from PG used for the adsorption of fluoride.&lt;SEP&gt;nHAp is the label used on the XRD graph to indicate the product nano-Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e992f3bad9db87c40308ea55e121bd8a-chunk-005</data>
