<node id="Kissinger Method">
  <data key="d0">Kissinger Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Kissinger Method is applied to determine the kinetic model of phosphogypsum decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Kissinger Method is a kinetic analysis technique used to calculate reaction active energy without relying on a reaction mechanism function.&lt;SEP&gt;A kinetic calculation method used to analyze reaction data, presented in Figure 9.&lt;SEP&gt;A kinetic calculation method used to determine activation energy and confirm the reaction mechanism model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-005</data>
