</node>
<node id="Kinetic Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Kinetic Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Kinetic Analysis involves evaluating the rate and conditions of the phosphogypsum decomposition process.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinetic analysis is performed on samples with masses between 10 and 20 mg using a nitrogen atmosphere and varying heating rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific approach used to interpret the shift of decomposition peaks to higher temperatures with increased heating rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinetic analysis is a scientific method used to determine reaction parameters, such as activation energy, from experimental data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792362494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core-Form and Growing Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Core-Form and Growing Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Core-Form and Growing Mechanism is the specific kinetic model identified for the decomposition process.&lt;SEP&gt;The identified reaction mechanism model for phosphogypsum decomposition, characterized by a specific kinetic equation and n=2 parameter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007</data>
