  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Coal Size is a variable that influences the amount of intermediate calcium sulfide produced during decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical parameter of coal used in the decomposition process, where different sizes significantly affect intermediate product formation and recovery rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-007</data>
