<node id="Dihydrate Processes">
  <data key="d0">Dihydrate Processes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dihydrate Processes are a production route for phosphogypsum that typically operates with higher solids content than hemihydrate processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group 1">
  <data key="d0">Group 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Group 1 is a morphological classification of phosphogypsum characterized by needle-shaped crystals and a uniform distribution of fine needles.&lt;SEP&gt;The top panel of the first figure displaying elongated, prismatic, and needle-like crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group 2">
  <data key="d0">Group 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Group 2 is a morphological classification of phosphogypsum characterized by fine agglomerated needles with weaker cohesive forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The second panel of the first figure displaying a dense, aggregated cluster of plate-like or flaky crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group 3">
  <data key="d0">Group 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Group 3 is a morphological classification of phosphogypsum described as polycrystalline aggregates forming bunches resembling pink sand.&lt;SEP&gt;The third panel of the first figure featuring a large, complex aggregate resembling a rosette or flower-like structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group 4">
  <data key="d0">Group 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Group 4 is a morphological classification of phosphogypsum consisting of small, roundish, pebble-like grains.&lt;SEP&gt;The fourth panel of the first figure showing a massive, porous aggregate resembling a sponge or fused mass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group 5">
  <data key="d0">Group 5</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Group 5 is a morphological classification of phosphogypsum consisting of very thin needle-like crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;The bottom panel of the first figure showing long, rod-like or prismatic crystals that are distinct and separated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electric Furnace">
  <data key="d0">Electric Furnace</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An Electric Furnace is used in the Dry Process to heat phosphate ore for phosphoric acid production.&lt;SEP&gt;An electric furnace is used in the dry process to heat phosphate ore and produce elemental phosphorus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792403958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
