  <data key="d0">7 Percent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">7 Percent is the phosphate ion content threshold above which the ardealite phase appears.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="40 Percent">
  <data key="d0">40 Percent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">40 Percent is the lower bound of HPO4 2- content where gypsum disappears from the mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="55 Percent">
  <data key="d0">55 Percent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">55 Percent is the upper bound of HPO4 2- content where gypsum disappears and ardealite coexistence with brushite begins.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="95 Percent">
  <data key="d0">95 Percent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">95 Percent is the upper bound of HPO4 2- content beyond which only brushite remains present.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solid Solution">
  <data key="d0">Solid Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The solid solution is a homogeneous mixture of gypsum and phosphate components that demixes into distinct phases at specific weight percentages.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid solution is a mixture containing syncrystallized ions characterized by distinct absorption bands correlated with ion quantity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorption Band">
  <data key="d0">Absorption Band</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Absorption bands are spectral features in infrared spectra corresponding to specific chemical vibrations, with intensity and wavelength shifting based on composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorption band is a spectral feature characterized by specific wavenumbers, intensity, and shifts, used to identify mineral phases and chemical compositions.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorption Band refers to specific regions in the FTIR spectrum highlighted by vertical dashed lines, corresponding to vibrational modes of chemical bonds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792427006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P/S Ratio">
  <data key="d0">P/S Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The P/S ratio is a compositional metric that dictates the disappearance of certain absorption bands and the emergence of ardealite bands.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792404947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Characteristic Bands Table">
  <data key="d0">Characteristic Bands Table</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The characteristic bands table summarizes the wavelengths corresponding to absorption bands of phosphate ions in brushite and syncrystallized forms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792405113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
