<node id="Syncrystallization">
  <data key="d0">Syncrystallization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Syncrystallization is a process where phosphate ions incorporate into the gypsum crystal lattice, producing a distinct absorption band.&lt;SEP&gt;Syncrystallization is a process where ions are incorporated into the solid solution, producing measurable absorption band peaks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792405113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Demixing">
  <data key="d0">Demixing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Demixing is a phase separation process where the solid solution gypsum splits into syncrystallized gypsum and ardealite phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
