</node>
<node id="Mixed Media">
  <data key="d0">Mixed Media</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixed Media is a combination of equal parts large and small milling media used to achieve stepwise particle refinement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Reactor">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Reactor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal Reactor is a vessel fixed within a shaker chest to provide periodic motion for simultaneous mechanical milling and mixing during synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shaker Chest">
  <data key="d0">Shaker Chest</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A shaker chest is the equipment implemented to facilitate in situ milling during hydrothermal synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Shaker Chest is a closed apparatus that provides the necessary periodic motion and agitation for the hydrothermal reactor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Milling">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Milling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical Milling is a process achieved through shaking that breaks down particles simultaneously with mixing during the reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ceramic Mortar and Pestle">
  <data key="d0">Ceramic Mortar and Pestle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ceramic Mortar and Pestle is a tool used to coarsely crush the resulting HA samples after the reaction and cooling process.&lt;SEP&gt;A tool used to coarsely crush hydrothermal treatment samples to break apart large clumps after reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ex Situ Milling">
  <data key="d0">Ex Situ Milling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ex situ milling is a post-synthesis processing technique used to break apart clumps and refine particle size distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Ex situ milling refers to milling processes conducted outside the primary reaction environment, such as dry milling.&lt;SEP&gt;A post-reaction milling process applied to HA samples outside the hydrothermal reactor.&lt;SEP&gt;Ex situ milling is a traditional dry post-synthesis processing method compared against in situ approaches for hydroxyapatite treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Ex Situ Milling is a processing technique used as a comparative baseline for In Situ Milling processed Hydroxyapatite samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region I">
  <data key="d0">Region I</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Region I represents the smallest particle size region in the size distribution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Region I is a particle size distribution category used in Table 1 to quantify volume percentages of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;A size region used to categorize HA particle volume fractions in the analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Region I is a specific compositional region tracked for volume percentage changes during reaction and milling processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region II">
  <data key="d0">Region II</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Region II is a targeted particle size region corresponding to a 10–100 nm diameter, used to evaluate milling and reaction effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Region II represents the intermediate particle size region in the size distribution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A size region used to categorize HA particle volume fractions in the analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Region II is a specific compositional region tracked for volume percentage changes during reaction and milling processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792426837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region III">
  <data key="d0">Region III</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Region III represents the largest particle size region in the size distribution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Region III is a particle size distribution category used in Table 1 to quantify volume percentages of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;A size region used to categorize HA particle volume fractions in the analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Region III is a specific compositional region tracked for volume percentage changes during reaction and milling processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-006</data>
