<node id="Aksin">
  <data key="d0">Aksin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Aksin co-studied the unit weight of bricks manufactured by partially replacing clay with phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Aksin is a researcher who co-authored a study on manufacturing bricks with phosphogypsum replacing clay.&lt;SEP&gt;Aksin co-conducted the 2012 brick manufacturing study analyzing shrinkage effects of PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shen">
  <data key="d0">Shen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shen is a researcher who manufactured calcium sulphoaluminate cement with PG and measured setting time.&lt;SEP&gt;Shen incorporated phosphogypsum and water-washed phosphogypsum with cement clinker and fly ash to study setting time.&lt;SEP&gt;Shen manufactured calcium sulphoaluminate cement with varying phosphogypsum contents and noted declines in compressive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Raw Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw gypsum is a natural mineral used as a baseline material compared to phosphogypsum in cement and binder studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw gypsum is a natural additive used as a baseline in cement mixtures to compare against treated phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw gypsum is an unprocessed mineral form compared to phosphogypsum in slag cement mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw gypsum is a natural mineral used as a baseline material in comparative studies of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw gypsum is a material used as a comparative baseline against PG in Taher's study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792450449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrated Lime">
  <data key="d0">Hydrated Lime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrated lime is a component in binder mixtures where phosphogypsum replaces fly ash to affect dry unit weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrated lime is a binder component mixed with fly ash and phosphogypsum to form composite binders.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrated lime is a binder component used in mixtures with fly ash and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrated lime is a material added to mixtures to enhance compressive strength when cured at elevated temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrated lime is a binding agent used in binder mixtures with fly ash and PG.&lt;SEP&gt;A component added to phosphogypsum and fly ash mixtures to enhance binder properties and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrated lime is a chemical additive used to modify the curing behavior and strength of construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792485322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulphoaluminate Cement">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulphoaluminate Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulphoaluminate cement is a specialized cement manufactured with varying PG contents.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphoaluminate cement is a specialized cement type manufactured with varying phosphogypsum contents to evaluate setting time effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphoaluminate cement is a specific cement type whose compressive strength declines with phosphogypsum addition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003</data>
