<node id="Freeze/Thaw Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Freeze/Thaw Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Freeze/thaw resistance is a durability property improved by incorporating polypropene fibers into the mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;A durability property of the matrix that improves with the addition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Freeze/Thaw Resistance is a material property indicating durability against repeated freezing and thawing cycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Freeze/thaw resistance is a physical property of the matrix studied in relation to phosphogypsum modifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcined PG">
  <data key="d0">Calcined PG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcined PG is a processed form of PG used in brick manufacturing with fly ash and lime binders to improve compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;A processed form of phosphogypsum used as a partial replacement material in bricks, mortar, and cement pastes.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcined PG is a processed form of PG used in cementitious mixtures to enhance compressive strength under specific curing conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcined PG is a processed form of phosphogypsum used in mixtures with fly ash and lime.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcined PG is a heat-treated form of phosphogypsum that improves mechanical strength and reduces water absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcined PG is a processed form of PG added at 5% to Portland cement with silica fume to improve hydraulic properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcined PG is heat-treated PG that significantly increases the compressive, flexural, and tensile strengths of mortars.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792503863</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mineral Fibers">
  <data key="d0">Mineral Fibers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mineral fibers are additives that enhance flexural strength, freeze/thaw resistance, anti-impact work, and water resistance at 0.35-1% concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral fibers are a type of additive incorporated into Hua's mixture to improve mechanical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Autoclave Condition">
  <data key="d0">Low Autoclave Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Low autoclave condition is a specific steam treatment (0.12 MPa at 120°C for 16 h) applied to PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Autoclave Condition">
  <data key="d0">High Autoclave Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">High autoclave condition is a specific steam treatment (0.8 MPa at 180°C for 8 h) applied to PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Impact Work">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Impact Work</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-impact work is a mechanical property of the mixture that is enhanced by the introduction of fibers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retarder Effect">
  <data key="d0">Retarder Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The phenomenon where PG significantly delays the setting time of cement mixtures due to protective coating formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Phosphate (Ca3(PO4)2)">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate (Ca3(PO4)2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">An inactive protective coating formed on cement particles that contributes to PG's retarder effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement Particles">
  <data key="d0">Cement Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The surface components of cement where protective coatings form, leading to retardation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Surface Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method applied to PG particles to eliminate impurities and mitigate the retarder effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nigade">
  <data key="d0">Nigade</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A researcher who recorded significant increments in the initial setting time of concrete mixtures with PG substitution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bagade">
  <data key="d0">Bagade</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bagade is a researcher who documented the decline in concrete workability with PG substitution.&lt;SEP&gt;Bagade partially substituted Portland cement with varying percentages of phosphogypsum to measure setting time prolongation.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who recorded significant increments in the initial setting time of concrete mixtures with PG substitution.&lt;SEP&gt;Bagade partially replaced cement in pastes in 2012 with PG to observe soundness expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ölzmen">
  <data key="d0">Ölzmen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ölzmen is a researcher who refined phosphogypsum using water and milk of lime washing after calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who depicted that PG impurities significantly affect the setting time of cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Sulfate Decahydrate">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Sulfate Decahydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium Sulfate Decahydrate is a chemical additive incorporated into cement mixtures prepared by Singh and Garg.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate decahydrate is a chemical additive used in mixture formulations with calcined phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydrated chemical compound added to mixtures by Singh and Garg.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iron Sulfate Heptahydrate">
  <data key="d0">Iron Sulfate Heptahydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron Sulfate Heptahydrate is a chemical additive incorporated into cement mixtures prepared by Singh and Garg.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792452838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chloride Ion Permeability">
  <data key="d0">Chloride Ion Permeability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chloride ion permeability is a durability metric for concrete that decreases with PG substitution for cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453181</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chloride Diffusion Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Chloride Diffusion Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chloride diffusion coefficient measures chloride permeability in concrete and shows significant decline with PG concrete compared to Portland cement concrete.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453181</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Porosity">
  <data key="d0">Total Porosity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total porosity is a physical property of materials that decreases with increasing calcination temperature of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Total porosity is a structural property of slag cement that decreases with PG calcination at higher temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Türket and Aksin">
  <data key="d0">Türket and Aksin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Türket and Aksin replaced clay with PG in brick manufacturing, noting declines in flexural strength and variable compressive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sindhuja et al.">
  <data key="d0">Sindhuja et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Sindhuja et al. investigated the effect of PG as a cement substitution on the compressive strength of concrete.&lt;SEP&gt;Sindhuja et al. substituted cement with PG in concrete, showing reduced chloride ion permeability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bouchhima et al.">
  <data key="d0">Bouchhima et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bouchhima et al. replaced natural sand with PG in brick manufacturing, resulting in lower water absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Press-forming">
  <data key="d0">Press-forming</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Press-forming is a manufacturing technique used to shape the non-fired bricks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453597</data>
