</node>
<node id="Değirmenci and Okucu">
  <data key="d0">Değirmenci and Okucu</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Değirmenci and Okucu are researchers who compared the performance of calcined phosphogypsum under dry and water curing.&lt;SEP&gt;Değirmenci and Okucu are researchers who analyzed the effect of PG on thermal conductivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Huang and Lin">
  <data key="d0">Huang and Lin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Huang and Lin are researchers who evaluated phosphogypsum content limits in steel slag-limestone mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Huang and Lin are researchers who documented increased expansion in specimens with higher PG content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdelhadi et al.">
  <data key="d0">Abdelhadi et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdelhadi et al. are researchers who prepared mortar mixtures incorporating dried phosphogypsum and clinker.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdelhadi et al. prepared mortar mixtures using clinker, phosphogypsum, and fine aggregate to evaluate mechanical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Curing">
  <data key="d0">Water Curing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Water curing is a specimen treatment method that exacerbates strength loss due to sulfate reactions in phosphogypsum mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Curing">
  <data key="d0">Dry Curing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry curing is a specimen treatment method that mitigates strength loss and enhances performance in calcined phosphogypsum mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Citric Acid Treated PG">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Citric Acid Treated PG</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqueous citric acid treated PG is a modified form of phosphogypsum that resulted in a decline in compressive strength when added to cement mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water-Washed Treated PG">
  <data key="d0">Water-Washed Treated PG</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Water-washed treated PG is a processed form of phosphogypsum that enhanced both flexural and compressive strength in cement mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Steel Fibers">
  <data key="d0">Steel Fibers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Steel fibers are added to concrete containing PG to enhance compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Steel fibers are reinforcement additives mixed with PG to improve fire resistance and tensile strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soundness Expansion">
  <data key="d0">Soundness Expansion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A volume change property in cement pastes that increases significantly with PG addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Soundness expansion is a dimensional change property in matrices that increases with the incorporation of PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Soundness expansion is a property that increases with phosphogypsum inclusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Soundness expansion is a physical property of the matrix associated with phosphogypsum applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abrasion Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Abrasion Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abrasion resistance is a durability property that declines when PG is incorporated into the matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Abrasion resistance is a property that deteriorates with the inclusion of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Abrasion Resistance is a property related to the ability to resist wear from friction.&lt;SEP&gt;Abrasion resistance is a physical property of the matrix studied in relation to phosphogypsum modifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freeze-Thaw Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Freeze-Thaw Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Freeze-thaw resistance is a durability property that improves with the inclusion of autoclaved PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Freeze-thaw resistance is a durability property evaluated in phosphogypsum-slag based cementitious materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Umadevi et al.">
  <data key="d0">Umadevi et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Umadevi et al. conducted research on concrete containing PG and steel fibers, documenting strength enhancements and declinations.&lt;SEP&gt;Umadevi et al. are researchers who studied the impact of PG on fire resistance and tensile strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792453914</data>
