<node id="Splitting Tensile Strength">
  <data key="d0">Splitting Tensile Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Splitting tensile strength is a mechanical property evaluated alongside compressive strength in concrete mixtures containing PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Splitting tensile strength is a mechanical property of mortars that declines as phosphogypsum replacement levels increase.&lt;SEP&gt;Splitting tensile strength is a mechanical property of concrete that follows a similar trend to fire resistance when PG is added.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-009</data>
