<node id="Mechanical Strength">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Property of the construction matrix evaluated in relation to phosphogypsum usage.&lt;SEP&gt;A critical performance metric of the matrix that is reduced by raw phosphogypsum but can be improved by calcined phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A key property of the matrix evaluated in relation to phosphogypsum usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical Strength is a property related to the load-bearing capacity of a material.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical strength is a physical property of the matrix that is reduced when phosphogypsum is included.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical strength is a performance metric for cement that is negatively affected by unslaked lime but improved by slaked lime.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad performance metric enhanced by the pozzolanic reaction accelerated by calcined phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
