  <data key="d2">Steam curing is a thermal treatment process applied at 65°C for 6 hours to accelerate mortar specimen hardening.&lt;SEP&gt;Steam curing is a hydration acceleration method applied to mortar specimens before chemical exposure testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A processing condition applied to cement mortar containing phosphogypsum to enhance its physical and mechanical properties.</data>
