<node id="Manjit">
  <data key="d0">Manjit</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Manjit is a researcher who tested aqueous ammonium hydroxide and citric acid solutions to reduce phosphate and fluoride contents in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who conducted follow-up work on PG purification using citric acid and investigated wet sieving and hydrocyclone trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Manjit developed methods for producing stable, high-strength anhydrite cement from phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Researcher who, with Mridul in 2005, explained the use of anhydrite plaster from heated phosphogypsum for flooring tiles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
