<node id="Hydrated Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Hydrated Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrated gypsum is a product of cement reaction that possesses a lower cementing value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cementing Value">
  <data key="d0">Cementing Value</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cementing value refers to the binding efficacy of cementitious materials in mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;Cementing Value refers to the binding capability of phosphogypsum, which is enhanced through heat treatment and subsequent hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.6 W/C Ratio">
  <data key="d0">0.6 W/C Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 0.6 W/C ratio is the water-to-cement ratio used in preparing the mortar mixes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inner Hydraulic Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Inner Hydraulic Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inner hydraulic pressure is the pressure exerted by pore water on the mortar's internal structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cracking">
  <data key="d0">Cracking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cracking is a structural failure mode in mortar caused by internal pressure and loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792502638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
