<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sulfuric Acid">
  <data key="d7">31.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Phosphogypsum and Sulfuric Acid constitutes a multifaceted, bidirectional industrial and chemical cycle encompassing production, resource recovery, purification, and scientific analysis. Industrially, sulfuric acid serves as a primary reactant that chemically attacks and digests phosphate ore to produce phosphoric acid, a process that yields phosphogypsum as a solid waste byproduct. Due to the reaction dynamics, the resulting phosphogypsum naturally retains unreacted or residual sulfuric acid, which imparts a distinctly acidic character to the material.

This compositional link establishes a practical recovery cycle where phosphogypsum functions as a foundational feedstock for sulfuric acid co-production. Through established methodologies such as thermal decomposition, wet decomposition, and solid-solid reaction technologies, the residual acid is extracted to yield commercial-grade sulfuric acid. Furthermore, elemental sulfur can be recovered from phosphogypsum via microbiological processes and subsequently converted into sulfuric acid, reinforcing the material's role in acid production.

Beyond production and recovery, sulfuric acid is extensively utilized to process and purify phosphogypsum for broader industrial applications. Acid leaching with sulfuric acid efficiently extracts valuable rare earth elements and increases the solubility of trace elements during sequential leaching, while simultaneously removing hazardous impurities. This purification enables the safe and economically advantageous utilization of phosphogypsum in construction sectors, including cement manufacturing and road building. In analytical and quality control contexts, diluted sulfuric acid is employed to wash the material for marketable quality assessment and to evaluate solubility constants for scientific characterization. Together, these interactions highlight a dynamic relationship where sulfuric acid drives both the formation and the valorization of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">acid leaching,application,by-product,chemical composition,chemical conversion,chemical industry,chemical production,chemical property,chemical reagent,chemical synthesis,co-product,co-production,composition,contains,contains residual chemical,conventional technique,decomposition,digestion,extraction,extraction agent,extraction process,impurity removal,leaching,processing,product,product derivation,production,production by-product,production process,production reactant,production source,purification,raw material,resource recovery,sequential leaching,solubility enhancement,solubility testing,solvent,treated by,treatment,washing</data>
