<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Bauxite Residue">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bauxite Residue and Phosphogypsum represent a relationship characterized by the application of phosphogypsum to modify and stabilize the chemical and physical properties of bauxite residue. When phosphogypsum is incorporated into the residue, frequently alongside poultry manure, it significantly alters and converts the material's inherent alkaline characteristics. This treatment effectively mitigates the saline-alkalinity present in the bauxite residue, transforming its chemical profile.

In addition to chemical modification, the addition of phosphogypsum directly impacts the structural integrity of the material by enhancing its aggregate stability. The amendment process improves the aggregate-associated characteristics of the bauxite residue, making it a functional stabilizing agent. When combined with organic materials like poultry manure, this application optimizes the residue's overall properties for environmental management or potential reuse.</data>
  <data key="d9">alkaline modification,application,chemical interaction,material interaction,neutralization,property modification,stabilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791774771</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
