<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Cement Retarder">
  <data key="d7">20.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The (Cement Retarder, Phosphogypsum) relation describes the industrial application of processed phosphogypsum as a functional additive to regulate cement setting times and control concrete strength. Raw phosphogypsum undergoes purification, chemical modification, and specialized industrial processing to transform it into an effective cement retarder, which is frequently utilized to replace natural gypsum. Once prepared, the material functions as a setting-time regulator that precisely controls the hydration and hardening rates of concrete mixtures. This application represents a traditional industrial product manufactured on a commercial scale.

This utilization pathway accounts for 33.7% of total phosphogypsum usage, making cement retarder its primary application. By converting an industrial byproduct into a valuable construction additive, the relation highlights a major pathway for the sustainable recycling and reuse of phosphogypsum. The processed material is widely deployed across construction projects and large-scale industrial operations, particularly within China’s construction and industrial sectors. Dedicated commercial enterprises, such as Company Q, actively convert raw phosphogypsum into standardized cement retarder products for market distribution, demonstrating the material's successful integration into modern cement manufacturing and construction practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement retarder is a primary utilization pathway for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as a key component in cement retarders, widely used across multiple provinces.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement retarder is a conventional industrial product manufactured using phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,construction additive,construction use,functional use,industrial additive,market application,material conversion,product derivation,product development,product output,raw material,recycling pathway,recycling use,resource utilization,traditional use,traditional utilization,utilization,utilization pathway,utilization route</data>
