<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Lime">
  <data key="d7">21.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Lime, Phosphogypsum) encompasses a multifaceted industrial, environmental, and chemical interaction focused on material stabilization, purification, and resource recovery. Primarily, lime is applied to phosphogypsum to neutralize its inherent and initial acidity, a critical treatment that renders the material safe for agricultural application and prepares it for industrial processing. Chemically, lime treatment significantly reduces impurity levels within phosphogypsum, notably decreasing soluble phosphorus and fluorine content, with documented fluoride reductions reaching 25.0%.

In engineering and construction applications, lime is extensively used to stabilize phosphogypsum, substantially improving its unconfined compressive strength, durability, and overall mechanical properties. This stabilized mixture is frequently integrated into road construction materials, pavement mixes, building products, and cement manufacturing processes. Lime often operates synergistically with fly ash, where it is blended with both treated phosphogypsum and fly ash to form construction specimens, stabilize pavement mixes, and modify fly ash mixtures, directly influencing the performance of resulting cementitious matrices.

Beyond its role as a treatment agent, the relationship also facilitates resource recovery, as phosphogypsum can be chemically processed to yield lime as a valuable byproduct. Collectively, these processes highlight the versatile utility of combining lime and phosphogypsum across construction, agriculture, and chemical manufacturing sectors, effectively transforming a waste byproduct into a stabilized, purified, and commercially viable material.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is applied to neutralize acidic impurities in raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime acts as an activator when combined with phosphogypsum and fly ash to form cementitious systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is used alongside class C fly ash to stabilize phosphogypsum for marine applications.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive combination,agricultural treatment,application,blending,byproduct generation,chemical activation,chemical conversion,chemical treatment,combination,composite formulation,construction application,durability enhancement,impurity reduction,material blending,material combination,material composition,mixing,neutralization,purification,purification method,stabilization,stabilization agent,stabilizing additive,strength improvement,supplement,treatment</data>
