<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="J. Clean. Prod.">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between the Journal of Cleaner Production and phosphogypsum encompasses a comprehensive body of peer-reviewed research focused on the environmental, material, and industrial dimensions of this industrial byproduct. The journal has consistently published studies detailing the synthesis of gypsum from cleaner phosphogypsum, alongside dedicated research on its stabilization, immobilization, and resource recycling. A central theme across these publications is the thorough examination of phosphogypsum's environmental effects and the potential risks associated with its utilization, providing critical insights into sustainable waste management practices.

In addition to environmental assessments, the journal features extensive research on the valorization and practical applications of phosphogypsum. These studies highlight its integration into road construction and building materials, emphasizing its transformation from waste into valuable resources. The publications also explore co-preparation methods designed to enhance the material's performance and safety. Collectively, this body of work underscores the journal's role in advancing cleaner production techniques and promoting the sustainable, circular-economy applications of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;J. Clean. Prod. featured studies on the sustainable use and application of phosphogypsum.</data>
