<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sulfur Trioxide">
  <data key="d7">14.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and Sulfur Trioxide share a direct compositional relationship, with sulfur trioxide functioning as a major and significant chemical component within phosphogypsum. Quantitative data indicates that phosphogypsum contains approximately 44.67% sulfur trioxide by mass. This specific proportion underscores the compound's fundamental role in the material's overall chemical makeup.

The exact concentration of sulfur trioxide in phosphogypsum is not uniform across all samples. Instead, the content varies significantly depending on the geographic source and country of origin. These regional differences reflect variations in raw materials and industrial processing methods, ultimately influencing the precise percentage of sulfur trioxide present in the final product.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Sulfur Trioxide as a major constituent at 41.1 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur trioxide is a major compound in phosphogypsum with a measured concentration of 48.12 ± 9.04.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur trioxide is a major component of phosphogypsum at 53.5 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur Trioxide is a major chemical composition found in raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains sulfur trioxide as a chemical component.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Sulfur Trioxide as the most abundant chemical constituent across most samples.</data>
