<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Calcium Oxide">
  <data key="d7">21.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The (Calcium Oxide, Phosphogypsum) relation encompasses both the inherent compositional characteristics of phosphogypsum and its multifaceted industrial applications. Phosphogypsum predominantly contains calcium oxide as a major chemical constituent, with the compound accounting for a significant portion of the material's total mass. Quantitative analyses indicate a baseline content of approximately 32.04%, though exact concentrations vary depending on the geographic region and country of origin. This natural abundance establishes phosphogypsum as a substantial reservoir of calcium oxide.

From an industrial processing perspective, the relation operates bidirectionally. On one hand, phosphogypsum functions as a primary feedstock for the production of high-purity calcium oxide. This extraction is achieved through thermal decomposition, a process that can be efficiently conducted at reduced or low temperatures and is typically optimized using a catalyst to maximize yield. On the other hand, calcium oxide is deliberately added to phosphogypsum in certain treatment processes to chemically reduce its phosphorus and fluorine content, thereby mitigating environmental hazards.

Furthermore, the calcium oxide extracted from or associated with phosphogypsum serves as a critical raw material in downstream manufacturing. Specifically, it acts as the primary calcium source in the synthesis of synthetic hydroxyapatite. Together, these factors highlight the (Calcium Oxide, Phosphogypsum) relation as a dynamic interplay between natural composition, resource recovery, chemical stabilization, and industrial feedstock utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Calcium Oxide as a major constituent at 30.2 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium oxide is a major component of phosphogypsum at 43 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum completely decomposes into Calcium Oxide when subjected to high temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium oxide is a major constituent found in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum decomposition yields calcium oxide as the main product.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Calcium Oxide as the second most abundant chemical constituent.</data>
  <data key="d9">calcium source,chemical component,chemical composition,chemical transformation,chemical treatment,composition,constituent,contains,decomposition,decomposition product,high concentration,impurity reduction,major element,primary component,primary constituent,product,production,recycling,secondary component,thermal decomposition</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020</data>
