Despite these discrepancies in reported abundance, it is consistently noted that potassium oxide is an inherent component of phosphogypsum. Furthermore, the available data indicates that the presence of potassium oxide in phosphogypsum remains stable, showing no significant changes following treatment processes. The variation in characterization likely reflects differences in source material, analytical methods, or specific industrial processing conditions, though the exact concentration remains subject to contextual variation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains potassium oxide as a chemical component.</data>
