<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Haplic Chernozem">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Haplic Chernozem and Phosphogypsum is defined by the targeted application of Phosphogypsum to Haplic Chernozem soil for agricultural and environmental management. Specifically, Phosphogypsum is utilized on this soil type to achieve both amelioration and remediation objectives. This application process has been rigorously evaluated through controlled model experiments designed to assess the efficacy of different application rates.

During these experimental studies, Haplic Chernozem serves as the designated soil matrix, providing a consistent medium for testing how varying quantities of Phosphogypsum influence soil conditions. Phosphogypsum was systematically introduced to the Haplic Chernozem at specific and differing doses to determine optimal treatment levels. These model experiments collectively establish a framework for understanding how precise Phosphogypsum dosing can effectively improve and remediate Haplic Chernozem soils.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,application site,experimental application,remediation target,soil amendment,soil treatment</data>
