<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Soil">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphogypsum and Soil exhibits a dual nature, characterized by both beneficial applications and significant environmental risks depending on management practices. When intentionally and regulatedly applied, phosphogypsum serves multiple functional purposes. It is utilized to treat soil acidity, improve structural integrity, enhance nutrient availability, and mechanically break apart fine soil elements. In agricultural and engineering contexts, it acts as a stabilizing additive that modifies soil plasticity and compaction behavior. Specific application protocols involve mixing the material with soil in a dry state for three minutes prior to water addition, and it is often applied at varying doses for both agronomic improvement and environmental impact research. These controlled applications are governed by strictly regulated permissible content limits that vary by land type.

Conversely, unregulated accumulation, inadequate storage, or improper disposal of phosphogypsum leads to severe ecological and chemical disruptions. Surface storage and the seepage of impurities into the ground cause substantial soil contamination and environmental pollution. These unmanaged conditions alter soil acidity, deplete organic matter, reduce microbial activity, and compromise structural stability. Furthermore, phosphogypsum accumulation disrupts the natural balance of water, air, and heat within the soil matrix, while toxic emissions and contaminated runoff exacerbate widespread degradation. A critical concern is the introduction of radioactive elements, particularly the increased concentration of Radium-226, which poses radiological hazards. Together, these factors demonstrate that while controlled integration of phosphogypsum can yield mechanical and agronomic benefits, unmanaged exposure or storage fundamentally degrades soil health and ecosystem functioning.</data>
  <data key="d9">acidification,additive,agricultural treatment,alters properties,application,contamination,contamination source,degrades quality,environmental impact,landscape alteration,material combination,mechanical division,mixing process,pollution,regulation,remediation,soil amendment,soil degradation,soil improvement,stabilization,structural disruption</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-005</data>
