<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="USEPA">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and the United States Environmental Protection Agency (USEPA) are linked through a regulatory and scientific framework focused on managing the material's radiological hazards. The USEPA officially classified phosphogypsum as Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material (TENORM) due to its inherent radioactive content, a classification supported by published reports on phosphate processing operations. In response to these radiological concerns, the agency restricted the commercial use of phosphogypsum in 1992, allowing only material that falls below specific radium concentration thresholds. To control ongoing environmental exposure, the USEPA establishes and enforces comprehensive rules governing radioactive emissions originating from phosphogypsum sources.

Beyond direct regulation, the USEPA actively conducts waste characterization and risk assessments for phosphogypsum and other naturally occurring radioactive material wastes. The agency has also been a central subject of investigation within broader research scopes dedicated to evaluating phosphogypsum's environmental footprint, handling practices, and compliance standards. Through these combined regulatory, analytical, and investigative efforts, the USEPA maintains a structured approach to mitigating potential public health and ecological risks associated with phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,compliance,environmental policy,regulation,regulatory assessment,regulatory classification,regulatory investigation,research scope,restriction,waste management</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001</data>
