<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Carbonation Process">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum serves as a primary starting material for the carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process treats phosphogypsum to concentrate rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process utilizes phosphogypsum as a raw material to extract calcium for carbonate formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as the primary feedstock for the carbonation process.</data>
  <data key="d9">feedstock,raw material,starting material,treatment,utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792124265</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d7">18.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphate Rock and Phosphogypsum is defined by an industrial manufacturing process in which phosphate rock serves as the primary raw material. In phosphoric acid and fertilizer factories, phosphate rock is digested and chemically processed with sulfuric acid to synthesize phosphoric acid. This production pathway inherently yields phosphogypsum as a direct waste byproduct, establishing a strict material dependency between the extraction of the raw mineral and the generation of the secondary output.

The physical, chemical, and morphological characteristics of the resulting phosphogypsum are fundamentally determined by the specific geological source and composition of the phosphate rock utilized. Because phosphogypsum inherits the mineralogical profile of the raw material, its purity, trace concentrations, and overall chemical makeup vary significantly depending on the rock's quality. Furthermore, the byproduct directly incorporates impurities and radioactive content from the phosphate rock, and frequently retains unreacted phosphate rock particles. Consequently, the nature of the original phosphate rock dictates both the structural morphology and the compositional profile of the generated phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">byproduct generation,composition,composition dependency,composition variation,conversion,determines,geological origin,impurity source,industrial association,industrial by-product,industrial byproduct,industrial origin,mineralogical variation,morphological factor,production by-product,production source,raw material,raw material influence,source material,trace concentration</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792409448</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
