<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Calcium Sulfate">
  <data key="d7">23.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Calcium Sulfate and Phosphogypsum is fundamentally defined by composition, as phosphogypsum is primarily composed of calcium sulfate, which serves as its main chemical component and primary source of calcium resources. Spectral data analysis confirms this identification, establishing calcium sulfate as the defining constituent of the material. However, phosphogypsum is not pure calcium sulfate; it contains various impurities alongside the target compound. Within the phosphogypsum matrix, calcium sulfate manifests across multiple mineral phases, encompassing gypsum, bassanite, and anhydrite, and is notably identified as a distinct phase in samples treated at a pH of 5. The hydration of calcium sulfate within this compound can be inhibited by the formation of calcium phosphate, indicating that specific chemical conditions significantly influence its structural state. Additionally, calcium sulfate within phosphogypsum decomposes efficiently under molten conditions.

Beyond its foundational role in chemical identity, the high concentration of calcium sulfate imparts specific physical and functional characteristics to phosphogypsum. The material shares thermal properties with natural gypsum and holds notable economic value. Industrially, the abundance of calcium sulfate enables phosphogypsum to function effectively as an oxygen carrier. Furthermore, it serves as a critical binding agent for radioactive materials, as several radionuclides are known to coprecipitate directly with the calcium sulfate within the phosphogypsum structure. Phosphogypsum also serves as the primary raw material for extracting calcium sulfate during phosphoric acid production. Together, these attributes underscore how calcium sulfate dictates both the practical utility and environmental behavior of phosphogypsum, linking its chemical composition directly to its industrial applications and resource potential.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical classification,chemical composition,component of,composition,composition contrast,constituent,contains,decomposition target,dissolution inhibition,hydration target,identification,initial compound,main component,main ingredient,material relation,pH dependency,phase identification,potential constituent,primary component,primary composition,primary constituent,primary source,purity,raw material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018</data>
