<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Citric Acid">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Citric Acid and Phosphogypsum are connected through an industrial purification and pre-treatment process. In this application, phosphogypsum is soaked or immersed in an aqueous citric acid solution, followed by a washing step. This treatment serves multiple chemical and functional purposes. Chemically, citric acid converts inhibitory impurities into soluble forms and transforms calcium sulfate within the material into gypsum.

From a purification standpoint, the citric acid treatment effectively leaches and removes various contaminants and residual impurities, notably reducing levels of phosphorus pentoxide and fluorine. It is also highly effective at mitigating radioactivity; as a leaching reagent, it reduces the relative proportion of radionuclides in phosphogypsum by 22%, ultimately yielding the lowest radionuclide content among comparable treatments. Additionally, citric acid is evaluated as a weak acid leaching agent specifically for the recovery of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.

The practical outcome of this citric acid pre-treatment is a significant enhancement in the material's utility. By purifying the phosphogypsum and removing harmful contaminants and radionuclides, the treated material demonstrates improved performance when utilized in cemented paste backfill applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Washing with citric acid considerably reduces soluble phosphorus pentoxide in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Citric acid removes impurities from phosphogypsum when used as an alternative chemical treatment.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical transformation,chemical treatment,extraction research,impurity reduction,impurity removal,leaching,leaching agent,leaching reagent,lowest concentration,pre-treatment method,purification,purification treatment,reduction,soaking,treatment,treats</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792489895</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Portland Cement">
  <data key="d7">19.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Phosphogypsum and Portland Cement is defined by a manufacturing and chemical synergy wherein phosphogypsum functions as a raw material, additive, and partial replacement in cement production and concrete formulation. Typically processed into purified or weathered forms, phosphogypsum serves as a direct substitute for natural gypsum and operates primarily as a set retarder. Its integration enables manufacturers to precisely adjust setting times while simultaneously lowering the required clinkerization temperature. Chemically, the soluble components within phosphogypsum actively interact with the hydration process of Portland cement, directly influencing its setting behavior and overall mechanical properties. Although this additive effectively modulates the setting rate, it is documented to considerably reduce the final compressive strength of the resulting cement.

Research frequently investigates Portland cement hydration in relation to phosphogypsum addition to better understand these performance modifications. Treated phosphogypsum is also compared to Portland cement based on calcium oxide content, highlighting compositional similarities and distinctions. Beyond its use in standard cement manufacturing, phosphogypsum is frequently combined with Portland cement and fly ash for broader reuse within the building industry. Ultimately, the incorporation of phosphogypsum into Portland cement systems supports eco-efficient construction practices, establishing the material as both a functional performance-adjusting agent and a valuable sustainable industrial byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a set controller in the manufacture of Portland Cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material or additive in the production of Portland cement.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,comparison,composite development,construction application,construction valorization,hydration interaction,hydration study,industrial application,industrial combination,manufacturing use,material application,material compatibility,material interaction,material substitution,production,property alteration,property modification,raw material,raw material for,retarder,set retarder</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
