<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Fluoride">
  <data key="d7">24.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Fluoride and Phosphogypsum is defined by fluoride's status as a primary, soluble impurity and characteristic pollutant within the industrial material. Although present as a trace element, fluoride exists in multiple chemical forms and consistently accumulates in elevated concentrations that pose significant environmental and health risks. During processing and storage, fluoride can be released into the surrounding environment as gas or dust. When exposed to water, phosphogypsum frequently generates leachate with fluoride levels that exceed established drinking water safety standards, although leaching rates vary depending on specific environmental conditions. Once introduced into ecosystems, fluoride readily migrates through groundwater and soil, adsorbs into topsoil, and is absorbed by vegetation. As a primary cause of fluorosis, this contamination severely restricts the material's potential for agricultural application, making fluoride management a critical factor in handling and disposal.

From an industrial and analytical perspective, fluoride acts as a soluble impurity that negatively affects processing by weakening the compressive strength of gypsum. This necessitates specific elimination protocols and rigorous monitoring to meet quality standards and prevent widespread environmental contamination. Due to its toxicity and pervasive presence, analytical methods are routinely employed to quantify and mitigate this hazardous component across various global sources, highlighting the ongoing scientific and regulatory focus on controlling this key pollutant within phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains fluoride impurities that contribute to atmospheric and groundwater contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride is a water-soluble impurity in phosphogypsum that is reduced through washing.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,characteristic pollutant,chemical analysis,chemical content,composition,contains,contains impurity,contaminant,contamination,contamination risk,determination,environmental concern,impurity,leachate composition,pollutant composition,pollution,presence,primary pollutant,toxicity,trace element source,waste composition,water-soluble removal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-010</data>
