  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Uranium-238">
  <data key="d7">23.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and Uranium-238 share a direct relationship defined by the presence of this radioactive isotope as a naturally occurring component within the industrial byproduct, originating from radioactive decay chains. This inherent presence classifies Uranium-238 as a radioactive contaminant that significantly shapes the material's overall radiological profile. The concentration and activity of Uranium-238 in phosphogypsum are not uniform; they fluctuate based on specific operational conditions at phosphoric acid plants and are notably higher within coarse particle fractions. Reported activity levels vary considerably, with documented concentrations ranging from 9.0 Bq/kg to 164 ± 12.5 Bq/kg.

Due to these radiological characteristics, phosphogypsum serves as a primary source material for extracting Uranium-238, though its natural contamination necessitates purification processes to ensure safe industrial application. Consequently, the isotope is routinely quantified and tracked during radiological and trace element assessments. Researchers measure Uranium-238 activity concentrations, often employing conversion factors derived from Uranium-235 to ensure accuracy, to monitor its distribution and the migration of its daughter isotopes. These analytical efforts are critical for managing the associated radiological implications, particularly regarding leaching risks posed by Uranium-238 and other uranium isotopes. Furthermore, environmental monitoring reveals that long-term amendments using phosphogypsum can lead to the accumulation of Uranium-238 in reclaimed marsh soils, underscoring the need for careful management of this industrial material.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains uranium-238 that can be removed via suitable organic extractants.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains measurable levels of uranium-238.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 concentrates in the phosphogypsum byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity concentration,analysis,byproduct accumulation,component of,composition,contains,environmental contamination,extraction target,isotope concentration,isotopic measurement,material,measured concentration,measured in,measurement,presence,radioactive component,radioactive content,radioactive isotope,radioactive source,radioactivity analysis,radiological analysis,radiometric analysis,radionuclide,radionuclide content,sample measurement,soil accumulation,source,source material,trace element analysis,variable content</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005</data>
