<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="P2O5">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">P2O5 is a chemical constituent in phosphogypsum that investigators aimed to mitigate.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 comprises less than 1% of phosphogypsum material, but high application rates increase available soil phosphorus.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a component of phosphogypsum that provides essential soil nutrients and benefits agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains P2O5, which is beneficial for agriculture without requiring purification.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 represents a quantified impurity component with an average mass fraction of 1.31%.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains P2O5, which exists in various forms like H3PO4 and Ca(H2PO4)2.H2O4.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains P2O5 as an impurity.</data>
  <data key="d9">agricultural benefit,chemical form,composition,impurity,impurity in,nutrient content</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-000</data>
