<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Water">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Phosphogypsum, Water) encompasses chemical, industrial, and environmental dimensions. Chemically, water is an integral component of phosphogypsum, existing as part of its hydrated calcium sulfate structure. In industrial and stabilization processes, water is routinely added to phosphogypsum as an initial input to form a mixture or pulp. This combination is sometimes prepared with other waste materials to facilitate chemical processing or to prepare the material for soil application.

Functionally, water serves as the medium from which phosphogypsum removes pollutants. Conversely, the environmental interaction between the two is significant, as the discharge of phosphogypsum into water bodies poses fundamental risks to both environmental quality and human health. Together, these aspects illustrate how water interacts with phosphogypsum across structural, operational, and ecological contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is used to wash and purify phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">added to,chemical composition,composition,contamination source,environmental impact,hydration,impurity,initial preparation,input,input mixture,mixing,mixture component,processing step,purification agent,treatment medium</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-25198f8665e133385fd54e5a03e28a44-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
