<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Nitric Acid">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Nitric acid is studied as a strong acid leaching agent to extract rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric acid serves as a diluted acidic medium to study phosphogypsum solubility and leaching efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric Acid was used in the acid digestion process to prepare Phosphogypsum samples for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric Acid is used to process phosphogypsum in conventional rare earth recovery techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric acid is coupled with sodium nitrate to remove fluoride and lanthanides from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">acidic leaching,chemical treatment,conventional technique,extraction agent,extraction research,leaching agent,purification method,sample preparation,solvent</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001</data>
