  <data key="d8">Hydrochloric acid is investigated as an alternative strong acid for leaching rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrochloric acid is used as a leaching agent to dissolve rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrochloric acid is utilized in leaching experiments to dissolve phosphogypsum and gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrochloric acid is used to leach and extract rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrochloric Acid is used to process phosphogypsum in conventional rare earth recovery techniques.</data>
  <data key="d9">conventional technique,dissolution,dissolution agent,extraction agent,extraction process,extraction research,leaching,leaching agent,solvent</data>
