  <data key="d8">Dehydration of phosphogypsum releases rare earth elements locked in its structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum undergoes dehydration as a primary transformation stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum undergoes dehydration and decomposition steps at specific temperature thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration is a process occurring in the phosphogypsum sample near 900°C.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration reduces the setting time and reverses conductometric curves in phosphogypsum.</data>
