  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sodium hydroxide treatment transforms phosphogypsum into calcium hydroxide, enriching rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium hydroxide is investigated for its effect on the properties of phosphogypsum-based cement.&lt;SEP&gt;The stoichiometric molar ratio between Phosphogypsum and Sodium Hydroxide is defined as 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium hydroxide is used as a reactant to prepare compounds from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium hydroxide is used to convert phosphogypsum into sodium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium hydroxide is added to phosphogypsum mixtures to reduce setting time and enhance early compressive and flexural strength.</data>
