<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Thorium-232">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains Thorium-232 as part of its uranium series radionuclide enrichment.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Thorium-232, which initiates the thorium decay chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Thorium-232 as a radioactive contaminant.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium-232 is a radioactive isotope in phosphogypsum evaluated for its environmental mobility.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium-232 concentration is measured in Phosphogypsum as part of the trace element analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium-232 is monitored in phosphogypsum to track radioelement concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Thorium-232 at a concentration of 1.0 Bq/kg.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,concentration tracking,contains,enrichment,isotopic measurement,measured concentration,radioactive component,radioactivity,radioelement monitoring,trace element analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791736238</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Potassium-40">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between phosphogypsum and potassium-40 is defined by the natural presence of the radioactive isotope within the industrial byproduct. Phosphogypsum inherently contains potassium-40 as a radioactive contaminant, occurring alongside other natural radionuclides. Reported concentrations of the isotope vary across different contexts, with measurements recording levels of 11 Bq/kg in some samples and 72 ± 4.9 Bq/kg in others, a discrepancy likely attributable to variations in raw material sources, processing methods, or analytical conditions. Despite its radioactive classification, potassium-40 contributes only minimally to the overall radioactivity measured in phosphogypsum.

From an industrial and practical standpoint, this relationship presents both management challenges and resource opportunities. The presence of potassium-40 necessitates purification processes to ensure the safe industrial application of phosphogypsum, a task that can be effectively accomplished by removing the isotope using organic extractants. Conversely, phosphogypsum also functions as the primary source material from which potassium-40 is extracted for various applications. This dual nature underscores the isotope's role as both a contaminant requiring mitigation and a valuable resource to be recovered.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,contains,enrichment,extraction target,isotopic measurement,minor contributor,radioactive component,radioactive content,radioactive isotope,radioactivity,radionuclide,source,source material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792457955</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
