  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum is transformed into sodium sulfate alongside calcium silicate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum waste is converted into sodium sulfate as an intermediate step.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate is synthesized from phosphogypsum during the preparation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is converted into sodium sulfate using sodium hydroxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate is produced from gypsum/phosphogypsum through reaction with sodium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is used as a raw material for the production of sodium sulfate.</data>
