<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Solidification/Stabilization">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The process is applied to Phosphogypsum to manage stockpiles and control Potentially Toxic Elements release.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a key material in solidification and stabilization processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification and stabilization are used to immobilize harmful substances in phosphogypsum and treat contaminated soils.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification and stabilization processes utilize phosphate resources like phosphogypsum to treat industrial residues.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification/stabilization is a method applied to phosphogypsum to immobilize contaminants and enable reuse.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,material application,phosphate resource,process application,treatment,treatment method,waste management,waste treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791723729</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Cement Industry">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The cement industry utilizes phosphogypsum as a raw material for production.&lt;SEP&gt;The cement industry utilizes phosphogypsum as a replacement for natural gypsum in setting regulator applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The cement industry uses phosphogypsum to reduce clinkerization temperature and adjust cement retarders.&lt;SEP&gt;The cement industry uses phosphogypsum as a setting regulator, though impurities can delay setting time.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,industrial application,process optimization,raw material substitution,setting regulator,utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792489894</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Concrete">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Concrete and phosphogypsum share a relationship centered on the integration of phosphogypsum as a supplementary material, additive, or partial replacement for cement within cement-based concrete production. Concrete, a foundational construction material, increasingly utilizes recycled phosphogypsum as a raw material to modify its physical and mechanical properties. This application is primarily driven by ongoing research aimed at enhancing material performance and exploring sustainable construction practices.

Scientific investigations focus on creating concrete specimens that incorporate phosphogypsum to systematically evaluate its impact on workability and structural integrity. Experimental testing has demonstrated that mixing phosphogypsum into concrete batches at an optimal content level of approximately 12% effectively maximizes compressive strength. Consequently, phosphogypsum is actively studied and experimentally validated as a viable partial replacement for traditional cement in concrete mixtures, confirming its potential as a functional and efficient additive in modern concrete production.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum radioactivity levels are frequently compared against concrete to assess environmental safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is incorporated into concrete to modify its permeability and strength characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is added to concrete to evaluate its impact on material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is investigated as a potential additive in concrete production.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as a replacement material in concrete experiments.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,comparative material,component,composite material,composition,construction use,manufacturing,material additive,material application,material composition,material substitution,partial replacement,potential use,property evaluation,radioactivity benchmark,strength enhancement,strength optimization,structural application</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
