<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Construction Materials">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Construction Materials, Phosphogypsum) describes the recycling and industrial utilization of phosphogypsum as a functional component within the building sector. Construction materials represent a primary application pathway and utilization sector for recycled phosphogypsum. In practice, phosphogypsum is routinely incorporated into various construction materials and building products, frequently serving as a direct substitute for natural gypsum during manufacturing processes.

Beyond material substitution, the integration of recycled phosphogypsum delivers both technical and sustainability benefits. Its inclusion actively enhances the mechanical properties of the resulting construction products. Simultaneously, diverting phosphogypsum into the construction industry significantly reduces industrial waste management costs and minimizes the overall environmental footprint associated with phosphogypsum disposal. Consequently, this application establishes a vital recycling pathway that transforms an industrial byproduct into a valuable, performance-optimizing resource for modern construction.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,application sector,industrial use,industrial utilization,recycling,recycling pathway,recycling target,recycling use,utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792458351</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
