  <data key="d8">Bassanite is a calcium sulfate species identified within phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Bassanite is a primary calcium sulfate component that composes phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Bassanite is a secondary compound found in phosphogypsum, formed from its reaction with sulphuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Bassanite is one of the calcium sulfate phases identified within phosphogypsum.</data>
