<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Anhydrite">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Anhydrite is a calcium sulfate compound present in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrite is a primary calcium sulfate component that composes phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrite proportions rise alongside increasing Phosphogypsum content in the bricks.&lt;SEP&gt;Adding Phosphogypsum to concrete increases the anhydrite content in the final product.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrite is derived from waste gypsum and phosphogypsum for use in cement and plaster manufacture.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,chemical conversion,composition,derivation,increased prevalence,mineral composition,primary constituent,processing</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-019</data>
