<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains phosphates that are often fixed with metals, reducing their bioavailability.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate is a key component of phosphogypsum that can enhance crop fertility but risks causing eutrophication.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains phosphate as a soluble impurity that affects industrial processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphates alter the crystal structure of phosphogypsum, which is detrimental to setting and hardening processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate in the form of Ca(PO3)2 contributed 0.2% to the overall constituents in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate exists in raw phosphogypsum as Ca(PO3)2.&lt;SEP&gt;Radionuclides in phosphogypsum form mobile complexes with phosphate.</data>
