  <data key="d8">Sulfate is a primary chemical constituent of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate is a dominant ion in the chemical composition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Excess sulfate enhances the partitioning of uranium into the gypsum crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains sulfate ions that can be extracted into aqueous solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains sulfate ions, which are assigned to specific stretching and bending vibration modes in the FTIR spectrum.</data>
