<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sulfur">
  <data key="d7">16.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Phosphogypsum and Sulfur is characterized by sulfur's fundamental presence and high abundance within the material. Sulfur serves as a predominant and major chemical component, consistently exhibiting the highest mass fraction among phosphogypsum's constituents. Alongside calcium, sulfur constitutes over ninety percent of the substance, a composition that is instrumental in confirming the bulk material's identity and gypsum nature. Analytical evaluations frequently treat sulfur as a volatile chemical species during sample analysis.

Beyond its compositional role, sulfur plays a significant part in the processing and practical applications of phosphogypsum. During certain treatment stages, sulfur concentration has been observed to decrease by approximately thirteen percent following leaching processes, and the element is often targeted for removal to meet specific processing requirements. Conversely, sulfur is also recognized as a key component for industrial recovery, particularly as a primary product recovered during the thermal decomposition of phosphogypsum. Furthermore, the material holds substantial agricultural value due to its sulfur content, functioning as a direct source of this nutrient for plant nutrition and effectively supplying it as a low-grade fertilizer component in agricultural soils. Together, these attributes highlight sulfur's critical role in defining the chemical identity of phosphogypsum while driving its environmental, industrial, and agricultural utility.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains high concentrations of sulfur, contributing to the economic valorization of the industrial by-product.</data>
  <data key="d9">agricultural component,chemical analysis,chemical composition,chemical content,composition,concentration analysis,confirmation,confirms composition,decomposition product,dominance,elemental composition,elemental content,elemental makeup,highly abundant,leaching effect,major element,nutrient source,predominant element,primary composition,primary constituent,recovery target,soil supplementation,volatile species</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-002</data>
