<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Scanning Electron Microscope">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and the Scanning Electron Microscope share a direct analytical relationship centered on the structural examination of the material. The Scanning Electron Microscope is utilized to visualize, analyze, and capture detailed micrographs of phosphogypsum samples. This instrumental approach serves as the primary method for investigating the physical characteristics of the substance, establishing a clear technical link between the analytical instrument and the material under study.

Through this imaging process, the Scanning Electron Microscope specifically targets the surface morphology, surface topography, microstructure, and granular structure of phosphogypsum particles. By revealing the irregular morphology and fine surface features of the material, the technique provides comprehensive insights into the physical properties and structural composition of phosphogypsum, enabling precise scientific evaluation of its particle-level characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope captures micrographs that illustrate the surface morphology and particle structure of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope examines the texture and morphology of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is utilized to visualize the particulate morphology of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope was used to analyze the microscopic morphology of phosphogypsum platelets.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,analytical tool,analyzed by,characterization,imaging,imaging application,imaging subject,imaging target,material analysis,microscopic imaging,microscopy,morphological study,morphology,morphology analysis,morphology examination,surface analysis,surface morphology</data>
