<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Chromium">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Chromium and Phosphogypsum indicates that phosphogypsum contains chromium as a trace element and potential toxic heavy metal impurity. This chromium exists as heavy metal ions that can be released into the environment, posing environmental risks and contributing to contamination. Despite these potential hazards, tabular data indicates that chromium concentrations in phosphogypsum generally remain below the rare effect concentration.

From a processing perspective, chromium exhibits high liquid/solid fractionation during leaching, meaning it readily partitions into the liquid phase when exposed to water. Consequently, this element can be effectively eliminated from phosphogypsum through simple water washing. Overall, the association highlights both the environmental considerations of chromium presence in phosphogypsum and the straightforward remediation methods available for its removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is the sample matrix analyzed to determine the percentage content of chromium.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains chromium as a trace element, with an initial concentration of about 5.4 ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains chromium, with higher levels observed in commercial potassium sulphate compared to synthetic versions.&lt;SEP&gt;Chromium is a naturally occurring heavy metal impurity contained within phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Chromium, exhibiting a uniform low-intensity distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains chromium, a heavy metal found in fine particle fractions.</data>
  <data key="d9">analytical target,composition,contains,elemental composition,elimination,fractionation,hazard,heavy metal,impurity,presence,sample composition,source,threshold compliance,toxic metal,trace content,trace element analysis,water washing</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad247a75dda6243453b4132b71670203-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009</data>
