<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Calcium Sulfide">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Calcium sulfide is formed as the primary decomposition product of phosphogypsum under lower temperatures and a reducing atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfide is obtained from the hydrolysis of phosphogypsum decomposition slag.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfide is produced via the sulfur reduction decomposition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is partially reduced to calcium sulfide, which can form sulfide residues in the slag.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum decomposition produces calcium sulfide as an intermediate.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical decomposition,decomposition product,derivation,product,production,reduction product,reduction stage,residue formation,source material</data>
