<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Japan">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Japan initiated the first research on phosphogypsum utilization in the 1970s.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan achieves a 100% comprehensive utilization rate for phosphogypsum due to a lack of gypsum resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan utilizes phosphogypsum primarily for gypsum construction products due to domestic gypsum shortages.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan recovers three million tons of phosphogypsum annually for profitable plaster manufacturing.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan considers phosphogypsum recovery profitable for plaster manufacturing due to local soil conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan emphasizes the comprehensive utilization of Phosphogypsum, primarily for building materials due to resource scarcity.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan primarily utilizes phosphogypsum for the production of building materials.</data>
