<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate Fertilizer Industry">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Phosphate Fertilizer Industry and Phosphogypsum are linked through a direct industrial production relationship. The Phosphate Fertilizer Industry serves as the primary producer of phosphogypsum, generating it as a major, significant, and substantial waste by-product. Due to the large quantities of this material produced, the industry necessitates the development and implementation of viable recycling technologies to manage the output effectively.

The scale of this production is clearly illustrated by regional data, particularly in Turkey, where the phosphate fertilizer industry generates approximately 3 million tons of phosphogypsum annually. This continuous and high-volume generation underscores the material's status as a direct industrial by-product and highlights the ongoing requirement for sustainable waste management and recycling solutions within the sector.&lt;SEP&gt;The phosphate fertilizer industry generates phosphogypsum as a by-product during phosphoric acid production.</data>
  <data key="d9">by-product,by-product generation,by-product of,byproduct,byproduct generation,generates,generation,industrial by-product,industrial byproduct,industrial origin,industrial source,production,production source</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-764bdde7c1b68efdbe7342cc41c2d3d4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-000</data>
