<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="South Africa">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum (South Africa) is recognized as a significant industrial byproduct and environmental challenge within the country. South Africa serves as a confirmed geographic source for this material, with samples frequently collected and analyzed in scientific literature to determine their elemental and trace concentrations. Research indicates that phosphogypsum originating from this region contains significantly higher levels of trace elements compared to materials sourced from other geographic areas.

Despite its compositional characteristics, phosphogypsum remains largely underutilized in South Africa, leading to ongoing disposal issues that are classified as both an environmental and industrial problem. To address this underutilization and mitigate waste, phosphogypsum sourced from South Africa has been actively investigated for potential industrial applications, including its evaluation and development as a cement set retarder.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical analysis,contamination levels,data source,disposal,environmental impact,geographic occurrence,geographic source,geographical sampling,geographical source,industrial waste,material testing,problem location,sample origin,sample source,source location</data>
