  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Zinc">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Phosphogypsum, Zinc) encompasses both the inherent presence of zinc within the material and its functional application in environmental remediation. Phosphogypsum consistently contains zinc as a trace element, a composition confirmed through analytical testing and tabular data. The mass content of zinc in phosphogypsum is significantly higher than natural environmental baselines; however, these concentrations typically remain below the rare effect concentration and fall beneath typical soil levels found in final commercial products. Furthermore, zinc levels exhibit significant variation depending on the specific product formulation, particularly when comparing commercial applications to synthetic calcium carbonate derivatives.

Beyond its intrinsic composition, phosphogypsum is widely utilized as an industrial byproduct and remediation medium. Its material properties enable it to effectively adsorb and remove zinc from aqueous environments and industrial solutions. This functional application highlights the dual role of phosphogypsum, serving simultaneously as a zinc-bearing material and a practical agent for zinc remediation in water treatment contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains zinc, a heavy metal.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum releases an estimated 6726 tons of zinc into the estuary.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains zinc, which demonstrates high transfer percentages to the aqueous phase during leaching.</data>
