</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Barium">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Barium and Phosphogypsum establishes that barium is a chemical constituent and trace element present within phosphogypsum byproducts and samples. Its distribution is systematically analyzed as part of the material's heterogeneous composition. Although classified as a trace element, barium occurs in phosphogypsum with significant concentration, yet it exhibits poor solubility and is essentially located in the residual phase.

Environmental and chemical assessments further demonstrate that barium possesses low mobility within this matrix. Specifically, its concentration shows only a slight decrease in leached samples, confirming its stable, residual nature. Consequently, barium remains a poorly soluble, low-mobility component embedded within the complex structure of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum releases an estimated 6509 tons of barium into the estuary.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains barium as part of its chemical composition.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,chemical presence,composition,concentration,concentration analysis,constituent,contains,contamination,distribution,mobility classification,presence,release,residual phase,trace elements</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792487794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Strontium">
  <data key="d7">16.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between phosphogypsum and strontium characterizes strontium as a chemical constituent, trace element, and metallic impurity within phosphogypsum byproducts, originating from the phosphate rocks utilized in production. Strontium is present at a relative proportion of approximately 0.49 wt%, with concentrations varying significantly and routinely measured in milligrams per kilogram. It is typically concentrated in the fine fraction of phosphogypsum, a distribution pattern that aids in differentiating various phosphogypsum types.

Within the phosphogypsum matrix, strontium exhibits intermediate mobility and poor solubility. It is strongly retained within the material, necessitating strong chemical dissolution for its release. Due to the heterogeneous composition of phosphogypsum, the spatial distribution and concentration of strontium are routinely evaluated as part of comprehensive trace element assessments.

The environmental behavior of strontium in phosphogypsum is actively investigated, particularly its leaching characteristics under conditions simulating acid rain exposure. Alongside other elements, strontium is studied to evaluate broader environmental impacts. Notably, phosphogypsum has been estimated to release approximately 54,219 tons of strontium into estuarine environments, underscoring the significance of monitoring its mobility and retention within the byproduct matrix.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical component,chemical composition,chemical dissolution,chemical presence,composition,concentration,contains,contamination,distribution,fractionation,leaching,measured concentration,mobility classification,presence,release,retention,trace element,trace element analysis,trace elements</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
