<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Radon-222">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The (Phosphogypsum, Radon-222) relation describes the environmental and radiological connection between phosphogypsum waste and radon-222 emissions. Phosphogypsum contains elevated levels of radon-222 radionuclides, which are continuously exhaled and released into the open air from storage stacks and piles. This exhalation process is a primary focus of environmental studies due to the material's role as a significant source of atmospheric radon transport.

The dynamics of this emission are highly variable, with exhalation rates differing by several orders of magnitude depending on specific material properties. These rates are directly correlated with radium-226 activity and are physically influenced by particle size, notably decreasing in coarser phosphogypsum fractions. Because of these emission patterns and the resulting environmental release, measuring radon-222 exhalation rates is essential. Such measurements are routinely conducted to evaluate associated radiological risks, underscoring the necessity for careful radiological evaluation and management of phosphogypsum storage and handling.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,contains,decay product,emission source,exhalation,exhalation source,impurity,radioactive emission,radiological hazard,transport modeling</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
