<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Recrystallization">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Recrystallization is a method proposed for removing radium isotopes from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a chemical process applied to phosphogypsum to remove rare earth elements and alter its hydrate structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is used alongside carbonation to process phosphogypsum into fertilizer compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is applied to phosphogypsum to increase rare earth element concentration prior to extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is used to remove heavy metals and lanthanides from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a technique used to purify gypsum derived from phosphoric acid production byproducts.</data>
  <data key="d9">concentration increase,industrial treatment,material transformation,pre-treatment,processing,processing method,purification method,purification process,radium removal,raw material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-016</data>
