<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Calcium sulfate hemihydrate becomes the predominant mineral in phosphogypsum after calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum processing involves Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate as an intermediate stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a primary chemical component of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a secondary chemical component found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains calcium sulfate hemihydrate as a primary chemical component.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains calcium sulfate hemihydrate as a main component.</data>
