<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Mortar">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum is used as a replacement material in mortar mixes to evaluate improvements in setting times.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is incorporated into mortar as a partial cement replacement, directly influencing compressive strength outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is added to mortar as a potential material enhancement.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is used as a replacement material in mortar mixes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as a replacement material in mortar experiments.</data>
  <data key="d9">material additive,material application,material substitution,property evaluation,setting time evaluation,strength impact,substitution material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-000</data>
