<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="India">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">India manufactures gypsum board, blocks, bricks, and cement using phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;India accounts for 6.35% of the global distribution of phosphogypsum production or reserves.&lt;SEP&gt;India utilizes phosphogypsum for producing cement, bricks, and fertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;India is listed as the origin for phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a source region for Phosphogypsum, with its chemical composition documented in Table 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum samples from India were analyzed and reported in scientific studies.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,construction application,data source,geographical sampling,geographical source,global distribution,industrial production,origin,production share,sample source,utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-525daf613910500054a23427717dab1f-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792487639</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
