<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Direct Leaching">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Direct leaching is applied to phosphogypsum but is costly and ineffective due to low rare earth element concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct leaching is a technique overviewed for recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct Leaching processes phosphogypsum and requires control of contact time, solid to liquid ratio, temperature, and agitation speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct leaching approaches could significantly limit the radioactivity of phosphogypsum.</data>
