<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Thermogravimetric Analysis">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Phosphogypsum, Thermogravimetric Analysis) describes the application of thermogravimetric analysis to investigate the thermal properties and decomposition behavior of phosphogypsum. This analytical technique is primarily employed to monitor and quantify mass changes, weight loss, and mass percentage as the material undergoes heating or thermal treatment. Specifically, the method is utilized to identify and measure distinct mass loss stages, including dehydration processes, that occur during the thermal decomposition of phosphogypsum.

Beyond general thermal behavior characterization, thermogravimetric analysis is also applied to examine specific chemical interactions under controlled conditions, such as the reaction between phosphogypsum and carbon within an inert atmosphere. Overall, this technique serves as a critical tool for tracking compositional changes, evaluating thermal stability, and mapping the decomposition pathways of phosphogypsum throughout its heating process.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric Analysis is used to characterize the decomposition process of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric Analysis is employed to characterize phosphogypsum properties.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,analytical method,analyzed using,application,characterization,experimental method,mass loss,mass loss measurement,mass measurement,mass tracking,material analysis,measurement,reacts with,substrate,thermal analysis,thermal characterization,thermal study</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d5e4f0f96b4ad61d23685552d3211225-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792408394</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Infrared Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infrared spectroscopy and phosphogypsum are connected through an analytical relationship in which the spectroscopic technique is systematically applied to characterize the material. This method is primarily utilized to identify and analyze water molecules, water of crystallization, and sulphate groupings within the phosphogypsum structure. By recording and interpreting the infrared spectra, researchers can determine the sample's transmittance, spectral characteristics, and overall chemical properties. The technique provides essential insights into the molecular composition and chemical behavior of the material, serving as a foundational tool for compositional analysis.

The application of this relationship extends to monitoring dynamic chemical changes, particularly those induced by processing conditions such as thermal treatment. Spectra are routinely recorded both before and after such treatments to track structural transformations and evaluate resulting chemical shifts. Furthermore, infrared spectroscopy is employed to assess the quantity and nature of impurities present in phosphogypsum samples. In experimental practice, this analytical approach is frequently utilized alongside other characterization techniques to ensure a comprehensive and accurate evaluation of the material's properties.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,analysis method,analytical application,analytical method,analyzed using,characterization,impurity evaluation,material characterization,spectral analysis,spectral recording,structural characterization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792504417</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
