<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Anhydrite III">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Heating phosphogypsum up to 280 °C leads to the formation of anhydrite III through the elimination of hydration water.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum undergoes dehydration to transform into Anhydrite III at specific temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum dehydrates to form anhydrite III at 66 and 133 degrees Celsius.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration of phosphogypsum leads to the formation of anhydrite III.</data>
  <data key="d9">dehydration,dehydration product,phase transformation,product,thermal transformation,thermal transition</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
