<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Oxalic Acid">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Oxalic acid is listed as a reagent in the table for studying phosphogypsum solubility.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid is applied as a leaching reagent to treat phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid is used as a leaching reagent on phosphogypsum, which increases the relative proportion of radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid is used to treat phosphogypsum, yielding gypsum and disodium catena-disilicate.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid is used to leach phosphogypsum but is less effective than citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxalic acid treatment results in the highest radionuclide content in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Washing with oxalic acid considerably reduces soluble phosphorus pentoxide in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical transformation,chemical treatment,highest concentration,impurity reduction,leaching,leaching reagent,purification,reagent,solubility study,treatment,treats</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-013</data>
