<edge source="Calcination" target="Phosphogypsum (PG)">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Calcination is one of the representative methods used to modify phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal pretreatment technique used to purify phosphogypsum for industrial applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination treats Phosphogypsum to reduce water-soluble impurities and mitigate setting time delays.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination at elevated temperatures reduces total porosity and mitigates strength degradation caused by raw PG.</data>
