<edge source="Calcination" target="Taher">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Taher determined that 600 degrees Celsius is the optimal calcination temperature for Egyptian phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Taher determined that 600 °C was the optimal calcination temperature for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Taher applied calcination at varying temperatures to phosphogypsum to modify its properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Taher linked the calcination process to reduced setting times by eliminating water-soluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Taher utilizes calcination at various temperatures to reduce impurities in phosphogypsum.</data>
