  <data key="d8">Mineral Carbonation captures and sequesters carbon dioxide by combining it with minerals to form stable carbonates.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral carbonation combines carbon dioxide with minerals to form stable carbonates.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon dioxide serves as the primary greenhouse gas targeted for sequestration via mineral carbonation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral carbonation utilizes Carbon Dioxide to form stable calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral carbonation is the primary method used to permanently store carbon dioxide in solid forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral carbonation captures carbon dioxide by converting it into stable mineral forms.</data>
  <data key="d9">capture,chemical reaction,environmental application,process application,reaction,reacts with,sequestration,target,target material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
