<edge source="Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate" target="Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Calcium sulfate hemihydrate dissolves and precipitates as calcium sulfate dihydrate during the setting process.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate dehydrates to form calcium sulfate hemihydrate during the plaster manufacturing reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate reacts with water to form calcium sulfate dihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate hydrates to form calcium sulfate dihydrate, releasing heat.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate transforms into Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate during the calcination process.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate transforms into calcium sulfate hemihydrate during temperature treatment.</data>
  <data key="d9">calcination product,chemical transformation,dehydration reaction,dissolution,hydration,phase conversion,phase transformation,precipitation,precursor relationship</data>
