<edge source="Sulfuric Acid" target="Phosphoric Acid">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphoric Acid and Sulfuric Acid encompasses several industrial and chemical processes where sulfuric acid serves as a key reagent in the production of phosphoric acid. In standard industrial practice, sulfuric acid is employed to treat apatite ores, facilitating the extraction and generation of phosphoric acid. Additionally, recovered or recycled sulfuric acid is actively utilized within industrial phosphoric acid manufacturing to improve efficiency and resource management.

Beyond apatite processing, sulfuric acid also participates in specific chemical reactions with thorium(IV) phosphate to yield phosphoric acid. This particular reaction pathway concurrently produces thorium sulfate as a byproduct. Collectively, these interactions highlight the versatile role of sulfuric acid as both a primary processing agent and a recyclable component in the synthesis and industrial production of phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is used to treat phosphate ore in the production of phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphoric acid production processes utilize sulfuric acid, which influences the quality of the resulting phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical input,chemical reactant,chemical transformation,industrial application,product formation,production,production process,raw material,reactant,reaction output</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3d20c90c2a00342300c9b55c3e29f23-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792407963</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
