<edge source="Sulfuric Acid" target="Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Residual sulfuric acid from the leaching process is repurposed as a slurrying aqueous in phosphate rock processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid reacts with phosphate rock to produce single superphosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid digests phosphate rock to convert phosphate rock into phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rock reacts with sulfuric acid in the wet process to produce phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rock is a primary input used in the production of sulfuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rock is reacted with sulfuric acid to produce concentrated phosphate fertilizers for agricultural use.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical digestion,chemical processing,chemical reaction,chemical reuse,fertilizer synthesis,industrial application,processing,production,raw material,reactant,wet process</data>
