<edge source="Cement" target="PGCM">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cement is a key component in PGCM that significantly influences its dissolution rate and strength coefficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement acts as a primary binding agent that constitutes the matrix of PGCM.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement is added to PGCM to increase the strength coefficient, though high dosing decreases antifreeze performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement is added to PGCM to increase its expansion degree by generating hydration products that squeeze surrounding aggregates.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement significantly influences the dissolution rate and strength coefficient of PGCM.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement increases the hardened body's density and strength but is not conducive to improving weathering resistance.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,admixture,component,composition,dissolution rate,expansion mechanism,key component,mechanical enhancement,performance enhancement,performance factor,strength coefficient</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791516804</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cement" target="Dissolution Rate">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cement significantly influences the dissolution rate of PGCM, acting as a key factor for antifreeze performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement has a significant influence on the dissolution rate of PGCM.</data>
  <data key="d9">significant influence</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011</data>
