<edge source="Rare Earth Elements" target="Phosphoric Acid">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rare earth elements are distributed into the phosphoric acid product, accounting for 20%-30% of the total elemental mass.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphoric Acid retains a minority share (20%–30%) of the Rare Earth Elements as a liquid product.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy rare earth elements are preferentially partitioned into phosphoric acid during the wet process.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earth elements are extracted from phosphoric acid and its associated sludge.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphoric acid reacts with rare earth elements during extraction to form specific ionic complexes.</data>
