<edge source="Calcium Carbonate" target="Carbonation Process">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Carbonation Process transforms Portlandite and CO2 into Calcium Carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium carbonate forms at 74 minutes as the final product of the carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonation Process chemically yields Calcium Carbonate as a final output.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process transforms phosphogypsum into calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process chemically transforms portlandite into calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process chemically synthesizes calcium carbonate from calcium ions in the feedstock.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process transforms calcium ions from phosphogypsum into high-purity calcium carbonate.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical product,chemical reaction,chemical synthesis,chemical transformation,final output,final product,formation,product,product formation,production,synthesis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80e3f6300e001922a5ca2a6a8ac2e0d2-chunk-012</data>
