<edge source="Fly Ash" target="Lime">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fly Ash and Lime function as complementary additives in geotechnical and construction applications, primarily utilized together to stabilize and modify phosphogypsum. When combined, these materials significantly enhance the mechanical strength and durability of construction mixtures, making them highly suitable for road construction, backfilling operations, and embankment projects. The standard application process involves stabilizing fly ash with lime to optimize mixture characteristics prior to its integration with phosphogypsum, ensuring reliable performance in civil infrastructure.

Chemically, the interaction between lime and fly ash facilitates a pozzolanic reaction with silica and alumina components, leading to the formation of robust cementitious bonds. In advanced material engineering, fly ash and lime are frequently co-activated, often utilizing calcined phosphogypsum as a key component, to develop alkali-activated systems. This chemical activation process further amplifies structural integrity, establishing the Fly Ash and Lime combination as a versatile and effective solution for sustainable construction and industrial waste valorization.</data>
  <data key="d9">binder formation,co-additive,combination,geotechnical mixture,material combination,reaction,stabilization,strength improvement,synergistic activation,synergistic additive</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-819484fd12a30d085e4eb297904c9e2b-chunk-018</data>
