<edge source="Phosphoric Acid" target="Uranium">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Uranium distributes primarily into phosphoric acid during the wet phosphoric acid process.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium isotopes are retained in approximately 70–85% of the extraction phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphoric acid retains 70-85% of uranium isotopes during phosphogypsum production.&lt;SEP&gt;Over 80% of uranium remains in phosphoric acid due to the high solubility of U(VI) in acidic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium primarily remains in phosphoric acid under oxidizing conditions, with up to 90% retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium tends to remain with the phosphoric acid product during production.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical retention,distribution,partitioning,retained in,retention,solubility</data>
