<edge source="PG" target="Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">PG addition generally influences mortar compressive strength, causing declines or improvements depending on mix design and curing.&lt;SEP&gt;PG acts as both an activator and filler, initially boosting compressive strength before causing a decline at higher concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Increasing PG replacement percentage decreases the compressive strength of mortar mixes.&lt;SEP&gt;Increasing the percentage replacement of PG reduces the compressive strength of mortar mixes.</data>
  <data key="d9">activator and filler,dual role,influence,inverse relationship,material substitution,mechanical property,strength reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e0549fcda95f7199440791b20bf85635-chunk-006</data>
