  <data key="d8">Hydroxyapatite belongs to the calcium phosphate class with a general stoichiometry close to Ca10(PO4)6Y2.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Phosphate layers convert to Hydroxyapatite during the hydrothermal synthesis process.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate is the chemical class to which hydroxyapatite belongs.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Phosphate layers convert to Hydroxyapatite during the hydrothermal synthesis process.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate serves as a primary precursor in the synthesis of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical classification,composition,phase conversion,precursor,stoichiometry,synthesis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
