<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Phosphate Group">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hydroxyapatite contains phosphate groups as fundamental structural units in its crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;The phosphate group is a surface component of hydroxyapatite whose electronic state is altered during photocatalytic activation under UV irradiation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Phosphate Group is a fundamental chemical component of the Hydroxyapatite lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Phosphate Group serves as a fundamental structural component within the Hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Phosphate Group serves as a fundamental structural component within the Hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,chemical framework,electronic state alteration,lattice moiety,structural component,structural unit</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008</data>
