<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Ca/P Ratio">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Ca/P Ratio in hydroxyapatite strongly correlates with and modifies its inherent acid-base properties.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P molar ratio is maintained at 1.67 during synthesis to ensure proper material stoichiometry.&lt;SEP&gt;Ca/P Ratio was measured to determine the chemical composition of the synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P ratio of hydroxyapatite is dependent on synthesis time and conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P ratio is a key quantitative metric measured to evaluate the purity of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P Ratio is a critical compositional metric for Hydroxyapatite coatings.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical measurement,composition,composition control,compositional parameter,material property,measurement,property dependence,quantitative data,stoichiometry,structural correlation,synthesis dependency</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b81aeff540d385f1d1eda298b44619be-chunk-001</data>
