<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="CTAB">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CTAB and Hydroxyapatite share a synthetic relationship in which CTAB functions as a multifunctional surfactant and structural template. CTAB actively regulates the nucleation, crystallization, and overall crystal growth of Hydroxyapatite. Mechanistically, it controls this crystallization process by forming a tetrahedral cation that structurally complements the phosphate anion framework. Furthermore, CTAB adsorbs directly onto the surface of Hydroxyapatite crystals, where it directs crystal growth patterns and modifies their spatial orientation.

Beyond its templating role, CTAB is specifically utilized to synthesize Hydroxyapatite nanorods and to modify base Hydroxyapatite materials or samples. Despite its active involvement in shaping the material's morphology and structure throughout the synthesis process, CTAB does not remain in the final product. It is thoroughly washed away after synthesis, ensuring that the resulting Hydroxyapatite is free of detectable CTAB impurities.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,crystallization control,growth regulation,impurity removal,material modification,material synthesis,regulation,sample preparation,surface modification,surfactant,surfactant modification,synthesis additive,templating</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792191009</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Hydrothermal Process">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The hydrothermal process provides the high temperature and pressure environment required to synthesize HAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hydrothermal Process is used to synthesize Hydroxyapatite, with temperature variations directly influencing its morphology and particle size.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrothermal Process is a method used to synthesize hydroxyapatite by controlling reaction parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite was successfully synthesized using the hydrothermal process.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrothermal process is frequently used to prepare nanocrystalline Hydroxyapatite with controlled size and morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrothermal process is frequently used to prepare nanocrystalline Hydroxyapatite with controlled size and morphology.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,controlled morphology,experimental condition,synthesis,synthesis method,synthesis technique,temperature dependence</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792191588</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="XRD Analysis">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Hydroxyapatite, XRD Analysis) encompasses the application of X-ray diffraction techniques to thoroughly characterize hydroxyapatite samples. XRD analysis is primarily employed to examine and verify the crystalline structure, phase composition, and overall crystallinity of the material. Additionally, this analytical method is utilized to assess sample purity by confirming the absence of detectable impurities and to verify specific particle size characteristics.

Through these applications, XRD analysis serves as a critical validation tool for confirming the successful synthesis of hydroxyapatite and ensuring its structural integrity. The technique consistently demonstrates that synthesized products align precisely with the expected crystalline phase of hydroxyapatite, thereby validating both the material's structural accuracy and its high degree of purity.</data>
  <data key="d9">analytical verification,characterization,crystallinity,examines,phase confirmation,phase identification,structural analysis,structural validation</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792191569</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
