<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="SEM">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The (Hydroxyapatite, SEM) relation encompasses the application of Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) to analyze the physical characteristics and structural properties of hydroxyapatite across various material states, including powders, synthesized samples, and calcined variants. SEM is primarily employed to examine the morphology, architecture, and surface features of hydroxyapatite particles, providing detailed insights into particle shape, size, spatial distribution, and arrangement. Additionally, this imaging technique is utilized to characterize the degree of particle aggregation and agglomeration within the material.

Depending on the specific synthesis method or thermal treatment applied, SEM imaging reveals distinct morphological outcomes. It has been used to identify uniform rod-like nanoparticle structures in certain preparations, while simultaneously capturing the irregular, desultory structures, pronounced agglomeration, and porous architectures characteristic of calcined hydroxyapatite. By delivering high-resolution visual data on these physical and structural attributes, SEM is frequently integrated alongside complementary analytical techniques to ensure a comprehensive evaluation of hydroxyapatite materials.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,characterization,microscopic imaging,morphological analysis,morphological inspection,morphology,morphology analysis,surface imaging,surface structure analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792428184</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
