<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="XRD">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hydroxyapatite and XRD (X-ray Diffraction) form a fundamental analytical relationship in materials characterization, where XRD is employed to evaluate the structural and phase properties of synthesized hydroxyapatite samples, powders, and products. XRD analysis is primarily utilized to assess the crystal structure, crystallinity, and phase composition of the material. A key objective of this technique is to verify and confirm the phase purity of the synthesized hydroxyapatite, ensuring that the resulting powders are homogeneous and consist of a single phase.

Furthermore, XRD is specifically applied to determine the crystalline elementary cell parameters, providing precise insights into the lattice arrangement of the hydroxyapatite. Collectively, XRD serves as an essential characterization method for validating the structural integrity, phase homogeneity, and crystalline quality of hydroxyapatite in both research and industrial synthesis applications.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is used to determine the poor crystalline nature of dried and calcined hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is used to determine the crystallinity and phase structure of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD was used to determine the crystallinity and primary crystallite size of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,analytical characterization,characterization,crystalline characterization,crystallinity,crystallinity analysis,crystallinity assessment,phase analysis,phase identification,phase verification,structural analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-176fa906dd9c8409d2d1c49b8bdf9948-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792428031</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="X-ray Diffraction">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Hydroxyapatite, X-ray Diffraction) encompasses the application of X-ray diffraction techniques to characterize and analyze the structural and phase properties of hydroxyapatite, particularly in synthesized powder forms. X-ray diffraction serves as a fundamental analytical method for evaluating the crystallinity, crystalline structure, and overall crystallographic framework of the material. By interpreting diffraction patterns, researchers can identify specific crystalline phases and verify phase purity, which is critical for confirming the material's compositional integrity and suitability for targeted applications.

Beyond qualitative structural assessment, X-ray diffraction is employed to quantify key microstructural parameters of hydroxyapatite. This includes determining crystallite size and particle size distributions, as well as measuring precise lattice spacing within the crystal matrix. Together, these analytical capabilities provide a comprehensive evaluation of hydroxyapatite's material properties, making X-ray diffraction an indispensable tool for quality control, structural validation, and advanced materials research involving this compound.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction is used to characterize the structural evolution of the synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction patterns reveal the poor crystalline nature of the dried and calcined hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction is employed to investigate the crystallinity and structural properties of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction was employed to assess the relative quality and identify crystalline phases in the hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray Diffraction assesses the crystallinity and domain sizes of HA samples.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,analysis method,analysis technique,analyzes,characterization,crystalline quality,crystallinity,crystallinity assessment,material analysis,phase identification,phase verification,structural analysis,structural characterization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792427993</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Transmission Electron Microscopy">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between hydroxyapatite and Transmission Electron Microscopy centers on the use of this high-resolution imaging technique to comprehensively characterize the material across various forms, including synthesized powders, nano-hydroxyapatite, and nanorods. Through Transmission Electron Microscopy, researchers are able to visualize and quantify critical physical attributes, such as particle size, crystal size, and detailed morphology. The technique is specifically employed to investigate the internal structure and dimensions of hydroxyapatite nanorods, while also enabling the direct observation of lattice fringes and mesoporous structures within the hydroxyapatite matrix. By leveraging this method, scientists can accurately determine the microstructural and dimensional properties of elaborated hydroxyapatite samples.

In addition to static structural analysis, Transmission Electron Microscopy is utilized to monitor dynamic morphological changes within the material. Notably, the technique captures the morphological transition of hydroxyapatite particles from rodlike to spherical shapes upon calcination. Overall, the application of Transmission Electron Microscopy to hydroxyapatite provides essential insights into its crystallographic features, porosity, particle dimensions, and phase-dependent structural evolution, thereby supporting thorough material characterization across various synthesis and processing stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmission electron microscopy was employed to analyze the synthesized hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmission Electron Microscopy examines HA particle agglomerations and individual particulates.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,characterization,high-resolution imaging,imaging,material characterization,methodology,microstructural analysis,morphological analysis,morphology analysis,morphology observation,nanorod analysis,particle sizing,size characterization,structure</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72ff3bbf1e2b594abc3ec5c8d86e3178-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792427994</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
