  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Carbonate ions substitute for phosphate or hydroxyl groups within the hydroxyapatite lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions substitute phosphate ions in hydroxyapatite to form Type B variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions substitute into the hydroxyapatite lattice, causing microscale stresses and deformations.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions are adsorbed onto the surface of Hydroxyapatite, with capacity significantly increased by CTAB.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate ions are adsorbed onto the surface of Hydroxyapatite, with capacity significantly increased by CTAB.</data>
  <data key="d9">Type B formation,adsorption,chemical substitution,ion substitution,structural modification,substitution,surface interaction</data>
