<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Urea">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Urea acts as an organic modifier and mineralizer to promote the formation of nanorods and nanobundles.&lt;SEP&gt;The crystalline structure of hydroxyapatite was altered through hydrothermal reaction using urea as an organic modifier.&lt;SEP&gt;Urea undergoes slow hydrolysis to provide an alkaline environment that facilitates the nucleation and growth of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Urea influences the formation and morphology of hydroxyapatite during double-step hydrothermal processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Urea affects the formation of hydroxyapatite during hydrothermal processing.</data>
  <data key="d9">alkaline environment,chemical effect,formation influence,mineralizer,nucleation,organic modifier,processing aid,structural modification</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791986138</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Naphthalene">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Naphthalene serves as an organic modifier that forms pore-forming structures with high surface area.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene serves as a template that creates pore-forming structures, increasing the surface area and porosity of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Naphthalene was used as an organic modifier to alter the crystalline structure of hydroxyapatite during synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d9">organic modifier,pore formation,porosity,structural modification,template</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001</data>
