<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="P123">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The (Hydroxyapatite, P123) relation describes the interaction where P123 functions as a specialized surfactant during the synthesis and modification of hydroxyapatite materials. P123 is actively utilized across various fabrication processes, including the production of base hydroxyapatite, modified hydroxyapatite samples, and specifically hydroxyapatite nanorods. Its primary role in these contexts is to serve as a structural and morphological directing agent that integrates with the material during its formation.

Mechanistically, P123 adsorbs directly onto the surface of the hydroxyapatite crystals. This surface interaction is critical for controlling and modifying the crystal growth and orientation. By regulating these fundamental crystallization parameters, P123 effectively tailors the nanostructure and physical properties of the resulting hydroxyapatite, ensuring the material achieves specific structural characteristics required for its intended applications.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,material modification,material synthesis,sample preparation,structural modification,surface modification,surfactant,surfactant modification,synthesis additive</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f07601cd9e687d5cc5c7d9b6b467f21e-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792191161</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
