<edge source="Phosphorus" target="Australia">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphorus is a critical element for the Australian economy and food system.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia acts as a net importer of phosphorus to replenish naturally deficient soils for its agricultural sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia acts as a net importer of phosphorus, bringing in approximately 80 kt annually.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia is the geographic region where the described phosphorus flows across agricultural, industrial, and environmental sectors occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia is a net importer of phosphorus despite being a net food exporter.&lt;SEP&gt;Australia imports phosphorus and experiences significant losses of this resource within its food system.</data>
  <data key="d9">economic significance,geographic scope,import dependency,imports,loses from food system,national context,net importer,resource dependency,supply chain,trade flow,trade status</data>
