<edge source="Radium-226" target="Lead-210">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lead-210 and Radium-226 form an isotopic pair within the uranium decay chain used for fractionation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 decays into lead-210, forming a chain used to evaluate secular equilibrium.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead-210 and Radium-226 are paired to calculate the Lead-210 to Radium-226 Activity Ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 decays into Lead-210 within the same radioactive series.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 and Lead-210 exhibit equal activity levels in undisturbed geological materials.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity ratio,decay chain,decay sequence,equal activity,equilibrium indicator,forms,isotopic pair,parent-daughter,radioactive balance</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025</data>
