</edge>
<edge source="Radium-226" target="Lead-214">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Radium-226 decays into Lead-214, which is used to determine its activity concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead-214 emission lines are used to determine the activity concentration of Radium-226.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead-214 is used to derive Radium-226 activity concentrations, though values may be lower due to Radon-222 escape.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is measured via its decay product Lead-214.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is measured in equilibrium with Lead-214 and Bismuth-214.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity derivation,analytical method,daughter isotope,decay chain,decay product,equilibrium,isotope correlation,measurement association,radioactive decay</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006</data>
