<edge source="HAP-BC" target="Pb(II)">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HAP-BC adsorbs Pb(II) ions with a higher maximum capacity than unmodified BC.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC is used as an adsorbent to remove Pb(II) ions from solution.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC removes Pb(II) ions primarily through chemical precipitation and hexagonal pyromorphite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Pb(II) ions with a maximum capacity of 961.54 mg/g in the ternary system.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Pb(II) through monolayer coverage, demonstrating the highest removal capacity among the tested metals.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC effectively adsorbs and removes Pb(II) ions from water solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pb(II) likely forms monolayer coverage on HAP-BC.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,adsorption mechanism,capacity measurement,chemical precipitation,enhanced capacity,heavy metal removal,monolayer coverage,removal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791289150</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HAP-BC" target="Zn(II)">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HAP-BC adsorbs Zn(II) ions with a higher maximum capacity than unmodified BC.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC is used as an adsorbent to remove Zn(II) ions from solution.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC removes Zn(II) ions primarily through electrostatic interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Zn(II) ions with a maximum capacity of 980.39 mg/g in the ternary system.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Zn(II) in multilayers, with removal capacity slightly reduced at high NaCl concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC effectively adsorbs and removes Zn(II) ions from water solutions.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,capacity measurement,electrostatic interaction,enhanced capacity,heavy metal removal,multilayer formation,removal</data>
