  <data key="d12">1791332011</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Scherrer Equation" target="Average Crystallite Size">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Scherrer equation calculates the average crystallite size by inversely relating it to the XRD peak width.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scherrer Equation calculates the average crystallite size using peak width and wavelength parameters.</data>
  <data key="d9">calculation,crystallite analysis,mathematical calculation,measurement formula</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791332023</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Scherrer Equation" target="CuKa">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Scherrer Equation utilizes the CuKa wavelength to calculate crystallite size.</data>
  <data key="d9">uses,wavelength parameter</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791332024</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Scherrer Equation" target="Bragg Angle">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Scherrer Equation incorporates the Bragg Angle to determine crystallite dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scherrer equation utilizes the Bragg angle to account for diffraction geometry.</data>
  <data key="d9">angular parameter,angular position,uses,utilizes</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017</data>
