<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Grashof Number Equation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Grashof Number is mathematically defined by the equation $Gr = \frac{g \beta \Delta T H^3}{v^2}$.</data>
  <data key="d9">formula,mathematical definition</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791674254</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Fluid Dynamics">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Grashof Number is a fundamental dimensionless parameter used within the field of fluid dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluid dynamics utilizes the Grashof Number to analyze flow characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,dimensionless parameter,domain,scientific field</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791674255</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Heat Transfer">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Grashof Number is applied in heat transfer analysis to model thermal processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat transfer utilizes the Grashof Number to evaluate thermal convection.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,dimensionless parameter,domain,scientific field</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791674255</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Natural Convection">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Grashof number is used alongside the Prandtl number to calculate the Rayleigh number for convection analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The Grashof Number determines the onset and characteristics of natural convection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Grashof Number characterizes natural convection in phosphogypsum processing.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,calculation parameter,characterization,dimensionless number,flow prediction,physical phenomenon</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791674256</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Grashof Number Variables">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Grashof Number is calculated using variables g, beta, Delta T, H, and v.</data>
  <data key="d9">components,mathematical definition</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791674256</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Grashof Number" target="Gravity">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
