<edge source="C/S Molar Ratio" target="Desulfurization Rate">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The C/S molar ratio significantly affects the desulfurization rate during the smelting process.&lt;SEP&gt;The C/S molar ratio is investigated for its impact on sulfur escape and desulfurization efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjusting the C/S molar ratio alters the desulfurization rate, with higher ratios causing a noticeable decline in efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The C/S molar ratio critically influences the desulfurization rate, with higher ratios increasing sulfide residues and lowering the rate.</data>
  <data key="d9">compositional factor,compositional parameter,performance influence,performance trend,process influence,process parameter</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008</data>
